local _, ns = ...
local E = ns.DB.entries
E["item:amethyst-phial"] = {t="item",n="Amethyst Phial",z="teldrassil",s="The Amethyst Phial is a delicate ceremonial vessel entrusted to young night elf adventurers by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar. It is crafted specifically to gather and preserve sacred waters from the premier moonwell beneath the Oracle Tree.",h="The Amethyst Phial is a delicate ceremonial vessel entrusted to young night elf adventurers by Corithras...",sec={{t="Vessel of Sacred Waters",b="Entrusted to initiates on Teldrassil, the Amethyst Phial is the final vessel used in the Crown of the Earth pilgrimage. Corithras Moonrage tasks travelers with carrying it to the far northwestern reaches of the boughs, nestled within the Oracle Glade. There, beneath the ancient canopy of the Oracle Tree, lies the island's first and most potent moonwell. The phial is carefully dipped into these radiant waters to draw out the essence of Elune's grace, allowing druids and priestesses to study and tend to the unpredictable growth of the World Tree.",sp=0},{t="A Burden of Unblessed Growth",b="Collecting this sample is more than a routine rite of devotion. Teldrassil was raised under the guidance of Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm without the blessings of the Dragon Aspects, who refused to endorse what they considered an act of arrogance. As a consequence, the boughs suffer from an unsettling corruption, and the kaldorei remain mortal. Filling the Amethyst Phial serves as both a spiritual ritual and an ongoing survey, allowing researchers in Dolanaar to scrutinize the purity of Teldrassil's sacred waters.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Amethyst Phial used for?",a="The phial is given to adventurers by Corithras Moonrage to gather water from the first and most powerful moonwell on Teldrassil, located in the Oracle Glade beneath the great Oracle Tree.",al={"amethyst phial purpose","what do i do with amethyst phial","amethyst phial use"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do I fill the Amethyst Phial?",a="It must be dipped into the moonwell situated far to the northwest of Dolanaar, past the gates of Darnassus, within the secluded grove known as the Oracle Glade.",al={"where to fill amethyst phial","amethyst phial location","oracle glade moonwell"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why is the water from the Oracle Glade so important?",a="The moonwell resting under the Oracle Tree is considered the first and most potent well established on the World Tree. Its waters are deeply suffused with the essence of Elune, making them vital for monitoring the spiritual and physical health of Teldrassil.",al={"why oracle glade water","oracle tree moonwell power","significance of oracle well"},it="motive"},{q="Who sends you to use this phial?",a="Corithras Moonrage, a night elf druid stationed in Dolanaar, provides the phial as part of the ritual tasks aimed at understanding the troubled nature of Teldrassil's growth.",al={"who gives amethyst phial","corithras moonrage phial","who wants the amethyst phial"},it="why_me"},{q="What is the Amethyst Phial?",a="The Amethyst Phial is an empty ceremonial vessel given to travelers in Teldrassil. Crafted specifically to hold pure, enchanted liquid, its purpose is to draw and safeguard water from the moonwell resting beneath the ancient Oracle Tree.",al={"amethyst phial","what is this phial","amethyst vial"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Corithras Moonrage want the Amethyst Phial filled?",a="Corithras Moonrage seeks water from the premier moonwell at the Oracle Glade to study the strange state of Teldrassil. Because the great World Tree lacks the blessings of the dragon aspects, its growth remains flawed and unpredictable, prompting the druids to scrutinize its most sacred waters.",al={"why fill the amethyst phial","why corithras wants phial","purpose of amethyst phial"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, filling this phial is a solemn duty that directly confronts the troubling flaws in Teldrassil's unblessed creation.",["class:Druid"]="Druids recognize the vessel as a critical tool for monitoring the vital energies and creeping corruptions threatening the World Tree's ecosystem."},kw={"amethyst phial","corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","moonwell","oracle glade","oracle tree","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:corithras-moonrage","item:filled-amethyst-phial","quest:921","subzone:oracle-glade","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune","topic:druid"},src={"Amethyst Phial","Crown of the Earth (5)","Teldrassil: The Burden of the Kaldorei"}}
E["item:black-feather-quill"] = {t="item",n="Black Feather Quill",z="teldrassil",s="The Black Feather Quill is a sacred night elf relic used by the Druids of the Talon during their rites of hibernation and awakening. Stored within a dedicated chest in the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, it is one of several vital focuses needed to safely call slumbering druids back from the Emerald Dream.",h="The Black Feather Quill is a sacred night elf relic used by the Druids of the Talon during their rites of...",sec={{t="A Vessel of Wakening",b="Night elf druidism relies on deeply attuned sacred items to navigate the threshold between the waking world and the Emerald Dream. The Black Feather Quill, along with the Raven Claw Talisman, the Sapphire of Sky, and the Rune of Nesting, forms the core set of ritual items required to break the delicate hibernation of the Druids of the Talon. Without these focuses, a slumbering druid risks remaining trapped within the Dream indefinitely, unable to rejoin their waking body.",sp=0},{t="The Threat in Ban'ethil",b="When corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs overran the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, the sacred chests housing these treasures fell into danger. Left unguarded in the winding depths, the relics had to be recovered swiftly by order of Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar before the captive druids were lost forever to the Dream.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Black Feather Quill used for?",a="The quill is one of the four Relics of Wakening necessary to safely wake Druids of the Talon from their ritual hibernation in the Emerald Dream.",al={"black feather quill purpose","why need black feather quill","what does the quill do"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the Black Feather Quill kept?",a="It is kept within the Chest of the Black Feather, located deep inside the Ban'ethil Barrow Den in central Teldrassil.",al={"black feather quill location","where is chest of black feather","quill location"},it="place"},{q="Why can't the druids wake up without the quill and other relics?",a="Druidic hibernation involves entering the Emerald Dream under delicate enchantments. Breaking that trance requires specific sacred focuses; without them, the slumbering spirit cannot properly navigate back to its physical body.",al={"why do druids need relics to wake","can druids wake up on their own"},it="power"},{q="Who asks for the Black Feather Quill?",a="Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar directs adventurers to recover the quill along with the other Relics of Wakening to rescue the imperiled druids.",al={"who needs the quill","black feather quill quest giver"},it="target"},{q="What is the Black Feather Quill?",a="The Black Feather Quill is one of four sacred Relics of Wakening preserved by the night elf Druids of the Talon within Teldrassil's Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Stored within a dedicated chest, it is an essential ceremonial component used to peacefully wake slumbering druids from the Emerald Dream.",al={"what is black feather quill","black feather quill item","black feather quill lore"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids, the quill represents the sacred tools that tether practitioners of the Talon to the waking world while their spirits commune with the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="Night elves view the defilement of Ban'ethil's relic chests by Gnarlpine furbolgs as another painful reminder of Teldrassil's encroaching corruption."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","ban'ethil barrow den","black feather quill","chest of the black feather","dolanaar","druids of the talon","relics of wakening"},rel={"quest:483","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","item:raven-claw-talisman","item:sapphire-of-sky","item:rune-of-nesting","npc:athridas-bearmantle","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Black Feather Quill","The Relics of Wakening"}}
E["item:bloodfeather-belt"] = {t="item",n="Bloodfeather Belt",z="teldrassil",s="A Bloodfeather Belt is a crude leather strap worn by the Bloodfeather harpies infesting northern Teldrassil. Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak collects these belts as proof that local nests encroaching on the Oracle Glade have been cleared.",h="A Bloodfeather Belt is a crude leather strap worn by the Bloodfeather harpies infesting northern Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Trophies from the Nests",b="The Bloodfeather harpies have nested aggressively in the boughs around the Oracle Glade, threatening the ancient Oracle Tree and choking travel through northern Teldrassil. When a runner carrying reports to Darnassus was ambushed and slain by the flock, Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak called on travelers to strike back directly at their nests. Taking the belts from fallen harpies serves as tangible proof that their numbers are being culled, securing the paths so communication with the capital can resume.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak want these belts?",a="Arynia Cloudsbreak and her small detachment of Sentinels are stationed to protect the sacred Oracle Tree from the surrounding Bloodfeather nests. Because the harpies recently killed a messenger bound for Darnassus, Arynia demands the belts as physical proof that adventurers are clearing the nests and thinning the flock's ranks.",al={"why arynia wants belts","bloodfeather belt purpose","why collect belts"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do Bloodfeather Belts come from?",a="They are taken from the Bloodfeather harpies residing in the trees and crags surrounding the Oracle Glade in northern Teldrassil. All varieties of harpies in the flock, including wind witches, sorceresses, rogues, and furies, carry them.",al={"who drops bloodfeather belt","where to get belts","bloodfeather belt location"},it="origin"},{q="Why are harpies a problem in the Oracle Glade?",a="The harpies have nested in close proximity to the Oracle Tree, an ancient and revered tree that monitors the health of the World Tree. Their aggressive presence isolates the Sentinels guarding the glade and violently disrupts messages traveling back to Darnassus.",al={"oracle glade harpies","why are harpies in teldrassil","harpy threat oracle tree"},it="conflict"},{q="What is a Bloodfeather Belt?",a="A Bloodfeather Belt is a personal ornament worn by the Bloodfeather harpies infesting the Oracle Glade in northern Teldrassil. To the night elves stationed at the glade, these crude belts serve as trophies and tangible proof that another vicious harpy has been culled from the sacred boughs.",al={"bloodfeather belt info","what are bloodfeather belts","bloodfeather belt lore"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Bloodfeather coven desecrates the natural canopy of Teldrassil, and reclaiming the Oracle Glade from their screeching nests is an essential duty for any protector of the Kaldorei homeland.",["faction:Alliance"]="Aiding Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak ensures the vital reports from the ancient trees of Teldrassil reach the leadership in Darnassus uninterrupted."},kw={"arynia cloudsbreak","bloodfeather","bloodfeather belt","harpy","oracle glade","teldrassil","the enchanted glade"},rel={"quest:937","npc:sentinel-arynia-cloudsbreak","subzone:oracle-glade","topic:harpy","zone:teldrassil","topic:sentinels","quest:940","zone:darnassus"},src={"Bloodfeather Belt","The Enchanted Glade (Classic)"}}
E["item:crystal-phial"] = {t="item",n="Crystal Phial",z="teldrassil",s="A pristine Crystal Phial entrusted to young night elf adventurers by the druid Tenaron Stormgrip in Shadowglen. It is used to draw sacred water from a nearby moonwell, beginning a series of rites meant to honor and nourish the growing World Tree, Teldrassil.",h="A pristine Crystal Phial entrusted to young night elf adventurers by the druid Tenaron Stormgrip in...",sec={{t="A Vessel for Sacred Waters",b="Given to novice night elves atop Aldrassil, this delicate glass phial serves a vital ceremonial purpose. Tenaron Stormgrip tasks young protectors with carrying it to the moonwell just north of the bough to collect its glowing waters. While simple in construction, the phial holds water infused with the sacred legacy of the Well of Eternity. Bringing back a Filled Crystal Phial marks the first step of the Crown of the Earth pilgrimage, teaching young kaldorei the precarious balance of magic, history, and nature in their new island home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Crystal Phial used for?",a="The phial is used to collect blessed water from the moonwell situated just north of Aldrassil in Shadowglen. Once filled, it is returned to Tenaron Stormgrip as part of the quest 'Crown of the Earth.'",al={"crystal phial purpose","use of crystal phial","what do i do with the phial"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives you the Crystal Phial?",a="The druid Tenaron Stormgrip provides the empty Crystal Phial when giving young adventurers their earliest duties atop the great bough of Aldrassil.",al={"who gives crystal phial","where to get crystal phial"}},{q="Why is gathering moonwell water significant?",a="Moonwells contain consecrated waters tied to the essence of the Well of Eternity and the grace of Elune. The water drawn in the phial is used to understand the aftermath of the Third War and to participate in rituals dedicated to nourishing Teldrassil.",al={"why moonwell water","significance of moonwell water","moonwell purpose"}},{q="What happens after the phial is filled?",a="It becomes a Filled Crystal Phial. Delivering it back to Tenaron Stormgrip completes your initial trial and opens up further lessons on the creation and care of the World Tree across Teldrassil.",al={"after filling phial","filled crystal phial use"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Crystal Phial?",a="The Crystal Phial is a delicate, specially crafted vessel provided by Tenaron Stormgrip atop Aldrassil in Shadowglen. Designed to safely transport sacred liquids, its pure crystal construction ensures that the delicate magical energies of moonwell water remain uncorrupted as you carry it back from the forest's holy shrines.",al={"what is crystal phial","crystal phial item"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Tenaron Stormgrip want the Crystal Phial filled?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip asks you to fill the Crystal Phial as the first step of your initiation into night elf society and the broader world. Moonwells contain waters blessed with the legacy of the Well of Eternity, revered by Sentinels as shrines to Elune and tended by druids. Gathering its water teaches you about the sacrifices made at Mount Hyjal and tests your readiness to understand the fragile state of Teldrassil.",al={"why fill crystal phial","why does tenaron want moonwell water","tenaron crystal phial why"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young kaldorei taking their first steps outside Aldrassil, filling this phial is a foundational rite of passage, connecting them directly to the waters of Elune and the recovery of their people after the Third War.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold moonwells in deep reverence, drawing on their serene properties to channel natural energies and nurture new growth without succumbing to the temptations of arcane sorcery."},kw={"aldrassil","crown of the earth","crystal phial","moonwell","shadowglen","teldrassil","tenaron stormgrip"},rel={"quest:921","item:filled-crystal-phial","npc:tenaron-stormgrip","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune","topic:nordrassil"},src={"Crystal Phial","Crown of the Earth"}}
E["item:dolanaar-delivery"] = {t="item",n="Dolanaar Delivery",z="teldrassil",s="The Dolanaar Delivery is a package of harvested herbs sent from the druidic grounds of Shadowglen to the village of Dolanaar. Entrusted to young travelers leaving the sheltered glen, it serves as a simple errand to connect them with Innkeeper Keldamyr down the road.",h="The Dolanaar Delivery is a package of harvested herbs sent from the druidic grounds of Shadowglen to the...",sec={{t="A Bundle from Shadowglen",b="Harvested within the shadowed groves of Aldrassil, this parcel contains fresh herbs gathered for the settlement of Dolanaar. Porthannius, detained by ongoing matters among the druids of Shadowglen, relies on fledgling adventurers bound southward along the road to ferry the bundle safely to Innkeeper Keldamyr.",sp=0},{t="Welcome to the Hearth",b="Delivering the parcel brings the traveler straight to the threshold of Dolanaar's inn. Keldamyr receives the goods with gratitude, using the exchange to remind weary wayfarers of the necessity of rest, peace of mind, and the sanctuary offered by an inn's hearth before they venture deeper into Teldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Dolanaar Delivery?",a="The package contains a selection of fresh herbs gathered in Shadowglen, intended to supply Innkeeper Keldamyr and the patrons of Dolanaar's inn.",al={"what herbs are inside","contents of dolanaar delivery","whats in the package"},it="item"},{q="Who sends this delivery?",a="Porthannius, an elf attending to business with the druids in Shadowglen, prepares the bundle but cannot spare the time to journey south himself.",al={"who gives the delivery","who sent the herbs","porthannius delivery"},it="origin"},{q="Who receives the package in Dolanaar?",a="The delivery is brought directly to Innkeeper Keldamyr, who manages the communal inn in the heart of Dolanaar.",al={"who do i bring the herbs to","dolanaar delivery recipient","keldamyr herbs"},it="target"},{q="Why couldn't Porthannius deliver the parcel himself?",a="Porthannius has urgent, unfinished business with the druids stationed around Aldrassil, forcing him to seek out a traveling adventurer heading south along the forest road.",al={"why porthannius stay","why did porthannius send me"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Dolanaar Delivery?",a="The Dolanaar Delivery is a package of fresh herbs gathered in Shadowglen and bound for the settlement of Dolanaar to the south. Entrusted to you by Porthannius, it represents routine trade and provisions passing from the sheltered groves of the barrow den down to the larger night elf community.",al={"what is dolanaar delivery","dolanaar parcel","shadowglen package"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Innkeeper Keldamyr want the Dolanaar Delivery?",a="Innkeeper Keldamyr relies on these fresh herbs from Shadowglen to maintain supplies at the Dolanaar inn. Herbs are essential for brewing draughts, cooking restorative meals, and tending to tired travelers and defenders who seek rest and healing on Teldrassil.",al={"why does keldamyr need herbs","dolanaar herbs purpose","why want dolanaar delivery"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="The delivery highlights the steady demand for flora harvested around Aldrassil to stock the outlying settlements of Teldrassil.",["race:NightElf"]="Taking the package marks a rite of passage for young kaldorei stepping beyond the protective boughs of Shadowglen into the wider realm."},kw={"aldrassil","delivery","dolanaar","herbs","keldamyr","porthannius","shadowglen"},rel={"quest:2159","npc:innkeeper-keldamyr","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid"},src={"Dolanaar Delivery","Dolanaar Delivery (quest)"}}
E["item:emerald-dreamcatcher"] = {t="item",n="Emerald Dreamcatcher",z="teldrassil",s="The Emerald Dreamcatcher is a sacred night elf amulet crafted to draw subtle vigor from the Emerald Dream. Bestowed upon Tallonkai Swiftroot by the druids of Ban'ethil Barrow Den, it was left behind in Starbreeze Village when the Gnarlpine furbolgs succumbed to corruption and overran the settlement.",h="The Emerald Dreamcatcher is a sacred night elf amulet crafted to draw subtle vigor from the Emerald Dream.",sec={{t="A Gift from Ban'ethil",b="Crafted under the auspices of Gaerolas Talvethren, the druidic warden of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, the Emerald Dreamcatcher is an enchanted relic given to only a chosen few. It is designed to siphon ambient energies directly from the Emerald Dream, blessing whoever carries it with fortune and protection. When Starbreeze Village fell to the maddened Gnarlpine furbolg, the amulet was left behind inside a dresser, stranded in the middle of hostile, corrupted territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the Emerald Dreamcatcher do?",a="According to Tallonkai Swiftroot, the amulet siphons raw energy from the Emerald Dream, granting luck and vitality to whoever possesses it. It is considered a rare token of favor from the Cenarion druids.",al={"emerald dreamcatcher powers","what is the dreamcatcher for","dreamcatcher lore"},it="power"},{q="Who made the Emerald Dreamcatcher?",a="It was gifted to Tallonkai by Gaerolas Talvethren, the druid warden watching over the sleeping Cenarion circle within the Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",al={"who crafted the dreamcatcher","who gave tallonkai the dreamcatcher"},it="origin"},{q="Why was the dreamcatcher left behind in Starbreeze Village?",a="Tallonkai had stored the amulet inside his dresser in Starbreeze Village. When the local Gnarlpine furbolgs were consumed by corruption and turned violent, the settlement had to be abandoned before he could retrieve it.",al={"why did tallonkai leave it","where was the dreamcatcher lost"},it="history"},{q="Why are the furbolgs in Starbreeze Village hostile?",a="The Gnarlpine tribe across Teldrassil has fallen victim to a dark, spreading corruption that drives them into an aggressive frenzy, forcing the night elves to flee outlying settlements like Starbreeze.",al={"why did star breeze fall","starbreeze village furbolgs"},it="hostile"},{q="What is the Emerald Dreamcatcher?",a="The Emerald Dreamcatcher is a rare and potent enchanted amulet crafted by the druids of Teldrassil. Capable of drawing power directly from the Emerald Dream, it channels soothing nature magic to grant fortune and clarity to whoever bears it. Tallonkai Swiftroot of Dolanaar considers it a prized personal heirloom, one bestowed only upon a favored few.",al={"what is emerald dreamcatcher","emerald dreamcatcher item","what kind of item is dreamcatcher"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Tallonkai Swiftroot want the Emerald Dreamcatcher back?",a="Tallonkai Swiftroot was forced to leave the amulet behind in his dresser when the Gnarlpine furbolgs fell to corruption and overran Starbreeze Village. Beyond its spiritual power to draw fortune from the Emerald Dream, the talisman holds great personal significance to him as a rare gift from Gaerolas Talvethren, warden of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",al={"why does tallonkai want dreamcatcher","why retrieve dreamcatcher","why is dreamcatcher important"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The amulet is a direct link to the slumbering druids of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, demonstrating how their communion with the Emerald Dream extends aid to the Kaldorei settlements below.",["race:NightElf"]="Recovering the relic is a small victory against the spreading sickness claiming Starbreeze Village and the surrounding boughs of Teldrassil."},kw={"ban'ethil barrow den","dolanaar","emerald dreamcatcher","furbolg","gaerolas talvethren","starbreeze village","tallonkai swiftroot","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:2438","npc:tallonkai-swiftroot","subzone:starbreeze-village","npc:gaerolas-talvethren","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","quest:2459","subzone:dolanaar","topic:emerald-dream"},src={"Emerald Dreamcatcher","The Emerald Dreamcatcher (quest)"}}
E["item:encrypted-sigil"] = {t="item",n="Encrypted Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="The Encrypted Sigil is a coded token delivered to newly awakened night elf rogues in Shadowglen. Bearing hidden instructions from the trainer Frahun Shadewhisper, it directs fledgling operatives to initiate their training amidst growing threats to Teldrassil.",h="The Encrypted Sigil is a coded token delivered to newly awakened night elf rogues in Shadowglen.",sec={{t="A Hidden Summons",b="Within the sheltered hollow of Shadowglen, emerging night elf scouts and infiltrators are contacted through discreet means. The Encrypted Sigil is passed directly into an initiate's hands by a quiet messenger on behalf of Frahun Shadewhisper. Concealing its contents in a manner fitting the profession, the sigil instructs the recipient to report to Frahun near Aldrassil. To Shadewhisper, reading and delivering the token proves an initiate can follow subtle directives and handle covert missives.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in the Shadows",b="Frahun uses the summons to stress the necessity of rogues in an unsettled world. With tensions simmering between the night elves and the distant Horde, Shadewhisper reminds his recruits that open warfare is not the only peril facing their people. Rogues must serve as the early eyes and unseen blades of the Kaldorei, gathering intelligence across Teldrassil and learning to strike before threats can take root in the boughs of the World Tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Encrypted Sigil?",a="It serves as an introductory summons for novice night elf rogues. Bearing concealed instructions, it directs the bearer to report to Frahun Shadewhisper near Aldrassil to begin their formal rogue training.",al={"what does the sigil do","what is encrypted sigil for","why do i have encrypted sigil"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends the Encrypted Sigil?",a="The sigil is dispatched by Frahun Shadewhisper, the rogue trainer stationed within Shadowglen beneath the boughs of Aldrassil.",al={"who wrote this sigil","who sent encrypted sigil","who is the sigil from"},it="origin"},{q="What does Frahun Shadewhisper want with me?",a="Frahun wishes to evaluate your readiness, emphasize the growing dangers threatening the night elves—including potential discord stirred by the Horde—and offer foundational combat instruction.",al={"why does frahun want me","frahun quest","why talk to frahun"},it="wants"},{q="Where should I take the sigil once I read it?",a="Bring it to Frahun Shadewhisper, who can be found near the great barrows and paths surrounding the central hollow of Aldrassil in Shadowglen.",al={"where to bring encrypted sigil","frahun location","where is frahun"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is the Encrypted Sigil?",a="The Encrypted Sigil is a coded missive delivered to promising night elf rogues beginning their journey in Shadowglen. Marked with concealed script to safeguard sensitive matters from prying eyes, it serves as an official summons from the local rogue trainer, Frahun Shadewhisper, who seeks to evaluate and mentor fresh talent for the shadowy challenges facing their people.",al={"what is encrypted sigil","encrypted sigil lore","what does the sigil do"},it="identity",rc="Night Elf",add=true},{q="Why does Frahun Shadewhisper want the Encrypted Sigil returned?",a="Frahun Shadewhisper asks you to bring the sigil back to him after deciphering it to verify that you received the summons and can follow tradecraft discreetly. Presenting the token confirms your identity and readiness to begin your formal training in stealth, information gathering, and weaponry.",al={"why does frahun want the sigil","why return encrypted sigil","who wants encrypted sigil"},it="why_wanted",rc="Night Elf",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="The sigil represents the starting point of a night elf rogue's journey, testing your ability to decode instructions and establish contact with your local mentor.",["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, covert operatives provide vital intelligence in a fragile era where ancient woodland borders face new encroachment from the Horde."},kw={"aldrassil","encrypted sigil","frahun shadewhisper","kaldorei rogue","rogue trainer","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:3118","npc:frahun-shadewhisper","subzone:shadowglen","subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","topic:rogue","topic:horde"},src={"Encrypted Sigil","Encrypted Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["item:etched-sigil"] = {t="item",n="Etched Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="An inscribed token delivered to aspiring night elf hunters awakening in Shadowglen. Carried by a woodland runner, it bears a summons from the hunter trainer Ayanna Everstride atop the great bough of Aldrassil.",h="An inscribed token delivered to aspiring night elf hunters awakening in Shadowglen.",sec={{t="Summons of the Wilds",b="Carved with the marks of the hunt, the Etched Sigil is handed to newly awakened night elf hunters as they step into Shadowglen. The token serves as an official notice and welcome from Ayanna Everstride, the local hunter trainer residing high within the hollowed boughs of Aldrassil. Instructing the novice to seek her out, the sigil begins a lifelong tutelage in archery, wilderness tracking, and the ancient night elven bond between stalker and beast.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Etched Sigil?",a="The sigil is a direct summons instructing a novice night elf hunter to seek out their trainer, Ayanna Everstride, atop Aldrassil in Shadowglen to begin formal instruction in survival, tracking, and archery.",al={"what does etched sigil do","etched sigil use","why do i have this sigil"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends the Etched Sigil?",a="It is crafted and dispatched by Ayanna Everstride, the hunter trainer who watches over fledgling woodland stalkers in Shadowglen.",al={"who sent etched sigil","where did etched sigil come from"},it="origin"},{q="Where should the sigil be taken?",a="It must be brought to the upper reaches of the great tree Aldrassil, situated at the heart of Shadowglen, where Ayanna Everstride awaits.",al={"where do i bring etched sigil","who do i give etched sigil to"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why do night elf hunters receive a sigil rather than a paper letter?",a="Kaldorei traditions favor natural carvings and durable tokens etched with sacred symbols of Elune and the wild over standard parchment, reflecting the nature of the hunter's bond with the forest.",al={"why a sigil instead of letter","what is the sigil made of"}},{q="What is the Etched Sigil?",a="The Etched Sigil is a token inscribed with a summons meant for aspiring night elf hunters within Shadowglen. Carried by a courier and placed in your hands upon your arrival in Teldrassil, it serves as an official introduction to Ayanna Everstride, inviting you to begin your formal discipline in marksmanship and beast training beneath Aldrassil's boughs.",al={"what is etched sigil","etched sigil item","about etched sigil"},it="identity",rc="Night Elf",add=true},{q="Why does Ayanna Everstride want you to bring her the Etched Sigil?",a="Ayanna Everstride sends the sigil to ensure you know where to find guidance in Shadowglen. Returning it to her at the top of Aldrassil proves you received her message and are ready to commence your training, learning to wield bows with unerring precision and respect the wild creatures of Kalimdor.",al={"why bring etched sigil","why does ayanna want the sigil","who wants the etched sigil"},it="why_wanted",rc="Night Elf",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This inscribed talisman marks the very beginning of a kaldorei hunter's journey to master the bow and the ways of beasts under the guidance of Ayanna Everstride.",["race:NightElf"]="Delivered in the secluded canopy of Shadowglen, the sigil honors the ancient traditions of night elven foresters dedicated to safeguarding Teldrassil."},kw={"aldrassil","ayanna everstride","etched sigil","hunter","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:3117","npc:ayanna-everstride","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:hunter","topic:elune"},src={"Etched Sigil","Etched Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["item:fel-cone"] = {t="item",n="Fel Cone",z="teldrassil",s="Fel Cones are corrupted seed pods that drop from the boughs of Teldrassil, easily spotted by the noxious green fumes drifting from their hulls. Though foul and tainted by dark energies, local night elf defenders find clever uses for them against nearby tricksters.",h="Fel Cones are corrupted seed pods that drop from the boughs of Teldrassil, easily spotted by the noxious...",sec={{t="Blight in the Canopy",b="Teldrassil is young, but corruption has already seeped into its living wood. Fel Cones are the visible evidence of this insidious rot—gnarled, fallen pine cones that billow with foul green smoke. Scattered beneath the boughs just east of Dolanaar, these pods are steeped in tainted magic that warps natural flora and makes them dangerous to touch or consume without caution.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Medicine",b="When careless travelers fall for the wiles of Zenn Foulhoof—a lurking satyr who tricks passersby into doing his bidding—local guardians demand penance. Syral Bladeleaf and the Sentinels direct remorseful adventurers to gather these noxious cones and hand them over to Foulhoof under the guise of an innocent snack. The concentrated corruption within the seed triggers a peculiar transformation, temporarily turning the foul satyr into a harmless frog.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a Fel Cone?",a="A Fel Cone is a corrupted pine cone that falls from the boughs of Teldrassil. Tainted by unnatural magic, it smolders with an eerie green smoke and contains volatile, transformative energies.",al={"what are fel cones","fel cone lore","what is fel cone"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Fel Cones be found?",a="They can be found resting on the forest floor beneath the trees just east of Dolanaar, in the heart of Teldrassil.",al={"where are fel cones","fel cone location","how to find fel cones"},gp=true},{q="Why does the Council of the Forest want them collected?",a="If you unwittingly helped the satyr Zenn Foulhoof harm nature's creatures, the Council of the Forest offers a chance to redeem yourself. They instruct you to gather Fel Cones and trick Zenn into eating them as a lesson.",al={"seek redemption cones","why collect fel cones","who wants fel cones"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens when someone eats a Fel Cone?",a="When Zenn Foulhoof eats the Fel Cones thinking they are a harmless snack, the concentrated magic immediately transforms the scheming satyr into a frog.",al={"what does fel cone do","eating fel cone","zenn foulhoof frog"},sp=1},{q="Where do Fel Cones come from, and who made them?",a="Fel Cones are not crafted by mortal hands; they are corrupted seed cones that naturally fall from the boughs of Teldrassil's trees. A foul, billowing green smoke rises from them, showing that the dark corruption plaguing the great world tree has seeped deep into its very seeds and soil.",al={"where do fel cones come from","who made fel cones","fel cone origin"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The existence of Fel Cones is a disturbing sign of sickness deep within Teldrassil's roots, proving that even the World Tree's fledgling growth is not safe from demonic corruption.",["class:Druid"]="Watching wholesome woodland seed pods curdle into smoking fel remnants is a grim reminder to druids of the fragile balance being fought for across Teldrassil."},kw={"dolanaar","fel cone","satyr","seek redemption","syral bladeleaf","teldrassil","zenn foulhoof"},rel={"quest:489","npc:zenn-foulhoof","npc:syral-bladeleaf","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:satyr","topic:night-elf"},src={"Fel Cone","Seek Redemption!"}}
E["item:fel-moss"] = {t="item",n="Fel Moss",z="teldrassil",s="Fel Moss is a tainted vegetative substance spreading through the forests of Teldrassil. Carrying demonic and corruptive energies, it is carried by hostile grell and grellkin and poses an insidious threat to the wildlife and native furbolg tribes of the World Tree.",h="Fel Moss is a tainted vegetative substance spreading through the forests of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Blight on the World Tree",b="Teldrassil was planted to restore the night elves' immortality and heal the natural world, but corruption has already crept into its pristine boughs. Fel Moss is one of the most visible signs of this degradation. Found clinging to and carried by the impish grells and grellkin infesting Shadowglen, this malevolent growth radiates an unnatural, wicked magic. Forest protectors like the dryad Tarindrella have begun gathering samples to measure just how deeply this rot has infiltrated the sacred woodland canopy.",sp=0},{t="Seeds of Madness",b="The danger of Fel Moss extends beyond mere woodland decay; it exerts a virulent influence over the minds of living creatures. Once-peaceful furbolgs native to the heights of Teldrassil have succumbed to its touch, abandoning their traditional dwellings and banding together into the hostile Gnarlpine tribe. Driven mad by the moss's evil powers under leaders like Ursal the Mauler, these afflicted creatures highlight the growing sickness taking root within the great tree.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Fel Moss?",a="Fel Moss is a vile, magically corrupted plant matter found in Teldrassil. Infused with foul energies, it clings to pestilential creatures and spreads madness and physical corruption to the surrounding ecosystem.",al={"fel moss lore","what is fel moss","what does fel moss do"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Fel Moss come from?",a="Within Teldrassil, adventurers recover clumps of Fel Moss from the twisted grell and grellkin roaming the hillsides around Shadowglen. It stems from foul corruptive forces that have taken root within the World Tree itself.",al={"where do you get fel moss","fel moss drop","source of fel moss"},it="origin"},{q="How does Fel Moss affect the furbolgs?",a="Fel Moss acts as a corrupting catalyst. Exposure to its evil powers drives furbolgs into violent mania, transforming the once-peaceful tribes of Teldrassil into the aggressive and xenophobic Gnarlpine tribe.",al={"furbolg corruption","why are gnarlpine mad","gnarlpine fel moss"},it="power"},{q="Who is trying to stop the spread of Fel Moss?",a="The dryad Tarindrella in Shadowglen asks fledgling defenders to gather samples of Fel Moss from grellkin to confirm her suspicions of woodland corruption. She directs concerned protectors onward to druids like Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar.",al={"who studies fel moss","who wants fel moss","tarindrella quest"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Tarindrella want Fel Moss?",a="Tarindrella seeks samples of Fel Moss to confirm whether the aggressive grell and grellkin infesting Shadowglen are acting under its wicked enchantment. By securing this tainted growth, she hopes to gauge how far the corruption has spread and understand the threat facing the nearby Gnarlpine furbolgs.",al={"why collect fel moss","tarindrella fel moss","why do they want fel moss"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids of the Cenarion Circle, Fel Moss represents an alarming cancer spreading through Teldrassil, proving that the newborn World Tree is deeply vulnerable to demonic blight.",["race:NightElf"]="Night elves venerate Teldrassil as their new homeland, making the presence of Fel Moss a distressing omen that peace remains elusive even atop their sacred boughs."},kw={"fel moss","gnarlpine","grell","grellkin","shadowglen","tarindrella","teldrassil","ursal the mauler"},rel={"npc:tarindrella","quest:458","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:furbolg","quest:476","quest:486","npc:athridas-bearmantle"},src={"Fel Moss","The Woodland Protector (2)"}}
E["item:filled-amethyst-phial"] = {t="item",n="Filled Amethyst Phial",z="teldrassil",s="The Filled Amethyst Phial contains sacred water taken from the ancient moonwell beneath the boughs of the Oracle Tree. Gathered on behalf of Corithras Moonrage, this purified water is used by the Cenarion druids to study the troubled, imperfect growth of Teldrassil.",h="The Filled Amethyst Phial contains sacred water taken from the ancient moonwell beneath the boughs of the...",sec={{t="Water of the Oracle Tree",b="Far to the northwest in Teldrassil lies the Oracle Glade, where the oldest and most potent of the island's moonwells rests beneath the great Oracle Tree. While the lesser moonwells across the boughs serve the day-to-day needs of the night elves, this well's waters are saturated with the raw essence of Elune's grace. Druids tasked with monitoring the health of the World Tree use specialized amethyst phials to collect and preserve this powerful liquid for testing and ritual cleansing.",sp=0},{t="A Flawed Renewal",b="Bringing this sample back to Corithras Moonrage serves a somber purpose. Despite Archdruid Fandral Staghelm's triumph in raising Teldrassil to replace the fallen Nordrassil, the Dragon Aspects refused to sanctify it. Without the blessing of Nozdormu to restore night elven immortality or Alexstrasza to protect its life force, Teldrassil's growth remains stunted and plagued by corruption. Samples from the glade reveal that even the island's most sacred waters cannot hide the creeping malaise taking root in the World Tree.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the water in this phial come from?",a="The water is scooped directly from the moonwell in the Oracle Glade, located in the northwestern reaches of Teldrassil beneath the vast roots of the Oracle Tree.",al={"where do i fill it","moonwell location","oracle tree well"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the moonwell in Oracle Glade special?",a="It is revered as the first and most powerful moonwell created on Teldrassil, holding the concentrated essence of Elune's power and watched over by the ancient Oracle Tree itself.",al={"why oracle glade","oracle moonwell importance"}},{q="Who asks you to gather this water?",a="Corithras Moonrage, a night elf druid stationed in Dolanaar, tasks young adventurers with collecting the water as part of the Crown of the Earth rituals.",al={"who wants the phial","corithras quest"}},{q="Why are the druids testing Teldrassil's moonwells?",a="Teldrassil was raised without the blessings of the Dragon Aspects, leaving it vulnerable. The druids sample the moonwells to monitor the World Tree's health, which is showing troubling signs of corruption and stunted growth.",al={"why test the water","teldrassil sickness"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Filled Amethyst Phial?",a="The Filled Amethyst Phial is a vessel containing sacred water drawn from the moonwell nestled beneath the Oracle Tree in the Oracle Glade. Known as the first and most powerful of Teldrassil's moonwells, its shimmering waters hold the concentrated essence of Elune's grace, making this sample crucial for the kaldorei examining the island's health.",al={"what is filled amethyst phial","filled amethyst phial item","amethyst phial purpose"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, filling this phial marks a grim realization: their glorious new home was rejected by the Dragon Aspects, and their lost immortality has not returned.",["class:Druid"]="Cenarion druids revere moonwells as conduits of nature and astral energy, using purified vessels like this phial to study the blighted ecology of Teldrassil."},kw={"amethyst phial","corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","filled amethyst phial","moonwell","oracle glade","oracle tree","teldrassil"},rel={"item:amethyst-phial","npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:oracle-glade","quest:921","zone:teldrassil","topic:nordrassil","topic:elune","subzone:dolanaar"},src={"Filled Amethyst Phial","Crown of the Earth (5)","Teldrassil: The Burden of the Kaldorei"}}
E["item:filled-crystal-phial"] = {t="item",n="Filled Crystal Phial",z="teldrassil",s="A Filled Crystal Phial contains sacred waters drawn from the moonwell just north of Aldrassil in Shadowglen. Gathered at the instruction of Tenaron Stormgrip, this water serves as a novice's introduction to the sacred and volatile power coursing through Teldrassil.",h="A Filled Crystal Phial contains sacred waters drawn from the moonwell just north of Aldrassil in Shadowglen.",sec={{t="Waters of the Moonwell",b="To prepare young night elves before they venture into the wider world, Tenaron Stormgrip sends them to gather water from the moonwell nestled in Shadowglen. The phial holds more than simple spring water; moonwells are infused with residual energies traced back to the ancient Well of Eternity. While the Sentinels honor these sites as blessed shrines of Elune and druids channel their restorative qualities into tending nature, the arcane sorcery of old remains strictly forbidden. Drawing this water is the first step in understanding the sacrifices of Mount Hyjal and the delicate balance required to nurture Teldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Filled Crystal Phial?",a="The phial holds water drawn from the moonwell north of Aldrassil in Shadowglen. These waters carry remnants of the ancient Well of Eternity, blessed by Elune's light and nurtured by druidic care.",al={"what water is in the phial","phial contents","what is in crystal phial"},it="item"},{q="Who asks you to fill the phial?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip, stationed atop the boughs of Aldrassil, sends fledgling adventurers to draw the water as part of their rite of passage and historical instruction.",al={"who wants the phial","who gives crystal phial quest","tenaron stormgrip quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Tenaron Stormgrip want this water?",a="Tenaron uses the gathering task as an opening lesson on night elf history following the Third War, teaching young adventurers about the sacrifice of Nordrassil, the power of moonwells, and the ongoing stewardship of Teldrassil.",al={"why fill crystal phial","crown of the earth purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Are the waters dangerous?",a="The waters carry potent magic rooted in the ancient Well of Eternity. While druids and priestesses safely use them for blessings and healing, reckless arcane manipulation of such waters brought catastrophe in ancient times and remains strictly outlawed.",al={"is moonwell water dangerous","is the water magic"},it="danger"},{q="What is the Filled Crystal Phial?",a="The Filled Crystal Phial is a delicate crystal vessel containing water gathered from the moonwell in Shadowglen. It holds the pure, sacred liquid infused with the ancient power of the Well of Eternity, meant to serve both as a sacred offering and a practical lesson in your people's ongoing spiritual stewardship.",al={"what is filled crystal phial","filled crystal phial","filled crystal phial item"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does the Filled Crystal Phial come from?",a="It is created when you take an empty crystal phial provided by Tenaron Stormgrip and immerse it directly into the waters of the sacred moonwell situated just north of Aldrassil in Shadowglen.",al={"filled crystal phial origin","where did the filled crystal phial come from","how to get filled crystal phial"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Every young kaldorei who begins their training beneath Aldrassil fills this phial, reflecting upon the sacrifice of Mount Hyjal and their sacred duty to protect nature.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold moonwell water in deep reverence, using its revitalizing energies to tend to corrupted flora and sustain the great trees."},kw={"aldrassil","crown of the earth","crystal phial","filled crystal phial","moonwell","shadowglen","tenaron stormgrip","well of eternity"},rel={"quest:921","item:crystal-phial","npc:tenaron-stormgrip","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune","topic:nordrassil"},src={"Filled Crystal Phial","Crown of the Earth"}}
E["item:filled-jade-phial"] = {t="item",n="Filled Jade Phial",z="teldrassil",s="The Filled Jade Phial holds sacred waters drawn from the moonwell near Starbreeze Village. Carried back to Dolanaar, it serves as part of an ongoing ritual to replenish the capital's central waters while young night elves learn the history of their people.",h="The Filled Jade Phial holds sacred waters drawn from the moonwell near Starbreeze Village.",sec={{t="Waters of Starbreeze",b="The druids of Darnassus rely on sacred moonwell waters drawn from across the boughs of Teldrassil to replenish their central wells. Specially crafted vessels, such as the jade phial entrusted to young adventurers by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar, are attuned to contain these pure waters safely. By venturing eastward to the moonwell outside Starbreeze Village, initiates collect the vital water while proving their devotion to the maintenance of the World Tree.",sp=0},{t="A Lesson in History",b="Returning the Filled Jade Phial to Dolanaar is more than a simple errand; each replenished vessel earns another chapter in the oral history of the kaldorei. Upon receiving the full phial, Corithras Moonrage speaks of the desperate era following the Third War—the burning of Nordrassil, the loss of night elf immortality, the release of the Betrayer, and the sudden disappearance of Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage into the Emerald Dream.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Jade Phial filled?",a="The Jade Phial is filled by interacting with the sacred waters of the moonwell located just outside Starbreeze Village, east of Dolanaar on Teldrassil.",al={"where do i fill the jade phial","how to get filled jade phial","starbreeze moonwell location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who requires the Filled Jade Phial?",a="Corithras Moonrage, an elder night elf stationed in the settlement of Dolanaar, instructs travelers to fetch the water as part of the Crown of the Earth ritual tasks.",al={"who wants the filled jade phial","corithras moonrage quest item"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why are moonwell waters collected in phials like this?",a="The druids residing in Darnassus must periodically replenish their primary moonwells. They use specially crafted vessels like the Jade Phial to safely transport pristine water from outlying wells across Teldrassil.",al={"why collect moonwell water","what is the jade phial for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What history does Corithras share when turning this in?",a="Upon receiving the filled phial, Corithras Moonrage recounts the dark aftermath of the Battle of Mount Hyjal, reflecting on the loss of night elf immortality, the release of Illidan Stormrage, and the baffling slumber of Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage.",al={"what does corithras tell you","crown of the earth lore"},it="history"},{q="What is the Filled Jade Phial?",a="The Filled Jade Phial is a specially crafted jade vessel holding sacred water drawn directly from the moonwell near Starbreeze Village. Infused with lunar energy and nature's grace, such consecrated water is vital to the night elves for sustaining the life of Teldrassil and carrying out their spiritual rites.",al={"what is filled jade phial","filled jade phial lore","filled jade phial"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Fetching the water reinforces a young kaldorei's sacred duty to Teldrassil while imparting crucial history about the loss of immortality after Mount Hyjal.",["class:Druid"]="Tending the moonwells connects druids directly to the restorative magic sustaining Darnassus and the Cenarion Circle's ongoing efforts to nurture the young World Tree."},kw={"corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","filled jade phial","jade phial","moonwell","starbreeze village","teldrassil"},rel={"item:jade-phial","npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:starbreeze-village","subzone:dolanaar","quest:921","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:shan-do"},src={"Filled Jade Phial","Crown of the Earth (3)"}}
E["item:filled-tourmaline-phial"] = {t="item",n="Filled Tourmaline Phial",z="teldrassil",s="The Filled Tourmaline Phial holds enchanted waters drawn from the moonwell bordering the Pools of Arlithrien in southern Teldrassil. Collected at the request of Corithras Moonrage, the water serves as part of an effort to monitor the health and balance of the growing World Tree.",h="The Filled Tourmaline Phial holds enchanted waters drawn from the moonwell bordering the Pools of Arlithrien...",sec={{t="Waters of Arlithrien",b="The Tourmaline Phial is prepared specifically to draw water from the moonwell located southeast of the road to Darnassus, on the shores of the Pools of Arlithrien. Gathering water from this shrine has become fraught with peril due to the sudden aggression of the Gnarlpine furbolgs, peaceful neighbors who have rapidly deteriorated into violent madness. Corithras Moonrage tasks travelers with braving the hostile groves to secure this water, aiming to diagnose the deepening corruption unsettling the land.",sp=0},{t="The Roots of Teldrassil",b="Bringing the phial back to Dolanaar prompts Corithras Moonrage to reflect on the genesis of the boughs above. Following the disappearance of Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage into the Emerald Dream, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm rallied the Circle of Ancients across the sea in Darkshore to plant Teldrassil in hopes of regaining their lost immortality. The waters carried within the gemmed phial reflect the state of that sacred experiment—an ambition now tainted by an unexplained sickness spreading into beasts and furbolgs alike.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Filled Tourmaline Phial used for?",a="It is an enchanted container of moonwell water requested by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar. He gathers waters from moonwells across Teldrassil to study the spread of corruption and explain the history of the World Tree to newly arrived defenders.",al={"filled tourmaline phial use","tourmaline phial purpose","why fill the phial"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where is the moonwell for the Tourmaline Phial located?",a="The moonwell is located southeast of the main gate of Darnassus, situated along the shores of the Pools of Arlithrien in southwestern Teldrassil. The area is heavily contested by enraged Gnarlpine furbolgs.",al={"where do i fill tourmaline phial","pools of arlithrien moonwell","arlithrien well location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the furbolgs near the moonwell attacking?",a="The Gnarlpine furbolgs, once peaceful bear-men living alongside the night elves, have fallen prey to a creeping corruption afflicting Teldrassil. Their sudden descent into mindless violence is one of several symptoms plaguing the young World Tree.",al={"why are gnarlpine mad","furbolg hostility arlithrien","crazed gnarlpine"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Corithras Moonrage?",a="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf scholar and caretaker stationed in Dolanaar. He guides young adventurers through the rite known as the Crown of the Earth, teaching them about the history of the night elves, the planting of Teldrassil, and the vanishing of Malfurion Stormrage.",al={"corithras role","corithras dolanaar"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Filled Tourmaline Phial?",a="It is an empty tourmaline phial filled with the sacred, luminescent waters of the moonwell near the Pools of Arlithrien in Teldrassil. Night elf druids use phials carved from distinct minerals to harvest pure moonwell water throughout the island, keeping each sample distinct for their sacred rites and the cleansing of the land.",al={"what is filled tourmaline phial","filled tourmaline phial item"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does the Filled Tourmaline Phial come from?",a="The vessel itself is provided by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar. You create the filled phial by taking it southeast of Darnassus to the moonwell resting along the shores of the Pools of Arlithrien and drawing water directly from the basin amidst the prowling, agitated Gnarlpine furbolgs.",al={"filled tourmaline phial origin","where did the filled tourmaline phial come from"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does Corithras Moonrage want the Filled Tourmaline Phial?",a="Corithras Moonrage collects the waters from Teldrassil's various moonwells to assess and preserve the spiritual vitality of the young World Tree. As corruption creeps into the boughs and maddens the native Gnarlpine furbolgs, collecting and examining water from across the boughs helps the druids maintain their sacred balance and understand what plagues their home.",al={"why does corithras want the phial","filled tourmaline phial purpose","why gather moonwell water"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids, carrying the phial touches directly upon the controversial legacy of Archdruid Fandral Staghelm, who pushed to plant Teldrassil during Shan'do Stormrage's unexplained absence.",["race:NightElf"]="The moonwell waters are an essential spiritual lifeline for the kaldorei, making the corruption of the surrounding Gnarlpine groves a deeply unsettling omen for their new home."},kw={"corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","filled tourmaline phial","gnarlpine","moonwell","pools of arlithrien","teldrassil","tourmaline phial"},rel={"item:tourmaline-phial","quest:921","npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:pools-of-arlithrien","subzone:dolanaar","npc:fandral-staghelm","topic:furbolg","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Filled Tourmaline Phial","Crown of the Earth (4)"}}
E["item:filled-vessel"] = {t="item",n="Filled Vessel",z="teldrassil",s="The Filled Vessel contains purified waters drawn from the various sacred moonwells across Teldrassil. Entrusted to couriers by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar, it is delivered to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus to aid his study of the World Tree's ailments.",h="The Filled Vessel contains purified waters drawn from the various sacred moonwells across Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Confluence of Sacred Waters",b="Teldrassil was planted without the blessings of the Great Aspects, Alexstrasza and Nozdormu, leaving its immense boughs vulnerable to unexpected corruption, strange beasts, and crazed furbolg tribes. In an attempt to monitor and cleanse the burgeoning boughs, night elf acolytes are dispatched to gather water samples from moonwells situated across the boughs. Corithras Moonrage consolidates these gathered phials into a single Filled Vessel, sending it onward to the capital. The mixture serves as a vital sample of Teldrassil's vitality for Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm, who works tirelessly in the Cenarion Enclave to uncover a remedy for the Great Tree's pervasive flaws.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Filled Vessel?",a="The vessel contains water collected from several moonwells scattered across Teldrassil, consolidated into a single container by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.",al={"vessel contents","what water is this","what is in the vessel"},it="identity"},{q="Who needs the Filled Vessel?",a="The Filled Vessel is brought to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm, who resides at the top of the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus.",al={"who do I give the filled vessel to","where does the vessel go","filled vessel hand in"},it="target"},{q="Why does Fandral Staghelm need these water samples?",a="Teldrassil lacks the traditional dragon aspects' blessings, causing strange corruptions, aggressive wildlife, and mad furbolgs to plague its branches. Staghelm studies these mingled waters to diagnose the tree's flaws and seek a remedy for its afflictions.",al={"why staghelm wants water","staghelm moonwell water purpose","why collect moonwell water"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who prepared the vessel?",a="Corithras Moonrage, a night elf stationed in Dolanaar, pours the phials gathered by young adventurers into the vessel before dispatching them to Darnassus.",al={"who made the filled vessel","who gives the filled vessel","corithras filled vessel"},it="origin"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For Cenarion initiates, delivering this vessel marks their first official errand to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm, showing firsthand the ecological fragility facing Teldrassil.",["race:NightElf"]="The moonwell waters inside represent the sacred lifelines of the kaldorei's new home, mingling the magic of Elune with the uncertain growth of the unblessed World Tree."},kw={"cenarion enclave","corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","darnassus","fandral staghelm","filled vessel","moonwell water","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:921","npc:fandral-staghelm","npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:cenarion-enclave","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},src={"Filled Vessel","Crown of the Earth (6)"}}
E["item:gargantuan-tumor"] = {t="item",n="Gargantuan Tumor",z="teldrassil",s="The Gargantuan Tumor is a massive, diseased growth torn from the corrupted timberling Oakenscowl in Teldrassil. It serves as glaring proof of the unnatural sickness spreading through the creatures inhabiting Lake Al'Ameth.",h="The Gargantuan Tumor is a massive, diseased growth torn from the corrupted timberling Oakenscowl in...",sec={{t="Blight Upon the Lake",b="Near the southern bank of Lake Al'Ameth, a cavern shelters Oakenscowl, once a noble timberling elder who has fallen prey to vile affliction. The creature was visibly poisoned by an enormous growth that warped its behavior and seeped taint into surrounding wildlife. Severing this grotesque tumor is crucial not only to end the beast's tormented rampage, but to allow local researchers to inspect the blight and understand how such a foul malady took root in the boughs of the newly grown World Tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Gargantuan Tumor come from?",a="The tumor is retrieved from Oakenscowl, a large corrupted timberling residing in a cave on the southern shore of Lake Al'Ameth in Teldrassil.",al={"tumor source","how to get gargantuan tumor","oakenscowl drop"},it="origin"},{q="What is causing the tumor to grow on Oakenscowl?",a="It is an outward symptom of the strange corruption poisoning the timberlings and wildlife around Lake Al'Ameth. Oakenscowl was once a grand leader of his kind, but succumbed entirely to this virulent growth.",al={"why does oakenscowl have a tumor","timberling sickness","lake al'ameth corruption"}},{q="Who wants to study this tumor?",a="Investigators in the area require the tumor to research the strange rot afflicting local timberlings, hoping to discern how to treat or halt the blight.",al={"who takes the tumor","turn in gargantuan tumor","oakenscowl quest turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Gargantuan Tumor?",a="It is a massive, grotesque growth cut from Oakenscowl, a corrupted timberling elder lurking in a cave along the southern bank of Lake Al'Ameth. The tumor is visibly poisoning the creature and driving it mad, fueling the spread of unnatural rot and affliction across the local waters and nearby wildlife.",al={"what is gargantuan tumor","gargantuan tumor","tumor of oakenscowl"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids striving to nurture the fledgling boughs of Teldrassil, the grotesque tumor is an alarming reminder that nature within the boughs is dangerously vulnerable to corruption.",["race:NightElf"]="Seeing a respected elder timberling reduced to a mad, blighted monster underscores the growing environmental troubles facing the kaldorei's new homeland."},kw={"corruption","gargantuan tumor","lake al'ameth","oakenscowl","teldrassil","timberling"},rel={"quest:2499","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},src={"Gargantuan Tumor","Oakenscowl (Classic)"}}
E["item:glowing-fruit"] = {t="item",n="Glowing Fruit",z="teldrassil",s="The Glowing Fruit is an exotic, luminescent specimen found growing amid strange fronds on the boughs of Teldrassil. Its unnatural radiance and bizarre interaction with the World Tree's soil make it an object of urgent botanical study for naturalists.",h="The Glowing Fruit is an exotic, luminescent specimen found growing amid strange fronds on the boughs of...",sec={{t="A Curious Specimen",b="Discovered hanging beneath unusual fronds on Teldrassil, this large, round fruit radiates an unmistakable light. Botanist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth recognizes it as non-native to the World Tree, speculating its seeds arrived from distant lands across the sea. Whatever its origin, the fruit reacts strangely to the rich, enchanted soil of Teldrassil, demonstrating how vulnerable the nascent world bough is to foreign and unpredictable flora.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Glowing Fruit?",a="It is an exotic, round fruit discovered growing under unusual fronds on Teldrassil. It emits an ethereal glow and appears to have reacted unusually with the local soil.",al={"glowing fruit teldrassil","what is this fruit","strange fruit quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where did this fruit come from?",a="According to the naturalist Denalan, the fruit is not native to Teldrassil. He suspects its seeds drifted or were transported from far across the sea, perhaps from the Eastern Kingdoms of Azeroth, before taking root in the soil.",al={"fruit origin","where did the seeds come from","is it native"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants to inspect the Glowing Fruit?",a="Denalan, a night elf researcher stationed at Lake Al'Ameth, studies the boughs and ecosystem of Teldrassil. He takes a keen interest in foreign plant life that has reacted with the World Tree's earth.",al={"who needs the fruit","where do i bring glowing fruit","denalan fruit"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids attuned to the fragile balance of Teldrassil, foreign flora that reacts erratically with the soil represents a potential disturbance to the burgeoning World Tree.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists will immediately note that the strange luminescence of the fruit points to an exotic, potent interaction between outside seed varieties and enchanted soil."},kw={"botany","denalan","glowing fruit","lake al'ameth","plant","teldrassil","timberlings"},rel={"quest:930","npc:denalan","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},src={"Glowing Fruit","The Glowing Fruit"}}
E["item:hallowed-sigil"] = {t="item",n="Hallowed Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="The Hallowed Sigil is an inscribed night elf token carried by young initiates within Shadowglen. Sent by the priest trainer Shanda, it serves as a formal summons directing prospective servants of Elune to the ancient boughs of Aldrassil.",h="The Hallowed Sigil is an inscribed night elf token carried by young initiates within Shadowglen.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Priesthood",b="Novice night elf priests stepping into the sacred canopy of Shadowglen often receive the Hallowed Sigil from a woodland messenger. Engraved with holy markings, the token acts as a personal writ from Shanda, the resident priest trainer at Aldrassil. Carrying and reading the sigil directs an acolyte upward to the towering hollow of Aldrassil, formally introducing them to the Sisterhood of Elune and initiating their spiritual service to the Kaldorei as new travelers arrive across Teldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Hallowed Sigil?",a="The Hallowed Sigil is an inscribed holy token given to young night elf priests in Shadowglen. It carries a summons instructing the initiate to seek out their mentor, Shanda.",al={"what is hallowed sigil","priest sigil shadowglen"},it="identity"},{q="Who sends the Hallowed Sigil?",a="It is dispatched via a local messenger on behalf of Shanda, the priest trainer stationed inside the great hollow tree of Aldrassil.",al={"who sent this sigil","shanda priest token"},it="origin"},{q="Where should I take the sigil?",a="Take the sigil to Shanda inside Aldrassil, situated at the heart of Shadowglen in Teldrassil. After reading it, presenting the token to her completes your initial introduction to your priesthood mentors.",al={"where do i bring hallowed sigil","hallowed sigil turn in"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Shanda want the Hallowed Sigil returned to her?",a="The sigil serves as a formal summons and an introductory token for novice night elf priests. Priestess Shanda sent it through a messenger to call you to Aldrassil, ensuring you seek out her guidance as the wider world stirs and travelers arrive upon Teldrassil's boughs. Returning with it confirms you received her message and stand ready to begin your sacred training.",al={"why bring hallowed sigil to shanda","why does shanda want the sigil","hallowed sigil purpose"},it="why_wanted",rc="Night Elf",add=true}},ang={["class:Priest"]="For night elf priests, the Hallowed Sigil represents their very first summons into formal training under the Sisterhood of Elune.",["race:NightElf"]="The sigil marks the start of a Kaldorei devotee's service at a time when Alliance travelers have only just begun arriving upon the boughs of Teldrassil."},kw={"aldrassil","hallowed sigil","initiate","kaldorei","priest","shadowglen","shanda","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:3119","npc:shanda","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","topic:priest","zone:teldrassil","topic:alliance"},src={"Hallowed Sigil","Hallowed Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["item:hyacinth-mushroom"] = {t="item",n="Hyacinth Mushroom",z="teldrassil",s="Hyacinth Mushrooms are distinctive fungi found sprouting at the roots of trees throughout Shadowglen on Teldrassil. Prized by local night elf herbalists for their medicinal properties, they also happen to be favored food and forage for the mischievous grell and grellkin.",h="Hyacinth Mushrooms are distinctive fungi found sprouting at the roots of trees throughout Shadowglen on...",sec={{t="Flora of Shadowglen",b="Hyacinth Mushrooms grow abundantly across Shadowglen, flourishing in the damp shadows at the bases of ancient barrows, mossy stones, and the sprawling roots of Aldrassil. While useful in woodland remedies, they have also caught the attention of the corrupted grell, who frequently hoard them. When young night elf sentinels or trainees are afflicted by local venomous fauna—such as the spiders of Shadowthread Cave—these mushrooms serve as a core component in soothing draughts and antivenoms concocted by forest healers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Hyacinth Mushrooms used for?",a="Priestess Dirania Silvershine uses them as a vital ingredient to concoct an antidote for Iverron, a young night elf who was bitten and poisoned by venomous spiders while exploring Shadowthread Cave.",al={"hyacinth mushroom use","what does it do","iverron cure"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do Hyacinth Mushrooms grow?",a="They sprout directly on the ground near the trunks and roots of large trees, as well as beside boulders throughout the secluded vale of Shadowglen on Teldrassil.",al={"mushroom location","where to find hyacinth mushroom","shadowglen mushrooms"},it="place"},{q="Why do the grell carry Hyacinth Mushrooms?",a="The mischievous grell and grellkin infesting southern Shadowglen have taken a peculiar liking to the mushrooms, foraging and hoarding them in their camps.",al={"grell drop mushrooms","why do grell have them","grellkin mushrooms"},it="ties"},{q="Are Hyacinth Mushrooms poisonous themselves?",a="No. Despite their bright appearance and the shady environment in which they flourish, local healers employ them safely as an ingredient in healing poultices and restorative antivenoms.",al={"is hyacinth mushroom toxic","poisonous mushroom"},it="power"},{q="What is a Hyacinth Mushroom?",a="A Hyacinth Mushroom is a native fungus found throughout the shadowy boughs of Teldrassil, particularly around the bases of trees and mossy stones in Shadowglen. Notable for their medicinal value, these woodland mushrooms possess natural properties capable of counteracting venom when properly brewed alongside other local flora.",al={"what is hyacinth mushroom","hyacinth mushroom info","about hyacinth mushrooms"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Though gathering these fungi in Shadowglen requires no formal training, any fledgling herbalist will appreciate their role in neutralizing virulent forest toxins.",["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves training within Shadowglen, harvesting wild flora like Hyacinth Mushrooms is an early lesson in utilizing nature's bounty to sustain their kin."},kw={"antidote","dirania silvershine","grell","grellkin","hyacinth mushroom","iverron","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:3521","npc:iverron","subzone:shadowglen","item:moonpetal-lily","item:webwood-ichor","zone:teldrassil","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowthread-cave"},src={"Hyacinth Mushroom","Iverron's Antidote (Classic)"}}
E["item:inscribed-bark"] = {t="item",n="Inscribed Bark",z="teldrassil",s="Inscribed Bark is a living parchment entrusted by the ancient Oracle Tree to carry word of Teldrassil's state to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm. It serves as an official report on the boughs of the World Tree and the lingering threats troubling its woods.",h="Inscribed Bark is a living parchment entrusted by the ancient Oracle Tree to carry word of Teldrassil's state...",sec={{t="A Message from the Oracle",b="Carved from the sacred wood of the Oracle Tree, this inscribed bark acts as a direct communique between the ancient guardian and the leadership of the Cenarion Circle in Darnassus. After adventurers suppress the encroaching harpies in the glades, the Oracle Tree entrusts them with this token, reluctant to risk ordinary couriers through the tainted paths of the boughs. The inscribed message informs Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm of both recent victories and the deeper, unsettling blight that continues to grip Teldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Inscribed Bark?",a="It is a piece of bark inscribed by the Oracle Tree containing a status report on the health and perils of the boughs, intended for Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.",al={"what is inscribed bark","oracle tree bark","inscribed bark purpose"},it="identity"},{q="Who sends this message and why?",a="The Oracle Tree bestows it upon adventurers after they drive harpies from their nests. Having grown wary of sending ordinary messengers across the endangered forest paths, the ancient entrusts a proven traveler to deliver its report.",al={"who wrote inscribed bark","who gives inscribed bark","oracle tree messenger"},it="origin"},{q="How does Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm react to the message?",a="Fandral acknowledges the respite gained from clearing the harpies, but notes with frustration that deeper problems persist. The report reinforces his lingering anxieties over whether his work on Teldrassil will ever truly restore the night elves' lost immortality.",al={"fandral reaction bark","what does fandral say about bark"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, messages borne on the bark of ancient trees represent the sacred bond between nature and their guardians, bridging the wild groves and the marble terraces of Darnassus.",["class:Druid"]="Druids recognize this inscribed wood as an urgent dispatch from an ancient ally, highlighting the delicate balance and ongoing afflictions plaguing the young World Tree."},kw={"cenarion circle","darnassus","fandral staghelm","inscribed bark","oracle tree","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:940","npc:fandral-staghelm","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","quest:937","quest:952","topic:druid"},src={"Inscribed Bark","Teldrassil (quest)"}}
E["item:iverron-s-antidote-item"] = {t="item",n="Iverron's Antidote (item)",z="teldrassil",s="Iverron's Antidote is a delicate medicinal draught concocted by Dirania Silvershine in Shadowglen. Specially brewed to neutralize the lethal venom of the local Webwood spiders, the mixture is highly unstable and spoils rapidly once prepared.",h="Iverron's Antidote is a delicate medicinal draught concocted by Dirania Silvershine in Shadowglen.",sec={{t="A Fragile Remedy",b="Crafted by the priestess Dirania Silvershine in Aldrassil, this antidote is formulated to counteract the potent venom afflicting the young night elf Iverron. Due to the volatile nature of its ingredients and herbal catalysts, the draught possesses an exceptionally short shelf life, remaining viable for only five minutes after brewing. Courier messengers must sprint north toward the Webwood cave without delay to deliver the concoction before it degrades into useless slurry.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Iverron's Antidote used for?",a="It cures Iverron of the toxic bite he sustained from the nearby Webwood spiders outside their cave in northern Shadowglen.",al={"antidote use","what does iverrons antidote do"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does the antidote have a time limit?",a="Dirania Silvershine notes that the concoction is fragile and only remains potent for five minutes after preparation. If it is not administered quickly, its medicinal properties completely break down.",al={"why 5 minutes","antidote timer","why does it expire"},it="power"},{q="Who brews the antidote?",a="Dirania Silvershine, a night elf healer stationed in Aldrassil within the Shadowglen, brews the potion using ingredients gathered to save Iverron.",al={"who made antidote","antidote maker"},it="origin"},{q="What happens if the antidote expires?",a="If the timer runs out, the draught spoils and will no longer work. The courier must return to Dirania Silvershine in Aldrassil to obtain a fresh batch.",al={"antidote expired","timer ran out"},gp=true},{q="What is Iverron's Antidote?",a="It is a freshly brewed medicinal draught concocted specifically to neutralize the deadly venom of the Webwood spiders lurking in the boughs of Teldrassil. Because of its delicate natural mixture, the curative is highly volatile and will quickly spoil if not consumed within minutes of its preparation.",al={"what is iverrons antidote","iverron antidote","iverrons cure"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elf adventurers starting in Shadowglen, rushing this cure to Iverron demonstrates the community's reliance on quick action and herbal knowledge against the creeping corruption in the boughs of Teldrassil.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The concoction demonstrates the extreme volatility of native Teldrassil reagents, highlighting how certain herbal remedies must be consumed immediately upon brewing."},kw={"aldrassil","dirania silvershine","iverron","iverron's antidote","shadowglen","spider poison","teldrassil","webwood venom"},rel={"quest:3521","npc:iverron","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Iverron's Antidote (item)","Iverron's Antidote (2)"}}
E["item:jade-phial"] = {t="item",n="Jade Phial",z="teldrassil",s="The Jade Phial is a specially crafted vessel provided by the night elf druid Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar. It is designed to safely draw and transport sacred water from Teldrassil's moonwells to replenish the druids' central well in Darnassus.",h="The Jade Phial is a specially crafted vessel provided by the night elf druid Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.",sec={{t="A Vessel for Sacred Waters",b="Teldrassil is dotted with moonwells that channel lunar and natural energies vital to night elf society and druidic worship. As part of maintaining this harmony, the central moonwell used by the druids in Darnassus must periodically be replenished from the outlying wells across the great bough. Corithras Moonrage entrusts young initiates with the Jade Phial, a receptacle carefully prepared to gather pure waters from the moonwell near Starbreeze Village without disturbing its delicate spiritual potency.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Jade Phial used for?",a="The Jade Phial is used to collect sacred water from the moonwell situated just outside Starbreeze Village. Once filled, it must be returned to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar to help replenish the druids' moonwell in Darnassus.",al={"jade phial purpose","why do i need jade phial","what does jade phial do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who provides the Jade Phial?",a="Corithras Moonrage, a night elf druid stationed in Dolanaar, provides the phial to adventurers undertaking the rite known as the Crown of the Earth.",al={"who gives jade phial","where to get jade phial","corithras jade phial"},it="origin"},{q="Where does the water from this phial end up?",a="The waters gathered in the phial are transported to sustain and replenish the central moonwell maintained by the Cenarion druids within the capital city of Darnassus.",al={"where does moonwell water go","jade phial destination","who uses the water"},it="target"},{q="What is the Jade Phial?",a="The Jade Phial is a specially crafted ritual vessel provided by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar. It is designed to safely contain and transport the sacred, blessed waters drawn from Teldrassil's moonwells without disturbing or degrading their inherent magical properties.",al={"jade phial","what is the jade phial","what is jade phial"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For young druids, carrying the Jade Phial is an early lesson in stewardship, emphasizing that the vitality of Teldrassil's moonwells requires constant reverence and care.",["race:NightElf"]="Moonwells represent the enduring bond between the kaldorei and Elune; tending to them with vessels like the Jade Phial is a sacred duty for every night elf."},kw={"corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","jade phial","moonwell","starbreeze village","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:corithras-moonrage","item:filled-jade-phial","quest:921","subzone:starbreeze-village","subzone:dolanaar","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid"},src={"Jade Phial","Crown of the Earth (3)"}}
E["item:melenas-head"] = {t="item",n="Melenas' Head",z="teldrassil",s="Melenas' Head is the severed bounty taken from Lord Melenas, a satyr commander encamped inside Fel Rock. Brought back as absolute proof of his demise, the trophy marks the quiet elimination of a lingering demonic threat on the boughs of Teldrassil.",h="Melenas' Head is the severed bounty taken from Lord Melenas, a satyr commander encamped inside Fel Rock.",sec={{t="An Unspoken Disgrace",b="To the night elves guarding Shadowglen and the surrounding reaches of Teldrassil, the mere existence of satyrs upon their new World Tree is a bitter disgrace. Lord Melenas chose to make his lair inside the twisted caverns of Fel Rock, just north of the elven settlements, rallying aggressive grell warriors to his banner. Because the kaldorei prize discretion when handling corruptions so close to their heartlands, this bloody trophy serves as private proof that his scheming has been snuffed out before his influence could spread.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Lord Melenas?",a="Lord Melenas was a satyr commander lurking inside the cave known as Fel Rock on Teldrassil. He gathered a war band of grell under his command to plot against the nearby kaldorei outposts.",al={"lord melenas lore","who is melenas","melenas story"},it="identity"},{q="Why must his death remain quiet?",a="The presence of satyrs—ancient, cursed night elves twisted by demonic corruption—so close to Teldrassil's sacred boughs is seen as a deep embarrassment by kaldorei authorities. Dealing with him swiftly and quietly prevents panic and minimizes shame.",al={"why secrecy","twisted hatred secret","why quiet"},it="motive"},{q="Where was Melenas' Head taken from?",a="The head is retrieved deep inside Fel Rock, a corrupted cavern located just north of Dolanaar and Shadowglen in central Teldrassil.",al={"where to find melenas","fel rock location","melenas location"},it="origin"},{q="What is Melenas' Head?",a="It is the severed head of Lord Melenas, a vile satyr who made his lair within Fel Rock just north of Shadowglen. Melenas rallied aggressive grell to his side and plotted dark deeds uncomfortably close to the night elves' sacred home, making his severed head undeniable proof that his corrupt influence has been extinguished.",al={"what is melenas head","melenas head item","whose head is this"},it="item",add=true},{q="Why does Tallonkai want Melenas' Head?",a="Tallonkai Swiftstrider seeks the head as absolute proof of Lord Melenas's demise. The presence of a satyr so close to Shadowglen is considered a dangerous humiliation for the night elves. Delivering his head ensures the foul plotter has been silenced swiftly and quietly before his schemes can spread further across Teldrassil.",al={"why bring melenas head","who wants melenas head","why does tallonkai want the head"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Satyrs represent a tragic, demonic perversion of ancient night elf lineage, making the quiet execution of Lord Melenas an act of both necessity and cultural shame.",["class:Warrior"]="Carrying the severed head of an enemy warlord offers unmistakable, primal proof that a dangerous adversary and his grell host have been broken."},kw={"fel rock","grell","lord melenas","melenas' head","satyr","teldrassil","twisted hatred"},rel={"quest:932","subzone:fel-rock","topic:satyr","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Melenas' Head","Twisted Hatred"}}
E["item:moonpetal-lily"] = {t="item",n="Moonpetal Lily",z="teldrassil",s="Moonpetal Lilies are large, luminous flora native to Teldrassil that flourish around freshwater pools. Renowned for their potent restorative qualities, their petals are prized as key ingredients in natural remedies and healing draughts.",h="Moonpetal Lilies are large, luminous flora native to Teldrassil that flourish around freshwater pools.",sec={{t="Flora of the Pools",b="Moonpetal Lilies grow exclusively along the moist banks of freshwater pools and ponds, particularly favored along the northwestern side of Aldrassil in Shadowglen. Like much of the plant life flourishing atop the newly grown World Tree, they absorb the unique essence of Teldrassil's sheltered groves. Their broad petals are gentle and radiant, easily spotted hugging the tranquil water's edge where natural moisture allows them to thrive.",sp=0},{t="Natural Antidotes",b="Night elf healers and herbalists value the Moonpetal Lily for its extraordinary healing properties. When combined with other forest flora, such as Hyacinth Mushrooms, the lily acts as a powerful soothing and stabilizing agent. This restorative quality makes it an essential component when brewing antidotes to counteract lethal toxins, notably the virulent venom produced by the Webwood spiders lurking within Shadowthread Cave.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do Moonpetal Lilies grow?",a="They grow along the banks of the two freshwater ponds situated on the northwestern side of Aldrassil within Shadowglen on Teldrassil.",al={"where to find moonpetal lilies","moonpetal lily location","lily spots"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are Moonpetal Lilies used for?",a="The lilies possess notable restorative and healing properties. In Shadowglen, Dirania Silvershine uses them alongside Hyacinth Mushrooms and Webwood Ichor to brew a potent antidote for spider venom.",al={"moonpetal lily uses","what does moonpetal lily do"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who needs an antidote made from these lilies?",a="A night elf named Iverron, who fell victim to the poisonous bite of the Webwood spiders near Shadowthread Cave, requires an antidote concocted from Moonpetal Lilies to survive.",al={"who is the antidote for","iverron poison"},it="target"},{q="Can Moonpetal Lilies be gathered outside of Teldrassil?",a="They are tied directly to the secluded pools of Teldrassil and are known locally within the sheltered boughs of Shadowglen.",al={"do lilies grow elsewhere","moonpetal lily other zones"},it="place"},{q="What is a Moonpetal Lily?",a="The Moonpetal Lily is a large, aquatic flower native to the tranquil waters of Teldrassil. Renowned for its potent natural healing properties, it flourishes in damp soil along the edges of shaded woodland pools and ponds, such as those nestled near Aldrassil in Shadowglen.",al={"what is moonpetal lily","moonpetal lily info","about moonpetal lily"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Though collected directly by hand during urgent crises, Moonpetal Lilies serve as a clear demonstration of Teldrassil's rich, restorative botanical potential.",["race:NightElf"]="For young kaldorei training in Shadowglen, learning the restorative properties of native plants like the Moonpetal Lily is a vital early lesson in living harmoniously with nature."},kw={"aldrassil","antidote","dirania silvershine","iverron","moonpetal","moonpetal lily","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:3521","item:hyacinth-mushroom","item:webwood-ichor","npc:iverron","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","subzone:shadowthread-cave","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Moonpetal Lily","Iverron's Antidote (Classic)"}}
E["item:nightsaber-fang"] = {t="item",n="Nightsaber Fang",z="teldrassil",s="A sharp tooth harvested from the predatory nightsabers roaming the wild branches of Teldrassil. While a common trophy of the hunt, these fangs are also sought out as raw reagents by local woodland residents with questionable motives.",h="A sharp tooth harvested from the predatory nightsabers roaming the wild branches of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Trophy of the Hunt",b="Nightsabers are among the deadliest natural predators native to northern Kalimdor, revered by the night elves for their agility, ferocity, and deep spiritual connection to Elune. Across the great boughs of Teldrassil, these feline beasts hunt in the shadows beneath the canopy. Striking one down yields sharp fangs that serve as undeniable proof of a hunter's skill, though certain unsavory figures in the forest seek them out for less noble ritual purposes.",sp=0},{t="A Satyr's Reagent",b="Outside the settlement of Dolanaar lurks Zenn Foulhoof, a deceptive satyr who preys on eager and inexperienced travelers. Claiming a need for woodland reagents, Zenn coaxes fledgling adventurers into harvesting nightsaber fangs alongside strigid feathers and spider silk. Handing over such predatory reagents directly aids the trickster, who openly mocks the naive hero upon delivery.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do Nightsaber Fangs come from?",a="Nightsaber Fangs are taken from the predatory nightsabers prowling the wilderness of Teldrassil, particularly throughout the forest surrounding Dolanaar.",al={"where to get nightsaber fangs","who drops nightsaber fangs","nightsaber fang source"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who wants Nightsaber Fangs in Teldrassil?",a="Zenn Foulhoof, a satyr lingering off the main road just outside Dolanaar, requests them as part of a task he gives to wandering adventurers.",al={"who needs nightsaber fangs","nightsaber fang turn in","who buys nightsaber fangs"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does Zenn Foulhoof want Nightsaber Fangs?",a="Zenn claims he needs animal reagents to conduct his business in the forest, though he keeps the exact nature of his work secret and delights in duping gullible travelers into serving him.",al={"why zenn wants fangs","zenn foulhoof reagent purpose","zenn bidding motive"},it="purpose"},{q="What other reagents does Zenn ask for alongside the fangs?",a="Along with two nightsaber fangs, Zenn demands two strigid owl feathers and two swatches of webwood spider silk.",al={"what else does zenn need","zenn bidding items","other reagents for zenn"}},{q="What is a Nightsaber Fang?",a="A Nightsaber Fang is a sharp canine tooth taken from the nightsabers prowling the forests of Teldrassil. While simply a natural part of these predatory great cats, such fangs are sought out by practitioners of dark arts who prize them as raw reagents for clandestine rituals and unsanctioned concoctions.",al={"what is nightsaber fang","nightsaber fang lore","about nightsaber fangs"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Nightsabers are cherished companions and symbols of the goddess Elune, making the hunting of these sacred predators on behalf of a treacherous satyr deeply shameful.",["class:Hunter"]="Felling a nightsaber and taking its fang proves your basic mastery of the wild, though providing beast parts to corrupt woodland spirits twists the spirit of the hunt."},kw={"dolanaar","fang","nightsaber","reagent","satyr","teldrassil","zenn foulhoof"},rel={"npc:zenn-foulhoof","quest:488","zone:teldrassil","subzone:dolanaar","item:strigid-owl-feather","item:webwood-spider-silk","topic:satyr","topic:night-elf"},src={"Nightsaber Fang","Zenn's Bidding"}}
E["item:partially-filled-vessel"] = {t="item",n="Partially Filled Vessel",z="teldrassil",s="The Partially Filled Vessel is an enchanted container used to transport blessed moonwell water across Teldrassil. Given to young night elf initiates by Tenaron Stormgrip in Aldrassil, it carries water drawn from Shadowglen toward the settlement of Dolanaar.",h="The Partially Filled Vessel is an enchanted container used to transport blessed moonwell water across...",sec={{t="A Sacred Delivery",b="Within the boughs of Aldrassil, initiates of the kaldorei collect blessed waters from the secluded moonwell of Shadowglen. Tenaron Stormgrip pours that pure sample into this specialized vessel, preparing it for travel across the World Tree. The vessel remains only partially filled because its journey has merely begun; more sacred waters from across Teldrassil must eventually be gathered to tend to the island's health.",sp=0},{t="Onward to Dolanaar",b="Carrying the vessel requires traveling south through the valley's gates and following the cobblestone roads west to Dolanaar. The journey marks a young adventurer's departure from the protected nursery of Shadowglen out into the broader wilds of Teldrassil. At Dolanaar's central moonwell, Corithras Moonrage takes custody of the vessel to direct the next phase of the ritual.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the vessel?",a="It contains pure moonwell water collected from the sacred pool in Shadowglen, poured into the container by the druid Tenaron Stormgrip.",al={"what's in the vessel","vessel contents","what water is in it"},it="item"},{q="Why is it only partially filled?",a="Shadowglen's moonwell provides only the first sample. The ongoing efforts to tend to Teldrassil require collecting water from multiple moonwells across the tree before the container is full.",al={"why partly filled","why is it not full"},it="power"},{q="Who do I take this vessel to?",a="Take the vessel south out of Shadowglen and follow the cobblestone road west to Dolanaar. There, deliver it to Corithras Moonrage, who tends the town's moonwell.",al={"who gets the vessel","where do i bring it","vessel turn in"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why is moonwell water being moved around Teldrassil?",a="The druids and priestesses monitor and nourish Teldrassil through the waters of its moonwells. Transporting water between wells helps maintain their blessings across the troubled boughs of the newly grown World Tree.",al={"why transport moonwell water","purpose of the water","why move water"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Partially Filled Vessel?",a="The Partially Filled Vessel is an enchanted container used by night elf druids to collect and transport the sacred waters of Teldrassil's moonwells. When Tenaron Stormgrip sends you forth from Shadowglen, he combines your gathered phial of blessed moonwell water into this vessel so that the sacred work can continue across the boughs of the World Tree.",al={"partially filled vessel lore","what is this vessel","what is the partially filled vessel"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where did the Partially Filled Vessel come from, and who made it?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip, one of the elder druids stationed atop Aldrassil in Shadowglen, provides you with this vessel. After you draw water from Shadowglen's moonwell, Tenaron pours your phial into the container to begin the collection, entrusting you to carry it onward into the wider reaches of Teldrassil.",al={"who made the vessel","where did the vessel come from","vessel origin"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does Corithras Moonrage want the Partially Filled Vessel?",a="Corithras Moonrage awaits the vessel at the moonwell in Dolanaar to continue a vital druidic task known as the Crown of the Earth. Gathering the waters of Teldrassil is essential for inspecting and tending to the young World Tree, and Corithras requires the water you carried from Aldrassil before he can direct you toward the next stages of the ritual.",al={"why does corithras want this","why take the vessel to dolanaar","why bring vessel to corithras"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Carrying this vessel represents a rite of passage, taking young night elves away from the sanctuary of Shadowglen and into the broader responsibilities of caring for Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="Transporting the sanctified waters is an essential duty in service to the Cenarion Circle's ongoing effort to nurture and inspect the health of the World Tree."},kw={"aldrassil","corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","moonwell","partially filled vessel","shadowglen","tenaron stormgrip","vessel"},rel={"quest:921","npc:tenaron-stormgrip","npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:shadowglen","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:aldrassil","item:filled-vessel","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Partially Filled Vessel","Crown of the Earth (2)"}}
E["item:rare-earth"] = {t="item",n="Rare Earth",z="teldrassil",s="Rare Earth is a specialized package of mineral-rich soil procured from Darnassus for botanic experiments on Teldrassil. It is sent via courier from Dolanaar to the herbalist researcher Denalan at his lakeside camp near Lake Al'Ameth.",h="Rare Earth is a specialized package of mineral-rich soil procured from Darnassus for botanic experiments on...",sec={{t="Soil of Darnassus",b="Teldrassil's newly grown ecosystem requires careful observation and nurturing, prompting herbalists across the island to study how various plants respond to foreign or enriched soils. This particular parcel of rare earth was requisitioned directly from Darnassus by Denalan, an eccentric botanist stationed along the eastern shore of Lake Al'Ameth. After languishing in transit and turning up late in Dolanaar, herbalist Syral Bladeleaf entrusts travelers passing south to deliver the perishable soil to Denalan before its potency fades.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Rare Earth used for?",a="The rare earth is intended for Denalan, an herbalist and botanic researcher camping on the shores of Lake Al'Ameth. He uses specialized mineral compounds and enriched soils imported from Darnassus to cultivate and experiment on native Teldrassil flora.",al={"rare earth use","what does denalan do with rare earth","rare earth purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends the Rare Earth to Denalan?",a="Syral Bladeleaf, an herbalist based in the town of Dolanaar, holds the package. It arrived late from Darnassus, and she asks passing adventurers heading south toward Lake Al'Ameth to deliver it on her behalf.",al={"who gives rare earth","where do you get rare earth","syral bladeleaf parcel"},it="origin"},{q="Why was Denalan worried about the delivery?",a="The shipment was delayed in transit to Dolanaar, leaving Denalan waiting by the lakeside for a considerable time. Upon receiving it, he immediately worries whether the earth has retained its freshness and vitality for his botanical experiments.",al={"is rare earth ruined","denalan fresh earth","why late earth"},it="motive"},{q="What is Rare Earth?",a="Rare Earth is a specially sourced, fertile soil shipment dispatched from Darnassus. It is carefully prepared and packaged for sensitive agricultural and botanical research, retaining specialized nutrients that require it to be delivered fresh to maintain its potency for delicate cultivation experiments.",al={"what is rare earth","rare earth item","rare earth lore"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Denalan want Rare Earth?",a="Denalan is an herbalist researcher stationed on the eastern shores of Lake Al'Ameth, studying and experimenting with the local flora of Teldrassil. He relies on this rare, nutrient-rich soil from Darnassus to nurture his delicate plantings and advance his botanical work on the island.",al={"why does denalan want rare earth","why want rare earth","why rare earth needed"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists will appreciate the meticulous efforts of researchers like Syral Bladeleaf and Denalan, who study how specialized earth can alter the growth and properties of Teldrassil's saplings.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves tending their young World Tree, every botanical experiment at Lake Al'Ameth offers insight into how life adapts to Teldrassil's untamed boughs."},kw={"darnassus","denalan","dolanaar","herbalism","lake al'ameth","rare earth","syral bladeleaf"},rel={"quest:997","npc:denalan","npc:syral-bladeleaf","subzone:lake-al-ameth","subzone:dolanaar","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},src={"Rare Earth","Denalan's Earth"}}
E["item:raven-claw-talisman"] = {t="item",n="Raven Claw Talisman",z="teldrassil",s="The Raven Claw Talisman is a sacred night elf relic tied to the Druids of the Talon. Kept deep within Ban'ethil Barrow Den on Teldrassil, it is one of the four essential Relics of Wakening required to safely guide slumbering druids back from the Emerald Dream.",h="The Raven Claw Talisman is a sacred night elf relic tied to the Druids of the Talon.",sec={{t="A Key to Awakening",b="The Raven Claw Talisman is preserved within a designated chest inside Ban'ethil Barrow Den, the subterranean sanctuary where Teldrassil's Druids of the Talon entered their deep meditative slumbers. Druidic hibernation is a delicate spiritual threshold. If a druid's link to the waking world is shattered without the proper ceremonial focus, their spirit risks being stranded within the Emerald Dream indefinitely. Alongside the Black Feather Quill, the Sapphire of Sky, and the Rune of Nesting, the talisman is required by Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar to conduct the ritual of awakening and bring the slumberers back safely.",sp=0},{t="The Threat in the Barrow Den",b="When corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs overran Ban'ethil Barrow Den, the sacred chests and the sleeping druids fell into immediate peril. The furbolg desecration severed the sanctum from outside aid and put the relics in danger of being lost or destroyed. Athridas Bearmantle tasks defenders of Teldrassil with braving the winding earthen corridors of the den to secure the Raven Claw Talisman before the displaced druids are lost to the Dream forever.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Raven Claw Talisman used for?",a="It is one of four sacred Relics of Wakening needed to perform the ritual that rouses the Druids of the Talon from their deep hibernation in the Emerald Dream.",al={"what does the raven claw talisman do","raven claw talisman purpose","why do i need raven claw talisman"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the Raven Claw Talisman found?",a="It rests inside the Chest of the Raven Claw, stored within the earthen tunnels of Ban'ethil Barrow Den, west of Dolanaar on Teldrassil.",al={"where is raven claw talisman","chest of the raven claw location","how to find raven claw talisman"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who needs the Raven Claw Talisman?",a="Athridas Bearmantle, a night elf druid stationed in Dolanaar, requires the talisman to prepare the wakening rites for his displaced kin.",al={"who wants raven claw talisman","who takes the raven claw talisman","who do i turn this in to"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why can't the druids wake up without it?",a="Entering the Emerald Dream through druidic hibernation involves a complex, delicate trance. Without the specific focus of the Relics of Wakening to anchor the awakening ritual, a sleeper's spirit risks remaining lost in the Dream indefinitely.",al={"why do druids need relics to wake up","why relics of wakening","can druids wake up without relics"},it="power"},{q="What is the Raven Claw Talisman?",a="The Raven Claw Talisman is one of the four sacred Relics of Wakening kept by the Druids of the Talon. Stored within a dedicated chest inside the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, it is an essential component of the delicate ritual required to safely call slumbering druids back from their hibernation in the Emerald Dream.",al={"what is raven claw talisman","raven claw talisman info","relic raven claw talisman"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The talisman is an emblem of the Druids of the Talon, illustrating how ritual foci safeguard a druid's spirit while wandering the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="Recovering this relic protects both ancient night elf tradition and the lives of the slumbering kin threatened by the madness of the Gnarlpine furbolgs."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","ban'ethil","barrow den","dolanaar","druids of the talon","raven claw talisman","relics of wakening","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:483","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","npc:athridas-bearmantle","item:black-feather-quill","item:sapphire-of-sky","item:rune-of-nesting","topic:emerald-dream","subzone:dolanaar"},src={"Raven Claw Talisman","The Relics of Wakening"}}
E["item:rune-of-nesting"] = {t="item",n="Rune of Nesting",z="teldrassil",s="The Rune of Nesting is one of the four sacred Relics of Wakening kept within the Ban'ethil Barrow Den on Teldrassil. It is an essential component in the delicate druidic ritual required to safely summon sleeping Druids of the Talon back from the Emerald Dream.",h="The Rune of Nesting is one of the four sacred Relics of Wakening kept within the Ban'ethil Barrow Den on...",sec={{t="A Sacred Focus for Awakening",b="Night elf druids undergo deep, cyclical hibernations within underground barrow dens to commune with nature through the Emerald Dream. Waking from this profound trance is not simply a matter of stirring; it requires a precise ritual guided by sacred instruments. The Rune of Nesting, kept safely within the Chest of Nesting deep in the winding chambers of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, anchors this process. Alongside the Raven Claw Talisman, the Black Feather Quill, and the Sapphire of Sky, the rune serves as a conduit to call the Druids of the Talon back to the waking world.",sp=0},{t="Crisis in Ban'ethil",b="When corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs overran the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, the barrow's slumbering defenders were placed in immediate peril. Without access to their relics, the druids risked being trapped within the Emerald Dream indefinitely while invaders desecrated their sanctuary. Recovering the Rune of Nesting and its companion artifacts allows Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar to prepare the ritual necessary to safely awaken the endangered druids.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Rune of Nesting used for?",a="It is one of the four Relics of Wakening required by Athridas Bearmantle to conduct the ritual that safely rouses the Druids of the Talon from their deep slumber in the Emerald Dream.",al={"what does rune of nesting do","rune of nesting purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the Rune of Nesting found?",a="It is stored inside the Chest of Nesting, located within the subterranean tunnels of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, west of Dolanaar on Teldrassil.",al={"where is rune of nesting","chest of nesting location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why can't the sleeping druids simply wake up on their own?",a="Entering the Emerald Dream in hibernation is a delicate, trance-like state. Without the guidance of sacred relics and an awakening ritual, returning can be impossible, leaving their minds adrift while their physical bodies are exposed to danger.",al={"why do druids need waking ritual","why can't druids wake up"}},{q="What other relics are needed alongside the Rune of Nesting?",a="The full ritual requires four Relics of Wakening: the Rune of Nesting, the Raven Claw Talisman, the Black Feather Quill, and the Sapphire of Sky.",al={"other relics of wakening","relics of wakening items"},it="item"},{q="What is the Rune of Nesting?",a="The Rune of Nesting is one of the four sacred Relics of Wakening kept by the Druids of the Talon in Teldrassil. Stored within a dedicated chest inside the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, it carries the specialized enchantments required to properly perform the awakening ritual for druids resting in deep communion with the Emerald Dream.",al={"rune of nesting","what is rune of nesting","rune of nesting lore"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids, the Rune of Nesting represents the sacred rituals of the Cenarion Circle, highlighting the vulnerability of the sleeping brethren when sacred sanctuaries are breached.",["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of the barrow dens and the loss of these wakening relics underscore the growing corruption plaguing the wildlife and furbolgs of Teldrassil."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","ban'ethil barrow den","chest of nesting","druids of the talon","emerald dream","relics of wakening","rune of nesting"},rel={"quest:483","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","npc:athridas-bearmantle","item:raven-claw-talisman","item:black-feather-quill","item:sapphire-of-sky","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream"},src={"Rune of Nesting","The Relics of Wakening"}}
E["item:sapphire-of-sky"] = {t="item",n="Sapphire of Sky",z="teldrassil",s="The Sapphire of Sky is one of four sacred Relics of Wakening kept by the night elves within Ban'ethil Barrow Den. It is an essential focus used to safely summon sleeping Druids of the Talon back from the Emerald Dream.",h="The Sapphire of Sky is one of four sacred Relics of Wakening kept by the night elves within Ban'ethil Barrow...",sec={{t="The Wakening Ritual",b="Deep within the roots of Teldrassil, Druids of the Talon commune with the wilds while resting in hibernation within Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Awakening from such deep trance-states into the waking world is a fragile, perilous process. To safeguard the transition, the druids rely on four consecrated artifacts known as the Relics of Wakening: the Black Feather Quill, the Raven Claw Talisman, the Rune of Nesting, and the Sapphire of Sky. Without this resonant gem, the harmony required to call sleeping spirits back from the Emerald Dream remains incomplete, leaving them vulnerable to eternal entrapment.",sp=0},{t="The Threat in Ban'ethil",b="When corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs overran the barrow den, the sacred artifacts were left behind in their ornate repositories. The Sapphire of Sky resides secured inside the Chest of the Sky amidst the winding subterranean corridors. With the druids incapacitated or abducted by the rampaging furbolgs, retrieving this jewel alongside its companion relics is an urgent matter for Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar before the sleepers are permanently lost.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Sapphire of Sky?",a="It is a sacred gemstone and one of the four Relics of Wakening stored within Ban'ethil Barrow Den. It works in conjunction with three avian talismans to safely guide Druids of the Talon out of the Emerald Dream.",al={"sapphire of sky lore","what is this gem","sky sapphire"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Sapphire of Sky kept?",a="It is preserved inside the Chest of the Sky, resting within the underground labyrinth of Ban'ethil Barrow Den in central Teldrassil.",al={"where to find sapphire of sky","chest of the sky location","sapphire location"},it="place"},{q="Why is the sapphire needed right now?",a="Corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs invaded Ban'ethil Barrow Den, putting the slumbering druids in grave danger. Druids deep in trance cannot simply wake up on their own; Athridas Bearmantle requires the sapphire and other relics to perform the delicate ritual of wakening before the sleepers are lost forever.",al={"why get the sapphire","relics of wakening purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who uses this artifact?",a="The Druids of the Talon and ritual keepers such as Athridas Bearmantle use it during the communal rites that wake slumbering brothers from their deep communion with nature.",al={"who uses sapphire of sky","druid ritual gem"},it="purpose"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The sapphire exemplifies the careful rituals required when projecting one's spirit into the Emerald Dream, demonstrating how easily a communion can turn fatal without sacred anchors.",["race:NightElf"]="Preserving the sacred artifacts in Ban'ethil Barrow Den is critical to safeguarding the fragile order of Teldrassil amidst mounting corruption."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","ban'ethil barrow den","chest of the sky","druid of the talon","emerald dream","relics of wakening","sapphire of sky"},rel={"quest:483","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","npc:athridas-bearmantle","item:raven-claw-talisman","item:black-feather-quill","item:rune-of-nesting","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Sapphire of Sky","The Relics of Wakening"}}
E["item:shaman-voodoo-charm"] = {t="item",n="Shaman Voodoo Charm",z="teldrassil",s="The Shaman Voodoo Charm is a dark ritual trinket carried by Gnarlpine furbolg shamans deep within the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Emanating a vile aura, this charm channels an unnatural magic capable of severing a slumbering druid's spirit from their physical flesh.",h="The Shaman Voodoo Charm is a dark ritual trinket carried by Gnarlpine furbolg shamans deep within the...",sec={{t="A Perverted Magic",b="The Gnarlpine tribe of Teldrassil has fallen into madness and corruption, but within the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, their shamans wield powers far beyond ordinary wilderness sorcery. Utilizing these strange voodoo charms, the shamans discovered a way to rip a sleeping druid's consciousness away from the mortal realm and trap it helplessly within the Emerald Dream. By severing the soul from the vessel, the furbolgs are able to animate the empty physical form, turning venerable night elf protectors into mindless guardians that slaughter anyone venturing into the barrows.",sp=0},{t="Unraveling the Curse",b="When the druid Oben Rageclaw fell victim to this ritual, his spirit found itself trapped in the Dream while his animated body terrorized the deep barrows. Reaching out through the veil, Oben tasked adventurers with slaying the Gnarlpine shamans and retrieving one of their voodoo charms. By examining the vile enchantment imbued in the trinket, Oben hoped to decipher the furbolgs' twisted craft and discover a means to break the binding on his stolen flesh.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Shaman Voodoo Charm used for?",a="Gnarlpine shamans use the charm to enact a powerful ritual that severs a sleeping druid's spirit from their physical body, trapping the mind in the Emerald Dream while animating the hollow flesh to attack intruders.",al={"voodoo charm purpose","what does the charm do","shaman charm use"},it="purpose"},{q="Who carries these charms?",a="The charms are carried by Gnarlpine shamans inhabiting the twisting depths of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den in Teldrassil.",al={"who drops the charm","where to find shaman voodoo charm","gnarlpine shaman charm"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Oben Rageclaw need one?",a="Oben Rageclaw is currently trapped in the Emerald Dream while his animated body runs amok. He needs to inspect the charm's vile aura and magical weave in order to figure out how to break the furbolgs' enchantment.",al={"why does oben want it","oben rageclaw charm","the sleeping druid item"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why do furbolgs have voodoo magic?",a="While traditional furbolg shamans revere nature spirits and the elements, the corruption gripping Teldrassil has driven the Gnarlpine to practice dark, perverted magics. The charm possesses an unnatural, vile aura quite unlike traditional nature worship.",al={"why do furbolgs use voodoo","furbolg voodoo lore"}},{q="What is the Shaman Voodoo Charm?",a="It is an enchanted furbolg talisman wielded by corrupted Gnarlpine shamans inside the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Emanating a vile magical aura, the charm harnesses dark rituals capable of severing a sleeping night elf druid's spirit from their physical form, leaving the spirit helpless while the furbolgs animate and control the slumbering body.",al={"what is shaman voodoo charm","voodoo charm lore","what are these charms"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For a druid, the charm represents a horrifying perversion of the sacred slumber, using dark magic to trap the dreamer in the Emerald Dream while puppet-mastering their physical form.",["race:NightElf"]="The discovery of these charms within the Ban'ethil Barrow Den reveals how deeply the Gnarlpine have desecrated one of the kaldorei's most holy communal resting places."},kw={"ban'ethil barrow den","emerald dream","furbolg","gnarlpine","oben rageclaw","shaman voodoo charm","sleeping druid","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:2541","npc:oben-rageclaw","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","topic:furbolg","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Shaman Voodoo Charm","The Sleeping Druid"}}
E["item:shimmering-frond"] = {t="item",n="Shimmering Frond",z="teldrassil",s="A Shimmering Frond is a specimen harvested from a strange, glowing plant growing within the Oracle Glade of Teldrassil. Its unusual luminescence and twisting aura reveal it to be an exotic species entirely alien to the boughs of the World Tree.",h="A Shimmering Frond is a specimen harvested from a strange, glowing plant growing within the Oracle Glade of...",sec={{t="A Specimen from Afar",b="While wandering the verdant canopies around the Oracle Glade, travelers may come across strange vegetation boasting a pulsing, radiant aura. The fronds plucked from this plant catch the filtered woodland light in unnatural ways, shimmering with vibrant vitality. Denalan, a botanist tending to his planters by Lake Al'Ameth, recognizes the foliage immediately as a species native to the distant Swamp of Sorrows in the Eastern Kingdoms. How seeds from a marsh so far across the Great Sea managed to take root and flourish upon the newly raised Teldrassil remains an intriguing mystery, prompting Denalan to sprout and study specimens in his own soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Shimmering Frond come from?",a="The frond is harvested from a strange fronded plant situated within the Oracle Glade on Teldrassil. The plant stands out due to the twisting, pulsing radiance that glows across its leaves in the forest light.",al={"where do i get shimmering frond","shimmering frond location","strange fronded plant"},it="origin"},{q="Who is interested in the Shimmering Frond?",a="Denalan, a night elf naturalist conducting botanical research beside Lake Al'Ameth, is eager to inspect the specimen. He takes great interest in strange vegetation taking root across Teldrassil.",al={"who wants shimmering frond","who to give shimmering frond","denalan shimmering frond"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What makes this plant so unusual on Teldrassil?",a="The plant is not native to Kalimdor or the World Tree. Denalan recognizes it as a species indigenous to the murky waters of the Swamp of Sorrows, located far across the Great Sea in the Eastern Kingdoms, making its thriving presence on Teldrassil quite unexpected.",al={"why is shimmering frond special","plant origin","swamp of sorrows plant"}},{q="What happens after giving the frond to Denalan?",a="Denalan immediately plants and cultivates the specimen in his planters beside Lake Al'Ameth to conduct tests on its rapid growth and exotic properties.",al={"what does denalan do with it","sprouted fronds lore"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is the Shimmering Frond?",a="It is a leaf taken from an unusual, overgrown flora known as the Strange Fronded Plant found in the Oracle Glade. The frond constantly glimmers under the forest canopy, radiating a twisting, pulsing aura uncommon to the boughs of Teldrassil.",al={"what is shimmering frond","shimmering frond item","what is this frond"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The appearance of an invasive marsh plant flourishing on the newborn branches of Teldrassil is a curious ecological anomaly worthy of any druid's attention.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists wandering Teldrassil can appreciate the rare resilience required for a Swamp of Sorrows native to cross the ocean and thrive in foreign soil."},kw={"botany","denalan","lake al'ameth","oracle glade","shimmering frond","strange fronded plant","swamp of sorrows","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:931","npc:denalan","subzone:oracle-glade","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:swampofsorrows","quest:2399","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Shimmering Frond","The Shimmering Frond"}}
E["item:simple-sigil"] = {t="item",n="Simple Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="A Simple Sigil is a modest training token presented to novice night elf warriors in Shadowglen. Carried as a summons from the warrior trainer Alyissia, it marks a young fighter's formal introduction into the martial defense of Teldrassil.",h="A Simple Sigil is a modest training token presented to novice night elf warriors in Shadowglen.",sec={{t="A Summons to Arms",b="Within the sheltered boughs of Shadowglen, young night elves are guided by Conservator Ilthalaine to find their calling. For fledgling warriors, Ilthalaine delivers a Simple Sigil sent by a runner from the warrior trainer Alyissia. Bearing an inscription that directs the recruit to report for instruction, this token represents the start of disciplined martial training amidst troubling times for the World Tree.",sp=0},{t="The Burden of Defense",b="When brought to Alyissia, the sigil opens a dialogue on the pressing state of the kaldorei. The recent growth of Teldrassil, the creeping corruption tainting forest beasts, and the rediscovery of distant lands like Feralas have stretched night elven protectors thin. The sigil is not an artifact of power, but a practical credential welcoming the recruit into the fold of guardians tasked with shielding their people from emerging threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Simple Sigil?",a="It is an introductory inscribed token given to novice night elf warriors by Conservator Ilthalaine in Shadowglen. It instructs the bearer to report to Alyissia for formal warrior training.",al={"simple sigil item","what does simple sigil do","what is this sigil"},it="identity"},{q="Who sends the Simple Sigil?",a="The sigil is dispatched by a messenger on behalf of Alyissia, the resident warrior trainer in Shadowglen, who wishes to begin schooling new warriors in the defense of Teldrassil.",al={"who made the sigil","who sent simple sigil"},it="origin"},{q="What should I do with it?",a="Read the inscribed text and deliver it to Alyissia near the base of Aldrassil in Shadowglen to begin your warrior instruction.",al={"where to turn in simple sigil","who takes simple sigil"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Does the sigil grant any special abilities?",a="No. It is simply a written notice and credential meant to introduce aspiring warriors to their mentor.",al={"sigil powers","simple sigil stats"},it="power",gp=true}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="For kaldorei warriors, this simple token is your very first credential, introducing you to the martial traditions required to safeguard Teldrassil.",["race:NightElf"]="The sigil highlights the urgency facing the kaldorei, as trainers like Alyissia recruit any capable hands to stem the growing corruption within the boughs of the World Tree."},kw={"alyissia","ilthalaine","kaldorei warrior","shadowglen","simple sigil","teldrassil","warrior training"},rel={"quest:3116","npc:alyissia","npc:ilthalaine","subzone:shadowglen","topic:warrior","topic:night-elf","zone:teldrassil","zone:feralas"},src={"Simple Sigil","Simple Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["item:strigid-owl-feather"] = {t="item",n="Strigid Owl Feather",z="teldrassil",s="Strigid Owl Feathers are gathered from the wild strigid owls nesting within the boughs of Teldrassil. While natural forest plumage, they are sought after by questionable figures seeking raw materials for their covert dealings.",h="Strigid Owl Feathers are gathered from the wild strigid owls nesting within the boughs of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Forest Plumage and Dark Dealings",b="Teldrassil's canopies are home to strigid owls and screechers, native birds of prey that hunt throughout the Crown of the Earth. While their down and feathers are common remnants of the forest floor, they occasionally attract the eye of practitioners seeking organic reagents. Outside Dolanaar, the renegade satyr Zenn Foulhoof exploits inexperienced travelers venturing down the road from Shadowglen, tricking them into harvesting strigid feathers alongside spider silk and nightsaber fangs for his own shady business.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Strigid Owl Feathers?",a="These feathers are collected from strigid owls and strigid screechers found inhabiting the woodlands around Dolanaar and across Teldrassil.",al={"feather location","where do strigid owl feathers drop","owl feather farm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants Strigid Owl Feathers?",a="A satyr named Zenn Foulhoof, lurking along the trail leading into Dolanaar, asks naive adventurers to retrieve them alongside webwood silk and nightsaber fangs.",al={"who needs owl feathers","owl feather turn in","zenn owl feather"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What does Zenn Foulhoof use the feathers for?",a="Zenn claims they are reagents required for his secret business within the forest, though he mostly relishes tricking unsuspecting recruits into doing his dirty work.",al={"why does zenn want feathers","zenn reagent purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="What is a Strigid Owl Feather?",a="A Strigid Owl Feather is a plumage plume gathered from the predatory strigid owls native to the boughs of Teldrassil. While simple bird feathers on their surface, they serve as potent natural reagents for those dabbling in craft, alchemy, or darker woodland rites.",al={"strigid owl feather","what is strigid owl feather","owl feather teldrassil"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does a Strigid Owl Feather come from?",a="These feathers are harvested directly from strigid owls and strigid screechers nesting throughout the forests of Teldrassil, particularly around Dolanaar. As natural biological materials shed or taken from the forest's avian predators, they are grown by nature rather than crafted by any mortal hands.",al={"where do strigid owl feathers come from","strigid owl feather source","who made strigid owl feather"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The owls of Teldrassil are considered creatures of Elune, making their exploitation by a lingering satyr like Zenn Foulhoof an insult to the sacred wood.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold the avian hunters of Teldrassil in high regard, making it unsettling to see their plumage gathered under false pretenses for suspicious reagents."},kw={"dolanaar","reagents","strigid owl","strigid owl feather","strigid screecher","teldrassil","zenn foulhoof"},rel={"quest:488","npc:zenn-foulhoof","item:nightsaber-fang","item:webwood-spider-silk","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:satyr","topic:night-elf"},src={"Strigid Owl Feather","Zenn's Bidding"}}
E["item:tainted-heart"] = {t="item",n="Tainted Heart",z="teldrassil",s="The Tainted Heart is a blighted floral core extracted from the corrupt flora of Teldrassil. Given to adventurers by the botanist Denalan, it requires magical and nutritive cleansing to rid it of lingering foul energies.",h="The Tainted Heart is a blighted floral core extracted from the corrupt flora of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Corrupted Core",b="Teldrassil's natural balance suffers from an unnatural malady, warping its native plants and beasts. After stripping away foul moss that clung to a blighted growth, Denalan presents this lingering core: the Tainted Heart. Though freed of its outer rot, darkness still permeates the tissue. Denalan seeks to discover whether specially prepared, nutrient-rich earth can counteract the lingering taint and restore life to what was corrupted.",sp=0},{t="Denalan's Remedy",b="When placed into Denalan's enchanted planter, the heart exhibits a strange, lingering vitality. It burrows eagerly into the rich soil, absorbing the curative nutrients. Within moments, the earth burns away the corruption, and the cleansed heart emerges alive and pulsing with clean energy, eager to defend those who healed it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Tainted Heart?",a="It is the inner core of a corrupted plant found on Teldrassil. Botanist Denalan stripped off the outer foul moss, but the heart itself remains steeped in corruption until purified.",al={"what is tainted heart","tainted heart item"},it="identity"},{q="Who cleanses the Tainted Heart?",a="Denalan directs adventurers to plant it inside his specially prepared planter at Lake Al'Ameth. The nutritive soil naturally purifies the heart and cleanses away its unnatural corruption.",al={"who cleanses it","how to clean tainted heart"}},{q="What happens after it is planted?",a="The heart actively burrows into the soil of the planter. Moments later, it reemerges fully cleansed and pulsing with vitality, ready to bond with whoever restored it.",al={"what happens to the heart","planted heart result"},sp=1},{q="Why is the heart corrupted in the first place?",a="A strange blight has been spreading across the World Tree Teldrassil, corrupting native flora, timberlings, and wildlife throughout the boughs.",al={"why corrupted","teldrassil corruption heart"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Denalan want you to plant the Tainted Heart?",a="Denalan has managed to strip away the foul moss clinging to the heart, but its inner core remains deeply tainted. He hopes the rich, nutritive soil in his specially prepared planter will heal the affliction, drawing out the corruption and restoring the living seed to vitality.",al={"why plant the tainted heart","tainted heart purpose","why does denalan want the tainted heart"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For Cenarion druids, working to cleanse the Tainted Heart provides direct insight into the creeping corruption that threatens the health of the young World Tree.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists and botanists can appreciate Denalan's craft in mixing specially enriched soils capable of drawing out unnatural rot from living plant matter."},kw={"cleansing","corruption","denalan","lake al'ameth","planter","tainted heart","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:941","npc:denalan","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Tainted Heart","Planting the Heart"}}
E["item:tallonkai-s-jewel"] = {t="item",n="Tallonkai's Jewel",z="teldrassil",s="Tallonkai's Jewel is a luminous emerald stolen from an enchanted druidic talisman on Teldrassil. Prized by the furbolg mystic Ferocitas the Dream Eater, it serves as the crucial centerpiece required to mend the Emerald Dreamcatcher.",h="Tallonkai's Jewel is a luminous emerald stolen from an enchanted druidic talisman on Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Stolen Core",b="Tallonkai Swiftroot crafted the Emerald Dreamcatcher as a potent focus tuned to nature and the sleeping realm. When his talisman was damaged, the central radiant emerald was pried loose and carried off into the wilds of eastern Teldrassil. The jewel fell into the paws of Ferocitas the Dream Eater, a corrupted Gnarlpine leader who fashioned the gleaming stone into a personal necklace. While the green stone cast an eerie glow in the forest gloom, its true harmonious resonance was entirely useless to the furbolg, serving merely as a trophy until retrieved.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Tallonkai's Jewel?",a="It is an enchanted glowing emerald that serves as the centerpiece for the Emerald Dreamcatcher, a druidic focus crafted by Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar.",al={"what is the jewel","tallonkai jewel lore"},it="identity"},{q="Who stole Tallonkai's Jewel?",a="It was stolen by Ferocitas the Dream Eater, a leader among the corrupted Gnarlpine mystics residing north of Starbreeze Village.",al={"who has the jewel","who stole it","who took tallonkais jewel"}},{q="Can the Gnarlpine furbolgs use the jewel's power?",a="No. Although Ferocitas wore the emerald around his neck as a glowing ornament, Tallonkai notes that the stone's druidic power is completely useless to the corrupted furbolg.",al={"can ferocitas use it","gnarlpine emerald power"},it="power"},{q="Where does the jewel go after it is recovered?",a="The stone is returned to Tallonkai Swiftroot on the upper tier of Dolanaar, where he uses it to fully restore and mend the damaged Emerald Dreamcatcher.",al={"what happens to the jewel","repairing dreamcatcher"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does anyone want Tallonkai's Jewel?",a="Tallonkai Swiftroot desperately needs this glowing emerald returned so he can repair his damaged Emerald Dreamcatcher. The corrupted Gnarlpine furbolg mystic, Ferocitas the Dream Eater, took it to wear as a shining necklace, drawn to its magical glow without understanding that its dream-attuned power is utterly useless in his hands.",al={"why is tallonkai's jewel wanted","why does tallonkai want the jewel","why steal tallonkai's jewel"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The emerald is an attuned druidic component designed to resonate with the Emerald Dream, making its misuse by corrupted furbolgs an affront to the balance.",["race:NightElf"]="Recovering the jewel helps restore order to Teldrassil by wresting sacred craftwork from the hands of the encroaching Gnarlpine."},kw={"dolanaar","emerald dreamcatcher","ferocitas the dream eater","gnarlpine mystics","starbreeze village","tallonkai swiftroot","tallonkai's jewel"},rel={"quest:2459","item:emerald-dreamcatcher","npc:tallonkai-swiftroot","quest:2438","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:starbreeze-village","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Tallonkai's Jewel","Ferocitas the Dream Eater (quest)"}}
E["item:timberling-seed"] = {t="item",n="Timberling Seed",z="teldrassil",s="Timberling Seeds are botanical kernels harvested from the agitated plant elementals inhabiting Teldrassil. Naturalists and druids study these seeds to understand why the forest's plant life has grown unusually aggressive.",h="Timberling Seeds are botanical kernels harvested from the agitated plant elementals inhabiting Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Seeds of a Restless Forest",b="The timberlings of Teldrassil are nature elementals whose temperament reflects the balance of the World Tree. Recently, these creatures have turned hostile and angry, troubling the night elves who tend the boughs. Herbalists like Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth believe the issue lies rooted in the soil, collecting seeds from wild timberlings in hopes that nurturing them under controlled, purified conditions might sprout docile offspring.",sp=0},{t="A Rooted Corruption",b="Efforts to cultivate gentle timberlings face grim reality. When specimen seeds are examined by Cenarion scholars such as Rellian Greenspyre in Darnassus, deeper problems emerge. The seeds carry the taint of their corrupted parent stock, suggesting that the unrest among Teldrassil's plant spirits is not merely poor growth, but an underlying corruption taking hold across the great tree's ecosystem.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a timberling seed?",a="A timberling seed is the reproductive kernel of a timberling, a plant-like nature elemental found across Teldrassil. Naturalists collect them to study timberling growth and ecology.",al={"timberling seeds","what are timberling seeds","seeds of timberling"},it="identity"},{q="Where are these seeds gathered?",a="They are collected from wild timberlings and bog beasts wandering the shores and shallows of Lake Al'Ameth in Teldrassil.",al={"where to get seeds","timberling seed drop","who drops timberling seed"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Denalan want timberling seeds?",a="Denalan suspects improper soil is driving the timberlings to rage. He hopes to plant wild seeds in specially prepared soil to see if he can sprout docile, uncorrupted timberlings.",al={"denalan purpose","why collect seeds","denalan's plan"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What does Rellian Greenspyre discover about the seeds?",a="Rellian discovers that a corruption has taken root within the timberlings, and the seeds carry their parents' taint. He finds them beyond his ability to mend, leaving hope with Denalan's horticultural experiments.",al={"rellian seed study","what did rellian find","are seeds tainted"},sp=1,it="threat"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The tainted seeds offer early warning signs of unnatural corruption spreading through Teldrassil's plant elementals, a critical concern for protectors of the Cenarion Enclave.",["profession:Herbalism"]="For botanists and herbal gatherers, studying the seeds highlights how heavily soil condition and ambient corruption influence wild flora."},kw={"corruption","darnassus","denalan","lake al'ameth","rellian greenspyre","teldrassil","timberling","timberling seed"},rel={"npc:denalan","quest:918","quest:922","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid"},src={"Timberling Seed","Timberling Seeds (Classic)","Rellian Greenspyre (Classic)"}}
E["item:timberling-sprout"] = {t="item",n="Timberling Sprout",z="teldrassil",s="Timberling Sprouts are young, nascent plant elementals taking root near the shores of Lake Al'Ameth in Teldrassil. Even in their earliest growth, these sprouts show signs of corruption, prompting night elf wardens to pull them before they mature into aggressive timberlings.",h="Timberling Sprouts are young, nascent plant elementals taking root near the shores of Lake Al'Ameth in...",sec={{t="Blighted Seedlings",b="Timberlings are plant spirits closely tied to the natural vitality of Teldrassil, but the seedlings sprouting along Lake Al'Ameth have worried the local night elves. Rather than emerging healthy and in harmony with the wild, they sprout already tainted and aggressive. Because these infant sprouts appear beyond cleansing or natural healing, caretakers at Lake Al'Ameth must gather and destroy them to prevent an uncontrolled spread of hostile timberlings across the fragile boughs of the newly planted World Tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are Timberling Sprouts found?",a="Timberling Sprouts grow close to the water's edge along the shores of Lake Al'Ameth, south of Dolanaar in Teldrassil.",al={"sprout location","where are timberling sprouts","find sprouts"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are night elves pulling Timberling Sprouts from the ground?",a="The sprouts are sprouting tainted from the very beginning. Left unchecked, they grow into violent timberlings that threaten the safety and balance of Teldrassil. Because they are considered beyond help, the caretakers remove them while they are still small.",al={"why kill sprouts","timberling sprout purpose","why destroy sprouts"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is causing the sprouts to become tainted?",a="A mysterious sickness has begun affecting the wildlife and plant elementals of Teldrassil. While the exact source of the taint is still an unsolved riddle to the botanist Denalan, it influences young timberlings from the moment they take root.",al={"why are timberlings corrupted","what is tainting them","sprout sickness"},it="threat"},{q="Who asks for Timberling Sprouts to be collected?",a="Denalan, the botanist tending Lake Al'Ameth, asks adventurers to collect and clear the sprouts from the lakeside to keep the land pure.",al={"who wants sprouts","sprout questgiver","timberling sprouts turn in"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What is a Timberling Sprout?",a="A Timberling Sprout is the juvenile form of a timberling, a small plant-like elemental being that takes root along the moist shores of Lake Al'Ameth. Left undisturbed, these shoots will eventually grow into full-sized timberlings. Unfortunately, the sprouts springing up around the lake are tainted and aggressive, prompting caretakers in the Shadowglen to have them plucked from the soil before they mature into dangerous threats.",al={"what is timberling sprout","timberling sprouts what are they","timberling sprout info"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids attuned to the plant life and elementals of Kalimdor, seeing natural woodland spirits sprout pre-corrupted from the soil is a grim omen for Teldrassil's future.",["race:NightElf"]="Young night elves beginning their training in Shadowglen are tasked with clearing these sprouts to safeguard their new woodland home."},kw={"aldrassil","corruption","lake al'ameth","shadowglen","teldrassil","timberling","timberling sprout"},rel={"quest:919","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},src={"Timberling Sprout","Timberling Sprouts"}}
E["item:tourmaline-phial"] = {t="item",n="Tourmaline Phial",z="teldrassil",s="The Tourmaline Phial is a specialized gem-crafted vessel given to travelers in Teldrassil by Corithras Moonrage. It is used to draw blessed waters from the moonwell beside the Pools of Arlithrien as part of ongoing rituals to monitor and soothe the boughs of the World Tree.",h="The Tourmaline Phial is a specialized gem-crafted vessel given to travelers in Teldrassil by Corithras...",sec={{t="Vessel of Arlithrien",b="Corithras Moonrage provides the Tourmaline Phial to aid in the rituals surrounding the World Tree. The druids in Dolanaar use such dedicated gemstone vials to safely collect pure moonwell waters from across Teldrassil. This particular phial is designated for the moonwell on the shores of the Pools of Arlithrien, southeast of the road leading to Darnassus, an area increasingly beleaguered by hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Tourmaline Phial used for?",a="The phial is used to collect sacred water from the moonwell located at the Pools of Arlithrien. Once filled, it must be returned to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar as part of the Crown of the Earth rituals.",al={"what does tourmaline phial do","tourmaline phial purpose","use tourmaline phial"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who provides the Tourmaline Phial?",a="Corithras Moonrage, a night elf druid stationed in the town of Dolanaar, entrusts adventurers with the empty phial.",al={"who gives tourmaline phial","where do i get tourmaline phial"},it="origin"},{q="Where is the moonwell for this phial?",a="The moonwell is located on the shores of the Pools of Arlithrien, southeast of the main gateway leading to Darnassus.",al={"pools of arlithrien moonwell","where to fill tourmaline phial"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Tourmaline Phial?",a="The Tourmaline Phial is an empty ceremonial vessel crafted to draw and transport sacred waters from the moonwells across Teldrassil. Entrusted to you by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar, it is specially designated to collect water from the secluded moonwell resting near the Pools of Arlithrien.",al={"what is tourmaline phial","tourmaline phial lore","tourmaline vial"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Corithras Moonrage want the Tourmaline Phial filled?",a="Corithras Moonrage requires water from each of Teldrassil's moonwells to study and assess the health of the World Tree and its sanctuaries. Drawing from the moonwell by the Pools of Arlithrien has become perilous due to violent Gnarlpine furbolg activity, prompting him to rely on capable travelers to safely retrieve a sample.",al={"why fill tourmaline phial","tourmaline phial purpose","why corithras wants phial"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Carrying dedicated gemstone phials to gather moonwell water is an essential ceremonial duty for young night elf druids learning to tend Teldrassil's fragile ecosystem.",["race:NightElf"]="The waters gathered in vessels like the Tourmaline Phial represent the night elves' reliance on Elune's grace and druidic vigilance as Teldrassil struggles against corruption."},kw={"corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","moonwell","pools of arlithrien","teldrassil","tourmaline phial"},rel={"npc:corithras-moonrage","item:filled-tourmaline-phial","quest:921","subzone:pools-of-arlithrien","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:furbolg"},src={"Tourmaline Phial","Crown of the Earth (4)"}}
E["item:verdant-sigil"] = {t="item",n="Verdant Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="The Verdant Sigil is an inscribed druidic token presented to fledgling night elf druids beginning their training in Shadowglen. Carried as a summons from the druid mentor Mardant Strongoak, it marks a novice's formal entry into the Cenarion teachings under the branches of Aldrassil.",h="The Verdant Sigil is an inscribed druidic token presented to fledgling night elf druids beginning their...",sec={{t="A Summons to the Path",b="In the sheltered boughs of Shadowglen, young night elves who feel the call of the wild receive the Verdant Sigil from Conservator Ilthalaine. Sent via messenger from the trainer Mardant Strongoak, the token directs novices to climb into the boughs of the great tree Aldrassil. Carrying the sigil serves as a formal invitation to leave basic chores behind and commence serious training in communion with nature spirits and the deep mysteries of the Emerald Dream.",sp=0},{t="The First Step Into the Dream",b="Presenting the sigil to Mardant Strongoak initiates the young druid into their lifelong craft. While novices are not yet prepared to walk the sleeping trance of the Emerald Dream, acknowledging the sigil marks the start of their mentorship. Under Mardant's instruction, initiates learn to interpret the whispers of the wilderness and master early shapeshifting and healing arts in service of Teldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Verdant Sigil?",a="The Verdant Sigil is an introductory token given to novice night elf druids in Shadowglen. It acts as a formal summons from the trainer Mardant Strongoak, directing new druids to seek him out within the tree Aldrassil to begin their formal education.",al={"what does verdant sigil do","why do i have verdant sigil","verdant sigil use"},it="purpose"},{q="Who hands out the Verdant Sigil?",a="Conservator Ilthalaine hands the sigil to budding druids shortly after they begin assisting him in Shadowglen, passing along a message sent from Mardant Strongoak.",al={"who gives verdant sigil","where do i get verdant sigil"},gp=true},{q="Where do I take the sigil once I receive it?",a="You bring the sigil to Mardant Strongoak, the druid trainer located within the central chambers of the great tree Aldrassil, situated at the heart of Shadowglen.",al={"where do i bring verdant sigil","who takes verdant sigil","verdant sigil turn in"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What happens after presenting the sigil to Mardant Strongoak?",a="Mardant accepts the sigil, formally welcoming you as his student. He establishes himself as your guide in mastering nature communion and promises to prepare you for the intricacies of the Emerald Dream as your strength increases.",al={"what does mardant do with sigil","after verdant sigil"}},{q="What is the Verdant Sigil?",a="The Verdant Sigil is an inscribed token sent by the druid mentor Mardant Strongoak to young night elf initiates in Shadowglen. Carried by a messenger to Conservator Ilthalaine, it serves as a formal summons and introductory token, calling promising novices to climb the boughs of Aldrassil and begin their instruction in the ways of nature and the Emerald Dream.",al={"what is verdant sigil","verdant sigil item","verdant sigil lore"},it="identity",rc="Night Elf",add=true},{q="Where does the Verdant Sigil come from, and who made it?",a="The sigil originates with Mardant Strongoak, the druid trainer stationed within the great boughs of Aldrassil in Shadowglen. Seeking out novices ready to attune themselves to nature, Mardant dispatched the token via a courier to Conservator Ilthalaine, ensuring it would reach promising young druids taking their first steps in Teldrassil.",al={"who made verdant sigil","where did verdant sigil come from","origin of verdant sigil"},it="origin",rc="Night Elf",add=true},{q="Why does anyone want the Verdant Sigil?",a="Mardant Strongoak asks you to bring the sigil to him as proof of your readiness and willingness to learn. By accepting the summons and returning it to the mentor, you establish your formal bond with him, demonstrating that you are prepared to study the spirits, master shapeshifting, and explore the mysteries of the Emerald Dream.",al={"why is verdant sigil wanted","why does mardant want verdant sigil","who wants the verdant sigil"},it="why_wanted",rc="Night Elf",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For young night elf druids, receiving the Verdant Sigil is the traditional first rite of passage, bridging the gap between basic forest tending and disciplined Cenarion tutelage.",["race:NightElf"]="Given under the canopy of Aldrassil, the sigil represents the enduring kaldorei tradition of attuning one's spirit to the natural world and the guardians of Teldrassil."},kw={"aldrassil","druid","emerald dream","ilthalaine","mardant strongoak","shadowglen","teldrassil","verdant sigil"},rel={"quest:3120","npc:mardant-strongoak","npc:ilthalaine","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Verdant Sigil","Verdant Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["item:voodoo-charm"] = {t="item",n="Voodoo Charm",z="teldrassil",s="The Voodoo Charm is a mystical talisman used within the barrows of Teldrassil to sever a sinister enchantment. Handed to adventurers by the spirit of Oben Rageclaw, it allows his corrupted, puppeted physical form to be permanently released so his soul may rest in the Emerald Dream.",h="The Voodoo Charm is a mystical talisman used within the barrows of Teldrassil to sever a sinister enchantment.",sec={{t="A Severing of Dark Bonds",b="Within the depths of the Gnarlpine barrow dens in Teldrassil, the furbolgs turned to foul magics to control the sleeping forms of sacred kaldorei protectors. The druid Oben Rageclaw found his spirit separated from his flesh, leaving his physical husk enthralled by Gnarlpine sorcery. After examining this enchanted charm, Oben recognizes that the dark tether holding his living vessel cannot simply be dispelled through traditional prayers. Instead, the charm serves as an instrument of final release: once his soulless body is struck down, the charm's magic must be channeled over the fallen form to completely purge the furbolg hold, freeing his wandering spirit to depart for the Emerald Dream forever.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Voodoo Charm?",a="The charm is used to break the Gnarlpine furbolgs' magical control over Oben Rageclaw. After striking down Oben's soulless, enthralled physical body, the talisman must be used directly on his remains to sever the dark enchantment and free his soul.",al={"what does voodoo charm do","voodoo charm use","how to use voodoo charm"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives you the Voodoo Charm?",a="The spirit of Oben Rageclaw gives you the charm during the quest Druid of the Claw. Having examined the talisman, he instructs you on how it can be used to free him from the Gnarlpine tribe's sorcery.",al={"where do i get voodoo charm","who gives the charm","oben charm"}},{q="Why is it called a Voodoo Charm in night elf lands?",a="The Gnarlpine furbolgs of Teldrassil have succumbed to corruption and bizarre tribal magics since the corruption began seeping into the Great Tree. The charm represents foreign or distorted occult magic used by the furbolg tribe to ensnare and puppeteer the bodies of resting druids.",al={"why voodoo in teldrassil","is it troll voodoo"},it="origin"},{q="What happens after the charm is used?",a="Once the charm breaks the enchantment on his body, Oben Rageclaw is finally liberated from the Gnarlpine tribe's grip. With his physical vessel laid to rest, his spirit departs Teldrassil to dwell peacefully forever within the Emerald Dream.",al={"what happens to oben","does oben survive"},sp=1},{q="What is the Voodoo Charm?",a="The Voodoo Charm is a magical talisman tied to the corrupted magic gripping Teldrassil's Gnarlpine furbolgs. The spirit of Oben Rageclaw inspects it to uncover how the furbolgs ensnared his physical form, realizing that only through the charm can the foul enchantment binding his soulless body be broken once and for all.",al={"what is voodoo charm","voodoo charm teldrassil","oben voodoo charm"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Oben Rageclaw want the Voodoo Charm used?",a="Oben Rageclaw requires the charm to sever the Gnarlpine furbolgs' hold over him. After his soulless body is defeated in battle, using the talisman over his fallen remains dispels the dark enchantment, releasing his trapped spirit so he can finally rest peacefully within the Emerald Dream.",al={"why use voodoo charm","why does oben want the charm","voodoo charm purpose"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For young druids training in Teldrassil, utilizing the charm to mercy-kill and release a brother Druid of the Claw underscores the tragic vulnerability of leaving one's physical shell behind while traversing the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="The existence of this charm reveals how deeply the Gnarlpine furbolgs have degenerated, turning sacred kaldorei barrow dens into sites of grotesque spiritual imprisonment."},kw={"druid of the claw","gnarlpine","oben rageclaw","teldrassil","the sleeping druid","voodoo charm"},rel={"quest:2561","quest:2541","npc:oben-rageclaw","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Voodoo Charm","Druid of the Claw (quest)"}}
E["item:webwood-egg"] = {t="item",n="Webwood Egg",z="teldrassil",s="A Webwood Egg is an unhatched specimen gathered from the brooding nests within Shadowthread Cave in Shadowglen. Naturalists studying the corruption on Teldrassil seek out these viable eggs to study the newly hatched arachnids in secure laboratory conditions.",h="A Webwood Egg is an unhatched specimen gathered from the brooding nests within Shadowthread Cave in...",sec={{t="A Contained Specimen",b="Taming or subduing a fully grown, venomous Webwood spider is a perilous task far beyond the reach of solitary researchers. Rather than wrestling mature predators, scholars like Gilshalan Windwalker rely on unhatched eggs collected directly from clutches hidden in the dark recesses of Shadowthread Cave. Securing an unhatched egg allows naturalists to safely transport the creature and contain the emerging spiderlings upon hatching, giving them live subjects to study without facing the deadly fangs of fully grown beasts.",sp=0},{t="Destined for Darnassus",b="The unnatural aggression and corruption plaguing the native wildlife of Teldrassil has alarmed scholars across the boughs. Once secured at Aldrassil, these collected eggs and gathered venoms are slated for transport down the boughs to the capital of Darnassus. Researchers hope that raising and examining the spiders in controlled environments will yield valuable insight into the dark affliction creeping through the World Tree's boughs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are Webwood Eggs found?",a="Webwood Eggs are found in clutches resting deep inside the damp tunnels of Shadowthread Cave, located in the northwestern reaches of Shadowglen.",al={"webwood egg location","where is webwood egg","find webwood egg"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants the Webwood Egg?",a="The researcher Gilshalan Windwalker at Aldrassil requests the egg to continue his scientific study into the aggressive arachnids troubling Shadowglen.",al={"who needs webwood egg","egg turn in","gilshalan egg"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why collect an egg instead of capturing a spider?",a="A mature Webwood spider is far too dangerous and massive to capture and contain easily. Retrieving an unhatched egg provides a live specimen that can be transported safely and placed into a secure enclosure before it hatches.",al={"why an egg","why not capture live spider"},it="motive"},{q="What happens to the egg after it is collected?",a="Gilshalan arranges for the egg and extracted spider venoms to be delivered to Darnassus, where scholars can conduct in-depth research on the creatures away from the immediate dangers of the wild.",al={"where does the egg go","egg destination"},it="next_step"},{q="What is a Webwood Egg?",a="A Webwood Egg is an unhatched spider egg laid by the giant Webwood spiders nesting within Shadowglen. It holds live spider specimens before they emerge, allowing researchers to study the aggressive arachnids without risking immediate harm.",al={"what is webwood egg","webwood egg lore"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does the Webwood Egg come from?",a="These eggs are produced naturally by the giant Webwood spiders infesting Shadowthread Cave in northwestern Shadowglen. Within the dark, web-draped recesses of the cave, the spiders maintain nesting clutches where their broods incubate before hatching.",al={"webwood egg origin","where do webwood eggs come from","who made webwood egg"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young kaldorei defending the sacred boughs of Teldrassil, securing these eggs helps scholars investigate the unnatural taint spreading through the World Tree's native wildlife.",["class:Druid"]="Understanding how the Webwood spiders reproduce and behave while tainted offers druids vital clues toward healing Teldrassil's disrupted natural balance."},kw={"aldrassil","gilshalan","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","spider egg","teldrassil","webwood egg"},rel={"quest:917","subzone:shadowthread-cave","subzone:shadowglen","subzone:aldrassil","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Webwood Egg","Webwood Egg (quest)"}}
E["item:webwood-ichor"] = {t="item",n="Webwood Ichor",z="teldrassil",s="Webwood Ichor is a potent fluid harvested from Webwood spiders prowling the shadowy reaches of Teldrassil. Prized for its volatile chemical properties, it serves as the crucial active component needed to brew an antivenom against the arachnids' virulent bites.",h="Webwood Ichor is a potent fluid harvested from Webwood spiders prowling the shadowy reaches of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Toxic Cure",b="The Webwood spiders that haunt the outskirts of Shadowglen and the depths of Shadowthread Cave carry a venom virulent enough to fell even hardy night elves. Paradoxically, the raw ichor taken directly from these predators contains the exact chemical basis needed to neutralize their own bite. When combined with cleansing flora like Hyacinth Mushrooms and Moonpetal Lilies, herbalists such as Dirania Silvershine can refine the toxic fluid into a life-saving antidote for victims like the reckless scout Iverron.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Webwood Ichor used for?",a="Webwood Ichor is the primary active ingredient used by Dirania Silvershine in Shadowglen to formulate an antivenom. It is required to save the poisoned night elf Iverron from succumbing to the lethal venom of the local spiders.",al={"webwood ichor use","what does webwood ichor do","why get ichor"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does Webwood Ichor come from?",a="It is harvested from the corpses of Webwood Spiders residing in northwestern Shadowglen, particularly those dwelling around and inside Shadowthread Cave.",al={"where to find webwood ichor","how to get webwood ichor","webwood ichor drop"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why use spider fluid to cure a spider bite?",a="Like many natural antivenoms, a counteragent often requires the raw toxins or biological fluids of the creature that inflicted the bite. Once properly counterbalanced with soothing herbs like moonpetal lilies and hyacinth mushrooms, the ichor helps create an effective neutralizing cure.",al={"spider poison cure","why venom for antidote"}},{q="What is Webwood Ichor?",a="Webwood Ichor is the bodily fluid extracted from the Webwood spiders lurking in Shadowglen. Though naturally venomous, the substance contains the vital biological essence of the arachnids, making it a potent base ingredient for crafting specialized antidotes.",al={"webwood ichor","what is webwood ichor","spider ichor"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does Webwood Ichor come from, and who made it?",a="It is not crafted or manufactured, but harvested directly from the Webwood spiders that infest the northwestern reaches of Shadowglen around Shadowthread Cave. The spiders produce the fluid naturally as part of their biology.",al={"webwood ichor source","where does webwood ichor come from","who made webwood ichor"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does anyone want Webwood Ichor?",a="Dirania Silveshine requires Webwood Ichor to concoct an urgent antidote for Iverron, who has fallen severely ill from spider poison. Combined with local Hyacinth Mushrooms and Moonpetal Lilies, the ichor is crucial to counteracting the venom that afflicted him.",al={"why gather webwood ichor","why do they need webwood ichor","who needs webwood ichor"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves defending Aldrassil, harvesting Webwood ichor teaches the harsh balance of nature: that the deadliest poisons of Teldrassil often harbor their own cures."},kw={"antidote","dirania silvershine","iverron","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","teldrassil","webwood ichor","webwood spider"},rel={"quest:3521","npc:iverron","subzone:shadowthread-cave","subzone:shadowglen","item:moonpetal-lily","item:hyacinth-mushroom","subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Webwood Ichor","Iverron's Antidote (Classic)"}}
E["item:webwood-spider-silk"] = {t="item",n="Webwood Spider Silk",z="teldrassil",s="Webwood Spider Silk is a fine, sticky thread harvested from Webwood Lurkers prowling the woods of Teldrassil. While spider silk has many craft uses, these particular swatches are sought out by suspicious figures in the boughs of the World Tree.",h="Webwood Spider Silk is a fine, sticky thread harvested from Webwood Lurkers prowling the woods of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Dubious Reagent",b="Spun by the overgrown Webwood Lurkers that nest around Dolanaar, Webwood Spider Silk is light, remarkably strong, and dangerous to harvest. The satyr Zenn Foulhoof, who lurks along the forest road, hires young adventurers to harvest swatches of this silk alongside nightsaber fangs and strigid owl feathers. Claiming they are simply rare reagents necessary for his forest business, he relies on the naivety of newcomers to gather the wild components without questioning his corrupt nature or his true motives.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Webwood Spider Silk be found?",a="Webwood Spider Silk is harvested from Webwood Lurkers and related spider beasts inhabiting the wilds of Teldrassil, particularly around the settlement of Dolanaar.",al={"webwood silk location","who drops webwood spider silk","where to get webwood spider silk"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants this silk?",a="The satyr Zenn Foulhoof, who conceals his dealings just north of the path between Shadowglen and Dolanaar, requests swatches of the silk alongside owl feathers and predator fangs.",al={"who needs webwood silk","webwood silk quest giver","zenn foulhoof silk"},it="target"},{q="Why does Zenn Foulhoof want Webwood Spider Silk?",a="Zenn claims to need the silk as a reagent for his forest business, though he ultimately mocks anyone gullible enough to run errands for a satyr.",al={"zenn foulhoof motive","why does zenn want silk"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"},{q="Can players use Webwood Spider Silk for tailoring?",a="No. Despite being genuine spider silk, this specific harvested thread serves as a quest reagent rather than standard tailoring cloth.",al={"is webwood silk tailoring mat","crafting webwood silk"},gp=true},{q="What is Webwood Spider Silk?",a="Webwood Spider Silk is raw, spun thread gathered from the giant arachnids that haunt the forests of Teldrassil. Fine yet resilient, swatches of this natural silk are prized by various practitioners across the boughs, though gathering it requires facing the venomous Webwood spiders directly in their shaded dens.",al={"what is webwood spider silk","webwood silk","spider silk teldrassil"},it="identity",add=true,nx={6}},{q="Where does Webwood Spider Silk come from?",a="The silk is produced naturally by Webwood spiders, such as the Webwood Lurkers that lurk in the tangled thickets around Dolanaar. These aggressive arachnids spin thick webs among the great roots and hollows of Teldrassil, crafting durable threads that adventurers must harvest directly from the beasts themselves.",al={"webwood silk origin","who produces webwood silk","where does webwood silk come from"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Young night elves leaving Shadowglen are warned to be mindful of the creatures they hunt, especially when coerced by a solitary satyr lurking right near their heartland.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Although spinners frequently seek out arachnid threads, these particular swatches are tied up in dark satyr bargains rather than standard loom crafting."},kw={"dolanaar","spider silk","teldrassil","webwood lurker","webwood spider silk","zenn foulhoof","zenn's bidding"},rel={"npc:zenn-foulhoof","quest:488","item:nightsaber-fang","item:strigid-owl-feather","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:satyr","topic:night-elf"},src={"Webwood Spider Silk","Zenn's Bidding"}}
E["item:webwood-venom-sac"] = {t="item",n="Webwood Venom Sac",z="teldrassil",s="A Webwood Venom Sac is an organ harvested from the overgrown arachnids inhabiting Shadowglen on Teldrassil. Naturalists seek these samples to determine how the unnatural growth of the new World Tree has altered local wildlife.",h="A Webwood Venom Sac is an organ harvested from the overgrown arachnids inhabiting Shadowglen on Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Symptom of Teldrassil's Growth",b="The webwood spiders dwelling around and within Shadowthread Cave are cousins to a far smaller breed of spider found elsewhere. Their sudden enlargement and predatory aggression have raised concerns among night elf researchers. Naturalists like Gilshalan Windwalker study the venom contained within these sacs to analyze its potency and composition, hoping to understand how the rapid, unblessed growth of Teldrassil is warping the creatures that live upon its boughs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are Webwood Venom Sacs found?",a="They are gathered from webwood spiders that infest the northern reaches of Shadowglen, particularly in and around Shadowthread Cave.",al={"where do these drop","webwood venom sac location","spider venom location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants these venom sacs?",a="Gilshalan Windwalker, a night elf researcher stationed at Aldrassil in Shadowglen, collects them to study the spiders' biology before eventually returning to Darnassus.",al={"who needs venom sacs","gilshalan windwalker quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are the webwood spiders so large?",a="Researchers believe that the emergence and rapid growth of the new World Tree, Teldrassil, has had a profound and distorting effect on local wildlife, causing ordinary arachnid species to grow into massive, aggressive predators.",al={"why are spiders big","webwood spider size"}},{q="Is this venom used to make an antidote?",a="Gilshalan collects these sacs strictly for comparative study. However, spider venom from this region is a known hazard, and remedies such as Iverron's antidote are separately required to save those bitten in the woods.",al={"is this for a cure","antidote ingredient"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What is a Webwood Venom Sac?",a="A Webwood Venom Sac is an intact gland harvested from the webwood spiders nesting in and around Shadowthread Cave. These unnatural arachnids produce potent venom that researchers are keen to analyze, especially given how drastically the spiders have mutated compared to their smaller kin.",al={"what is webwood venom sac","webwood venom sac item","venom sac"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does a Webwood Venom Sac come from?",a="These sacs are harvested directly from the bodies of the webwood spiders that infest northern Shadowglen. They are biological organs produced naturally by the arachnids, whose alarming growth and venomous potency are believed to be influenced by the presence of Teldrassil itself.",al={"where do webwood venom sacs come from","origin of webwood venom sac","who made webwood venom sac"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids attuned to the balance of nature, the corrupted potency of these venom sacs provides alarming physical evidence that all is not well atop the boughs of Teldrassil.",["race:NightElf"]="Young night elf adventurers in Shadowglen are tasked with gathering these specimens to assist scholars trying to understand the strange new ecology of their bough-top homeland."},kw={"aldrassil","gilshalan windwalker","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","teldrassil","venom","webwood spider","webwood venom sac"},rel={"quest:916","npc:gilshalan-windwalker","subzone:shadowthread-cave","subzone:shadowglen","subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","quest:3521","zone:darnassus"},src={"Webwood Venom Sac","Webwood Venom"}}
E["npc:alyissia"] = {t="npc",n="Alyissia",z="teldrassil",s="Alyissia is a kaldorei warrior trainer stationed inside the hollow boughs of Aldrassil in Shadowglen. She guides newly awakened night elf warriors in the fundamentals of martial combat, helping them harness raw strength and discipline to defend their nascent world tree.",h="Alyissia is a kaldorei warrior trainer stationed inside the hollow boughs of Aldrassil in Shadowglen.",sec={{t="Martial Mentor of Shadowglen",b="Standing within the sheltered sanctuary of Aldrassil, Alyissia instructs young night elves who feel drawn to the path of steel and shield rather than nature magic or the priesthood. While the kaldorei military is traditionally renowned for its Sentinels and stealthy archers, the perilous state of modern Kalimdor requires resolute frontline fighters. Alyissia teaches foundational techniques, ensuring that fresh recruits can direct their battle fury, master their stances, and withstand the aggressive wildlife and corrupted grells encroaching on Shadowglen.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Alyissia?",a="Alyissia is a night elf warrior trainer located in Aldrassil, the central sanctuary of Shadowglen. She provides initial guidance, training, and simple martial exercises for fledgling warriors starting their journey in Teldrassil.",al={"who is alyissia","alyissia npc","what does alyissia do"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Alyissia?",a="She is stationed on the ground level within the great hollow trunk of Aldrassil, situated at the heart of Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",al={"alyissia location","where is alyissia","find alyissia"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests does Alyissia offer?",a="Alyissia gives introductory training quests to newly arrived night elf warriors, such as Simple Sigil, directing them to practice new combat maneuvers and report to fellow leaders in the boughs.",al={"alyissia quests","quests from alyissia"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Alyissia on?",a="Alyissia stands firmly with the night elves of Darnassus and the wider Alliance. Stationed in Aldrassil at the heart of Shadowglen, she serves her people by schooling promising young night elf warriors in the fundamentals of combat and duty, helping protect Teldrassil from surrounding threats.",al={"alyissia faction","who does alyissia serve","alyissia alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Alyissia here?",a="Alyissia is stationed in Aldrassil to guide newly awakened and aspiring night elf warriors taking their first steps in Shadowglen. She ensures that those who take up arms possess the discipline, combat techniques, and resolve needed to defend their secluded woodland sanctuary.",al={"why is alyissia in aldrassil","alyissia purpose shadowglen","what does alyissia do here"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="What does Alyissia want?",a="Alyissia seeks capable recruits who can learn the arts of martial combat and prove their valor. She wants incoming warriors to hone their discipline and martial skills so they can safeguard their woodland home and aid their kin across Teldrassil.",al={"what are alyissia goals","what does alyissia need","alyissia motive"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="For young night elf warriors, Alyissia is the very first mentor, providing early stance training and martial discipline before they venture deeper into the wilds of Teldrassil.",["race:NightElf"]="Alyissia represents the front-line martial discipline of the kaldorei, readying defenders to protect the roots of Aldrassil from corruption."},kw={"aldrassil","alyissia","night elf","shadowglen","teldrassil","warrior trainer"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil","quest:3116","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},src={"Alyissia"}}
E["npc:athridas-bearmantle"] = {t="npc",n="Athridas Bearmantle",z="teldrassil",s="Athridas Bearmantle is a night elf sentinel residing in Dolanaar within the boughs of Teldrassil. Tasked with safeguarding the local settlement, he directs young adventurers to investigate the encroaching corruption affecting the local wildlife and the nearby Gnarlpine furbolgs.",h="Athridas Bearmantle is a night elf sentinel residing in Dolanaar within the boughs of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Guardian of Dolanaar",b="Stationed within Dolanaar, Athridas Bearmantle stands as an early line of defense for the night elves emerging from Shadowglen. As the boughs of the newly grown world tree Teldrassil exhibit unnatural signs of decay and unrest, Athridas works tirelessly to coordinate local scouting efforts and protect the peaceful township from surrounding threats.",sp=0},{t="The Furbolg Affliction",b="Much of Athridas's concern centers on the neighboring Gnarlpine tribe of furbolgs. Once peaceful neighbors, the Gnarlpine have succumbed to a spreading madness and corruption that poisons their shamans and chieftains, driving them into violent frenzy against the Kaldorei. Athridas mobilizes willing champions to contain the threat and unearth the deeper taint taking root in the wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Athridas Bearmantle?",a="Athridas Bearmantle is a night elf stationed in Dolanaar on the island of Teldrassil. He serves as an organizer for local defense, enlisting adventurers to combat the dark forces creeping through the boughs of the World Tree.",al={"who is athridas","athridas bearmantle lore","athridas dolanaar"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Athridas Bearmantle?",a="Athridas is located in Dolanaar, the first major town night elf adventurers reach after leaving Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",al={"athridas location","where is athridas","find athridas bearmantle"},gp=true},{q="What threats does Athridas focus on?",a="Athridas primarily focuses on the aggressive Gnarlpine furbolgs who have fallen prey to a corrupting influence, directing travelers to quell their attacks, investigate their madness, and recover vital relics.",al={"athridas quests","what does athridas want","athridas bearmantle tasks"},it="threat"},{q="Is Athridas related to Broll Bearmantle?",a="While Athridas shares the prominent Bearmantle surname with renowned night elf figures such as Broll Bearmantle, the exact nature of their familial relationship is not explicitly chronicled.",al={"is he related to broll","broll bearmantle relation","athridas and broll"},it="ties"},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine furbolgs attacking Dolanaar?",a="The Gnarlpine tribe has fallen victim to a dark, unnatural corruption seeping through Teldrassil, which has driven their shamans and warriors mad with hostility toward the night elves.",al={"why are gnarlpine mad","gnarlpine corruption","furbolg hostility teldrassil"}},{q="What role does Athridas play in securing Teldrassil?",a="Athridas acts as an early sentinel and organizer, ensuring that the spreading corruption among the beasts and furbolgs of Teldrassil is confronted before it can overrun the settlement of Dolanaar.",al={"athridas role","athridas importance"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Athridas Bearmantle on?",a="Athridas stands firmly with the night elves of Darnassus and the Alliance. Stationed in Dolanaar, he devotes his efforts to protecting his kin and maintaining order across Teldrassil against encroaching corruption.",al={"athridas faction","who does athridas serve","athridas bearmantle allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Athridas Bearmantle want?",a="Athridas seeks to cleanse the sudden blight poisoning Teldrassil's wildlife and to quell the frenzy overtaking the local Gnarlpine furbolgs. He enlists capable travelers to investigate the corruption, recover sacred relics, and neutralize dangerous rogue furbolgs threatening Dolanaar.",al={"athridas goal","what is athridas trying to do","athridas bearmantle motivation"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Athridas Bearmantle here in Dolanaar?",a="Dolanaar serves as the first major settlement travelers reach beyond Shadowglen, making it ground zero for managing local crises. Athridas remains stationed here to coordinate defensive efforts, monitor the troubled forests, and direct adventurers against escalating woodland threats.",al={"why is athridas in dolanaar","athridas post","reason athridas is here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young Kaldorei leaving Shadowglen, Athridas represents the grounded reality of Teldrassil's struggles, pointing out that their new home is already threatened from within.",["class:Druid"]="Athridas's missions against the corrupted Gnarlpine and his concern for ancient relics directly touch upon the balance of nature that druids are sworn to restore."},kw={"athridas","bearmantle","dolanaar","furbolg","gnarlpine","kaldorei","night elf","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:476","quest:475","quest:483","quest:486","topic:night-elf"},src={"Athridas Bearmantle"}}
E["npc:ayanna-everstride"] = {t="npc",n="Ayanna Everstride",z="teldrassil",s="Ayanna Everstride is a kaldorei hunter trainer stationed in Aldrassil within the Shadowglen of Teldrassil. She instructs fledgling night elf rangers in the foundational arts of marksmanship, tracking, and wilderness survival. Young hunters taking their first steps beneath the boughs of the World Tree seek her guidance to hone their woodland discipline.",h="Ayanna Everstride is a kaldorei hunter trainer stationed in Aldrassil within the Shadowglen of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Mentor in Shadowglen",b="Perched inside Aldrassil at the very heart of the Shadowglen, Ayanna Everstride stands ready to instruct newly awakened kaldorei in the ways of the wild. To the night elves, a hunter is not merely a trapper or sharpshooter, but an indispensable guardian of the sacred forests. Ayanna provides guidance on early martial techniques, helping novices master ranged combat and survive in the perilous woods of Teldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ayanna Everstride?",a="Ayanna Everstride is a night elf hunter trainer located in Aldrassil, situated in the starting area of Shadowglen on Teldrassil. She teaches novice hunters fundamental combat skills and outdoor survival techniques.",al={"ayanna everstride","who is ayanna","aldrassil hunter trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Ayanna Everstride?",a="She can be found in the interior of Aldrassil, the massive hollowed tree settlement located in Shadowglen at the heart of Teldrassil.",al={"ayanna location","where is ayanna","find ayanna everstride"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests involve Ayanna Everstride?",a="New night elf hunters are directed to Ayanna via early training quests, such as receiving an Etched Sigil from early instructors, after which she provides introductory training for aspiring woodland rangers.",al={"ayanna quests","etched sigil quest","ayanna quest giver"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Ayanna Everstride on?",a="Ayanna stands firmly with the night elves of Darnassus and the Alliance. Stationed at Shadowglen within Aldrassil, she guides newly awakened night elves in communion with the wilds, offering her loyalty to her kin and the defense of Teldrassil.",al={"ayanna everstride faction","who does ayanna everstride serve","ayanna everstride alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Ayanna Everstride want?",a="Ayanna is dedicated to guiding novice hunters. She wants to ensure that young night elves learn the ways of tracking, marksmanship, and surviving in harmony with nature before venturing deeper into the world.",al={"ayanna everstride goal","what does ayanna want","ayanna everstride purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Ayanna Everstride here in Shadowglen?",a="Ayanna resides in Aldrassil to serve as a hunter trainer. As young night elves awaken within the sheltered grove of Shadowglen, she prepares those drawn to the path of the hunter with essential skills, weapons, and instruction.",al={"why is ayanna in aldrassil","why is ayanna everstride here","ayanna everstride shadowglen role"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="For fledgling night elf hunters starting their journey in Shadowglen, Ayanna Everstride serves as the very first mentor in weapon handling, tracking, and surviving the untamed wilderness.",["race:NightElf"]="Stationed within the sacred hollows of Aldrassil, Ayanna helps safeguard the young World Tree by preparing raw recruits to defend the surrounding forest from encroaching corruption."},kw={"aldrassil","ayanna","everstride","hunter trainer","night elf","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil","quest:3117","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},src={"Ayanna Everstride"}}
E["npc:corithras-moonrage"] = {t="npc",n="Corithras Moonrage",z="teldrassil",s="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf scholar and quest giver stationed in the village of Dolanaar on Teldrassil. He guides newly arrived adventurers in understanding the nature of the great World Tree and tasks them with maintaining its sacred moonwells. Through his lessons, he reveals both the spiritual importance of Teldrassil and the growing burdens carried by the kaldorei.",h="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf scholar and quest giver stationed in the village of Dolanaar on Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Scholar of Dolanaar",b="Residing in the shaded settlement of Dolanaar, Corithras Moonrage serves as an instructor to travelers leaving the sheltered bounds of Shadowglen. As young kaldorei venture into the wider boughs of Teldrassil, Corithras ensures they understand the history of their new home. He teaches that survival in this changing era requires vigilance and reverence for the natural order.",sp=0},{t="Crown of the Earth",b="Much of Corithras's duty revolves around overseeing the ritual purification of the Crown of the Earth. He directs adventurers to collect pure waters from moonwells across Teldrassil and cleanse sacred phials throughout the forest. Through these trials, he monitors the health of the World Tree and seeks to maintain the delicate balance of the wilderness against creeping corruption.",sp=0},{t="The Burden of the Kaldorei",b="Beneath Corithras's guidance lies an uneasy truth regarding Teldrassil's creation. Unlike the ancient Nordrassil, this new World Tree was raised without the blessings of the Dragon Aspects, who refused Fandral Staghelm's ambitious creation. Corithras reflects on the loss of night elven immortality and the fragile, uncertain future the kaldorei now face under the boughs of an unblessed bough.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Corithras Moonrage?",a="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf scholar located in Dolanaar. He introduces adventurers to the history of Teldrassil and tasks them with tending to the sacred moonwells and testing the waters of the World Tree.",al={"corithras moonrage role","who is corithras","dolanaar quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Corithras Moonrage be found?",a="He can be found standing outdoors in Dolanaar, the central crossroads village situated in the southern reaches of Teldrassil.",al={"corithras location","where is corithras","find corithras"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Crown of the Earth questline about?",a="The Crown of the Earth quests involve drawing water from various moonwells scattered across Teldrassil and applying it to sacred groves. Corithras uses these rituals to observe the vitality and purity of the boughs.",al={"crown of the earth meaning","corithras quests","moonwell quests"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is Corithras concerned about Teldrassil's origins?",a="Corithras shares the history of how Teldrassil was planted after the Third War to restore night elven immortality. Because the Dragon Aspects refused to bless the tree, Corithras remains acutely aware that the tree lacks divine protection and that his people remain mortal.",al={"why burden of kaldorei","aspects refusal","why no immortality"},it="motive"},{q="What does Corithras teach new adventurers?",a="He imparts lessons on the recent sacrifices of the Third War, the founding of Teldrassil, and the responsibility each kaldorei bears to defend their new woodland home.",al={"corithras lore","dolanaar history","what does corithras tell you"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Is Corithras aligned with the Cenarion Circle or Darnassus?",a="He serves as a loyal citizen and scholar of Darnassus in Dolanaar, working closely with druids and priests alike to monitor the well-being of the forest and its waters.",al={"corithras faction","is corithras a druid"},it="side"},{q="What does Corithras Moonrage want?",a="Corithras seeks to tend and understand the health of the young World Tree. Through the ritual known as the Crown of the Earth, he tasks travelers with gathering vital waters from sacred moonwells across Teldrassil to bless the great boughs, striving to nurture the land and unravel the burdens weighing upon the kaldorei.",al={"what does corithras want","corithras moonrage goals","corithras objective"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar?",a="Stationed in the bustling settlement of Dolanaar, Corithras acts as a guide to newly arrived night elf adventurers venturing out from Shadowglen. Positioned at the heart of Teldrassil, he enlists able hands to carry out essential rituals and investigate the growing ecological and spiritual troubles surrounding the World Tree.",al={"why is corithras here","why is corithras in dolanaar","corithras moonrage dolanaar purpose"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, speaking with Corithras is a foundational lesson in the post-Third War reality, confronting the loss of ancient immortality and the disputed creation of Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="Druids will find Corithras's tasks deeply connected to their calling, as his moonwell rites directly track the health and creeping ailments of the World Tree.",["class:Priest"]="Priests of Elune assist Corithras in carrying the blessed waters of the moonwells, maintaining the spiritual and physical harmony of Dolanaar's surrounding wilds."},kw={"corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","fandral staghelm","kaldorei","moonwell","night elf","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:929","quest:940","topic:night-elf"},src={"Corithras Moonrage"}}
E["npc:dazalar"] = {t="npc",n="Dazalar",z="teldrassil",s="Dazalar is a night elf hunter trainer stationed in Dolanaar within Teldrassil. He guides fledgling sentinels and scouts as they hone their marksmanship and learn the sacred art of bonding with the wild beasts of the great boughs.",h="Dazalar is a night elf hunter trainer stationed in Dolanaar within Teldrassil.",sec={{t="The Dolanaar Encampment",b="Standing within the settlement of Dolanaar, Dazalar serves as a primary mentor for young hunters venturing beyond the sheltered glade of Shadowglen. Night elf society relies heavily on its rangers and sentinels to patrol the wilderness, and Dazalar ensures newcomers possess the discipline and patience necessary to protect Teldrassil's fragile ecosystem.",sp=0},{t="Bonding with the Wild",b="A critical rite of passage under Dazalar's guidance is learning to tame and care for beasts. Rather than bending creatures to a hunter's whim through sheer force, the Kaldorei way emphasizes forming a mutual pact with forest predators like nightsabers, owls, and strigid hunters, training them to fight alongside their masters with respect.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dazalar?",a="Dazalar is a night elf hunter trainer located in the village of Dolanaar in Teldrassil. He teaches novice hunters new combat abilities and guides them in the ways of taming wild beasts.",al={"who is dazalar","dazalar lore","dazalar identity"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Dazalar?",a="He is stationed outdoors in Dolanaar, the central hub of Teldrassil that adventurers reach shortly after leaving the starting grounds of Shadowglen.",al={"dazalar location","where is dazalar","dolanaar hunter trainer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What training does Dazalar provide?",a="Dazalar teaches various ranged attacks, traps, and survival techniques suitable for developing hunters, and he sends novices on trials to master the taming of wilderness animals.",al={"what does dazalar teach","dazalar skills","hunter training dazalar"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Does Dazalar offer any special quests?",a="Yes, Dazalar offers pivotal hunter training quests, including The Hunter's Path, the multi-part trial Taming the Beast, and Training the Beast, which teach young hunters how to bond with and maintain animal companions.",al={"dazalar quests","hunter quests dolanaar","taming the beast quest"},gp=true},{q="Why do night elves rely so heavily on hunters?",a="For millennia, the Kaldorei have lived in harmony with the ancient forests of Kalimdor. Archers and scouts form the backbone of the Sentinel army, utilizing stealth, marksmanship, and animal allies to safeguard their lands without disrupting nature.",al={"night elf hunters lore","why sentinels use hunters","kaldorei hunters"},it="history"},{q="What kind of beasts does Dazalar send hunters to tame?",a="He directs hunters to track down native Teldrassil fauna, including local spiders, nightsabers, and birds of prey, testing the hunter's ability to approach and calm wild predators.",al={"what beasts to tame","dolanaar taming trial","tame beasts teldrassil"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Dazalar on?",a="Dazalar is loyal to the night elves of Darnassus and serves as part of the Alliance. Stationed in Dolanaar, he devotes his craft to guiding young kaldorei hunters in communion with the wilds of Teldrassil, ensuring they can defend their people and preserve the balance of their new woodland home.",al={"dazalar faction","is dazalar alliance","who does dazalar serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Dazalar want?",a="Dazalar aims to train aspiring hunters in the foundational disciplines of tracking, marksmanship, and wilderness survival. Beyond standard combat prowess, he seeks to ensure every kaldorei hunter masters the art of bonding with, taming, and training the diverse beasts native to the boughs of Teldrassil.",al={"what is dazalar's goal","dazalar purpose","why does dazalar train hunters"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Dazalar here?",a="Dazalar makes his home in Dolanaar because the settlement is the first major haven young night elves visit after leaving the Shadowglen. Positioned right along the forest trails, he can instruct fledgling scouts, sentinels, and rangers before they venture deeper into the untamed reaches of Teldrassil.",al={"why is dazalar in dolanaar","dazalar teldrassil role","dazalar location reason"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Dazalar is one of the earliest mentors a night elf hunter encounters, guiding them through the foundational trials of beast mastery and pet training.",["race:NightElf"]="He upholds the traditions of the Kaldorei sentinels and scouts, teaching young night elves how to live in balance with nature's fierce predators."},kw={"dazalar","dolanaar","hunter","night elf","taming the beast","teldrassil","the hunter's path","trainer"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:6061","quest:6065","quest:6081","topic:night-elf","quest:940"},src={"Dazalar"}}
E["npc:denalan"] = {t="npc",n="Denalan",z="teldrassil",s="Denalan is an accomplished night elf herbalist and botanist who tends a quiet lakeside plot along the eastern shore of Lake Al'Ameth. Working under a simple awning, he devotes his days to studying the island's plant life and seeking botanical remedies for the strange corruption affecting Teldrassil. He frequently enlists young adventurers to gather samples, study violent timberlings, and test enchanted soils.",h="Denalan is an accomplished night elf herbalist and botanist who tends a quiet lakeside plot along the eastern...",sec={{t="A Botanist at Lake Al'Ameth",b="While many kaldorei focus on martial vigilance or high druidic rites, Denalan pursues the patient, meticulous craft of herbalism. Stationed along the tranquil eastern banks of Lake Al'Ameth, he has established a modest research camp consisting of a cloth awning, simple field tools, and tidy rows of cultivated planter boxes. Rather than retreating to the grand barrows of Darnassus, he prefers to remain close to the loam, directly examining the unusual flora that has sprouted since the planting of the new World Tree.",sp=0},{t="Investigating Teldrassil's Blemishes",b="Denalan's research is far more than an academic curiosity; it addresses the growing unrest among Teldrassil's native wildlife. The timberlings, normally docile woodland beings of wood and sprout, have turned increasingly aggressive. Denalan enchants specialized soil to nurse wild seeds in captivity and analyze how malignant forces seep into the root systems. By studying strange specimens like shimmering fronds, glowing fruit, and moss-twined growths, he seeks to isolate whatever dark taint is troubling the forest boughs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Denalan?",a="Denalan is located on the eastern bank of Lake Al'Ameth in southern Teldrassil, south of Dolanaar. He maintains a small camp with an awning and several cultivated planting beds right near the water's edge.",al={"denalan location","where is denalan","denalan map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Denalan researching at his campsite?",a="Denalan is an herbalist studying the unusual flora of Teldrassil and the aggressive behavior of local woodland spirits. He uses enchanted planter boxes to grow timberling seeds, analyze curious wild plant specimens, and find ways to cleanse corruption seeping into the new World Tree's ecosystem.",al={"what does denalan do","denalan purpose","why is denalan at the lake"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are the timberlings attacking people?",a="Timberlings are plant-like nature spirits native to the boughs of Teldrassil. Normally peaceful parts of the forest ecology, they have become violent and erratic due to an unnatural corruption spreading through the soil and roots of the World Tree, prompting researchers like Denalan to investigate their seeds.",al={"why are timberlings aggressive","timberling lore","corrupted timberlings"},it="threat"},{q="What are Denalan's planter boxes used for?",a="Denalan keeps specially prepared planter beds filled with enchanted earth. He uses them to cultivate wild seeds and strange botanical cuttings, allowing him to safely observe how the forest's flora reacts to purified soil away from wild contaminants.",al={"denalan planter","denalans earth","denalan dirt boxes"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who does Denalan work with?",a="Denalan has worked closely with fellow herbalists such as Sylvia Whisperbloom and stays in regular communication with druidic researchers and scholars across Teldrassil, including Rellian Greenspyre in Darnassus.",al={"denalan allies","who does denalan report to"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Moss-twined Heart that Denalan examines?",a="The Moss-twined Heart is a blighted botanical core recovered from Blackmoss the Fetid, a corrupted timberling in Teldrassil. Denalan studies it in his enchanted soil to understand the unnatural sickness twisting the island's plant life.",al={"moss twined heart","moss-twined heart quest","blackmoss heart"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a renowned night elf herbalist and researcher residing along the shores of Lake Al'Ameth. Known for his deep understanding of Kalimdor's plant life, he dedicates his craft to studying the flora of Teldrassil and finding natural remedies for the ecological distress troubling the World Tree.",al={"who is denalan","denalan lore","about denalan"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Denalan on?",a="Denalan is loyal to the night elves of Darnassus and allied with the Alliance. He works openly with his fellow Kaldorei herbalists and druids, aiding any travelers who wish to protect Teldrassil from corruption and harm.",al={"denalan faction","is denalan alliance","who does denalan serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Denalan want?",a="Denalan seeks to cleanse Teldrassil of the spreading corruption tainting its soils and wildlife. He collects seeds and rare plant specimens from the surrounding forest, using specially enchanted earth to nurture healthy growth and find a remedy for the maddened timberlings.",al={"what does denalan want","denalan goal","denalan objective"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Denalan here at Lake Al'Ameth?",a="Denalan established his campsite by the lake to study Teldrassil's native vegetation up close. The shores provide an ideal outdoor laboratory for his planter boxes and enchanted soil, placing him near the epicenter of the agitated timberling population he aims to understand.",al={"why is denalan here","why lake alameth denalan","denalan campsite purpose"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Why is Denalan famous?",a="Denalan is widely respected as a famed herbalist among the night elves. His lifelong study of Kalimdor's botany and expertise in purifying tainted seeds and soil have earned him a reputation as one of the realm's foremost authorities on plant lore.",al={"why is denalan famous","denalan herbalist fame","is denalan well known"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Denalan exemplifies the kaldorei tradition of botanical study, demonstrating how gathering and cultivating wild plants can diagnose deeper ailments in the natural world.",["class:Druid"]="Druids will find common cause with Denalan's lakeside experiments, as his work directly assists the Cenarion Circle's efforts to trace and purge the taint spreading through Teldrassil's roots.",["race:NightElf"]="Denalan's research at Lake Al'Ameth represents early kaldorei attempts to understand the unexpected flaws and growing pains of their new home, Teldrassil."},kw={"blackmoss","botany","denalan","herbalist","kaldorei","lake al'ameth","oakenscowl","planter","teldrassil","timberlings"},rel={"subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil","quest:997","quest:918","quest:919","quest:927","quest:941","quest:922"},src={"Denalan"}}
E["npc:dirania-silvershine"] = {t="npc",n="Dirania Silvershine",z="teldrassil",s="Dirania Silvershine is a night elf resident of Shadowglen in Teldrassil. Deeply loyal and observant, she watches over the tranquil grove and looks out for her companion Iverron when his reckless ventures land him in peril.",h="Dirania Silvershine is a night elf resident of Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Watcher in Shadowglen",b="Dirania stands among the tranquil boughs of Shadowglen, the secluded vale where young night elves begin their service to Kalimdor and the Alliance. While many in the barrow mounds and sanctuaries look to broad spiritual duties, Dirania stays mindful of those nearest to her, attentive to the quiet dangers that stir even in the heart of Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="A Friend's Peril",b="Dirania's immediate concern is her companion Iverron. Overeager and careless around the poisonous woodland creatures creeping across the glen, Iverron frequently gets into trouble. When he succumbs to a venomous bite from the local webwood spiders, Dirania takes it upon herself to seek out willing hands to gather ingredients and prepare a remedy before the venom takes a permanent toll.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dirania Silvershine?",a="Dirania Silvershine is a night elf found in Shadowglen on Teldrassil. She acts as a quest giver, primarily concerned with rescuing and curing her friend Iverron after he runs afoul of local poisonous wildlife.",al={"dirania","who is dirania","dirania silvershine lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Dirania Silvershine?",a="Dirania is located within Shadowglen, the starter vale inside Teldrassil, not far from the central path near Aldrassil.",al={"dirania location","where is dirania","find dirania silvershine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Dirania's relationship to Iverron?",a="Dirania and Iverron are close friends. Dirania is the more sensible and watchful of the pair, stepping in to arrange an antidote whenever Iverron acts foolishly and suffers a poisonous bite from the local fauna.",al={"is dirania related to iverron","iverron and dirania","dirania's friend"},it="ties"},{q="What quests does Dirania offer?",a="She offers quests centered on helping her companion, notably 'A Friend in Need' and 'Iverron's Antidote', tasking adventurers with securing ingredients to brew a cure for Iverron's spider venom.",al={"dirania quests","quests from dirania silvershine","iverron quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why is Dirania worried about spiders in Shadowglen?",a="The webwood spiders dwelling in the boughs of Shadowglen carry a potent venom. While experienced sentinels can handle them, novice elves like Iverron frequently underestimate the danger and risk succumbing to their bites.",al={"shadowglen spiders","why spiders in teldrassil","webwood danger"},it="threat"},{q="Does Dirania belong to any formal order or faction?",a="Dirania is an Alliance night elf living peacefully in Teldrassil. She is not depicted as an active member of the Sisterhood of Elune or the Cenarion Circle, but rather a caring civilian looking out for her fellow kin.",al={"dirania faction","is dirania a druid","is dirania a sentinel"},it="side"},{q="What does Dirania Silvershine want?",a="Dirania is desperately seeking help for her close friend Iverron. He ventured out into Shadowglen and was severely poisoned by the native webwood spiders, leaving him incapacitated. She needs someone to quickly gather the necessary ingredients across the glade so that an antidote can be brewed to save his life.",al={"dirania silvershine goal","what does dirania need","dirania silvershine wants"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Dirania Silvershine here?",a="Dirania resides in Shadowglen, making her home within the sheltered boughs of Aldrassil alongside her fellow night elves. She remains stationed here in distress after her friend Iverron fell victim to spider venom nearby, waiting for capable travelers to come to his aid.",al={"why is dirania in shadowglen","dirania silvershine location reason","why dirania here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves stepping into Shadowglen, Dirania serves as an early reminder of the bonds of friendship and the creeping dangers threatening even the newest sanctuaries of the World Tree."},kw={"antidote","dirania","iverron","shadowglen","silvershine","teldrassil","webwood"},rel={"npc:iverron","subzone:shadowglen","quest:3519","quest:3521","quest:4495","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},src={"Dirania Silvershine"}}
E["npc:elder-bladeleaf"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Bladeleaf",z="teldrassil",s="Elder Bladeleaf is an honored night elf ancestral spirit who appears in Dolanaar during the Lunar Festival. Revering the ancestors is a core aspect of the festival, and Bladeleaf welcomes travelers wishing to pay their respects beneath the canopy of Teldrassil.",h="Elder Bladeleaf is an honored night elf ancestral spirit who appears in Dolanaar during the Lunar Festival.",sec={{t="A Spirit of Dolanaar",b="Standing amidst the trees of Dolanaar, Elder Bladeleaf manifests as a spectral ancestor during the Lunar Festival. Night elves hold their forebears in high regard, and during this auspicious season, the barrier between the living and the honored dead thins. Bladeleaf bestows blessings and festival tokens upon any who seek him out in friendship, offering a quiet reminder of the wisdom and longevity carried within night elf heritage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Bladeleaf?",a="Elder Bladeleaf is a night elf ancestral spirit who manifests in Dolanaar during the annual Lunar Festival. He exists to share wisdom, receive the honor of visiting adventurers, and offer traditional festival tokens.",al={"elder bladeleaf lore","who is bladeleaf","bladeleaf ghost"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Elder Bladeleaf only here sometimes?",a="Elder Bladeleaf is tied to the Lunar Festival, a time when spirits and ancestors across Azeroth return to walk among the living. When the festival concludes, his spirit returns to the realm beyond until the next cycle.",al={"where is elder bladeleaf","can't find elder bladeleaf","is bladeleaf seasonal"},it="why_here"},{q="Is Elder Bladeleaf related to the other Bladeleafs in Dolanaar?",a="Given that several living night elves in Dolanaar—such as Syral Bladeleaf—share his surname, he is believed to be an ancient forebear of their family line watching over his kin's modern settlement.",al={"syral bladeleaf related","bladeleaf family","hannah bladeleaf relation"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Elder Bladeleaf on?",a="Elder Bladeleaf belongs to the night elves and the Alliance, dwelling among his people in Dolanaar. As an honored ancestral elder visiting during the Lunar Festival, however, his spirit stands to share the wisdom and celebrations of ancient times with travelers who come to pay their respects peacefully.",al={"is Elder Bladeleaf alliance","Elder Bladeleaf faction","whose side elder bladeleaf"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Elder Bladeleaf want?",a="Elder Bladeleaf seeks travelers to honor the ancestors and partake in the remembrance of the Lunar Festival. When you seek him out and offer your respects, his spirit imparts blessings of wisdom and coin from a long-past age to aid you on your journeys across Azeroth.",al={"what does elder bladeleaf want","elder bladeleaf purpose","why talk to elder bladeleaf"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Honoring Elder Bladeleaf is a sacred observance in your homelands, connecting you to ancient forebears who walked Kalimdor long before Teldrassil was grown.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance adventurers visiting Teldrassil during the Lunar Festival can easily pay homage to Elder Bladeleaf just outside the barrow dens of Dolanaar."},kw={"ancestor","bladeleaf the elder","dolanaar","elder bladeleaf","lunar festival","spirit","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:8715","subzone:dolanaar","npc:syral-bladeleaf","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},src={"Elder Bladeleaf"}}
E["npc:fandral-staghelm"] = {t="npc",n="Fandral Staghelm",z="teldrassil",s="Archdruid Fandral Staghelm leads the druids of the Cenarion Circle from the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus. Stepping into power after Malfurion Stormrage vanished into the Emerald Dream, he championed the planting of the new World Tree, Teldrassil. Proud, abrasive, and relentlessly ambitious, Fandral advocates for an aggressive Kaldorei resurgence that frequently pits him against High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind.",h="Archdruid Fandral Staghelm leads the druids of the Cenarion Circle from the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus.",sec={{t="Architect of Teldrassil",b="Following the Third War and the sacrifice of Nordrassil atop Mount Hyjal, the night elves lost their immortality and their sacred sanctuary. While Malfurion Stormrage cautioned patience and warned against vanity, Fandral championed the bold creation of a new World Tree off the coast of Kalimdor. When Malfurion subsequently fell comatose within the Emerald Dream, Fandral seized the initiative and led the druids in raising Teldrassil. He envisioned the colossal bough as a monument to Kaldorei endurance and a vessel to restore their lost supremacy, even though the Dragon Aspects pointedly withheld their blessings from the unapproved endeavor.",sp=0},{t="Tragedy in the Shifting Sands",b="A millennium before the First War, Fandral served as the Kaldorei field commander in Silithus during the War of the Shifting Sands. Renowned among the insectoid qiraji as 'Kar'sis'—the Hand of Earth—he held the front lines alongside his beloved only son, Valstann. Exploiting Fandral's devotion, the qiraji General Rajaxx engineered a feint against Southwind Village and captured Valstann, ruthlessly executing him directly in front of the horrified Archdruid. The loss shattered Fandral's spirit, precipitating a devastating retreat and cementing an abiding, bitter hatred for the swarm that remains etched into his haughty demeanor.",sp=0},{t="Rivalry and Hubris",b="Within the marble boughs of Darnassus, Fandral governs Kaldorei affairs with a haughty, unyielding hand. Unlike High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind, who favors spiritual preservation and cautious diplomacy, Fandral views military expansion and decisive strength as paramount to the survival of their people.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Fandral Staghelm?",a="Fandral Staghelm is the acting Archdruid of the Cenarion Circle in Darnassus, presiding over Kaldorei druids in Malfurion Stormrage's absence. Known for his fiery temperament and imperial ambitions, he is the primary visionary behind the creation of Teldrassil.",al={"fandral lore","who is the archdruid","archdruid of darnassus"},it="identity"},{q="Why doesn't Fandral get along with Tyrande?",a="Fandral advocates for Kaldorei military resurgence, aggressive expansion, and reclaiming lost immortality. Tyrande Whisperwind pursues cautious spiritual guidance through Elune. Their competing visions for the night elves' post-Hyjal future spark fierce political friction within Darnassus.",al={"fandral and tyrande","why do druids and priestesses disagree","staghelm vs whisperwind"},it="conflict"},{q="Why was Teldrassil planted against Malfurion's wishes?",a="Malfurion believed planting a replacement for Nordrassil was an act of hubris that nature would not condone. When Malfurion vanished into his coma, Fandral rallied the remaining druids to plant Teldrassil regardless, seeking to restore Kaldorei power and reclaim their lost immortality.",al={"who created teldrassil","why did fandral plant teldrassil","origin of teldrassil"},it="origin"},{q="What happened to Fandral's son?",a="During the War of the Shifting Sands in Silithus, Fandral's son Valstann was lured into an ambush at Southwind Village. The qiraji General Rajaxx captured Valstann and slaughtered him in front of Fandral, leaving the Archdruid grief-stricken and permanently embittered.",al={"fandral son","who was valstann","valstann staghelm"},it="history"},{q="Where can Fandral Staghelm be found?",a="Fandral stands atop the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus, surrounded by his loyal druids and overseeable business of the Kaldorei capital.",al={"where is fandral","fandral location","cenarion enclave leader"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Fandral Staghelm on?",a="Fandral stands as the Archdruid of Darnassus and a leader within the Cenarion Circle, championing the Kaldorei and the Alliance. However, his loyalties are fiercely nationalistic. Rather than submitting meekly to the traditional caution of the Cenarion elders or the priesthood of Elune, Fandral acts strictly in what he perceives to be the bold, militaristic interest of the night elven people.",al={"fandral staghelm faction","who does fandral serve","fandral allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Fandral Staghelm want?",a="Fandral desires the restoration of night elven power, immortality, and territorial dominance. Frustrated by centuries of passive isolation, he pushed to plant the World Tree Teldrassil to replace Nordrassil. He envisions an aggressive Kaldorei nation ready to conquer its borders, expand boldly across Kalimdor, and reclaim the lost glory and vigor of its ancient past.",al={"what is fandral staghelm's goal","fandral ambitions","what does archdruid staghelm want"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus?",a="With Malfurion Stormrage trapped and incapacitated in the Emerald Dream, Fandral stepped into the void as Archdruid. He governs the druids of the Cenarion Circle from the heights of the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus, ruling alongside High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind and actively steering the political and magical future of Teldrassil.",al={"why is fandral in darnassus","fandral staghelm location why","why is fandral here"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Why is Fandral Staghelm famous?",a="Long before he led the planting of Teldrassil, Fandral served as a brilliant Kaldorei field commander during the War of the Shifting Sands in Silithus. His devastating tactical command against the insectoid swarm earned him the title Kar'sis—the Hand of Earth—among the qiraji, who feared his battlefield fury until they orchestrated the tragic execution of his son.",al={"fandral famous","why is fandral feared","hand of earth fandral"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Staghelm commands the Darnassian druids, pushing the Cenarion Circle toward direct worldly authority while clashing with the traditional teachings of the sleeping Malfurion Stormrage.",["race:NightElf"]="As one of Darnassus's primary leaders, Fandral embodies Kaldorei pride and fury, driving the settlement of Teldrassil even as ordinary citizens feel the rift between his enclave and the Temple of the Moon.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though Teldrassil serves as an Alliance bastion in northern Kalimdor, Staghelm views the younger races with thinly veiled disdain, tolerating their presence only as political expediency demands."},kw={"cenarion circle","darnassus","fandral","malfurion","rajaxx","shifting sands","staghelm","teldrassil","valstann"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:cenarion-circle","npc:malfurion-stormrage","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","subzone:southwind-village","zone:silithus","topic:nordrassil"},src={"Fandral Staghelm"}}
E["npc:frahun-shadewhisper"] = {t="npc",n="Frahun Shadewhisper",z="teldrassil",s="Frahun Shadewhisper is a night elf rogue trainer stationed at Aldrassil within Shadowglen. He provides newly initiated night elf scouts and rogues with foundational techniques in stealth, agility, and covert strikes. He shares a family name with Erion Shadewhisper, another trainer of his craft in Darnassus.",h="Frahun Shadewhisper is a night elf rogue trainer stationed at Aldrassil within Shadowglen.",sec={{t="A Mentor in the Shadows",b="Within the safe haven of Aldrassil in the heart of Teldrassil, Frahun Shadewhisper instructs emerging rogues in the quiet arts of concealment and bladecraft. While night elf society often honors priests, sentinels, and druids, the specialized trade of scouts and infiltrators remains essential for safeguarding the boughs of the World Tree. Frahun welcomes recruits who arrive bearing an encrypted sigil, evaluating their potential and guiding their early development.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Frahun Shadewhisper?",a="Frahun Shadewhisper is a night elf rogue trainer stationed at Aldrassil in Teldrassil. He teaches novice rogues the fundamentals of stealth, precision combat, and covert tactics.",al={"frahun lore","who is frahun","frahun shadewhisper role"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Frahun Shadewhisper be found?",a="He is located in Aldrassil, the central stronghold of the starting area of Shadowglen on Teldrassil.",al={"frahun location","where is frahun","find frahun shadewhisper"},gp=true},{q="Is Frahun related to Erion Shadewhisper?",a="Given their shared surname and mutual dedication to training rogues in Teldrassil, Frahun is widely believed to be kin to Erion Shadewhisper, who trains rogues in Darnassus.",al={"erion shadewhisper brother","frahun erion related","shadewhisper family"},it="ties"},{q="What role does the Encrypted Sigil play with him?",a="Novice night elf rogues begin their journey by carrying an encrypted sigil directly to Frahun, marking them as candidates ready for formal instruction in the rogue's trade.",al={"encrypted sigil turn in","frahun sigil","rogue starting quest"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Frahun Shadewhisper on?",a="Frahun stands firmly with Darnassus and the Alliance. Stationed among the ancient boughs of Aldrassil in the Shadowglen, he serves his fellow kaldorei by ensuring that those with an aptitude for stealth and subterfuge can hone their crafts to protect night elf lands.",al={"frahun faction","frahun allegiance","is frahun alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Frahun Shadewhisper want?",a="Frahun seeks to instruct aspiring night elf rogues in the arts of shadows, lockpicking, and stealthy combat. He ensures new scouts and operatives understand their discipline thoroughly before venturing beyond the protected borders of the Shadowglen into greater Teldrassil.",al={"frahun motive","frahun goal","what does frahun do"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Frahun Shadewhisper here in Aldrassil?",a="Frahun is stationed at Aldrassil to guide newly awakened or novice night elves who walk the path of the rogue. In the safe haven of Shadowglen, he provides foundational training to ensure fledgling practitioners do not succumb to the dangers lurking in the woods.",al={"why is frahun in aldrassil","frahun shadowglen why","frahun location purpose"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Frahun Shadewhisper serves as the very first class mentor for night elf rogues, providing their initial introduction to stealth, ambush tactics, and weapon finesse.",["race:NightElf"]="Frahun demonstrates how night elves adapt their natural nocturnal affinity and elusiveness into lethal, practical combat skills to protect Teldrassil."},kw={"aldrassil","encrypted sigil","erion","frahun","rogue trainer","shadewhisper","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","quest:3118","quest:2259","topic:night-elf"},src={"Frahun Shadewhisper"}}
E["npc:gaerolas-talvethren"] = {t="npc",n="Gaerolas Talvethren",z="teldrassil",s="Gaerolas Talvethren is a night elf sentinel standing watch over the ruins of Starbreeze Village in Teldrassil. Appointed as the protector of the Sleeping druids, he seeks aid in confronting the aggressive furbolgs and dark corruption unsettling the boughs.",h="Gaerolas Talvethren is a night elf sentinel standing watch over the ruins of Starbreeze Village in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Sleeping",b="Positioned amid the troubled settlement of Starbreeze Village, Gaerolas Talvethren bears the solemn mantle of protecting the Sleeping druids who slumber in communion with the Emerald Dream. His vigilance has grown fraught as unnatural corruption creeps through the forest, unsettling the balance of Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="The Gnarlpine Menace",b="Gaerolas directs travelers to push back against the Gnarlpine tribe of furbolgs, whose minds have turned to madness and savagery. By investigating the taint spreading from their shamans and finding the roots of their distress, he hopes to preserve what sanctity remains in eastern Teldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gaerolas Talvethren?",a="He is a night elf defender stationed at Starbreeze Village, charged with safeguarding the slumbering druids and investigating the strange corruption afflicting the area.",al={"gaerolas","who is gaerolas","gaerolas role"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Gaerolas Talvethren?",a="He is located in Starbreeze Village, in the eastern boughs of Teldrassil, east of Dolanaar.",al={"gaerolas location","where is gaerolas talvethren","find gaerolas"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who are 'the Sleeping' that Gaerolas protects?",a="The Sleeping refers to the night elf druids who entered long slumbers in barrows and sanctuaries to traverse the Emerald Dream, leaving their physical forms vulnerable to physical harm.",al={"the sleeping","who are the sleeping","sleeping druids"},it="people"},{q="What threats is Gaerolas concerned about?",a="He is deeply troubled by the corruption afflicting the local wildlife and the sudden, maddened hostility of the Gnarlpine furbolg tribe.",al={"starbreeze threats","gaerolas quests","gnarlpine trouble"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Gaerolas Talvethren on?",a="Gaerolas stands firmly with the night elves of Darnassus and the Alliance. As the sworn guardian of the slumbering druids resting in Starbreeze Village, his loyalties lie with the Cenarion Circle, his kin, and the defense of Teldrassil.",al={"gaerolas faction","who does gaerolas serve","gaerolas allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Gaerolas Talvethren want?",a="Gaerolas wants to safeguard the slumbering druids from the corrupting forces encroaching on Starbreeze Village. He seeks your aid in investigating the troubling blight spreading through the area and rooting out the aggression of the corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs.",al={"gaerolas goal","what is gaerolas trying to do","gaerolas purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Gaerolas Talvethren here?",a="Gaerolas remains stationed in Starbreeze Village because he is the designated protector of the Sleeping. While the druids commune in the Emerald Dream, they are completely vulnerable to physical danger, leaving Gaerolas to stand watch against any outside menace.",al={"why is gaerolas in starbreeze village","gaerolas reason for being here","why is gaerolas talvethren here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves departing Dolanaar, assisting Gaerolas offers a sobering look at how deeply the taint has penetrated Teldrassil's sacred boughs.",["class:Druid"]="Gaerolas's duty as guardian of the slumbering druids makes aiding his efforts a personal matter of protecting fellow practitioners of the Cenarion Circle."},kw={"a troubling breeze","gaerolas talvethren","gnarlpine corruption","starbreeze village","teldrassil","the sleeping"},rel={"subzone:starbreeze-village","quest:475","quest:476","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},src={"Gaerolas Talvethren"}}
E["npc:gilshalan-windwalker"] = {t="npc",n="Gilshalan Windwalker",z="teldrassil",s="Gilshalan Windwalker is a night elf researcher resting at the base of the great tree Aldrassil in Shadowglen. Concerned by the sudden corruption taking root within Teldrassil, he studies the local wildlife to understand the unnatural aggression plaguing the boughs. His investigations into the Webwood spiders provide early clues about the rot afflicting the World Tree.",h="Gilshalan Windwalker is a night elf researcher resting at the base of the great tree Aldrassil in Shadowglen.",sec={{t="A Scholar at the Roots",b="Sitting calmly on the stone steps leading into Aldrassil, Gilshalan Windwalker watches over the tranquil canopy of Shadowglen with growing unease. Teldrassil was planted to restore the night elves' lost sanctuary and harmony with nature, but signs of deep spiritual malaise have emerged almost immediately. Gilshalan dedicates himself to examining how this corruption manifests in the local beasts, beginning with the venomous arachnids that weave their webs nearby.",sp=0},{t="The Webwood Menace",b="Gilshalan's primary focus centers on the Webwood spiders lurking in the Shadowthread Cave to the north. These creatures, once a balanced part of the forest ecosystem, have grown unnaturally hostile and tainted. By sending young novices to gather venom sacs and intact spider eggs, Gilshalan works to analyze the venom's altered potency and discern whether the corruption is passed down through generations or spread externally through the soil of Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="Word to the Archdruid",b="With the venom and an egg in hand, Gilshalan believes the spiders' venom will show properties linked to the recent growth of the new World Tree. He arranges for the specimens to be sent to Darnassus, where he will continue his studies. He also passes word to promising protectors that Tenaron Stormgrip has been asking for them in the highest room of Aldrassil, where the druidic leadership watches over the fledgling World Tree.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gilshalan Windwalker?",a="Gilshalan Windwalker is a night elf scholar seated at the base of Aldrassil in Shadowglen. He investigates the mysterious corruption creeping into the wildlife of Teldrassil.",al={"gilshalan","who is gilshalan","windwalker night elf"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Gilshalan want Webwood venom?",a="Gilshalan seeks to study the chemical and spiritual properties of the venom to understand why the forest's spiders have become so aggressive and mutated.",al={"why webwood venom","webwood venom quest","spider venom gilshalan"},it="wants"},{q="What does he do with the Webwood egg?",a="He wants live specimens to study, but a grown giant spider is too dangerous to capture. An unhatched egg is far easier to transport, so he has it sent to Darnassus along with the venom, where the hatchlings can be contained and studied.",al={"webwood egg quest","why spider eggs","egg of webwood"},it="motive"},{q="Where does Gilshalan send adventurers next?",a="After the egg is delivered, he tells adventurers that Tenaron Stormgrip has been asking for them, and sends them up to the highest room atop Aldrassil.",al={"tenaron summons","who do i see after gilshalan","after webwood egg"},it="next_step"},{q="Where is Gilshalan Windwalker located?",a="He sits on the stone pathway at the northern base of Aldrassil, just outside the hollow entrance of the central tree in Shadowglen.",al={"gilshalan location","where is windwalker","find gilshalan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the wildlife in Teldrassil aggressive?",a="An unknown blight has begun seeping through the roots and soil of Teldrassil, corrupting the minds and nature of its creatures and drawing scholarly concern from residents like Gilshalan.",al={"why are spiders mad","teldrassil corruption","corrupted beasts shadowglen"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Gilshalan Windwalker on?",a="Gilshalan stands firmly with his fellow night elves and the Alliance. Stationed at the roots of Aldrassil within the Shadowglen, he assists young adventurers in understanding and combating the strange, corrupting forces afflicting the local wildlife of Teldrassil.",al={"gilshalan faction","who does gilshalan serve","gilshalan windwalker alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Gilshalan Windwalker here?",a="He sits at the base of Aldrassil to monitor the emerging taint in Shadowglen. By studying venom samples and unhatched eggs from the agitated Webwood spiders, Gilshalan seeks to uncover what is poisoning the natural harmony of the great world tree.",al={"why is gilshalan in shadowglen","gilshalan windwalker aldrassil purpose"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Gilshalan Windwalker tied to?",a="Gilshalan answers to Tenaron Stormgrip, one of the elder druids stationed high above in the boughs of Aldrassil. Once his initial investigations into the Webwood spiders are concluded, he directs promising recruits up to Tenaron to continue aiding Teldrassil's defense.",al={"who does gilshalan report to","gilshalan tenaron","gilshalan connections"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Gilshalan represents the early efforts of your people to understand why the newly grown World Tree is already producing afflicted, violent wildlife.",["class:Druid"]="His research directly supports the Cenarion Circle's attempts to diagnose the ecological imbalance festering in the boughs of Shadowglen."},kw={"aldrassil","gilshalan","shadowglen","spider","tenaron","venom","webwood","windwalker"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil","quest:916","quest:917","quest:920","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","quest:940"},src={"Gilshalan Windwalker"}}
E["npc:ilthalaine"] = {t="npc",n="Ilthalaine",z="teldrassil",s="Ilthalaine is a night elf guardian standing watch over the sacred glade of Shadowglen in Teldrassil. He serves as the primary greeter and mentor for young night elves taking their very first steps into the world. Vigilant and attuned to the wilderness, he guides novice adventurers toward maintaining the delicate balance of nature across the boughs of the World Tree.",h="Ilthalaine is a night elf guardian standing watch over the sacred glade of Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Glen",b="Positioned just outside the heart of Shadowglen, Ilthalaine is often the first face a fledgling night elf sees upon beginning their journey. He observes the woodland paths and notices the subtle shifts within the forest that go unseen by ordinary eyes. His duty is to welcome returning kin and ensure that any newly awakened defenders are grounded in the traditions of their people, ready to face the responsibilities that come with tending to Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="The Balance of Nature",b="Even in the sheltered canopy of Shadowglen, unnatural aggression stirs among the local beasts. Ilthalaine tasks young defenders with hunting stray nightsabers and boars whose growing numbers and viciousness threaten to upend the harmony of the bough. He views culling not as cruelty, but as a vital sacred duty to preserve life and curb the uncharacteristic unrest that has begun to seep into the new World Tree.",sp=0},{t="A Guide to Discipline",b="Beyond testing an adventurer's martial prowess against corrupted wildlife, Ilthalaine directs young elves toward their chosen callings. Entrusting each traveler with a class sigil, he points them directly to their mentors within the Aldrassil sanctuary—whether they follow the path of the warrior, druid, rogue, priest, or hunter. Through him, every novice learns where their service to the Kaldorei begins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ilthalaine?",a="Ilthalaine is a Kaldorei overseer located in Shadowglen, the sheltered starting bower of Teldrassil. He serves as the first quest giver for newly created night elf adventurers, introducing them to their duties and the state of the forest.",al={"ilthalaine lore","who is this night elf","shadowglen quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="What is Ilthalaine's role in Shadowglen?",a="He watches over the wildlife in Shadowglen and ensures new night elves understand the importance of nature's equilibrium. He sends young initiates on basic hunts and directs them to their respective class trainers inside the great tree of Aldrassil.",al={"what does ilthalaine do","why is he here","ilthalaine purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Ilthalaine want the young nightsabers and boars culled?",a="The woodland creatures of Shadowglen have grown unusually fierce and aggressive, upsetting the natural harmony of the forest. Ilthalaine directs young champions to cull their overpopulated ranks to restore order to the bough.",al={"balance of nature quest","why kill nightsabers","why kill boars"},it="wants"},{q="What are the sigils he gives out?",a="Ilthalaine gives class-specific inscribed sigils to novices, instructing them to seek out their trainers—such as priestesses, druids, warriors, and rogues—sheltered within the roots of Aldrassil.",al={"etched sigil","simple sigil","verdant sigil","encrypted sigil","hallowed sigil"},it="item"},{q="Where can Ilthalaine be found?",a="He stands right on the central path of Shadowglen, just south of the massive hollow bough of Aldrassil in Teldrassil.",al={"ilthalaine location","where is ilthalaine","ilthalaine coords"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is Ilthalaine affiliated with the druids or the sentinels?",a="Ilthalaine acts as a general caretaker and representative of the Kaldorei in Shadowglen. While deeply attuned to nature and the druidic ethos of harmony, he works on behalf of all Darnassian leadership to guide novices of every discipline.",al={"is he a druid","what faction is ilthalaine"},it="side"},{q="Why is Ilthalaine in Shadowglen?",a="Ilthalaine stands watch in Shadowglen to welcome nascent night elf defenders and preserve the delicate equilibrium of Teldrassil's sacred nursery. As local wildlife grows restless and signs of corruption seep into the boughs, he remains stationed near Aldrassil to guide new arrivals and direct early efforts toward healing and protecting the Great Tree.",al={"why is ilthalaine here","ilthalaine shadowglen purpose","why is ilthalaine in teldrassil"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Ilthalaine is the first mentor every young night elf encounters, offering foundational wisdom about stewardship and the sacred balance of their newfound home on Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="For budding druids, Ilthalaine's teachings on culling and natural equilibrium provide their very first practical lessons in Cenarion principles.",["faction:Alliance"]="He represents the calm, enduring vigilance of the Kaldorei, welcoming new champions into the service of Darnassus and the broader Alliance."},kw={"aldrassil","balance of nature","ilthalaine","kaldorei","quest giver","shadowglen","sigil","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","quest:456","topic:night-elf","quest:3116","quest:3117","quest:3118","quest:3120"},src={"Ilthalaine"}}
E["npc:innkeeper-keldamyr"] = {t="npc",n="Innkeeper Keldamyr",z="teldrassil",s="Innkeeper Keldamyr manages the hearth and lodgings of the central inn in Dolanaar, Teldrassil. He offers food, drink, and a resting place for young night elves venturing forth from Shadowglen into the wider boughs of the World Tree.",h="Innkeeper Keldamyr manages the hearth and lodgings of the central inn in Dolanaar, Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Hearth of Dolanaar",b="Dolanaar is the primary village newcomers reach after departing the sheltered glade of Aldrassil. Innkeeper Keldamyr maintains the community's central haven, providing bread, spring water, and soft beds beneath the canopy of Teldrassil. Travelers, sentinels, and young novices bound for Darnassus frequently pause at his counter to rest their spirits, secure their hearthstones, and stock rations for the journey through the boughs.",sp=0},{t="Town Deliveries",b="Running an inn high within the branches requires steady supply lines from nearby settlements and tradesfolk. Local couriers often find themselves directed straight to Keldamyr's desk to drop off goods, linking him directly into the daily trade and logistics keeping the settlement of Dolanaar running smoothly.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Innkeeper Keldamyr?",a="Keldamyr is located inside the main inn building at the heart of Dolanaar, the first major settlement south of Shadowglen on the boughs of Teldrassil.",al={"keldamyr location","where is keldamyr","dolanaar innkeeper location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services does Innkeeper Keldamyr offer?",a="He serves as the local innkeeper, meaning you can bind your Hearthstone to his hearth, purchase basic provisions such as water, milk, juice, and bread, or log out rested beneath his roof.",al={"keldamyr wares","what does keldamyr sell","dolanaar inn food"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What quests involve Innkeeper Keldamyr?",a="He is the recipient of the local courier task 'Dolanaar Delivery,' receiving parcels meant for the upkeep and supply of the settlement's inn.",al={"keldamyr quests","dolanaar delivery turn in"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who is Innkeeper Keldamyr?",a="Innkeeper Keldamyr is a night elf host who manages the inn in Dolanaar. As travelers journey between the shaded glades of Shadowglen and the wider reaches of Teldrassil, Keldamyr provides a quiet hearth, refreshing drink, and provisions for weary adventurers venturing through the great boughs.",al={"who is keldamyr","innkeeper keldamyr lore"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Innkeeper Keldamyr on?",a="Innkeeper Keldamyr is loyal to Darnassus and the Alliance. He serves the night elven community of Dolanaar, opening his doors to fellow elves and visiting Alliance allies seeking rest beneath Teldrassil's canopy.",al={"keldamyr faction","is keldamyr alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Innkeeper Keldamyr want?",a="Keldamyr aims to keep Dolanaar's inn well-stocked and welcoming. He attends to incoming supplies, coordinates local deliveries, and ensures every passing traveler has food, water, and a safe place to bind their hearthstone before setting out into the wilds.",al={"keldamyr goals","what does keldamyr want"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Innkeeper Keldamyr here in Dolanaar?",a="Dolanaar is the primary crossroads and settlement for young night elves leaving their training in Shadowglen. Keldamyr maintains the village inn right along the road to offer shelter and sustenance at this crucial juncture on Teldrassil.",al={"why is keldamyr here","keldamyr dolanaar"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves freshly setting out from the training grounds of Shadowglen, Keldamyr's inn is usually the very first home away from home where they bind their hearthstones."},kw={"dolanaar","hearthstone","inn","innkeeper","keldamyr","night elf","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:2159","topic:night-elf"},src={"Innkeeper Keldamyr"}}
E["npc:iverron"] = {t="npc",n="Iverron",z="teldrassil",s="Iverron is a young night elf found in Shadowglen, the sheltered starting bough of Teldrassil. Stricken by the venom of the woodland's increasingly agitated arachnids, his plight serves as an early warning of the growing corruption within the World Tree.",h="Iverron is a young night elf found in Shadowglen, the sheltered starting bough of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Bitter Bite",b="While wandering through the quiet canopies of Shadowglen, Iverron ran afoul of the webwood spiders nesting in the vale. Succumbing quickly to their toxic bite, the young elf was left incapacitated, unable to return to safety on his own. His helpless condition highlights the sudden aggression sweeping through creatures that once shared the glade in peace.",sp=0},{t="Desperate Remedies",b="Iverron's survival falls upon the quick thinking of his companions and local healers, who require potent woodland ingredients—such as hyacinth mushrooms, moonpetal lilies and webwood ichor—to brew an antidote. His brush with death is a sober reminder to all young kaldorei in Shadowglen that the boughs of Teldrassil are far from unblemished sanctuary.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Iverron?",a="Iverron is a young night elf dwelling in Shadowglen within Teldrassil. During his travels through the woodland, he fell victim to the poisonous fauna haunting the boughs and required urgent aid to survive.",al={"iverron lore","who is iverron","iverron night elf"},it="identity"},{q="What poisoned Iverron?",a="He was bitten by the aggressive webwood spiders that inhabit the thickets of Shadowglen, suffering from a debilitating venom that standard rest could not cure.",al={"why is iverron sick","what bit iverron","iverron poison"},it="threat"},{q="How is Iverron cured?",a="He is cured through a concoction made of local Teldrassil plant matter, including hyacinth mushrooms and moonpetal lilies, mixed with webwood ichor from the spiders to create a targeted antidote.",al={"cure iverron","iverron antidote","saving iverron"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Where can Iverron be found?",a="He is located in Shadowglen, the secluded starting glade in the crown of Teldrassil where novice night elves begin their training.",al={"iverron location","where is iverron","find iverron"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is helping Iverron?",a="Iverron sends adventurers to his friend Dirania Silvershine, who gathers the ingredients for an antidote and sends it back to him before it loses its potency.",al={"who saves iverron","iverron friends","dentaria silverglade iverron"},it="allies"},{q="Why are the spiders in Shadowglen so hostile?",a="The sudden aggression of Shadowglen's spiders is part of an unnatural malady creeping into Teldrassil, warping normally reclusive beasts into violent predators.",al={"why spiders attack","teldrassil spider corruption"},it="conflict"},{q="Whose side is Iverron on?",a="Iverron is an ordinary night elf loyal to his people and the Alliance. He lives peacefully within the sheltered boughs of Shadowglen on Teldrassil, relying on the aid of fellow kaldorei like his close friend Dirania Silvershine to look after him when misadventure strikes.",al={"iverron faction","is iverron alliance","who does iverron serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Iverron want?",a="Right now, Iverron simply wants to survive. Struck down by deadly spider venom while venturing through Shadowglen, he is incapacitated and desperately needs a potent counter-venom before the poison claims his life.",al={"iverron goal","what does iverron need","iverron motive"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Iverron in Shadowglen?",a="Iverron resides in Shadowglen, the sheltered starting vale of Teldrassil. He ventured into the surrounding woods, only to run afoul of the grove's aggressive webwood spiders. Overcome by their venom, he collapsed and now lies stricken on the forest floor.",al={"why is iverron here","iverron shadowglen reason","what happened to iverron"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Iverron tied to?",a="Iverron is close friends with Dirania Silvershine, a sentinel stationed at Aldrassil. When he fell gravely ill to spider venom, Dirania immediately sought help from passing adventurers and druids to brew an antidote and save his life.",al={"iverron connections","who are iverrons friends","iverron dirania"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For fledgling night elves taking their first steps outside Aldrassil, Iverron's misfortune is an early lesson in how quickly the wilds of Teldrassil are falling into imbalance.",["class:Druid"]="Druids studying in Shadowglen view Iverron's poisoning as a symptom of a deeper affliction gripping nature, requiring remedies forged directly from the flora and fauna of the glade.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Iverron's survival depends on the prompt gathering of local Shadowglen flora, emphasizing the critical value of herbal knowledge in preserving life."},kw={"antidote","dentaria","iverron","kaldorei","shadowglen","spider","teldrassil","venom"},rel={"quest:3521","quest:3519","quest:4495","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","npc:tarindrella"},src={"Iverron"}}
E["npc:jocaste"] = {t="npc",n="Jocaste",z="teldrassil",s="Jocaste is a night elf hunter trainer residing within the verdant Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus. Working alongside the Cenarion Circle, she mentors young night elf marksmen and beastmasters who arrive from the wilds of Teldrassil.",h="Jocaste is a night elf hunter trainer residing within the verdant Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus.",sec={{t="A Mentor in the Enclave",b="Stationed among the tranquil groves of the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus, Jocaste serves as an instructor for night elf hunters. When fledgling trackers finish their initial training in Shadowglen and venture into the capital city, Jocaste guides their transition into seasoned survivalists. She teaches the arts of marksmanship, wilderness survival, and the sacred bond between a hunter and the wild beasts of Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Jocaste?",a="Jocaste is a night elf hunter trainer located within the Cenarion Enclave in the capital city of Darnassus, offering instruction and guidance to practitioners of the hunt.",al={"jocaste lore","who is jocaste","jocaste darnassus"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Jocaste?",a="She can be found among the trees and pavilions of the Cenarion Enclave, in the northwest district of Darnassus on the boughs of Teldrassil.",al={"jocaste location","where is jocaste","jocaste spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does she play for young hunters?",a="Hunters directed to Darnassus seek her out to advance their discipline through tasks like The Hunter's Path and learn how to properly train and master wild beasts.",al={"jocaste quests","the hunter's path jocaste","training the beast"},it="purpose"},{q="Is Jocaste affiliated with the Cenarion Circle?",a="Yes. While training hunters rather than druids, she operates within the Cenarion Enclave and explicitly welcomes visiting hunters into the presence of the Cenarion Circle.",al={"is jocaste cenarion circle","jocaste faction"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Jocaste on?",a="Jocaste stands firmly with Darnassus, the Night Elves, and the wider Alliance. Stationed among the Cenarion Circle in their enclave, she shares their dedication to safeguarding nature and guiding those who live in harmony with the wild.",al={"jocaste faction","who does jocaste serve","jocaste allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Jocaste want?",a="Jocaste is dedicated to passing on the traditions of the hunt. She seeks to nurture aspiring hunters in Darnassus, ensuring they learn the discipline, marksmanship, and spiritual bond required to tame and command beasts in service to nature and their people.",al={"jocaste motive","what is jocastes goal","jocaste purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Jocaste here in Darnassus?",a="Jocaste resides in the Cenarion Enclave to offer her wisdom and training to hunters visiting the capital. Amid the ancient trees of Teldrassil, she provides vital instruction to both novice scouts and seasoned wilderness stalkers.",al={"why is jocaste in darnassus","why is jocaste in cenarion enclave"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="For night elf hunters stepping into Darnassus for the first time, Jocaste is a key teacher who refines your combat techniques and helps solidify the bond with your animal companions.",["race:NightElf"]="Rooted in the Cenarion Enclave, Jocaste reflects the close harmony between night elf wayfarers, the wild beasts of Teldrassil, and the teachings of the Cenarion Circle."},kw={"cenarion enclave","darnassus","hunter trainer","jocaste","night elf hunter","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:darnassus","subzone:cenarion-enclave","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:night-elf","zone:teldrassil","quest:6065","quest:6081"},src={"Jocaste"}}
E["npc:laurna-morninglight"] = {t="npc",n="Laurna Morninglight",z="teldrassil",s="Laurna Morninglight is a night elf priest trainer residing in the tranquil settlement of Dolanaar within Teldrassil. Devoted to the Sisterhood of Elune, she guides budding acolytes emerging from Shadowglen in the spiritual rites and healing graces of the Moon Goddess. Her teachings prepare young night elf priests for the growing threats encroaching on the boughs of the World Tree.",h="Laurna Morninglight is a night elf priest trainer residing in the tranquil settlement of Dolanaar within...",sec={{t="A Guide in Dolanaar",b="Situated amidst the boughs of Dolanaar, Laurna Morninglight serves as one of the primary mentors for young priests who have completed their initial rites in Shadowglen. As new initiates step out into the broader reaches of Teldrassil, she instructs them on expanding their communion with Elune, balancing the light of healing with defensive rites necessary to survive an increasingly hostile wild.",sp=0},{t="Devotion to the Moon Goddess",b="Priestcraft among the kaldorei is deeply intertwined with the worship of Elune rather than the abstract Holy Light revered by humans and dwarves. Laurna tasks her students with spiritual labors such as receiving sacred robes and healing a wounded Sentinel. Through these traditions, acolytes learn that their powers are direct gifts of the Mother Moon, meant to preserve and mend the kaldorei people.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Laurna Morninglight?",a="Laurna Morninglight is stationed in the village of Dolanaar, located in the central reaches of Teldrassil just down the road from Shadowglen.",al={"laurna location","where is laurna","dolanaar priest trainer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Laurna Morninglight do?",a="She is a priest trainer for night elf characters. She teaches new spells, refines ranks of known abilities, and provides early guidance through class-specific rites.",al={"what does she do","laurna role","laurna priest trainer"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What kind of quests does she offer?",a="She initiates class quests for fledgling priests, directing them to aid wounded allies and seek Elune's divine favor through ceremonial vestments and prayers.",al={"laurna quests","priest quests dolanaar"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Does she train other races?",a="While she is culturally rooted in the Sisterhood of Elune, priest trainers in the Alliance will instruct any allied priest who comes seeking spiritual discipline.",al={"can humans train here","priest trainer any race"},gp=true},{q="Is she affiliated with the Temple of the Moon?",a="Yes, as a kaldorei priestess, her vows and magic are dedicated entirely to the Goddess Elune and the broader traditions overseen by the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",al={"is she sisterhood of elune","laurna temple of the moon"},it="ties"},{q="Does she share a family name with other night elves?",a="No relatives of Laurna are known among the kaldorei of Teldrassil.",al={"morninglight family","laurna relatives"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Laurna Morninglight?",a="Laurna Morninglight is a night elf priestess and mentor residing in the village of Dolanaar. Devoted to the worship of Elune, she guides young acolytes and initiates stepping out into Teldrassil, teaching them to channel the goddess's soothing radiance and call upon divine protection.",al={"who is laurna morninglight","who is laurna","laurna morninglight lore"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Laurna Morninglight on?",a="She is steadfastly loyal to the night elves of Darnassus, the Sisterhood of Elune, and the Alliance. As an acolyte of the moon goddess, her heart lies with protecting her people and guiding the spiritual well-being of the Kaldorei upon Teldrassil.",al={"laurna morninglight faction","who does laurna morninglight serve","laurna morninglight alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Laurna Morninglight want?",a="Her primary devotion is to nurture novice priests in the ways of Elune. She wants promising acolytes to cultivate their divine connection, master healing prayers, and wield sacred garments to aid their kin across the boughs of Teldrassil.",al={"laurna morninglight motive","what does laurna morninglight do"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Laurna Morninglight here in Dolanaar?",a="Dolanaar is the primary crossroads and gathering point for young adventurers leaving the secluded glades of Shadowglen. Laurna is stationed here to ensure that developing priests receive proper guidance, instruction, and sacred rites as they take on greater duties in Teldrassil.",al={"why is laurna in dolanaar","why is laurna morninglight here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Priest"]="For night elf priests arriving from Shadowglen, Laurna Morninglight is your first major mentor outside the starting vale, teaching foundational spells and guiding your early devotion to Elune.",["race:NightElf"]="Laurna embodies the traditional kaldorei devotion to the Moon Goddess, reminding adventurers that priestcraft in Teldrassil draws from Elune rather than the Holy Light."},kw={"dolanaar","elune","kaldorei","laurna","morninglight","priest trainer","sisterhood of elune","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune","topic:night-elf","quest:5621","quest:5622","quest:5634","quest:5628"},src={"Laurna Morninglight"}}
E["npc:mardant-strongoak"] = {t="npc",n="Mardant Strongoak",z="teldrassil",s="Mardant Strongoak is a night elf druid trainer residing in Aldrassil in the heart of Teldrassil. He guides fledgling druids in communing with the spirits of nature and introduces them to the mysteries of the Emerald Dream.",h="Mardant Strongoak is a night elf druid trainer residing in Aldrassil in the heart of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Instructor of the Wilds",b="Within the boughs of Aldrassil, young night elves who feel the call of the wild turn to Mardant Strongoak. His primary task is teaching novitiates how to open their senses to nature spirits, interpret their murmurs, and channel rejuvenating magics. For those taking their initial steps as protectors of the wild, he is often the first master to unveil the vast complexities and ancient perils of the Emerald Dream.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mardant Strongoak?",a="Mardant Strongoak is a night elf druid trainer stationed in Shadowglen within Aldrassil. He mentors newly awakened druids on Teldrassil in the basic arts of communion and spellcraft.",al={"mardant strongoak lore","who is mardant","mardant aldrassil"},it="identity"},{q="What does he teach new druids?",a="He teaches novitiates how to decipher the messages of wild spirits, cast rudimentary spells like Moonfire and healing arts, and grasp the nature of the Emerald Dream.",al={"what does mardant teach","mardant abilities","druid trainer shadowglen"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can I find Mardant Strongoak?",a="He is located inside or near Aldrassil in Shadowglen, the starting vale for night elf adventurers on Teldrassil.",al={"mardant location","where is mardant strongoak"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Verdant Sigil?",a="The Verdant Sigil is an instructional token presented to fledgling night elf druids in Shadowglen, directing them to seek out Mardant Strongoak for their early training.",al={"verdant sigil quest","sigil for mardant"},it="item"},{q="Whose side is Mardant Strongoak on?",a="Mardant Strongoak is devoted to the night elves, the Alliance, and the sacred tenets of the Cenarion Circle. He stands firmly within Shadowglen to safeguard the fledgling World Tree and ensure the traditions of the kaldorei druids endure in these uncertain times.",al={"mardant strongoak faction","who does mardant serve","is mardant alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Mardant Strongoak want?",a="Mardant wants young night elf initiates to deepen their communion with nature. He seeks to guide new druids through their initial trials, helping them decipher the whisperings of the spirits and navigate the profound mysteries and perils of the Emerald Dream.",al={"what does mardant want","mardant strongoak goals","what is mardant's goal"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Mardant Strongoak here?",a="Stationed within the hollow boughs of Aldrassil, Mardant serves as a mentor for newly awakened druids taking their first steps in Teldrassil. He remains in Shadowglen to watch over novices, instruct them in their innate powers, and direct them toward those in need of aid across the glade.",al={"why is mardant in aldrassil","why is mardant strongoak here","mardant strongoak location reason"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Mardant Strongoak tied to?",a="Mardant is closely tied to the Cenarion Circle and his fellow teachers in Aldrassil, such as the priestesses of Elune and the sentinels guarding the sanctuary. Together, they guide and nurture the young defenders of the night elves.",al={"mardant strongoak allies","who is mardant affiliated with","mardant connections"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For young night elf druids, Mardant Strongoak is the first bridge between mundane existence and the sacred duties of the Cenarion circle.",["race:NightElf"]="Stationed at the core of Aldrassil, Mardant exemplifies the kaldorei devotion to harmonizing with Teldrassil's burgeoning ecosystem."},kw={"aldrassil","druid","emerald dream","mardant","shadowglen","strongoak","teldrassil","trainer"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream","topic:night-elf","quest:3120"},src={"Mardant Strongoak"}}
E["npc:melithar-staghelm"] = {t="npc",n="Melithar Staghelm",z="teldrassil",s="Melithar Staghelm is a night elf stationed just outside Aldrassil in Shadowglen, Teldrassil's starting glade. He assists young night elf adventurers as they embark on their early training, sending them to nearby instructors and addressing minor local disturbances. While he shares the prominent Staghelm surname with Archdruid Fandral Staghelm, his exact connection to the ruling druid remains unconfirmed.",h="Melithar Staghelm is a night elf stationed just outside Aldrassil in Shadowglen, Teldrassil's starting glade.",sec={{t="A Guide at Aldrassil",b="Standing directly outside the entrance to the great bough of Aldrassil, Melithar serves as an early point of contact for night elves emerging into the world. He directs newly awakened youth bearing various sigils to their respective class trainers, ensuring they receive proper tutelage in the martial and mystical arts. Beyond administrative guidance, Melithar watches over the immediate grounds of Shadowglen, enlisting help to deal with mischievous local wildlife and minor impish intrusions that threaten the sanctuary's peace.",sp=0},{t="The Staghelm Name",b="Bearing the surname Staghelm inevitably draws attention, as Archdruid Fandral Staghelm currently leads the Cenarion Circle in Darnassus following Malfurion Stormrage's disappearance into the Emerald Dream. However, Melithar makes no outward boast of grand heritage, nor does he actively speak of his lineage. Whether he is a distant kinsman of the Archdruid's venerable family line or merely shares an ancient Kaldorei family name, Melithar remains content fulfilling humble duties at the roots of Aldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Melithar Staghelm?",a="Melithar Staghelm is a night elf quest giver stationed on the pathway outside the bough of Aldrassil in Shadowglen. He helps newly arrived night elf adventurers get their bearings and directs them toward their mentors.",al={"melithar","who is melithar","melithar shadowglen"},it="identity"},{q="Is Melithar related to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm?",a="Their exact kinship is unknown. While they share the Staghelm name, Melithar never comments on being related to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm or his late son Valstann. It remains unclear whether he is a distant relative or simply shares a common Kaldorei surname.",al={"fandral relative","fandral brother","staghelm family"},it="ties"},{q="What role does Melithar play for new adventurers?",a="Novice night elves are directed to Melithar with their introductory sigils. Melithar receives these tokens and points each novice to the proper trainer nestled inside Aldrassil to begin their formal class education.",al={"melithar quests","sigil quests","what does melithar do"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can I find Melithar Staghelm?",a="He stands right on the wooden rampway outside the entrance of Aldrassil, in the center of Shadowglen on Teldrassil.",al={"melithar location","where is melithar","find melithar staghelm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Melithar Staghelm on?",a="Melithar stands with the night elves of Darnassus and the Alliance. Stationed at Shadowglen right outside Aldrassil, he assists young night elf defenders and recruits as they take their first steps in safeguarding the World Tree.",al={"melithar faction","who does melithar serve","melithar allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Melithar Staghelm want?",a="Melithar works to protect Shadowglen and cleanse Teldrassil of burgeoning threats. He asks incoming adventurers to deal with nearby pests and troublesome wildlife, as well as recovering lost possessions stolen by local grells and woodland interlopers.",al={"melithar goal","what is melithar doing","melithar purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Melithar Staghelm here?",a="Melithar is stationed just outside Aldrassil in Shadowglen to watch over the bough and direct nascent night elf adventurers. He provides early guidance, tasking new defenders with curbing local corruption and maintaining harmony in Teldrassil's sacred nursery.",al={"why is melithar in shadowglen","melithar location reason"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves embarking on their journey in Shadowglen, Melithar is one of the very first faces encountered after departing Aldrassil's shelter."},kw={"aldrassil","melithar","shadowglen","sigils","staghelm","teldrassil","trainer"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil","npc:fandral-staghelm","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","quest:458","quest:3116","quest:3117","quest:3118"},src={"Melithar Staghelm"}}
E["npc:moon-priestess-amara"] = {t="npc",n="Moon Priestess Amara",z="teldrassil",s="Moon Priestess Amara is a night elf priestess stationed along the main road west of Dolanaar in Teldrassil. Flanked by loyal huntress guards, she keeps watch over the woodland pathways connecting the heart of the bough to the capital city of Darnassus.",h="Moon Priestess Amara is a night elf priestess stationed along the main road west of Dolanaar in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Boughways",b="Stationed at a quiet wayside post west of Dolanaar, Moon Priestess Amara represents both the spiritual authority of the Sisterhood of Elune and the practical vigilance required to keep Teldrassil's roadways secure. She travels and watches with two huntress companions, Nhemai and Yaeliura. To travelers journeying westward, Amara acts as a guiding hand, directing adventurers along the road toward Darnassus and tasking those with burdened spirits to seek out paths of redemption.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Moon Priestess Amara?",a="Moon Priestess Amara, also known in sentinel duties as Amara Nightwalker, is a priestess of the Sisterhood of Elune stationed on the road between Dolanaar and Darnassus in Teldrassil. She oversees the security and spiritual health of travelers heading through the bough.",al={"who is amara","priestess amara","sentinel amara nightwalker"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Moon Priestess Amara?",a="She is located along the paved highway just west of Dolanaar in Teldrassil, standing watch beside two sentinel huntresses.",al={"where is amara","amara location","priestess amara map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who are the huntresses standing with her?",a="She is guarded and accompanied by Huntress Nhemai and Huntress Yaeliura, two night elf sentinels who assist in protecting the thoroughfare from beasts and hostile corruption.",al={"amara companions","nhemai and yaeliura","amara guards"},it="allies"},{q="Whose side is Moon Priestess Amara on?",a="Moon Priestess Amara serves the Priesthood of Elune and the Alliance, watching over the sacred boughs of Teldrassil. Alongside her Sentinel companions, she stands dedicated to guiding travelers and defending the kaldorei heartland from the corruption that threatens its tranquil forests.",al={"amara faction","amara allegiance","who does amara serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Moon Priestess Amara stationed here?",a="Amara is stationed along the main road west of Dolanaar to safeguard travelers making the journey toward Darnassus. Teldrassil's pathways are increasingly besieged by corrupted beasts and lurking timberlings, making her presence vital in keeping the woodland paths secure.",al={"why is amara here","amara location purpose","why is moon priestess amara on the road"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="What does Moon Priestess Amara want?",a="She seeks capable adventurers to help secure the road to the capital city of Darnassus. Amara tasks travelers with dispatching the foul gnarlpine fulborgs and vicious forest creatures that harass those who journey westward beneath the boughs of the World Tree.",al={"what does amara need","amara quest motive","why does amara send you on quests"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a member of the Sisterhood of Elune, Priestess Amara embodies the night elven devotion to the Moon Goddess, serving as a pastoral and spiritual guide to young acolytes venturing out from Shadowglen.",["race:NightElf"]="Amara marks an important milestone on your journey away from Dolanaar, offering guidance and tasks that lead into the great city of Darnassus."},kw={"amara nightwalker","dolanaar","elanaria","moon priestess amara","nhemai","teldrassil","the road to darnassus","yaeliura"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil","npc:elanaria","quest:487","quest:489","topic:night-elf"},src={"Moon Priestess Amara"}}
E["npc:oben-rageclaw"] = {t="npc",n="Oben Rageclaw",z="teldrassil",s="Oben Rageclaw is the restless spirit of a night elf druid haunting the corrupted depths of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den in Teldrassil. While his spirit wanders trapped in the barrow den, his slumbering physical form has fallen under the sway of foul furbolg magic.",h="Oben Rageclaw is the restless spirit of a night elf druid haunting the corrupted depths of the Ban'ethil...",sec={{t="A Slumber Desecrated",b="Like many Druids of the Claw, Oben Rageclaw retreated into the subterranean sanctum of Ban'ethil Barrow Den to commune with nature and wander the Emerald Dream. However, when the native Gnarlpine furbolgs fell to corruption and overran the barrows, Oben was caught entirely defenseless in his trance. Rather than simply slaying him, the corrupted Gnarlpine shaman used dark rituals to seize control of his comatose mortal frame, leaving his displaced spirit lingering as an anguished ghost unable to pass on or wake.",sp=0},{t="Severing the Vessel",b="Unable to reclaim his own flesh from the shaman's enthrallment, Oben relies on travelers navigating the dangerous tunnels to end his torment. Only by locating and destroying his puppeted physical body can his mortal ties be severed. Once his hijacked vessel is slain, Oben's tortured ghost is finally released from the subterranean gloom to find eternal rest within the Emerald Dream.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Oben Rageclaw?",a="Oben Rageclaw is a night elf Druid of the Claw whose ghost haunts Ban'ethil Barrow Den in Teldrassil after being severed from his physical body by corrupted furbolgs.",al={"who is oben","oben rageclaw lore","spirit in barrow den"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Oben Rageclaw a ghost?",a="While Oben slept in a deep druidic trance communing with the Emerald Dream, Gnarlpine furbolg shamans infiltrated the den and cast foul magic on his body, taking control of it and trapping his spirit outside as an apparition.",al={"why is oben dead","how did oben die","why is oben a ghost"},it="why_here"},{q="Where is Oben's physical body?",a="His physical body lies deeper within the winding corridors of Ban'ethil Barrow Den, guarded and manipulated by the Gnarlpine shamans who corrupted the den.",al={"find oben body","where is oben body","sleeping druid location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after Oben's body is destroyed?",a="Destroying his puppeted body breaks the Gnarlpine shamans' dark hold over him, allowing his spirit to peacefully depart Teldrassil and rest forever in the Emerald Dream.",al={"oben fate","what happens to oben spirit","saving oben"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Oben Rageclaw on?",a="Oben Rageclaw is aligned with the night elves and the Cenarion Circle. Though a corrupted Gnarlpine shaman currently manipulates his slumbering physical form deep within the barrows, Oben's true spirit remains faithful to his people and seeks aid from passing adventurers to end his torment.",al={"is oben rageclaw friendly","oben rageclaw faction","who does oben serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Oben Rageclaw want?",a="Oben desires release from the unnatural hold binding his spirit to Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Because foul Gnarlpine magic has seized control of his physical body, he asks you to destroy his corrupted form so that his restless spirit may finally find peace in the Emerald Dream.",al={"what does oben want","oben rageclaw goal","oben rageclaw motive"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Oben's fate is a harrowing reminder of the vulnerability of druids during their trance-like communion with the Emerald Dream when sacred barrow dens are left undefended.",["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of Oben Rageclaw by the Gnarlpine furbolgs illustrates just how deeply corruption has tainted Teldrassil's native denizens and sacred sanctuaries."},kw={"ban'ethil barrow den","druid of the claw","emerald dream","gnarlpine","oben rageclaw","teldrassil","the sleeping druid"},rel={"subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","quest:2541","quest:2561","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream","topic:night-elf"},src={"Oben Rageclaw"}}
E["npc:orenthil-whisperwind"] = {t="npc",n="Orenthil Whisperwind",z="teldrassil",s="Orenthil Whisperwind is a night elf resident of Teldrassil, commonly encountered resting under the boughs of Dolanaar. He serves as an welcoming liaison for rare travelers, presenting gifts sent across the world to newly arrived champions. Given his prominent surname, many wonder whether he shares kinship with High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind herself.",h="Orenthil Whisperwind is a night elf resident of Teldrassil, commonly encountered resting under the boughs of...",sec={{t="A Friendly Face in Teldrassil",b="Standing amidst the shaded terraces of Dolanaar, Orenthil Whisperwind offers a quiet welcome to fledgling adventurers emerging from Shadowglen. While he remains modest and keeps mostly to himself beneath the canopy of the World Tree, he is notably tasked with greeting select travelers and delivering special companion creatures to those carrying rare tokens from abroad.",sp=0},{t="The Whisperwind Line",b="Bearing the name Whisperwind immediately invites speculation in night elven lands. While Orenthil has never made grand claims of nobility or spiritual authority, his surname suggests potential ties to High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind. Whether he belongs to an extended branch of her ancestral line or merely shares an ancient Kaldorei family name remains a point of quiet curiosity among passing travelers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Orenthil Whisperwind?",a="He is a night elf found in Dolanaar on Teldrassil. He serves as a welcoming figure for adventurers setting out into the boughs of the World Tree.",al={"orenthil","orenthil whisperwind info","who is this elf"},it="identity"},{q="Is Orenthil related to Tyrande Whisperwind?",a="His surname suggests he may be part of the extended family or ancestral lineage of High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind, though he does not flaunt high station or claim direct power in Darnassus.",al={"orenthil tyrande brother","tyrande relative","is he related to tyrande"},it="ties"},{q="Where can I find Orenthil Whisperwind?",a="Orenthil resides in Dolanaar, the first major settlement night elf adventurers encounter after departing Shadowglen in central Teldrassil.",al={"orenthil location","where is orenthil","orenthil map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quest does Orenthil offer?",a="He offers the quest 'Welcome!', which allows travelers bearing special collector tokens to claim an exotic companion pet to accompany them on their journeys.",al={"orenthil quest","welcome quest dolanaar","collector quest teldrassil"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Orenthil Whisperwind on?",a="Orenthil stands firmly with the night elves of Darnassus and the greater Alliance. Found dwelling among his kin on the boughs of Teldrassil, he greets new travelers arriving to assist his people.",al={"orenthil whisperwind faction","is orenthil alliance","who does orenthil serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Orenthil Whisperwind here?",a="Stationed in Teldrassil, Orenthil serves as a welcoming presence to fledgling adventurers making their way through the great World Tree, offering greetings and rare companions to those recognized under special circumstances.",al={"orenthil whisperwind purpose","why is orenthil in dolanaar","what is orenthil doing"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Meeting a Kaldorei who shares the name of High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind in humble Dolanaar serves as an early reminder of the sprawling, ancient history behind Kalimdor's elven bloodlines."},kw={"collector","dolanaar","orenthil","shadowglen","teldrassil","welcome","whisperwind"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:5805","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","subzone:shadowglen","topic:night-elf"},src={"Orenthil Whisperwind"}}
E["npc:saelienne"] = {t="npc",n="Saelienne",z="teldrassil",s="Innkeeper Saelienne manages the inn situated on the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus. She provides weary travelers and local artisans with food, drink, and a peaceful hearthstone retreat in the heart of the night elven capital.",h="Innkeeper Saelienne manages the inn situated on the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus.",sec={{t="Hospitality on the Terrace",b="Situated amidst the bustling workshops and trade stalls of the Craftsmen's Terrace, Innkeeper Saelienne offers a calm respite for both residents and visitors to Darnassus. As a keeper of the hearth, she caters to adventurers arriving from across Kalimdor and beyond, serving staple night elven refreshments alongside goods brought into the city port. Her establishment serves as a primary gathering place for tradesfolk seeking rest after long hours at the forge or loom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Innkeeper Saelienne?",a="Saelienne is located on the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus, running the local inn tucked among the trade trainers and crafting shops.",al={"saelienne location","where is saelienne","darnassus innkeeper location","craftsmens terrace inn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services does Saelienne provide?",a="She acts as an innkeeper, allowing players to bind their Hearthstone to Darnassus. She also sells various food and drink items suitable for restoring health and mana.",al={"what does saelienne do","saelienne vendor","bind hearthstone darnassus"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Does Saelienne offer any seasonal tasks?",a="During the Hallow's End festivities, Saelienne participates in holiday celebrations, offering Alliance adventurers the quest Dancing for Marzipan in exchange for holiday treats.",al={"saelienne quests","hallows end saelienne","dancing for marzipan"},gp=true},{q="Who is Saelienne?",a="Saelienne is a night elf innkeeper residing in the Craftsmen's Terrace within Darnassus. She manages hospitality for travelers and locals alike, offering food, refreshing drink, and a restful place to bind your hearthstone beneath the boughs of Teldrassil.",al={"who is saelienne","saelienne identity","innkeeper saelienne"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Saelienne on?",a="She stands firmly with Darnassus and the greater Alliance. As an innkeeper in the heart of the night elven capital, she welcomes all allied adventurers who arrive on the world tree in need of respite and provisions.",al={"saelienne faction","is saelienne alliance","saelienne loyalty"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Saelienne want?",a="Saelienne desires nothing more than to tend her inn and ensure that travelers visiting the Craftsmen's Terrace find shelter, nourishment, and a comfortable bed. Beyond providing hospitality and trade, she stays clear of politics and conflict.",al={"what does saelienne want","saelienne motive","saelienne goals"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Saelienne in Darnassus?",a="She makes her living running the inn in the Craftsmen's Terrace, tending to the artisans, merchants, and voyagers passing through the district. Her post places her right in the bustling heart of Teldrassil's daily commerce.",al={"why is saelienne here","saelienne craftsmen terrace","why is saelienne in darnassus"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elf adventurers returning from the wild reaches of Teldrassil, Saelienne's inn offers a familiar hearth among the artisans of Darnassus.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance envoys and tradesfolk traveling to the remote canopy of Teldrassil rely on Saelienne for food, drink, and a warm hearthstone sanctuary."},kw={"craftsmen's terrace","darnassus","hallow's end","hearthstone","innkeeper","saelienne","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:darnassus","subzone:craftsmen-s-terrace","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","quest:8357","topic:alliance"},src={"Saelienne"}}
E["npc:sentinel-arynia-cloudsbreak"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak",z="teldrassil",s="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak is a night elf guardian stationed within the serene groves of the Oracle Glade on Teldrassil. Charged with monitoring the sacred balance of the northern boughs, she keeps a wary watch over the glade's enchanted waters and woodland wildlife.",h="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak is a night elf guardian stationed within the serene groves of the Oracle Glade on...",sec={{t="Watcher of the Oracle Glade",b="Arynia Cloudsbreak serves the Sentinel army in one of the most secluded and mystical reaches of Teldrassil: the Oracle Glade. Amid ancient trees and ethereal springs, she carries out her watch far from the bustling avenues of Darnassus, ensuring the sanctity of the wilderness remains undisturbed.",sp=0},{t="Trouble in the Glade",b="Despite Teldrassil's sacred birth, creeping disharmony has begun to unsettle its creatures. Arynia relies on passing adventurers and young night elves to investigate local disruptions, such as strange behaviors among the glade's wildlife and mystical phenomena around the enchanted springs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak?",a="She is a night elf Sentinel standing guard in the Oracle Glade, deep in northern Teldrassil. She looks after the mystical glade and recruits travelers to assist in preserving its natural harmony.",al={"arynia cloudsbreak","who is arynia","sentinel arynia"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Arynia Cloudsbreak be found?",a="Arynia is stationed out in the open at the Oracle Glade, located in the northwestern reaches of Teldrassil, north of Dolanaar.",al={"arynia location","where is arynia","arynia cloudsbreak map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What duties does she perform in the Sentinels?",a="As a Sentinel stationed in the wilderness, she patrols the outlying forest boughs, monitoring the local spirits, wildlife, and natural phenomena for any signs of corruption or imbalance.",al={"arynia role","what does arynia do"},it="purpose"},{q="Is she related to anyone else on Teldrassil?",a="She shares her surname with Mavoris Cloudsbreak, suggesting a familial bond among the night elves dwelling on the world tree.",al={"arynia family","mavoris cloudsbreak"},it="ties"},{q="What tasks does she give to adventurers?",a="She offers tasks that involve investigating the enchanted glade and tending to mysterious disturbances and wandering beasts nearby, including aiding creatures caught in distress.",al={"arynia quests","oracle glade quests"},it="wants"},{q="Why is the Oracle Glade significant to the night elves?",a="The Oracle Glade is a sacred sanctuary within Teldrassil known for its tranquil pools and spiritual reverence, overseen by druids and Sentinels seeking guidance and omen from nature.",al={"why oracle glade","oracle glade lore"},it="place"},{q="Whose side is Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak on?",a="Arynia serves the Sentinels, the renowned martial arm of the night elf people, and is steadfastly loyal to the Darnassus leadership and the greater Alliance. Stationed among the peaceful groves of Teldrassil, her duty is to protect her homeland and ensure the spiritual sanctuaries of the Kaldorei remain undisturbed by corruption or outside threats.",al={"arynia cloudsbreak faction","arynia cloudsbreak alliance","who does arynia serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak in the Oracle Glade?",a="Arynia is stationed at the Oracle Glade to watch over the tranquil northern reaches of Teldrassil. The glade holds sacred significance for the night elves, and as a Sentinel, she remains on guard to look after local wildlife and attend to any disturbances that threaten the sanctity of the enchanted woods.",al={"why is arynia cloudsbreak here","arynia cloudsbreak oracle glade","why is sentinel arynia in oracle glade"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves coming of age on Teldrassil, assisting Sentinel Cloudsbreak offers practical experience in protecting the wild balance of their new homeland.",["faction:Alliance"]="Arynia represents the vigilance of the Kaldorei Sentinels, maintaining defense over the Alliance's vital woodland stronghold in Kalimdor."},kw={"arynia cloudsbreak","enchanted glade","kaldorei","mist","night elf","oracle glade","sentinel","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:oracle-glade","zone:teldrassil","quest:937","quest:938","quest:940","topic:night-elf"},src={"Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak"}}
E["npc:shanda"] = {t="npc",n="Shanda",z="teldrassil",s="Shanda is a night elf priestess and mentor located within the hollow trunk of Aldrassil in Shadowglen. Serving the Sisterhood of Elune, she instructs novice night elf priests in the fundamental prayers, wards, and rites of the Moon Goddess. Her guidance helps fledgling acolytes balance the light of Elune with their duties in defending Teldrassil.",h="Shanda is a night elf priestess and mentor located within the hollow trunk of Aldrassil in Shadowglen.",sec={{t="Acolyte of the Moon Mother",b="Standing within the tranquil sanctuary of Aldrassil, Shanda serves as one of the first spiritual guides for young night elves dedicated to Elune. While the druids tend to the waking roots and boughs of Teldrassil, priestesses like Shanda ensure that the spiritual heart of the Kaldorei remains tethered to the White Lady. She instructs new initiates on channeling lunar grace for healing and protective wards, preparing them to face the corruption creeping into the boughs of the World Tree.",sp=0},{t="Guiding New Initiates",b="When young priests awaken to their calling in Shadowglen, they are directed to Shanda to prove their devotion and learn their first prayers. Through rites such as In Favor of Elune, she tests their resolve and provides them with blessed regalia and basic incantations. Under her tutelage, students learn that a priestess of the Kaldorei must be both a gentle hand to the wounded and a steadfast shield against the shadows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Shanda?",a="Shanda is a night elf priest trainer located inside Aldrassil, the central hollow tree settlement of Shadowglen in Teldrassil. She instructs newly awakened night elf priests in the teachings of the Sisterhood of Elune.",al={"who is this npc","shanda lore","priest trainer aldrassil"},it="identity"},{q="What role does Shanda play for new priests?",a="She introduces novice priests to basic prayers, curative spells, and protective magic gifted by Elune. She also offers early quests to equip young acolytes with their initial robes and holy sigils.",al={"priest trainer role","what does shanda teach","what does shanda do"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can I find Shanda?",a="Shanda is found on the ground level inside the hollow trunk of Aldrassil, the massive tree that serves as the starter hub in Shadowglen on Teldrassil.",al={"where is shanda","shanda location","how to find shanda"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What organization does Shanda belong to?",a="Shanda is a member of the Sisterhood of Elune, the ancient religious order of night elf priestesses that has guided Kaldorei spiritual and cultural life for thousands of years.",al={"shanda faction","sisterhood of elune","is shanda a priestess of the moon"},it="side"},{q="What does Shanda want?",a="Shanda is dedicated to preparing the next generation of night elf priests to serve the Moon Goddess and protect their people. She seeks to guide young novices in channeling the divine grace of Elune, teaching them how to mend injuries, shield their allies, and smite the growing corruption creeping into the Shadowglen.",al={"what are shanda's goals","shanda motive","what does priest trainer shanda want"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Shanda in Aldrassil?",a="As newly awakened defenders gather within the sacred haven of Aldrassil, seasoned mentors are needed to hone their raw talents. Shanda remains stationed at the foot of the great bough in the Shadowglen to watch over emerging priest novices, ensuring they learn the rites and powers of Elune before venturing deeper into Teldrassil.",al={"why is shanda here","why is shanda in shadowglen","shanda location reason"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Priest"]="For night elf priests starting their journey in Shadowglen, Shanda is the very first mentor to bestow sacred words, holy sigils, and guidance in Elune's grace.",["race:NightElf"]="Shanda represents the enduring tradition of the Sisterhood of Elune, tending to the spiritual well-being of the Kaldorei youth as they take their first steps on Teldrassil."},kw={"aldrassil","elune","night elf","priest trainer","shadowglen","shanda","sisterhood of elune","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune","topic:night-elf","quest:5622","quest:940"},src={"Shanda"}}
E["npc:syral-bladeleaf"] = {t="npc",n="Syral Bladeleaf",z="teldrassil",s="Syral Bladeleaf is a night elf resident of Dolanaar in Teldrassil who serves as a liaison for the Council of the Forest. She guides young adventurers who arrive from Shadowglen, directing them toward local caretakers, herbalists, and elders who watch over the crown's delicate boughs.",h="Syral Bladeleaf is a night elf resident of Dolanaar in Teldrassil who serves as a liaison for the Council of...",sec={{t="A Voice in Dolanaar",b="Found standing near the heart of Dolanaar, Syral Bladeleaf helps organize local affairs in the shadow of Teldrassil's canopy. Acting on behalf of the Council of the Forest, she directs newly arrived night elves to community leaders and herbalists across the village and the nearby wilderness. Through her guidance, travelers connect with the botanist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth and replenish supplies for the village elders.",sp=0},{t="Ties to the Village",b="Bearing the Bladeleaf surname, Syral shares ties with other prominent villagers in Dolanaar, including Elder Bladeleaf. Her responsibilities keep her focused on communal welfare, ensuring that medicinal elixirs reach those in need and that any disruptions in the local ecosystem receive swift attention.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Syral Bladeleaf?",a="Syral Bladeleaf is a night elf in Dolanaar who conveys directives on behalf of the Council of the Forest, helping incoming adventurers assist the surrounding woodland communities.",al={"who is syral","syral bladeleaf lore","syral dolanaar"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Syral Bladeleaf be found?",a="She is located in Dolanaar, the central settlement of Teldrassil situated just southwest of Shadowglen along the main road.",al={"syral bladeleaf location","where is syral","syral map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is she related to Elder Bladeleaf?",a="She shares her family name with Elder Bladeleaf and Hannah Bladeleaf in Dolanaar, pointing to deep family roots in the settlement.",al={"elder bladeleaf relative","syral family","bladeleaf family"},it="ties"},{q="What tasks does she assign to adventurers?",a="Syral sends travelers to assist botanist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth, helps organize delivery of herbal elixirs for the elders, and points adventurers toward tasks that aid Teldrassil's natural balance.",al={"syral bladeleaf quests","what does syral want","syral tasks"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Syral Bladeleaf on?",a="Syral serves Darnassus and the Alliance. Stationed in Dolanaar, she acts directly on behalf of the Council of the Forest, helping ensure that the local wilderness and its caretakers remain safeguarded against Teldrassil's creeping troubles.",al={"syral bladeleaf faction","who does syral bladeleaf serve","syral bladeleaf allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Syral Bladeleaf want?",a="Syral wants to see the will of the Council of the Forest carried out. She relays their directives to capable adventurers, seeking aid for nearby allies like Denalan and working to keep the growing corruption in Teldrassil under control.",al={"what does syral bladeleaf want","syral bladeleaf goals","syral bladeleaf motives"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Syral Bladeleaf in Dolanaar?",a="Syral is stationed in Dolanaar to serve as a vital liaison for the Council of the Forest. From this central settlement, she can easily recruit passing travelers and young night elves to tend to the needs of the boughs and support local caretakers.",al={"why is syral bladeleaf here","syral bladeleaf dolanaar reason","why is syral in dolanaar"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves stepping out of the secluded barrows of Shadowglen, Syral Bladeleaf is one of the first voices of Dolanaar's civic and natural leadership.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Syral works closely with local naturalists and herbal supply chains, directing travelers to assist botanical research at Lake Al'Ameth and ensure fresh elixirs reach the elders."},kw={"bladeleaf","council of the forest","denalan","dolanaar","elder bladeleaf","syral","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","npc:elder-bladeleaf","npc:denalan","quest:997","quest:1581","quest:489","topic:night-elf"},src={"Syral Bladeleaf"}}
E["npc:tallonkai-swiftroot"] = {t="npc",n="Tallonkai Swiftroot",z="teldrassil",s="Tallonkai Swiftroot is a night elf resident of Dolanaar in Teldrassil. Concerned with the emerging corruption tainting the great boughs, he enlists young adventurers to recover enchanted relics and stem the foul forces plaguing the woods.",h="Tallonkai Swiftroot is a night elf resident of Dolanaar in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Sentinel of Dolanaar",b="Dwelling in the canopy settlement of Dolanaar, Tallonkai Swiftroot keeps a watchful eye over the surrounding woods. Like many night elves living beneath the boughs of the newly grown World Tree, he is alarmed by the unnatural agitation of the wildlife and the unsettling shadows gathering at the edges of their settlements.",sp=0},{t="Threats in the Canopy",b="Tallonkai directs adventurers to confront foul entities disturbing Teldrassil's peace. His concerns include corrupted dream catchers crafted to protect sleeping druids, vicious gnarlpine furbolgs succumbing to a dark malaise, and the corrupted Gnarlpine mystics led by Ferocitas the Dream Eater. To Tallonkai, cleansing these disturbances is crucial to defending the fragile home of the Kaldorei.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tallonkai Swiftroot?",a="Tallonkai Swiftroot is a night elf quest giver stationed in Dolanaar on the boughs of Teldrassil, dedicated to safeguarding the settlement from local threats.",al={"who is tallonkai","tallonkai swiftroot","dolanaar questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Tallonkai Swiftroot?",a="He is located in the town of Dolanaar, the central night elf village found just outside Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",al={"tallonkai location","where is tallonkai","find tallonkai swiftroot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What tasks does Tallonkai give?",a="He asks travelers to retrieve the Emerald Dreamcatcher from the gnarlpine furbolgs, defeat the Gnarlpine furbolg Ferocitas the Dream Eater, and confront the warped gnarlpine threat in quests like Twisted Hatred.",al={"tallonkai quests","what does tallonkai want"},gp=true},{q="Why is he concerned about the dreamcatchers?",a="Dreamcatchers are sacred night elf talismans tied to the Emerald Dream, used to ward against nightmares and dark visions. Their theft and corruption by hostile creatures poses a spiritual danger to the local druids and denizens of Teldrassil.",al={"emerald dreamcatcher lore","why dreamcatchers"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Ferocitas the Dream Eater?",a="Ferocitas the Dream Eater is the leader of a band of corrupted Gnarlpine mystics north of Starbreeze. He stole the emerald from Tallonkai's dreamcatcher and wears it on a necklace that glows green in the night.",al={"who is ferocitas","ferocitas lore"},it="target"},{q="What is causing the unrest Tallonkai fights against?",a="A growing sickness and unnatural corruption has seeped into Teldrassil, driving previously peaceful creatures like the gnarlpine furbolgs into violent madness.",al={"why are furbolgs mad","twisted hatred lore"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Tallonkai Swiftroot on?",a="Tallonkai stands firmly with the night elves of Darnassus and the Alliance. Stationed in Dolanaar, he works to protect Teldrassil's burgeoning settlements from corruption and the wild beasts disturbed across the boughs.",al={"tallonkai swiftroot faction","who does tallonkai serve","tallonkai swiftroot allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Tallonkai Swiftroot want?",a="Tallonkai wants to safeguard Dolanaar and soothe the corrupted wildlife of Teldrassil. He seeks the recovery of sacred Emerald Dreamcatchers stolen by tainted gnarlpine furbolgs, and demands the eradication of foul threats like Ferocitas the Dream Eater and the corrupted satyrs whose hatred poisons the woods.",al={"what does tallonkai want","tallonkai goal","tallonkai motives"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar?",a="Tallonkai is stationed in Dolanaar to monitor rising disturbances in the surrounding wilderness. As corrupted furbolgs and vile beasts threaten the road and settlements of Teldrassil, he remains in town to recruit capable adventurers to strike back at the woodland's blights.",al={"why is tallonkai here","why is tallonkai swiftroot in dolanaar","what brings tallonkai to dolanaar"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Tallonkai Swiftroot represents the vigilance needed to protect Teldrassil during its vulnerable early years, asking young Kaldorei to purge corruption taking root in their new home.",["class:Druid"]="Tallonkai's concerns center on relics that tether minds safely to the Emerald Dream, making his requests deeply relevant to druidic spiritual traditions."},kw={"dolanaar","dreamcatcher","ferocitas","tallonkai swiftroot","teldrassil","twisted hatred"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:2438","quest:2459","quest:932","topic:emerald-dream","topic:night-elf"},src={"Tallonkai Swiftroot"}}
E["npc:tarindrella"] = {t="npc",n="Tarindrella",z="teldrassil",s="Tarindrella is a dryad found watching over the sheltered woods of Shadowglen in Teldrassil. As a daughter of Cenarius, she works closely with night elf protectors to investigate the unnatural corruption afflicting the World Tree's wildlife.",h="Tarindrella is a dryad found watching over the sheltered woods of Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Daughter of Cenarius in Shadowglen",b="Dryads are fierce caretakers of nature, born of the demigod Cenarius. While many remain deep within ancient Kalimdor forests like Ashenvale, Tarindrella dwells in the protected glade of Shadowglen atop the boughs of Teldrassil. She acts as a vital bridge between the wild spirits and young night elf defenders taking their first steps outside Aldrassil. Her primary concern is the lingering taint creeping into the forest, tasking reliable adventurers with driving back local pests and gathering clues about the root of the affliction.",sp=0},{t="Investigating Teldrassil's Affliction",b="Despite Teldrassil's grandeur as the new crown of the night elf people, its pristine groves harbor an unexpected sickness. The once-peaceful furbolgs have deserted their homes to gather as the Gnarlpine tribe, and grells and grellkin tainted by wicked Fel Moss infest the hills around Shadowglen. Tarindrella suspects the Fel Moss behind these changes and directs initiates to confront the grells and bring back samples, seeking to stem the corruption before it can overtake the sanctuary of the young grove.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tarindrella?",a="Tarindrella is a dryad residing in Shadowglen atop Teldrassil. She aids local night elves in monitoring the wilderness and directing young defenders to combat the strange sickness threatening the boughs of the World Tree.",al={"tarindrella lore","who is tarindrella","dryad shadowglen"},it="identity"},{q="What is a dryad?",a="Dryads are enchanted woodland beings who are daughters of the demigod Cenarius. Possessing the upper torso of a night elf and the lower body of a fawn, they serve as dedicated guardians of Kalimdor's sacred groves and balance.",al={"dryad lore","what are dryads","daughters of cenarius"},it="people"},{q="Why is Tarindrella concerned about Shadowglen?",a="Even in the safe heart of Teldrassil, unnatural corruption has begun twisting local creatures, driving the furbolgs to gather as the hostile Gnarlpine tribe and filling the hills with grells tainted by Fel Moss. Tarindrella seeks to cleanse this taint and protect the young grove from spreading decay.",al={"shadowglen corruption","tarindrella quests","what is wrong with shadowglen"},it="why_here"},{q="What threats does she send adventurers to face?",a="Tarindrella enlists aid to confront the grells and grellkin infesting Shadowglen and collect the wicked Fel Moss they carry, to confirm whether it lies behind the corruption.",al={"tarindrella spiders","shadowthread cave quests"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Tarindrella on?",a="Tarindrella is aligned with the kaldorei and the Cenarion Circle, standing as a protector of nature alongside the night elves. As a daughter of Cenarius, she serves the natural balance and aids young night elf adventurers who set out to defend Teldrassil from harm.",al={"tarindrella faction","who does tarindrella serve","tarindrella alliance or horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Tarindrella want?",a="Tarindrella seeks to root out and cleanse the unnatural corruption afflicting the boughs of Teldrassil. She enlists you to investigate the tainted wildlife of Shadowglen and combat the dark blight spreading through the glade's woods and dens.",al={"what does tarindrella want","tarindrella goal","tarindrella purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Who is Tarindrella tied to?",a="As a dryad, Tarindrella is a daughter of the demigod Cenarius, sharing kinship with the keepers of the grove and other woodland spirits of Kalimdor. Her bonds tie her deeply to the night elves and the druids who revere her father's teachings.",al={"tarindrella family","tarindrella ties","who is tarindrella related to"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves starting in Shadowglen, Tarindrella is one of the first dryads they will meet, embodying the ancient covenant between the Kaldorei and the children of Cenarius.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold dryads in high esteem as kindred spirits of the wild, making Tarindrella's guidance on Teldrassil's sickness an urgent call to maintain balance."},kw={"aldrassil","dryad","shadowglen","shadowthread","tarindrella","teldrassil","webwood"},rel={"subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","subzone:shadowthread-cave","quest:458","quest:940","topic:elune"},src={"Tarindrella"}}
E["npc:tenaron-stormgrip"] = {t="npc",n="Tenaron Stormgrip",z="teldrassil",s="Tenaron Stormgrip is a night elf druid situated high within Aldrassil, the central great bough of Shadowglen. Serving the Cenarion Circle, he oversees the early ritual purifications that young kaldorei perform across the crown of Teldrassil.",h="Tenaron Stormgrip is a night elf druid situated high within Aldrassil, the central great bough of Shadowglen.",sec={{t="Watcher of Aldrassil",b="Perched upon the winding wooden platforms of Aldrassil, Tenaron Stormgrip stands as an early mentor to young night elves stepping forth from the boughs of Shadowglen. From his vantage point, he monitors the health of the local woods and the vital moonwells that sustain them. His role is to instruct novices in understanding their profound spiritual connection to the World Tree.",sp=0},{t="Crown of the Earth",b="Tenaron is best known for directing initiates in the sacred rite known as Crown of the Earth. By having acolytes gather pure moonwell water and carry it across the reaches of Teldrassil, he seeks to nourish and purify the land's boughs while observing whether the young tree is flourishing or afflicted by hidden sickness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Tenaron Stormgrip located?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip stands atop the wooden ramp structures of Aldrassil, the massive central tree at the heart of Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",al={"tenaron location","where is tenaron","tenaron stormgrip spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Tenaron Stormgrip's role in Shadowglen?",a="He is an elder guide and member of the Cenarion Circle who instructs young night elves in tending to the sacred moonwells and testing the vitality of the World Tree through the ritual of the Crown of the Earth.",al={"what does tenaron do","tenaron stormgrip purpose","who is tenaron"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Crown of the Earth quest?",a="It is a rite overseen by Tenaron where initiates take purified water drawn from the moonwells of Shadowglen and pour it into ritual phials and sacred spots across Teldrassil to nurture the boughs and investigate the health of the tree.",al={"crown of the earth lore","why carry moonwell water"}},{q="Why is Tenaron concerned about Teldrassil's waters?",a="The moonwells are essential vessels of Elune's grace and natural purity. Because Teldrassil is young and lacks the full blessing of the Aspects, caretakers like Tenaron closely monitor every water source for signs of corruption or taint.",al={"why precious waters","teldrassil water issues"},it="motive"},{q="Does Tenaron send adventurers beyond Shadowglen?",a="Yes. Once an initiate demonstrates reverence and competence in handling the sacred waters, Tenaron directs them outward into greater Teldrassil, sending them down to Dolanaar to continue serving the kaldorei.",al={"tenaron next quest","where does tenaron send you"},it="next_step"},{q="Is Tenaron a druid or a priest?",a="The sources never say outright. Tenaron operates closely with the Cenarion Circle, focusing on the ecological health and balance of Teldrassil's boughs, while honoring the sacred lunar magic of the moonwells.",al={"tenaron stormgrip class","is tenaron druid"},it="identity"},{q="Whose side is Tenaron Stormgrip on?",a="Tenaron is devoted entirely to the night elves of Darnassus and the well-being of Teldrassil. He works alongside the druids and priests tending the Great Tree, guiding fledgling defenders who step forth from Aldrassil to protect their homeland and serve the Alliance.",al={"tenaron faction","is tenaron alliance","who does tenaron serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Tenaron Stormgrip want?",a="Tenaron seeks to nurture and protect Teldrassil from the corruption creeping into its boughs. He watches over the waters of Shadowglen and tasks promising adventurers with gathering vital samples and vitalizing the local moonwells to ensure the Great Tree flourishes.",al={"what does tenaron want","tenaron goal","tenaron stormgrip mission"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Tenaron Stormgrip here?",a="Stationed high within the great tree Aldrassil, Tenaron oversees the heart of Shadowglen. He remains here to evaluate new night elven initiates, monitor the sacred waters that feed the boughs, and coordinate the first steps in preserving Teldrassil's burgeoning growth.",al={"why is tenaron in aldrassil","why is tenaron here","tenaron shadowglen role"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves, Tenaron Stormgrip provides one of the very first introductions to the communal and spiritual duties required to keep Teldrassil alive and pure.",["class:Druid"]="Tenaron's tasks highlight the druidic stewardship needed to monitor Teldrassil's unprecedented growth and guard against subtle corruption."},kw={"aldrassil","cenarion circle","crown of the earth","moonwell","shadowglen","stormgrip","teldrassil","tenaron"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","quest:929","quest:940","topic:night-elf"},src={"Tenaron Stormgrip"}}
E["npc:zarrin"] = {t="npc",n="Zarrin",z="teldrassil",s="Zarrin is a night elf culinary mentor located in Dolanaar on the boughs of Teldrassil. Tending an open hearth behind the village inn, he instructs young night elves and visitors in traditional Kaldorei cooking techniques.",h="Zarrin is a night elf culinary mentor located in Dolanaar on the boughs of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Hearthkeeper of Dolanaar",b="Situated behind the Dolanaar inn away from the main thoroughfare, Zarrin tends an open fire where he shares the culinary arts of the Kaldorei. Survival in Teldrassil requires utilizing the native flora and fauna of the giant tree, and Zarrin serves as an instructor for those seeking to sustain themselves through foraging and home-cooked meals.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Zarrin?",a="Zarrin stands behind the inn in Dolanaar on Teldrassil, working over a cooking fire in the open yard opposite the road.",al={"zarrin location","where is zarrin","dolanaar cooking trainer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Zarrin teach?",a="He is a Cooking trainer who teaches the basics of culinary preparation and traditional night elf recipes to novices.",al={"zarrin trainer","what does zarrin teach"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What tasks does Zarrin offer?",a="Zarrin asks travelers to help him prepare traditional dishes, offering the quest 'Recipe of the Kaldorei' to teach newcomers local culinary practices.",al={"zarrin quest","recipe of the kaldorei quest"},gp=true},{q="Who is Zarrin?",a="Zarrin is a night elf culinary mentor tending his hearth in Dolanaar. Stationed just behind the village inn, he spends his days by the open fire instructing young travelers and local sentinels in the traditional culinary arts of the kaldorei.",al={"who is zarrin","zarrin lore","zarrin identity"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Zarrin on?",a="Zarrin stands loyally with Darnassus and the greater Alliance. He resides peacefully within Teldrassil's borders, offering his hearth and culinary knowledge to any friendly travelers who visit the settlement of Dolanaar.",al={"zarrin faction","zarrin alliance","who does zarrin serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Zarrin want?",a="Zarrin is dedicated to preserving and passing along the traditional culinary heritage of the kaldorei. He seeks to instruct emerging adventurers on how to prepare wholesome meals from the bounteous wildlife and flora of Teldrassil.",al={"what does zarrin want","zarrin goals","zarrin purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Zarrin in Dolanaar?",a="Dolanaar is the primary crossroads for young night elves venturing forth from Shadowglen. Zarrin keeps his spit and cookfire behind the local inn so he can readily supply novice wanderers with vital survival recipes before they brave deeper perils.",al={"why is zarrin in dolanaar","why is zarrin here","zarrin location why"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="For adventurers beginning their journey in Teldrassil, Zarrin is the primary mentor for learning how to turn wild beast meats and foraged goods into nourishing meals.",["race:NightElf"]="Zarrin preserves everyday Kaldorei foodways, ensuring that traditional tastes and methods endure within the canopy of the World Tree."},kw={"cooking","dolanaar","kaldorei","teldrassil","trainer","zarrin"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","quest:4161","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},src={"Zarrin"}}
E["npc:zenn-foulhoof"] = {t="npc",n="Zenn Foulhoof",z="teldrassil",s="Zenn Foulhoof is an exiled satyr lingering just east of Dolanaar in Teldrassil. While he feigns innocence to passersby and tries to trick young adventurers into helping him, the local night elves keep a close eye on his scheming. Though tolerated for a time through minor punishments, his affinity for dark magic makes him an unwelcome presence on the boughs of the World Tree.",h="Zenn Foulhoof is an exiled satyr lingering just east of Dolanaar in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Schemer in the Woods",b="Unlike most satyrs, who are outright hostiles serving demonic masters, Zenn Foulhoof somehow secured a tenuous tolerance just outside Dolanaar. He maintains a friendly facade, claiming he has changed or wants to trade in harmless forest reagents like spider fangs and tiger lily scents. In reality, he manipulates gullible youths to procure ingredients for foul rituals. Dolanaar's council refuses to let him operate unchecked; rather than executing him immediately, they order adventurers to humiliate him by feeding him corrupted forest fruit, temporarily transforming the scheming satyr into a harmless frog.",sp=0},{t="Exile to Darkshore",b="Zenn's petty trickery in Teldrassil quickly escalates into dangerous corruption. After being thoroughly chased out of the World Tree for his dark magic, he establishes a lair in Cliffspring Hollow near Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore. Stripping away all pretense of repentance, Zenn allies with grell and rogue alchemists, actively spreading a foul blight that maddens the local wildlife until Tharnariun Treetender marks him for death.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why isn't Zenn Foulhoof immediately attacked by the night elves?",a="Zenn maintains a friendly veneer and has not yet openly committed atrocities on the World Tree, leading the council of Dolanaar to discipline him through public humiliation and watchfulness rather than an immediate death sentence.",al={"why is zenn friendly","why don't night elves kill zenn","is zenn foulhoof evil"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens when you feed Zenn the corrupted cones and berries?",a="As penance ordered by the elders of Dolanaar, an adventurer forces Zenn to ingest the tainted woodland flora he sought to exploit. The foul magic backfires instantly, turning him into a small, squawking frog.",al={"zenn redemption quest","seek redemption quest","zenn frog"},sp=1},{q="Where does Zenn Foulhoof go after leaving Teldrassil?",a="Once driven off the World Tree, Zenn flees to Darkshore and takes up residence in Cliffspring Hollow near Cliffspring Falls.",al={"where is zenn foulhoof in darkshore","zenn foulhoof location","cliffspring hollow satyr"},sp=1,it="place"},{q="What is a satyr?",a="Satyrs are night elves who were warped into horned, cloven-hoofed fiends during the War of the Ancients after pledging service to the Burning Legion. Most are utterly corrupted and violently hostile to their uncorrupted kin.",al={"what are satyrs","satyr lore"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Zenn Foulhoof?",a="Zenn Foulhoof is a solitary satyr found lurking just east of Dolanaar in Teldrassil. While satyrs are demonic beings and ancient enemies of the night elves, Zenn claims to seek a peaceful existence, living quietly among the boughs of the World Tree rather than openly attacking the local denizens.",al={"who is zenn","zenn foulhoof lore","who is foulhoof"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Zenn Foulhoof on?",a="Zenn is ultimately on his own side, cloaking sinister intentions beneath a harmless, cooperative facade. Though he presents himself peacefully to young adventurers and interacts without overt hostility, he is up to no good, manipulating outsiders into aiding his corrupt schemes while walking a fine line under the watchful eyes of Dolanaar's council.",al={"is zenn evil","zenn foulhoof faction","is zenn friendly"},sp=1,it="side",add=true},{q="What does Zenn Foulhoof want?",a="Zenn seeks materials and components under the guise of simple tasks, tricking unsuspecting adventurers into gathering tainted items like woodland creature pelts and herbs. His true goal is to quietly practice perverse magic and spread foul corruption right beneath the notice of the night elven sentinels.",al={"what does zenn want","zenn foulhoof motives","zenn bidding goal"},sp=1,it="wants",add=true},{q="Who is Zenn Foulhoof tied to?",a="In Teldrassil, Zenn appears to act alone, keeping his ties hidden from the night elves. Beyond the island, however, his malicious work aligns him with other dark forces, including local grell packs under leaders like Licillin and shadowy collaborators such as Apothecary Furrows.",al={"who does zenn work with","zenn foulhoof allies","zenn ties"},sp=1,it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Satyrs represent the ultimate betrayal of kaldorei heritage. Seeing one lounging on the sacred boughs of Teldrassil is an insult to Elune and the spirits of the wild.",["class:Druid"]="Zenn's tampering with wild reagents and deliberate spreading of corrupting taints directly offends Cenarion teachings, which seek to keep Teldrassil pristine."},kw={"cliffspring falls","corrupted cone","dolanaar","satyr","seek redemption","teldrassil","zenn foulhoof"},rel={"topic:satyr","subzone:dolanaar","quest:488","quest:489","zone:darkshore","subzone:cliffspring-falls","npc:tharnariun-treetender","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Zenn Foulhoof"}}
E["quest:1581"] = {t="quest",n="Elixirs for the Bladeleafs",z="teldrassil",s="In the boughs of Dolanaar, Syral Bladeleaf seeks an alchemist to restock her family's burgeoning trade. Her husband spends endless hours over brewing cauldrons, and Syral hopes a batch of fresh elixirs will lighten his workload and earn the contributor a bundle of rare herbs.",h="In the boughs of Dolanaar, Syral Bladeleaf seeks an alchemist to restock her family's burgeoning trade.",sec={{t="A Burden of Prosperity",b="The settlement of Dolanaar serves as a vital crossroad for travelers, sentinels, and druids navigating Teldrassil's canopy. With so many wanderers passing through, the herb and alchemy trade run by Syral Bladeleaf and her husband has flourished. However, high demand brings its own cost. Her husband spends nearly all his hours bent over vials and cauldrons to keep shelves stocked, leaving the couple almost no time to spend together.",sp=0},{t="A Trader's Exchange",b="Rather than letting her partner burn out beneath compounding orders, Syral turns to passing herbalists and brewers. By commissioning pre-mixed draughts—specifically Elixirs of Lion's Strength and Minor Defense—she shores up the shop's inventory while offering freshly harvested, uncommon herbs in exchange. For a fledgling alchemist practicing their craft beneath the Great Tree, it is an ideal opportunity to turn common forest flora into coveted regional flora.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Syral Bladeleaf need these potions?",a="Their family herbal and alchemy shop in Dolanaar has grown extremely busy. Her husband spends all his time brewing potions to keep up with demand, leaving them no personal time together. Outsourcing the work gives him a much-needed break.",al={"why need elixirs","syral bladeleaf motive","bladeleaf shop problem"},it="motive"},{q="What potions are required for the task?",a="Syral asks for six Elixirs of Lion's Strength and two Elixirs of Minor Defense. Both are staple draughts frequently purchased by adventurers and local sentinels in Teldrassil.",al={"which elixirs","what do i need to brew","potions needed"},gp=true},{q="What herbs are needed to brew the required elixirs?",a="Brewing the requested batch requires Silverleaf and Earthroot, both of which grow abundantly across the forest floor of Teldrassil, alongside standard Crystal Vials.",al={"ingredients needed","mats for elixirs","what herbs do i pick"},gp=true},{q="Who can undertake this request?",a="Only practitioners of Alchemy who have attained a basic competence in the craft are offered the task. Syral seeks dependable, well-mixed remedies for her shop rather than amateur brews.",al={"level requirement","profession requirement","can anyone do this quest"},gp=true},{q="What does Syral offer in exchange for the elixirs?",a="Syral rewards helpful alchemists with a bundle of freshly gathered, uncommon herbs that are difficult to locate casually along the woodland trails of Teldrassil.",al={"reward lore","what does syral give","bladeleaf trade reward"},gp=true},{q="Where is Syral Bladeleaf located?",a="She can be found outside the northern building in Dolanaar, near the central road that runs through the forest village.",al={"where is syral","bladeleaf location","where do i turn this in"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Elixir of Lion's Strength for?",a="The Elixir of Lion's Strength is a staple draught among frontline warriors and alchemists, brewed to temporarily bolster the physical might of anyone who drinks it. Syral Bladeleaf stocks it in Dolanaar to meet the constant demands of hunters, sentinels, and travelers preparing to face the dangerous wildlands of Teldrassil.",al={"elixir of lions strength use","why lion strength elixir","elixir of lion's strength purpose"},it="item",add=true},{q="What is the Elixir of Minor Defense for?",a="The Elixir of Minor Defense is an alchemical concoction designed to harden the skin and fortify natural armor against physical strikes. Syral Bladeleaf keeps it on hand to sell in her shop, catering to protectors and adventurers who need reliable, basic safeguarding while patrolling the boughs of the great tree.",al={"elixir of minor defense use","why minor defense elixir","elixir of minor defense purpose"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Teldrassil's rich soil teems with Silverleaf and Earthroot, making it straightforward to forage the raw greens needed to satisfy Syral's shop order.",["race:NightElf"]="Supporting local tradesfolk like the Bladeleafs helps sustain the fledgling settlement of Dolanaar as it grows beneath the canopy of Teldrassil.",["faction:Alliance"]="Keeping Dolanaar well-supplied with restorative and defensive draughts ensures defenders and traveling allies are prepared for woodland threats."},kw={"alchemy","dolanaar","earthroot","elixir of lion's strength","elixir of minor defense","elixirs for the bladeleafs","silverleaf","syral bladeleaf","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:syral-bladeleaf","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},m={start="Syral Bladeleaf",faction="Alliance",id=1581,ri={"Elixir of Lion's Strength","Elixir of Minor Defense"}},src={"Elixirs for the Bladeleafs"}}
E["quest:2159"] = {t="quest",n="Dolanaar Delivery",z="teldrassil",s="Dolanaar Delivery is an errand entrusted to young night elves leaving the sheltered boughs of Shadowglen for the wider reaches of Teldrassil. Porthannius, detained by affairs with the local druids, tasks travelers with carrying a parcel of herbs south to Innkeeper Keldamyr. The simple journey marks an initiate's transition into the bustling hub of Dolanaar.",h="Dolanaar Delivery is an errand entrusted to young night elves leaving the sheltered boughs of Shadowglen for...",sec={{t="A Messenger for Shadowglen",b="Before new adventurers depart the training grounds of Shadowglen, Porthannius seeks someone heading down the road toward the rest of Teldrassil. Entangled in pressing business with the druids tending the glade, he cannot step away to run routine errands himself. Instead, he places a bundle of freshly harvested herbs into the hands of an aspiring hero to ensure vital supplies make it south along the forest path.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Dolanaar",b="Following the southern road out of the secluded vale leads travelers to Dolanaar, one of the foremost night elf settlements upon the great boughs of Teldrassil. There, Innkeeper Keldamyr oversees hospitality, rest, and supplies for wanderers, sentinels, and druids alike. Receiving the herbs on Porthannius's behalf, Keldamyr uses the occasion to urge young adventurers to rest their minds and spirits before confronting the growing corruption across the world tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Porthannius?",a="Porthannius is a night elf residing in Shadowglen, Teldrassil's starting glade. While working closely alongside the local druids, he enlists travelers leaving the glade to ferry supplies southward on his behalf.",al={"porthannius","who gives dolanaar delivery","quest giver porthannius"},it="identity"},{q="Why can't Porthannius deliver the herbs himself?",a="Porthannius has urgent, unfinished business with the druids of Shadowglen. Because his duties keep him occupied within the sheltered vale, he must rely on passing adventurers to make the journey south.",al={"why does porthannius need help","why cant porthannius go"},it="why_me"},{q="What is inside the package?",a="The package contains a collection of herbs gathered within Shadowglen, destined for use at the inn in Dolanaar.",al={"dolanaar delivery package contents","what are the herbs"},it="item"},{q="Who is Innkeeper Keldamyr?",a="Innkeeper Keldamyr manages the inn in Dolanaar. Aside from providing hospitality, lodging, and hearthstones to travelers, he frequently coordinates trade and supply exchanges with other settlements across Teldrassil.",al={"keldamyr","dolanaar innkeeper","who receives the herbs"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Dolanaar located?",a="Dolanaar lies south of Shadowglen. Following the primary road leading out of the glade's exit takes travelers directly into the town center.",al={"where is dolanaar","dolanaar location","directions to dolanaar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is this delivery important for young adventurers?",a="It serves as an introduction to the world beyond Shadowglen, encouraging novitiates to venture outside their training grounds and discover Dolanaar's inn, trainers, and service providers.",al={"significance of delivery","why deliver herbs"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Porthannius need this package delivered to Dolanaar?",a="Porthannius has prepared a vital bundle of fresh herbs gathered in Shadowglen that Innkeeper Keldamyr is awaiting down in Dolanaar. However, urgent duties keep Porthannius occupied with the local druids, preventing him from making the journey down the road himself. To ensure the innkeeper receives these necessary supplies without delay, he relies on a passing traveler heading out into Teldrassil.",al={"porthannius delivery motive","why send herbs to dolanaar","dolanaar delivery purpose"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Taking this task marks a night elf's departure from the protected cradle of Aldrassil out into the broader responsibilities of safeguarding Teldrassil.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The delivery illustrates how vital raw herbs from Shadowglen's verdant soils are to the healers, cooks, and caretakers of Dolanaar.",["class:Druid"]="Porthannius's preoccupation with Shadowglen's druids hints at the deeper spiritual duties and natural imbalances occupying the Cenarion Circle within the boughs."},kw={"delivery","dolanaar","dolanaar delivery","herbs","innkeeper keldamyr","night elf","porthannius","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","subzone:shadowglen","npc:innkeeper-keldamyr","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid"},m={start="Porthannius",["end"]="Innkeeper Keldamyr",faction="Alliance",id=2159},src={"Dolanaar Delivery (quest)"}}
E["quest:2399"] = {t="quest",n="The Sprouted Fronds",z="teldrassil",s="Following Denalan's botanical experiments at Lake Al'Ameth, the planted frond seeds take root and bloom. This quiet moment marks a successful harvest in understanding Teldrassil's strange and vital flora. Travelers inspecting the garden beds can witness the rapid growth firsthand.",h="Following Denalan's botanical experiments at Lake Al'Ameth, the planted frond seeds take root and bloom.",sec={{t="A Garden by Lake Al'Ameth",b="Tucked away near Lake Al'Ameth, the botanist Denalan dedicates himself to cataloging the peculiar plant life of Teldrassil. After sowing the seeds recovered from a mysterious shimmering frond, the soil quickly yields result. In his tended planter, strange, trembling fronds shoot up from the rich loam, eager to be gathered and examined.",sp=0},{t="The Strange Flora of the World Tree",b="Teldrassil is young, vast, and teeming with rapid natural development that both fascinates and troubles night elf herbalists. The shimmering fronds and their sprouted offshoots are emblematic of how swiftly life takes hold on the boughs of the great tree, hinting at the powerful yet unpredictable vitality woven into the island's soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the sprouted fronds?",a="They are the mature plants that sprouted from seeds sown by Denalan at his lakeside camp. Cultivated from the shimmering fronds found elsewhere in Teldrassil, these peculiar plants tremble with energy when ready for harvest.",al={"sprouted fronds","what are these plants","denalans fronds"},it="item"},{q="Where is Denalan's garden located?",a="Denalan keeps his garden and research camp along the eastern edge of Lake Al'Ameth, southeast of Dolanaar in Teldrassil.",al={"denalan location","where is denalan","wellspring lake garden"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Denalan plant these fronds?",a="Denalan studies the curious and rapid growth patterns of Teldrassil's plant life. By planting seeds in controlled soil, he investigates their nature and tests whether they possess useful restorative or herbal properties.",al={"why plant fronds","denalan experiment","purpose of fronds"},it="purpose"},{q="Are the sprouted fronds dangerous?",a="No. Unlike some of the corrupted or hostile flora elsewhere on the boughs of Teldrassil, these sprouted fronds are harmless botanical specimens waiting to be plucked.",al={"are fronds dangerous","do fronds attack","is the plant harmful"},it="danger"},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="Adventurers first discover a shimmering frond in the wilds of Teldrassil and bring it to Denalan, who plants the seeds in his garden planter to await their sprouting.",al={"prereq for sprouted fronds","what quest comes first"},it="history",gp=true},{q="Why do the fronds tremble?",a="The soil and magic coursing through Teldrassil imbue native plants with vibrant, restless energy. The fronds tremble as a sign of their vitality and readiness to be harvested.",al={"trembling fronds","why do they shake"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Denalan's research reflects the practical arts of gathering and studying Teldrassil's unique vegetation, demonstrating how quickly local seeds adapt to nurtured soil.",["race:NightElf"]="Tending the newly sprouted flora reflects the kaldorei responsibility to monitor and nurture the life taking root across their young World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="Druids observing Denalan's planter can appreciate the quiet balance of nature, seeing life flourish under attentive care even amid Teldrassil's growing perils."},kw={"denalan","herbalism","planter","seeds","shimmering frond","sprouted fronds","teldrassil","wellspring lake"},rel={"quest:931","npc:denalan","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Sprouted Frond",faction="Alliance",id=2399},src={"The Sprouted Fronds"}}
E["quest:2438"] = {t="quest",n="The Emerald Dreamcatcher",z="teldrassil",s="Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar asks adventurers to recover a cherished heirloom from his abandoned home in Starbreeze Village. The Emerald Dreamcatcher, gifted to him by the druid warden Gaerolas Talvethren, was left behind when corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs overran the tranquil settlement. Reclaiming this amulet prevents its gentle nature-magic from falling into foul hands.",h="Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar asks adventurers to recover a cherished heirloom from his abandoned home in...",sec={{t="A Druidic Talisman",b="The emerald dreamcatcher is far more than a decorative trinket. Fashioned by Gaerolas Talvethren, the honored warden of the sleeping druids within Ban'ethil Barrow Den, the amulet was crafted to channel the serene currents of the Emerald Dream. By siphoning this pure spiritual energy, the dreamcatcher bestows peace and fortune upon its bearer. Such tokens are exceedingly rare, bestowed upon only a trusted few whose lives are intertwined with the forest's stewardship.",sp=0},{t="Fleeing Starbreeze Village",b="Until recently, Starbreeze Village was a peaceful settlement nestled amid the boughs of Teldrassil. That quiet life ended when the local Gnarlpine furbolgs succumbed to a violent madness, driving the night elves from their ancestral dwellings. In the terror and confusion of the evacuation, Tallonkai was forced to leave his most treasured possession hidden inside his dresser in the village's southeastern quarter, powerless to reclaim it on his own.",sp=0},{t="The Threat of Corruption",b="Leaving a focus of Emerald Dream magic in the heart of an overrun village carries grave risks. The Gnarlpine have proven susceptible to dark influences, and an artifact pulsing with the energies of the Dream could easily be tainted or weaponized. Recovering the dreamcatcher safely returns a piece of Starbreeze's heritage to Tallonkai before the furbolgs or other foul denizens can defile its lingering magic.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Emerald Dreamcatcher?",a="It is a rare amulet crafted by Gaerolas Talvethren, warden of the druids in Ban'ethil Barrow Den. The dreamcatcher siphons energy from the Emerald Dream to bestow good luck and spiritual harmony upon whoever carries it.",al={"what is the dreamcatcher","dreamcatcher lore","emerald dreamcatcher"},it="item"},{q="Why was the dreamcatcher left behind in Starbreeze Village?",a="Starbreeze Village was rapidly overrun when the local Gnarlpine furbolgs fell into a violent, corrupted frenzy. Tallonkai Swiftroot was forced to flee for his life to Dolanaar, leaving the precious heirloom tucked away in his bedroom dresser.",al={"why leave it behind","starbreeze village dresser","tallonkai dresser"}},{q="Who is Tallonkai Swiftroot?",a="Tallonkai is a night elf refugee currently staying in Dolanaar. Having escaped the fall of Starbreeze Village, he seeks brave travelers to venture back into the occupied ruins to salvage his family heirlooms and safeguard druidic relics.",al={"who is tallonkai","tallonkai swiftroot"},it="identity"},{q="Who made the dreamcatcher?",a="It was crafted and gifted by Gaerolas Talvethren, the warden who watches over the slumbering druids inside Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",al={"who made it","gaerolas talvethren dreamcatcher","gaerolas"},it="origin"},{q="Where in Starbreeze Village is the dreamcatcher located?",a="It rests inside Tallonkai's personal dresser, situated inside the far south-eastern house of Starbreeze Village, which is now heavily prowled by hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs.",al={"where is the dresser","starbreeze dresser location","find dreamcatcher"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after the dreamcatcher is returned?",a="Once Tallonkai inspects the recovered amulet, he discovers that its emerald is missing, stolen by the Gnarlpine leader Ferocitas the Dream Eater, leading directly into the hunt for him.",al={"quest continuation","next quest after dreamcatcher"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Tallonkai Swiftroot want the Emerald Dreamcatcher back?",a="The Emerald Dreamcatcher is a rare and deeply personal treasure. It was gifted to Tallonkai by Gaerolas Talvethren, warden of the druids in Ban'ethil Barrow Den, and carries potent magic drawn from the Emerald Dream to bestow luck. When Starbreeze Village fell to the corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs, Tallonkai was forced to leave it behind. He fears the sacred relic will be defiled or destroyed by the rampaging furbolgs if it remains inside his abandoned home.",al={"why does tallonkai want dreamcatcher","tallonkai motive","why recover emerald dreamcatcher"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The amulet is a direct work of Gaerolas Talvethren, the warden tending to your sleeping kin in Ban'ethil Barrow Den, making its recovery a matter of druidic honor.",["race:NightElf"]="Starbreeze was once a tranquil haven for your people. Helping Tallonkai recover his heritage strikes a small blow against the madness seizing Teldrassil's wildlife.",["faction:Alliance"]="Aiding the displaced Kaldorei of Dolanaar secures local stability as Teldrassil struggles with spreading corruption among the furbolg tribes."},kw={"ban'ethil barrow den","dolanaar","emerald dream","emerald dreamcatcher","furbolg","gaerolas talvethren","gnarlpine","starbreeze village","tallonkai swiftroot","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:tallonkai-swiftroot","quest:2459","subzone:starbreeze-village","subzone:dolanaar","npc:gaerolas-talvethren","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","topic:emerald-dream","topic:furbolg"},m={start="Tallonkai Swiftroot",faction="Alliance",id=2438,ri={"Emerald Dreamcatcher"}},src={"The Emerald Dreamcatcher (quest)"}}
E["quest:2459"] = {t="quest",n="Ferocitas the Dream Eater",z="teldrassil",s="Ferocitas the Dream Eater is an Alliance quest given by Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar. After recovering his damaged heirloom dreamcatcher, Tallonkai discovers its potent emerald core was pried away by Gnarlpine furbolgs north of Starbreeze Village. Adventurers are sent to slay the corrupted mystics and recover the stolen jewel from their leader, Ferocitas.",h="Ferocitas the Dream Eater is an Alliance quest given by Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar.",sec={{t="A Defiled Heirloom",b="When Tallonkai Swiftroot examined the dreamcatcher recovered from the corrupted wilds, relief quickly turned to dismay. The sacred artifact had been vandalized, its vibrant emerald centerpiece pried from the woven frame. Word among the night elves held that a band of Gnarlpine mystics north of Starbreeze Village had fallen under the influence of a furbolg leader known as Ferocitas the Dream Eater, who brazenly wore a brilliant green stone around his neck. Knowing the sacred gem was useless and perverse in the creature's clutches, Tallonkai sent defenders to wrest it back.",sp=0},{t="Purging the Mystics",b="The Gnarlpine furbolgs inhabiting Teldrassil's northern reaches were once peaceful neighbors, but the growing corruption seeping into the World Tree drove them into frenzy and madness. Their mystics, who once practiced harmonious nature rites, began tapping into distorted magical energies. By tracking down Ferocitas and cutting through the mystic retinue guarding his woodland enclave, travelers restore balance to the woods and recover Tallonkai's jewel so the dreamcatcher can finally be made whole.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find Ferocitas the Dream Eater?",a="Ferocitas the Dream Eater is located in the forest north of Starbreeze Village on Teldrassil, surrounded by corrupted Gnarlpine mystics and other woodland hazards.",al={"ferocitas location","where is ferocitas","find dream eater"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Who is Ferocitas?",a="Ferocitas is a Gnarlpine furbolg leader who commands a band of corrupted Gnarlpine mystics north of Starbreeze Village. He took the emerald from Tallonkai Swiftroot's dreamcatcher and fashioned it into a crude necklace.",al={"who is ferocitas","ferocitas lore","what is dream eater"},it="target"},{q="Why does Tallonkai Swiftroot want the jewel back?",a="The missing emerald is the core power source of Tallonkai's dreamcatcher. Without it, the talisman cannot be repaired or channel the protective energies of the Emerald Dream.",al={"why tallonkai wants jewel","tallonkai jewel purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Can the Gnarlpine actually use the emerald's magic?",a="No. According to Tallonkai Swiftroot, the emerald's magical properties are completely useless to creatures like Ferocitas and the Gnarlpine mystics, who coveted it merely as a glowing bauble.",al={"can gnarlpine use dreamcatcher","does ferocitas use emerald"}},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="This quest is the final chapter of the two-part chain that began with The Emerald Dreamcatcher. Once you deliver the jewel to Tallonkai in Dolanaar, he can finally repair his heirloom.",al={"quest after ferocitas","next quest dreamcatcher"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine mystics hostile?",a="Like much of the wildlife and furbolg tribes across Teldrassil, the Gnarlpine have succumbed to a strange corruption warping the boughs of the newly planted World Tree, twisting their minds and turning them aggressive.",al={"why are furbolgs mad","gnarlpine corruption"},it="hostile"},{q="What is Tallonkai's Jewel for?",a="The missing emerald is the vital focus of Tallonkai Swiftroot's damaged dreamcatcher. Without it, the talisman cannot function, and he needs the stone returned intact so he can finally repair the sacred ward.",al={"what is tallonkais jewel","tallonkai jewel purpose","missing emerald use"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Gnarlpine were once allies of the Kaldorei, making the corruption of their mystics and their thievery of sacred talismans a poignant tragedy for any night elf defending Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="Dreamcatchers are potent instruments tied to the Emerald Dream; seeing one defiled by a corrupted furbolg demands swift natural retribution."},kw={"dolanaar","dream eater","emerald dreamcatcher","ferocitas","gnarlpine mystics","starbreeze village","tallonkai swiftroot","tallonkai's jewel","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:2438","npc:tallonkai-swiftroot","subzone:starbreeze-village","subzone:dolanaar","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Tallonkai Swiftroot",faction="Alliance",id=2459,ri={"Tallonkai's Jewel"}},src={"Ferocitas the Dream Eater (quest)"}}
E["quest:2498"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Denalan",z="teldrassil",s="Return to Denalan is an Alliance quest connecting the botanists investigating corruption within Teldrassil. After studying the mossy tumors afflicting local timberlings, Rellian Greenspyre sends you back south to Lake Al'Ameth to assist Denalan with an alarming new discovery.",h="Return to Denalan is an Alliance quest connecting the botanists investigating corruption within Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Message Across the Boughs",b="While examining the strange mossy tumors afflicting Teldrassil's timberlings, Rellian Greenspyre receives urgent word from his colleague Denalan. Stationed beside the tranquil waters of Lake Al'Ameth, Denalan believes he has finally isolated what is causing these unnatural growths on the forest's nature spirits. Recognizing the gravity of the situation, Rellian dispatches you back south immediately to lend a hand.",sp=0},{t="The Threat at the Lake",b="Denalan's research at Lake Al'Ameth is critical to understanding the ailments creeping across the young World Tree. What began as an investigation into corrupted plant life and diseased timberlings quickly escalates into a direct confrontation with the blighted entities poisoning the boughs, starting with the corrupted timberling Oakenscowl.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf researcher and naturalist stationed at Lake Al'Ameth in southern Teldrassil. He dedicates his time to studying the island's flora, strange seedling mutations, and the unnatural afflictions spreading among the local timberlings.",al={"denalan lore","who is denalan","denalan lake al'ameth"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Rellian Greenspyre send you back to Lake Al'Ameth?",a="Rellian receives word that Denalan has discovered the likely root cause behind the tumors corrupting the timberlings. Because the situation is developing rapidly and poses a growing danger to the forest, Rellian sends you to provide immediate field assistance.",al={"why go to denalan","rellian greenspyre mission"},it="motive"},{q="What are the tumors afflicting the timberlings?",a="Timberlings are peaceful nature spirits born from the island's plant life, but a pervasive corruption taking root in Teldrassil causes them to sprout bizarre mossy growths. These tumors drive the creatures hostile and maddened.",al={"timberling tumors","why do timberlings have tumors","mossy tumors"},it="threat"},{q="Where can I find Denalan?",a="Denalan makes his camp along the shores of Lake Al'Ameth, just south of Dolanaar in the southern woodlands of Teldrassil.",al={"denalan location","where is denalan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after you reach Denalan?",a="Upon arriving, Denalan reveals that a corrupted timberling named Oakenscowl is responsible for the blighted tumors spreading through the grove, tasking you with destroying the beast to halt the contamination.",al={"what comes next","oakenscowl follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="How does this errand connect Rellian and Denalan?",a="The errand links Rellian Greenspyre's timberling research at Wellspring Hovel to Denalan's camp at Lake Al'Ameth, carrying Rellian's study of the tumors to Denalan's new discovery about their cause.",al={"why does rellian send me to denalan","return to denalan purpose"},gp=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The timberlings are living manifestations of Teldrassil's vitality; aiding Denalan is part of the sacred duty to heal the growing corruption threatening your people's new home.",["class:Druid"]="Investigating unnatural tumors on woodland spirits cuts to the core of the Cenarion mandate to maintain the natural balance and cleanse insidious blights."},kw={"denalan","dolanaar","lake al'ameth","oakenscowl","rellian greenspyre","teldrassil","timberlings","tumors"},rel={"quest:923","quest:2499","npc:denalan","quest:922","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Rellian Greenspyre",["end"]="Denalan",level="9",faction="Alliance",id=2498},src={"Return to Denalan"}}
E["quest:2499"] = {t="quest",n="Oakenscowl",z="teldrassil",s="Denalan asks adventurers to put an end to Oakenscowl, a powerful timberling corrupted by a massive growth. Dwelling in a cave along the southern bank of Lake Al'Ameth, the maddened creature now spreads blight across the local wildlife.",h="Denalan asks adventurers to put an end to Oakenscowl, a powerful timberling corrupted by a massive growth.",sec={{t="A Fallen Guardian",b="Oakenscowl was once a grand leader among the timberlings, the wood spirits that tend to the lush boughs of Teldrassil. Tragically, the corruption creeping through the world tree does not discriminate between humble wildlife and ancient protectors. Driven wild by a gargantuan tumor swelling upon its bark, Oakenscowl has become a vessel of blight rather than a steward of growth.",sp=0},{t="Purging Lake Al'Ameth",b="Lurking in a cavern on the southern shore of Lake Al'Ameth, Oakenscowl's toxic presence actively poisons surrounding waters and woodland beasts. Denalan, unable to face the beast alone, seeks the creature's destruction not out of malice, but to mercifully sever the source of corruption and study the bizarre, overgrown tumor plaguing the lake's spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Oakenscowl?",a="Oakenscowl is a massive timberling—a forest spirit tied to Teldrassil's plant life. He was once regarded as a noble leader among his kind before falling victim to a malignant growth.",al={"who is oakenscowl","oakenscowl lore","what kind of creature is oakenscowl"},it="target"},{q="Why must Oakenscowl be destroyed?",a="Oakenscowl is afflicted by a gargantuan tumor that has twisted his mind and made him violently aggressive. His presence in the cavern along Lake Al'Ameth actively spreads the strange blight to neighboring timberlings and beasts.",al={"why kill oakenscowl","oakenscowl hostile"},it="motive"},{q="Where does Oakenscowl reside?",a="Oakenscowl dwells deep within a cavern situated along the southern shore of Lake Al'Ameth in southern Teldrassil.",al={"oakenscowl location","where is oakenscowl cave"},it="place"},{q="Who is Denalan and why is he studying the tumor?",a="Denalan is an herbalist and naturalist living on the eastern shore of Lake Al'Ameth. He studies the flora and fauna of the world tree, striving to understand and cure the strange rot that infects the local timberling population.",al={"who gives oakenscowl quest","denalan oakenscowl"},it="identity"},{q="What caused the tumor on Oakenscowl?",a="The tumor is a symptom of a deeper, insidious sickness creeping through the soil and roots of Teldrassil, corrupting nature spirits from within.",al={"why do timberlings have tumors","source of corruption"},it="origin"},{q="Is Oakenscowl beyond saving?",a="By the time adventurers encounter him, the affliction has progressed too far. The tumor has completely warped the creature, leaving Denalan no choice but to call for a mercy kill.",al={"can oakenscowl be healed","cure oakenscowl"},it="threat"},{q="What does Denalan need the Gargantuan Tumor for?",a="Denalan needs the Gargantuan Tumor to study the unnatural affliction poisoning Teldrassil's timberlings. As a nature researcher living on Lake Al'Ameth, he has watched the creatures fall to madness and corruption. Because Oakenscowl bore the largest growth he has ever seen, examining such an extreme specimen provides Denalan his best chance to understand the disease upsetting the local wildlife.",al={"why gargantuan tumor","purpose of gargantuan tumor","gargantuan tumor use"},it="item",add=true},{q="Why does Denalan need your help against Oakenscowl?",a="Denalan is an isolated researcher and herbalist, not a warrior capable of battling a massive, corrupted timberling in its den. He admitted he dared not even get close to the beast when scouting the southern bank. Because you already proved your capability gathering mossy tumors and aiding his work, he entrusts you with removing the threat that endangers his lakeside home.",al={"why me denalan","why send an adventurer oakenscowl","why can't denalan fight oakenscowl"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Seeing a guardian timberling corrupted by strange tumors is a harrowing reminder to druids that Teldrassil's burgeoning ecosystem is deeply unwell.",["race:NightElf"]="The tragic downfall of Oakenscowl strikes near the heart of night elf society, threatening the very lake beneath the shadow of Aldrassil.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists aiding Denalan observe firsthand how botanical life can warp into malignant, mossy blights under the influence of unseen rot."},kw={"corruption","denalan","gargantuan tumor","lake al'ameth","mossy tumors","oakenscowl","teldrassil","timberling"},rel={"npc:denalan","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Denalan",level="9",faction="Alliance",id=2499,ri={"Gargantuan Tumor"}},src={"Oakenscowl (Classic)"}}
E["quest:2541"] = {t="quest",n="The Sleeping Druid",z="teldrassil",s="Deep within the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, the slumbering night elf Oben Rageclaw faces a dire magical predicament. Hostile Gnarlpine furbolg shamans have severed his dreaming spirit from his physical body, using foul enchantments to animate his flesh into a rampaging guardian.",h="Deep within the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, the slumbering night elf Oben Rageclaw faces a dire magical predicament.",sec={{t="A Slumber Disrupted",b="Night elf druids enter barrow dens across Kalimdor to commune with nature through centuries of slumber, wandering the Emerald Dream while their mortal frames rest securely in stone alcoves. However, the corruption afflicting Teldrassil has driven the local Gnarlpine tribe of furbolgs to acts of desperate savagery. In Ban'ethil Barrow Den, Gnarlpine shamans uncovered a method to breach the sanctified rest of Oben Rageclaw, prying his living spirit away from his sleeping vessel.",sp=0},{t="Voodoo and Corruption",b="Rather than killing Oben, the Gnarlpine shamans used a sinister talisman—a Shaman Voodoo Charm—to forcibly animate his empty shell. Trapped helplessly in the Emerald Dream, Oben's displaced spirit can only watch as his physical form stalks the corridors, blindly attacking any who enter the den. To unravel the enchantment and find a path toward restoring his body, his ethereal projection tasks adventurers with retrieving one of the Gnarlpine charms for study.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Oben Rageclaw?",a="Oben Rageclaw is a night elf druid who entered a sacred slumber inside the Ban'ethil Barrow Den to commune with the Emerald Dream. Hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs hijacked his physical vessel, leaving his spirit displaced.",al={"oben rageclaw","who is the sleeping druid","sleeping night elf in barrow den"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Oben's body attacking people?",a="Gnarlpine shamans performed a ritual separating Oben's consciousness from his flesh. They animated his empty, physical form with dark magic to serve as an aggressive guardian guarding the depths of the barrow den.",al={"why is oben hostile","why is oben attacking","oben rageclaw body attacking"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Shaman Voodoo Charm?",a="It is an enchanted focus carried by the Gnarlpine shamans inside Ban'ethil Barrow Den. They use its dark power to wrench sleeping druids' spirits out of their bodies and animate their physical husks.",al={"shaman charm","voodoo charm teldrassil","what is shaman voodoo charm"},it="item"},{q="Where is Oben's true spirit during the quest?",a="Oben's consciousness is trapped wandering the Emerald Dream, unable to rejoin his mortal shell. He can only communicate with the waking world as a shimmering spirit near his resting place.",al={"where is oben","oben spirit location","emerald dream oben"},it="place"},{q="Why are the furbolgs in Ban'ethil Barrow Den hostile?",a="The Gnarlpine tribe has fallen victim to the rising taint and madness corrupting Teldrassil's wildlife and forests, causing them to turn against their former night elf allies and desecrate sacred druidic sites.",al={"why are gnarlpine mad","furbolg corruption teldrassil","why furbolgs aggressive"},it="hostile"},{q="Can Oben's body be saved without killing it?",a="Studying the Shaman Voodoo Charm is Oben's first hope of breaking the ritual. By examining the vile enchantments binding his flesh, he hopes to understand the magic and find a way to resolve the crisis.",al={"save oben rageclaw","can oben be saved","cure oben"},gp=true},{q="Why does Oben Rageclaw want the charm?",a="Gnarlpine furbolg shamans have managed to rip Oben Rageclaw's spirit away from his sleeping physical form. His wandering body has been animated by their dark magic to violently attack anyone who enters the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, while his true consciousness remains trapped in the Emerald Dream. Oben wants a charm so he can inspect its foul enchantment and search for a way to break the furbolgs' hold over his body.",al={"oben rageclaw motive","why does oben want the charm","why help oben rageclaw"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine shaman in Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="The Gnarlpine tribe has overrun the sacred Ban'ethil Barrow Den, exploiting the vulnerability of slumbering night elf druids. Their shamans have begun practicing vile rituals to separate the druids' spirits from their flesh, seizing control of the physical bodies as violent sentries to guard their newly occupied subterranean domain.",al={"why gnarlpine shamans here","gnarlpine in barrow den","who are gnarlpine shamans"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does Oben need you to retrieve the charm?",a="Oben is completely helpless to act on his own. His spirit is severed from the waking realm and trapped within the Emerald Dream, while his physical body is an animated puppet controlled by the Gnarlpine shamans. Without physical form or agency, he relies entirely on an outside adventurer to face the furbolgs and bring the charm to his spirit.",al={"why does oben need me","why cant oben get the charm himself","why me oben quest"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids, Oben's situation is a waking nightmare: having one's body hijacked while communing in the Emerald Dream violates the very foundation of druidic slumber.",["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of Ban'ethil Barrow Den demonstrates how deeply the Gnarlpine furbolgs have fallen from their ancient kinship with the Kaldorei."},kw={"ban'ethil barrow den","barrow den","emerald dream","gnarlpine","oben rageclaw","shaman voodoo charm","teldrassil","the sleeping druid"},rel={"npc:oben-rageclaw","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","topic:druid","topic:furbolg","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Oben Rageclaw",faction="Alliance",id=2541,ri={"Shaman Voodoo Charm"}},src={"The Sleeping Druid"}}
E["quest:2561"] = {t="quest",n="Druid of the Claw",z="teldrassil",s="Deep within the barrows of Teldrassil, the spectral form of Oben Rageclaw asks for a tragic release. Corrupted furbolgs have placed a dark enchantment over his physical vessel, forcing you to destroy his soulless shell and break the bond so his spirit may return to the Emerald Dream.",h="Deep within the barrows of Teldrassil, the spectral form of Oben Rageclaw asks for a tragic release.",sec={{t="A Severed Spirit",b="While resting in the barrows beneath Teldrassil, Oben Rageclaw suffered a terrible fate. The corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs subjected his slumbering body to a foul voodoo enchantment, severing his spirit from his mortal flesh. Trapped in the Emerald Dream, Oben's spirit lingers nearby, unable to rest or reclaim his own body.",sp=0},{t="Mercy for the Flesh",b="Examining the Gnarlpine's voodoo charm revealed the grim truth: Oben's physical shell is entirely under the furbolgs' dominion. To break the enchantment, an adventurer must enter the nearby chamber, strike down the mindless, hostile husk of Oben Rageclaw, and use the furbolg charm over his remains to finally shatter the magic binding his soul.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why do I have to kill Oben Rageclaw?",a="The Gnarlpine furbolgs cast a powerful voodoo enchantment over Oben while he slumbered, turning his physical body into a soulless puppet. Because his flesh is fully under their thrall, destroying the physical vessel is the only way to sever the enchantment and free his lingering spirit.",al={"why kill oben","kill sleeping druid","oben rageclaw body"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Voodoo Charm used for?",a="The charm holds the key to the enchantment controlling Oben. Once you slay his corrupted, soulless body, activating the charm over his fallen remains unravels the dark magic holding his spirit hostage.",al={"voodoo charm use","how to use voodoo charm","gnarlpine charm oben"},it="item"},{q="Where does Oben go after this quest?",a="Once his physical body is slain and the enchantment is dispelled, Oben Rageclaw's spirit is released from the mortal world. He is finally able to journey into the Emerald Dream to rest in peace.",al={"oben fate","what happens to oben rageclaw","does oben survive"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine using voodoo magic?",a="The Gnarlpine furbolgs have fallen deep into corruption and madness, turning away from their ancestral harmony to dabble in foul sorceries and crude dark magic to subjugate the creatures and sleeping druids around them.",al={"furbolg voodoo","gnarlpine voodoo magic","why do furbolgs have charms"}},{q="Who was Oben Rageclaw?",a="Oben was a night elf Druid of the Claw who entered a sacred slumber in the barrows of Teldrassil, communing with the Emerald Dream before the Gnarlpine furbolgs disturbed his rest and enslaved his mortal shell.",al={"who is oben","oben lore","oben rageclaw background"},it="identity"},{q="Is Oben's spirit still talking to me while his body is alive?",a="Yes. The dark enchantment severed Oben's soul from his flesh. His spirit manifested as a ghost near the chamber entrance, completely unable to control or re-enter the enchanted, empty shell inside.",al={"oben ghost and body","two obens","why is oben in two places"}},{q="Who is the target I am sent against in Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="You are sent to destroy the soulless physical body of Oben Rageclaw himself. While his spirit lingers outside, his sleeping mortal shell has fallen under a powerful enchantment wielded by the Gnarlpine furbolgs inside Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Devoid of his soul, the husk now acts under their corrupt dominion.",al={"who am i killing","oben target","soulless body oben"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does Oben Rageclaw need me instead of doing this himself?",a="Oben is currently an ethereal spirit, entirely severed from his mortal form. Trapped as an apparition outside the barrow chamber, he lacks physical substance to confront his enchanted shell or wield the Voodoo Charm needed to break the magic. Deep within the barrow den, far from the reach of night elf sentinels, you are the only one present capable of intervening.",al={"why does oben need me","why cant oben kill his body","why me oben rageclaw"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Seeing a slumbering Druid of the Claw desecrated by corrupted furbolgs is a chilling reminder of the perils of leaving one's physical body unattended while communing with the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="Teldrassil was meant to be a refuge for the night elves, but the rapid corruption of native furbolgs like the Gnarlpine poses an immediate threat even within their sacred barrows."},kw={"ban'ethil","druid of the claw","emerald dream","gnarlpine","oben rageclaw","teldrassil","the sleeping druid","voodoo charm"},rel={"quest:2541","npc:oben-rageclaw","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Oben Rageclaw",faction="Alliance",id=2561},src={"Druid of the Claw (quest)"}}
E["quest:3116"] = {t="quest",n="Simple Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="The Simple Sigil is an introductory summons directed to aspiring night elf warriors in Shadowglen. Delivered by Conservator Ilthalaine on behalf of the trainer Alyissia, it formally marks the recruit's transition into combat training to protect the fledgling boughs of Teldrassil.",h="The Simple Sigil is an introductory summons directed to aspiring night elf warriors in Shadowglen.",sec={{t="A Call to Arms in Shadowglen",b="After proving their basic survival skills against the restless wildlife of Shadowglen, young night elf warriors receive an inscribed sigil passed through Conservator Ilthalaine. The token is a formal request from Alyissia, the local warrior trainer stationed at Aldrassil, bidding the novice to step forward and dedicate their martial strength to defending their people.",sp=0},{t="A Tumultuous New Era",b="When reporting to Alyissia, she places the warrior's training against a backdrop of rapid and troubling changes. In just a few short years, the night elves have raised the World Tree Teldrassil, watched an insidious taint spread through forest beasts both near and far, and reconnected with ancient ancestral regions once thought lost, such as Feralas. In the face of these perils, capable defenders are urgently required.",sp=0},{t="Opening the Boughs",b="Beyond martial discipline, Alyissia prepares young Kaldorei for the world outside their sheltered glade. She advises recruits to withhold prejudice against outsiders arriving upon Teldrassil from other races. While cautioning that not every traveler acts from pure altruism, she emphasizes that allies are vital to the defense of the Kaldorei, urging her pupils to extend reasonable trust as they take up their role as protectors.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Simple Sigil?",a="It is an inscribed token sent by Alyissia, the warrior trainer in Shadowglen, delivered to novice night elf warriors to summon them for formal combat instruction.",al={"simple sigil item","what is this sigil","sigil of the warrior"}},{q="Who sends you to find Alyissia?",a="Conservator Ilthalaine delivers the sigil and directs you to Alyissia after you complete your initial tasks maintaining the balance in Shadowglen.",al={"who gives the simple sigil","quest giver simple sigil"}},{q="Where can Alyissia be found?",a="Alyissia is located within the safe haven of Shadowglen, standing near the great trunk of Aldrassil where she trains aspiring night elf warriors.",al={"alyissia location","where is alyissia","warrior trainer shadowglen"}},{q="Why does Alyissia say warriors are needed right now?",a="Recent years have brought drastic challenges: the founding of Teldrassil, widespread corruption infecting local wildlife, and the rediscovery of long-lost lands like Feralas. Skilled combatants are required to shield the Kaldorei from these encroaching threats.",al={"why do night elves need warriors","shadowglen warrior lore"}},{q="What does Alyissia say about other races visiting Teldrassil?",a="She counsels against prejudice, explaining that outsiders of other races will soon visit Teldrassil's boughs. While acknowledging that not all arrivals are purely altruistic, she advises extending a measure of trust so they might assist in the tree's defense.",al={"alyissia on other races","night elves and outsiders","alliance in teldrassil"}},{q="What is the significance of mentioning Feralas?",a="Feralas represents ancient night elf lands that were long cut off or believed lost following the Great Sundering. Its rediscovery highlights how rapidly the Kaldorei are reconnecting with the wider world after millennia of isolation.",al={"why mention feralas","feralas connection"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="This quest marks your official beginning as a Kaldorei warrior, introducing you to Alyissia as your initial mentor in arms.",["race:NightElf"]="The sigil speaks directly to the rapid changes surrounding the Kaldorei—from the planting of Teldrassil to opening their secluded home to foreign allies.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alyissia's counsel reflects the night elves' early efforts to welcome other Alliance races to their boughs despite centuries of isolation."},kw={"aldrassil","alyissia","feralas","ilthalaine","shadowglen","simple sigil","teldrassil","warrior"},rel={"npc:alyissia","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","zone:feralas"},m={start="Conservator Ilthalaine",["end"]="Alyissia",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=3116},src={"Simple Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3117"] = {t="quest",n="Etched Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="The Etched Sigil is a written summons delivered through Conservator Ilthalaine to young night elf hunters in Shadowglen. It calls them up the great boughs of Aldrassil to meet their trainer, Ayanna Everstride, and formally begin their path of archery and beastcraft.",h="The Etched Sigil is a written summons delivered through Conservator Ilthalaine to young night elf hunters in...",sec={{t="A Summons to the Boughs",b="After proving their early vigilance in defending Shadowglen, young kaldorei hunters are handed an inscribed token by Conservator Ilthalaine. Carried originally by a messenger from the hunter mentor Ayanna Everstride, the etched sigil directs the novice to climb high into the upper reaches of Aldrassil, where the trainers keep watch over the canopy.",sp=0},{t="The Path of the Hunter",b="Meeting Ayanna marks the formal start of a hunter's training on Teldrassil. She instructs novices in the dual arts of marksmanship and understanding the wild creatures of Kalimdor. Ayanna emphasizes that a true hunter must treat their beast companions with respect, maintaining awareness and humility in a world full of unseen perils.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Etched Sigil?",a="It is an inscribed message sent by the hunter trainer Ayanna Everstride to direct promising night elf novices to her post atop Aldrassil.",al={"etched sigil","what is this sigil","sigil item"}},{q="Where is Ayanna Everstride located?",a="She can be found on the upper terraces of Aldrassil, the great world-tree hollow in the center of Shadowglen.",al={"where is ayanna","find ayanna everstride","ayanna everstride location"}},{q="Who hands out the Etched Sigil?",a="Conservator Ilthalaine hands it to night elf hunters once they begin proving themselves by defending the local woodland.",al={"who gives the quest","quest giver","where do i get etched sigil"}},{q="What does Ayanna Everstride teach?",a="She trains hunters in the traditions of marksmanship, beast management, and wilderness survival while warning them never to underestimate the dangers abroad.",al={"hunter training","what does ayanna teach","why talk to ayanna"}},{q="Why does Ayanna caution hunters about their pets?",a="She reminds her students that the wilderness harbors threats far more formidable than novice hunters realize, meaning a hunter must respect their companion animals rather than treat their abilities casually.",al={"beast danger","why respect beasts","pet caution"}},{q="Is this quest available to other classes?",a="No, the Etched Sigil is specifically an introductory class summons meant solely for night elf hunters.",al={"can druids do this","is this hunter only","other classes"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This quest marks your official introduction to hunter mentorship in Teldrassil, opening the door to learning bow craft, tracking, and beast mastery.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, hunting is a sacred discipline intertwined with natural harmony and reverence for Elune, rather than mere sport."},kw={"aldrassil","ayanna everstride","etched sigil","hunter","ilthalaine","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:ayanna-everstride","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune"},m={start="Conservator Ilthalaine",["end"]="Ayanna Everstride",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=3117},src={"Etched Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3118"] = {t="quest",n="Encrypted Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="The Encrypted Sigil is an introductory summons directed to nascent night elf rogues arriving in Shadowglen. Carried by Conservator Ilthalaine on behalf of Frahun Shadewhisper, it directs covert operatives to initiate their training and heed the fragile peace threatening Kalimdor.",h="The Encrypted Sigil is an introductory summons directed to nascent night elf rogues arriving in Shadowglen.",sec={{t="A Message in the Shadows",b="While younger night elves study nature's balance under Conservator Ilthalaine, those inclined toward stealth and subterfuge receive a quieter summons. The Encrypted Sigil arrives by runner from Frahun Shadewhisper, Shadowglen's rogue mentor. Inscribed with ciphers meant solely for initiates of the trade, it instructs the bearer to decipher its contents and seek out Frahun near the roots of Aldrassil to formally begin their instruction.",sp=0},{t="Watching the Horizon",b="Frahun's message is more than a simple training appointment; it serves as a sober warning regarding the geopolitical realities of Kalimdor. With the Third War concluded, the peace between the Alliance and the emergent Horde remains paper-thin. In Shadowglen, rogue scouts and informers are urged to cultivate their eyes and ears early, monitoring potential threats and covert provocations that could spark renewed war across the borders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Encrypted Sigil?",a="It is a coded token sent by the rogue mentor Frahun Shadewhisper to new rogues in Shadowglen, directing them to report to him beneath Aldrassil for formal training.",al={"what is this sigil","encrypted sigil quest","sigil item"}},{q="Who hands the sigil to young night elves?",a="Conservator Ilthalaine delivers the sigil on Frahun's behalf once an initiate has proven basic competence in managing the local wildlife around the boughs of Shadowglen.",al={"who gives quest","quest giver","conservator ilthalaine"}},{q="Where can Frahun Shadewhisper be found?",a="Frahun Shadewhisper is stationed within the shelter of the Great Tree Aldrassil in Shadowglen, ready to instruct newly arrived night elf rogues.",al={"where is frahun","find frahun shadewhisper","frahun location"}},{q="Why are rogues needed in peaceful Teldrassil?",a="As Frahun notes, the prevailing truce with external factions is tenuous. Stealthy scouts and intelligence gatherers are vital for uncovering subterfuge, particularly concerning Horde movements and internal threats to the boughs.",al={"why do night elves need rogues","rogues in shadowglen","purpose of rogues"}},{q="What happens after presenting the sigil to Frahun?",a="Frahun accepts the cipher, acknowledges your readiness, and invites you to return as you gain experience so he can teach combat techniques, weapon handling, and the arts of stealth.",al={"what comes next","after encrypted sigil","sigil reward lore"}},{q="Does the Horde actively threaten Shadowglen directly?",a="While the remote canopy of Teldrassil is largely secluded from open Horde assault, whispers of Horde agents sowing distrust across Kalimdor keep kaldorei sentries and operatives on high alert.",al={"is horde in teldrassil","horde threat shadowglen","horde seeds of distrust"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="This task marks your entry into the kaldorei network of scouts, assassins, and intelligence gatherers tasked with protecting Teldrassil from unseen adversaries.",["race:NightElf"]="Even in the secluded haven of Aldrassil, the kaldorei maintain watchful eyes on Kalimdor's shifting borders to defend their newly planted boughs.",["faction:Alliance"]="Shadowglen's trainers remind recruits that cross-faction treaties are fragile and that intelligence work is critical to preventing Horde incursions."},kw={"aldrassil","conservator ilthalaine","encrypted sigil","frahun shadewhisper","rogue trainer","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:frahun-shadewhisper","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:horde"},m={start="Conservator Ilthalaine",["end"]="Frahun Shadewhisper",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=3118},src={"Encrypted Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3119"] = {t="quest",n="Hallowed Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="The Hallowed Sigil is an introductory summons delivered to young night elf priests beginning their training in Shadowglen. Conservator Ilthalaine passes along the message from the priest trainer Shanda, directing novice practitioners to seek guidance within Aldrassil as they learn to wield Elune's grace.",h="The Hallowed Sigil is an introductory summons delivered to young night elf priests beginning their training...",sec={{t="A Calling to Service",b="Priests in night elf culture occupy a sacred place as handmaidens and servants of the moon goddess, Elune. When a young kaldorei in Shadowglen shows an affinity for the divine light and devotion, Conservator Ilthalaine entrusts them with a hallowed sigil. Sent by messenger from the priest trainer Shanda, the token serves as a formal invitation to present oneself at the tree of Aldrassil to begin dedicated spiritual tutelage.",sp=0},{t="A Changing World",b="Upon meeting Shanda, the young acolyte finds that the sheltered sanctuary of Teldrassil is experiencing unusual upheaval. Shanda notes that the boughs of the World Tree are stirring with travelers, including members of the wider Alliance granted leave to meet with the kaldorei. While the broader world calls, Shanda advises novices to ground themselves in the troubles immediately facing Shadowglen before venturing into the wider conflicts beyond.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Hallowed Sigil?",a="It is an inscribed token sent by the priest trainer Shanda via messenger to Conservator Ilthalaine, meant to summon a novice priest for instruction in Aldrassil.",al={"hallowed sigil item","what is this sigil","sigil of shanda"}},{q="Who is Shanda?",a="Shanda is the priest trainer stationed at Aldrassil in Shadowglen. She guides fledgling night elf priests in the fundamental rites, disciplines, and prayers of the Sisterhood of Elune.",al={"priest trainer aldrassil","who is shanda"}},{q="Where is Shanda located?",a="Shanda resides inside the hollow base of Aldrassil, the massive central tree at the heart of Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",al={"find shanda","where to turn in hallowed sigil","shanda location"}},{q="Why are Alliance members visiting Teldrassil?",a="The night elves have forged ties with the Alliance following the Third War. Outside races are beginning to arrive on Teldrassil's boughs to coordinate and confer with the kaldorei as both sides prepare for the challenges facing Azeroth.",al={"alliance in teldrassil","why outsiders on world tree"}},{q="What should a priest do after completing this task?",a="Shanda advises priests to assist the local defenders and caretakers across Shadowglen, returning to her whenever they need to learn new prayers and techniques.",al={"what next after sigil","after hallowed sigil"}},{q="Why does Ilthalaine give this quest?",a="Conservator Ilthalaine oversees the earliest trials of novices in Shadowglen. When a messenger from Shanda arrived with the sigil, Ilthalaine held it until the aspiring priest proved capable of taking their next steps.",al={"conservator ilthalaine priest","why talk to ilthalaine"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="This rite of passage connects a novice kaldorei priest with Shanda, initiating their formal training in the light and wisdom of Elune.",["race:NightElf"]="The priesthood is central to kaldorei culture, governed by ancient traditions of lunar devotion that have guided their people for millennia.",["faction:Alliance"]="Shanda's remarks highlight how newly established Alliance alliances are bringing unfamiliar races and travelers directly onto Teldrassil's boughs."},kw={"aldrassil","conservator ilthalaine","elune","hallowed sigil","priest","shadowglen","shanda","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:shanda","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:alliance"},m={start="Conservator Ilthalaine",["end"]="Shanda",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=3119},src={"Hallowed Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3120"] = {t="quest",n="Verdant Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="The Verdant Sigil is a written summons delivered to newly awakened night elf druids in Shadowglen. Conservator Ilthalaine passes it along to direct fledgling shapeshifters to Mardant Strongoak within the boughs of Aldrassil. It marks the formal beginning of a druid's tutelage in the mysteries of nature and the Emerald Dream.",h="The Verdant Sigil is a written summons delivered to newly awakened night elf druids in Shadowglen.",sec={{t="A Call to the Boughs",b="Once a young night elf shows promise in maintaining the local balance of Shadowglen, a formal introduction to their order is required. Conservator Ilthalaine receives the Verdant Sigil via a runner and entrusts it to the initiate. The small token signifies that the circle in Aldrassil has taken notice and invites the young druid to formally begin their training.",sp=0},{t="Communion and the Dream",b="Upon presenting the sigil to Mardant Strongoak inside Aldrassil, the initiate is welcomed into the fold. While deeper communion with the Emerald Dream and mastering animal forms lie ahead, Mardant establishes himself as their first guide, tasked with teaching them how to interpret nature's spirits and channel raw woodland power.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Verdant Sigil?",a="It is a inscribed summons delivered through Conservator Ilthalaine on behalf of Mardant Strongoak, calling a novice druid to begin their formal training inside Aldrassil.",al={"verdant sigil item","what is this sigil","druid sigil"}},{q="Where do I take the Verdant Sigil?",a="Bring it to Mardant Strongoak, the druid trainer stationed within the great barrow-tree of Aldrassil in the heart of Shadowglen.",al={"where is mardant","turn in verdant sigil","where do i go"}},{q="Why does Mardant mention the Emerald Dream?",a="Druids draw much of their power and wisdom from the Emerald Dream through long sleeping trances. Though a novice is not yet ready to wander the Dream freely, Mardant introduces it as the foundational mystery they will eventually study.",al={"why emerald dream","mardant dream dialogue","druid trance"}},{q="Who sends the sigil to Ilthalaine?",a="A messenger sent by Mardant Strongoak delivered the sigil to Conservator Ilthalaine so it could be placed directly into the hands of a promising young druid.",al={"who sent the sigil","sigil messenger"}},{q="What happens after presenting the sigil?",a="Mardant Strongoak becomes your primary mentor in Shadowglen, allowing you to learn your earliest druidic spells and magical techniques as you grow in power.",al={"what do i learn next","after verdant sigil"}},{q="Can non-druids receive this quest?",a="No. The Verdant Sigil is strictly meant for night elf druids beginning their journey in Shadowglen. Other classes receive their own distinct summons to their respective trainers.",al={"is this druid only","who gets verdant sigil"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="This quest represents your formal initiation into the Cenarion circle's teachings under Mardant Strongoak, setting you on the long path toward understanding the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="Druidism is deeply woven into night elf culture; presenting this sigil at Aldrassil marks the first step of an initiate stepping into an ancient tradition."},kw={"aldrassil","druid trainer","emerald dream","ilthalaine","mardant strongoak","shadowglen","verdant sigil"},rel={"npc:mardant-strongoak","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Conservator Ilthalaine",["end"]="Mardant Strongoak",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=3120},src={"Verdant Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3519"] = {t="quest",n="A Friend in Need",z="teldrassil",s="A Friend in Need is an urgent plea for aid from Iverron, a young night elf found suffering from venomous spider bites in Shadowglen. Struck down by the deadly beast Githyiss the Vile, Iverron sends travelers to find Dirania Silvershine before the venom claims him.",h="A Friend in Need is an urgent plea for aid from Iverron, a young night elf found suffering from venomous...",sec={{t="A Reckless Venture",b="Shadowglen's sprawling canopies shelter all manner of wildlife, but the nearby webbed hollows house far darker threats. Ignoring past warnings, Iverron ventured too close to the local webwood caverns and encountered Githyiss the Vile, a vicious spider whose venom quickly overwhelmed the young elf. Stricken with dizziness and failing strength, he is entirely unable to reach safety on his own.",sp=0},{t="A Call to Aldrassil",b="Desperate for survival, Iverron directs any passerby to race back toward the central tree of Aldrassil and alert Dirania Silvershine. Dirania, accustomed to looking out for him and familiar with the hazards of the glen, represents his only hope of preparing a life-saving antidote before the toxin proves fatal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Iverron?",a="Iverron is a young night elf living in Shadowglen within Teldrassil. He frequently wanders into dangerous places despite the warnings of his companions, which leads to his near-fatal encounter with Githyiss the Vile.",al={"iverron lore","who is the poisoned elf","who gives a friend in need"},it="identity"},{q="What attacked Iverron?",a="He was bitten by Githyiss the Vile, a notorious, highly poisonous spider lurking inside the spider cave nestled within Shadowglen.",al={"what bit iverron","who is githyiss","what spider poisoned him"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Dirania Silvershine?",a="Dirania Silvershine is a night elf residing at Aldrassil in Shadowglen. She is a close friend and guardian figure to Iverron who knows how to treat venomous injuries.",al={"dirania role","who to talk to for iverron"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The quest takes place entirely within Shadowglen, the sheltered starting vale of the night elves nestled high on the crown of Teldrassil.",al={"where is a friend in need","iverron location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after reporting Iverron's condition to Dirania?",a="Dirania immediately sets to work preparing a remedy, dispatching adventurers across the grove to gather the rare reagents needed to brew an antidote before Iverron succumbs to the poison.",al={"what next after a friend in need","does iverron get saved"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why are there deadly spiders inside Shadowglen?",a="Though Shadowglen is considered a safe haven for young night elves, the corruption spreading across Teldrassil has stirred wild beasts and vermin like the webwood spiders into unusually aggressive, venomous predators.",al={"why are there spiders in shadowglen","spider corruption teldrassil"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Iverron want this done?",a="Iverron was bitten by the venomous webwood spider Githyiss the Vile while exploring a nearby cave. The deadly poison is rapidly spreading through his veins, leaving him weak, dizzy, and fearing for his life. Knowing he cannot cure the affliction on his own, he urgently needs Dirania Silvershine to intervene before the venom overcomes him entirely.",al={"why does iverron need help","iverron motive","what happened to iverron"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Iverron need you instead of seeking help himself?",a="The venom from Githyiss the Vile has struck Iverron hard, leaving him severely disoriented and barely able to stand. Stranded alone in the wild, he cannot make the trek back to Aldrassil without collapsing. You are the only capable traveler who found him in time to sprint back and summon Dirania's aid.",al={"why can't iverron go himself","why me a friend in need","why doesn't iverron get guards"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young kaldorei beginning their training beneath Aldrassil, Iverron's predicament is a stark reminder that even the sheltered boughs of Shadowglen are no longer free from corruption and deadly peril.",["class:Druid"]="Druids learn early on that the imbalance in the local wildlife can strike down the unwary, underscoring the urgent need to understand and counter nature's venoms."},kw={"aldrassil","dirania silvershine","githyiss","iverron","poison","shadowglen","spider","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:iverron","npc:dirania-silvershine","quest:4495","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Iverron",["end"]="Dirania Silvershine",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=3519},src={"A Friend in Need (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3521"] = {t="quest",n="Iverron's Antidote",z="teldrassil",s="Iverron's Antidote is an urgent task in Shadowglen to save a poisoned night elf scout. By gathering wild mushrooms, lilies, and spider ichor, adventurers help Dirania Silvershine brew a remedy before the venom takes full hold.",h="Iverron's Antidote is an urgent task in Shadowglen to save a poisoned night elf scout.",sec={{t="A Race Against Venom",b="While scouting the boughs of Shadowglen, young Iverron fell victim to the poisonous fangs of the local Webwood spiders. Collapsed and dying, his survival depends entirely on the herbal knowledge of Dirania Silvershine at Aldrassil. With the youth fading fast, she must quickly prepare a specialized concoction to neutralize the aggressive venom coursing through his blood.",sp=0},{t="Reagents of Shadowglen",b="Dirania's recipe relies on the restorative flora of Teldrassil balanced against the venom itself. Hyacinth mushrooms, favored by the thieving grell to the south, provide an earthy base, while delicate Moonpetal lilies gathered from tranquil forest pools offer purifying qualities. To finish the draft, a sample of Webwood ichor must be extracted directly from the spiders prowling near Shadowthread Cave to tailor the cure to their specific poison.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Iverron?",a="Iverron is a young night elf in Shadowglen who ventured too close to the hostile Webwood spiders and was struck down by their lethal venom.",al={"iverron","who is iverron","who poisoned"},it="identity"},{q="Who gives the quest Iverron's Antidote?",a="Dirania Silvershine, an attendant stationed outside the great boughs of Aldrassil in Shadowglen, provides the quest and concocts the remedy.",al={"quest giver","dirania","dirania silvershine"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the antidote need spider ichor?",a="In traditional herbal remedies, introducing a component of the creature's own bodily fluids or venom helps counteract the specific toxins inflicting the victim.",al={"why spider ichor","webwood ichor use","spider venom cure"},it="item"},{q="Where are Hyacinth Mushrooms found?",a="Hyacinth mushrooms grow at the bases of large trees throughout Shadowglen and can also be pried from the clutches of grell who hoard them to the south.",al={"where to find hyacinth mushrooms","hyacinth mushroom location"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where do Moonpetal Lilies grow?",a="Moonpetal lilies bloom along the edges of the quiet, fresh-water pools tucked away on the northwestern side of Aldrassil.",al={"moonpetal lily location","where are lilies"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where are the Webwood spiders located?",a="Webwood spiders dwell in the northern woods of Shadowglen, especially around the dark entrance of Shadowthread Cave.",al={"webwood spider location","spider location shadowglen"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why does Dirania Silvershine want this done?",a="Dirania knows how to brew a remedy that can neutralize the deadly poison coursing through Iverron. Without quick intervention, his condition will deteriorate, and she relies on your speed to gather the necessary forest ingredients before it is too late to save him.",al={"dirania silvershine motive","why help iverron","why make the antidote"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Hyacinth Mushroom used for?",a="Hyacinth mushrooms are native fungi that grow beneath the great boughs of Shadowglen. Dirania uses them as a primary herbal component to brew the antidote, balancing the harsher venoms and neutralizing the toxin invading Iverron's body.",al={"hyacinth mushroom purpose","why hyacinth mushroom","hyacinth mushroom lore"},it="item",add=true},{q="What is the Moonpetal Lily used for?",a="Moonpetal lilies are delicate aquatic blossoms that thrive along the tranquil forest pools of Shadowglen. Dirania blends them into her remedy to harness their soothing natural properties and counter the virulent spider venom.",al={"moonpetal lily purpose","why moonpetal lily","moonpetal lily lore"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Tending to fallen kin is sacred duty in Shadowglen, where every defender is needed to protect the newly budding World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="Crafting remedies from local flora and neutralizing natural poisons reflects the fundamental balance druids strive to maintain within the wild.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Gathering Moonpetal lilies and Hyacinth mushrooms showcases how wild plants of Teldrassil possess potent medicinal properties when handled with care."},kw={"aldrassil","antidote","dirania silvershine","hyacinth mushroom","iverron","moonpetal lily","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","webwood ichor"},rel={"npc:iverron","npc:dirania-silvershine","subzone:shadowglen","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowthread-cave","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune"},m={start="Dirania Silvershine",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=3521,ri={"Hyacinth Mushroom","Moonpetal Lily","Webwood Ichor"}},src={"Iverron's Antidote (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3522"] = {t="quest",n="Iverron's Antidote",z="teldrassil",s="This errand tasks an adventurer with racing against time to deliver freshly brewed medicine to a poisoned night elf scout. Stranded outside a spider-infested cave in Shadowglen, Iverron depends entirely on Dirania Silvershine's herbal concoction before the potent mixture loses its efficacy.",h="This errand tasks an adventurer with racing against time to deliver freshly brewed medicine to a poisoned...",sec={{t="A Race Against the Clock",b="Dirania Silvershine crafts the curative brew using freshly harvested venom sacs, lily roots, and hyacinth fungi, but its unstable alchemical nature poses a grave risk. The medicine retains its potency for a mere five minutes after distillation. Anyone carrying the vial must sprint directly from the glade toward the northern heights without hesitation.",sp=0},{t="A Habit of Trouble",b="Iverron has fallen victim to the Webwood spiders lurking around the barrows and caves of Shadowglen. By his own admission, he possesses an unfortunate knack for stumbling into danger, relying frequently on Dirania's herbal expertise to extract him from perilous circumstances. Even after quaffing the antidote, his recovery remains fragile, leaving him wary of the hostile arachnids that still guard his way home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is there a time limit on delivering the antidote?",a="The antidote mixed by Dirania Silvershine relies on raw natural ingredients and fresh venom. Its active healing properties degrade rapidly once prepared, rendering it completely useless if not consumed within five minutes of leaving her care.",al={"why five minutes","antidote timer","timed quest"},it="item"},{q="Where is Iverron located?",a="Iverron is slumped against the exterior rocks outside the northern cave in Shadowglen, north of the main path through the grove.",al={"where is iverron","iverron location","find iverron"},it="target",gp=true},{q="How was Iverron poisoned?",a="He was struck by the venomous Webwood spiders that inhabit the northern outskirts of Shadowglen, an aggressive breed that has multiplied around the roots and caves of Teldrassil.",al={"who poisoned iverron","why is iverron sick","iverron poison"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after Iverron drinks the antidote?",a="Though the poison is neutralized, Iverron remains too weak and shaken to travel safely on his own, prompting him to ask for aid in clearing out the nearby Webwood spiders blocking his route back to safety.",al={"what next iverron","after iverron antidote","iverron follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What relationship do Dirania and Iverron have?",a="Dirania Silvershine is a capable herbalist and healer in Shadowglen who frequently rescues Iverron from his misadventures. Iverron openly acknowledges that getting into trouble is second nature to him and that Dirania is constantly bailing him out.",al={"dirania and iverron","who is dirania to iverron","are they friends"},it="ties"},{q="What happens if the antidote expires before reaching him?",a="If the volatile brew spoils before delivery, the task cannot be completed. You must return to Dirania Silvershine in Shadowglen to obtain a fresh dose and make the run again.",al={"antidote expired","failed timer","lost antidote"},gp=true},{q="Why does Dirania Silvershine want you to deliver the antidote?",a="Iverron has fallen victim to deadly spider venom in the wilds of Shadowglen and will die without immediate intervention. Dirania Silvershine has already prepared the cure, but the mixture is unstable and will spoil quickly if it is not administered without delay. She cares for Iverron and routinely helps bail him out of trouble, making your rapid delivery a matter of life and death.",al={"dirania silvershine motive","why help iverron","why does dirania want this done"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves training within Shadowglen, rescuing Iverron serves as a sobering reminder of the growing corruption and aggression stirring among Teldrassil's native wildlife.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The volatile nature of the draught demonstrates the challenges of working with raw woodland flora, where botanical concoctions lose their vital properties almost immediately without proper preservation."},kw={"antidote","dirania silvershine","iverron","shadowglen","teldrassil","venom","webwood spider"},rel={"npc:iverron","npc:dirania-silvershine","quest:3521","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Dirania Silvershine",["end"]="Iverron",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=3522},src={"Iverron's Antidote (2)"}}
E["quest:4161"] = {t="quest",n="Recipe of the Kaldorei",z="teldrassil",s="Recipe of the Kaldorei is a lesson in balance taught by Zarrin, a culinary instructor in Dolanaar. By gathering a precise number of spider legs across Teldrassil, aspiring cooks learn that sustaining oneself from nature requires restraint and respect.",h="Recipe of the Kaldorei is a lesson in balance taught by Zarrin, a culinary instructor in Dolanaar.",sec={{t="Children of the Stars",b="Behind the inn in Dolanaar, Zarrin tends a bubbling cauldron and instructs young adventurers on the traditions of his people. Long before the modern age, night elves knew themselves as the kaldorei, meaning 'children of the stars.' For Zarrin, understanding that ancestral heritage begins not on the battlefield, but in the relationship between a hunter, their food, and the surrounding boughs of Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="Taking Only What Is Needed",b="The core of the lesson lies in restraint. Zarrin charges his pupils with gathering small spider legs from the woodland arachnids outside Shadowglen, but specifically commands that only seven be taken—no more. In night elven culture, living in harmony with nature demands taking strictly what is necessary and returning kindness to the wild. This delicate balance must be upheld even in troubled times, a philosophy that transforms a simple spider kabob into a moral discipline.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zarrin?",a="Zarrin is a night elf culinary mentor found tending a cauldron behind the inn in Dolanaar. He instructs young adventurers in cooking while emphasizing the importance of ancestral kaldorei values.",al={"zarrin","who is zarrin","dolanaar cook","cooking trainer dolanaar"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Zarrin insist on collecting exactly seven spider legs?",a="Zarrin emphasizes that the kaldorei must live in harmony with nature, taking only what is needed to survive. Gathering strictly the required amount instills respect for the living forest and preserves the natural balance.",al={"why seven legs","why only seven","take no more than seven"},it="motive"},{q="What does the word 'kaldorei' mean?",a="In the Darnassian tongue, kaldorei translates to 'children of the stars,' the ancient name by which the night elf people have known themselves for thousands of years.",al={"what does kaldorei mean","kaldorei meaning","children of the stars"},it="origin"},{q="Where are the spider legs gathered?",a="The legs can be harvested from webwood spiders roaming the forests of Teldrassil outside of the sheltered borders of Shadowglen.",al={"where do spiders drop legs","spider leg location","which spiders"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What do night elves prepare with spider legs?",a="Zarrin teaches adventurers how to prepare Kaldorei Spider Kabobs, a traditional wilderness dish that turns woodland spider meat into a nourishing, travel-ready meal.",al={"what is the recipe","kaldorei spider kabob","spider food"},it="item"},{q="Do all spiders in Teldrassil yield the legs needed?",a="No. The immature spiders found within the protected vale of Shadowglen do not yield the proper legs for Zarrin's recipe; one must hunt the spiders wandering the broader woods of Teldrassil.",al={"do shadowglen spiders work","shadowglen spider legs"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What spiders are you hunting in Teldrassil?",a="You are sent to hunt the wild webwood spiders roaming the forests outside Shadowglen. While spiders are a natural part of the boughs of Teldrassil, Zarrin asks you to cull only what you need so that you respect the forest's harmony rather than slaughter aimlessly.",al={"what spiders drop legs","which spiders to hunt","teldrassil spiders"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="This task serves as an early introduction to wilderness cooking in Teldrassil, rewarding the recipe for Kaldorei Spider Kabobs.",["race:NightElf"]="The lesson reinforces the core kaldorei worldview: maintaining harmony with nature by exercising restraint and taking only what is necessary."},kw={"cooking","dolanaar","kaldorei","recipe of the kaldorei","spider kabob","teldrassil","zarrin"},rel={"npc:zarrin","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","subzone:shadowglen","topic:alliance"},m={start="Zarrin",level="7",faction="Alliance",id=4161,ri={"Small Spider Leg"}},src={"Recipe of the Kaldorei"}}
E["quest:4495"] = {t="quest",n="A Good Friend",z="teldrassil",s="Dirania Silvershine grows anxious when her regular visitor, Iverron, fails to appear on time at Aldrassil. Knowing he frequents the hills near the spider-infested Shadowthread Cave to the north, she asks passing adventurers to search for him.",h="Dirania Silvershine grows anxious when her regular visitor, Iverron, fails to appear on time at Aldrassil.",sec={{t="A Missing Visitor",b="Daily routine runs deep in the tranquil boughs of Shadowglen, making any break in pattern stand out immediately. Dirania Silvershine, tending her affairs beneath the sheltering canopy of Aldrassil, is accustomed to visits from Iverron like clockwork every day. When hours pass without a sign of him, her concern drives her to seek assistance from those setting out into the wilds of the barrow bough.",sp=0},{t="Peril at Shadowthread Cave",b="Iverron has a well-known habit of wandering near the northern hollows of Shadowglen, despite the encroaching menace of webwood spiders. With Shadowthread Cave crawling with aggressive arachnids, stepping off the established paths is increasingly hazardous for careless travelers. Searching the rugged slopes just west of the cavern mouth reveals Iverron tucked away in hiding, desperate for aid.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dirania Silvershine?",a="Dirania Silvershine is a night elf residing in Shadowglen beneath Aldrassil. She maintains a steady daily friendship with Iverron and notices immediately when he fails to keep his customary visiting hours.",al={"dirania","dirania silvershine lore","who starts a good friend"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Iverron?",a="Iverron is a night elf in Shadowglen known for wandering the hills near Shadowthread Cave. After failing to make his daily visit to Dirania Silvershine, he is found stranded on the cliffs just west of the cavern entrance.",al={"iverron","where is iverron","who is the missing friend"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Iverron be found?",a="Iverron is hiding among the rocks and brush on the hillside directly west of the entrance to Shadowthread Cave, in the northern part of Shadowglen.",al={"iverron location","finding iverron","shadowthread cave iverron"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the northern cave considered dangerous?",a="Shadowthread Cave and its surrounding slopes are overrun with venomous webwood spiders. The swelling corruption on Teldrassil has agitated these creatures, making the area perilous for solitary travelers.",al={"why is shadowthread cave dangerous","spiders in shadowglen","spider cave teldrassil"},it="danger"},{q="What happens after finding Iverron?",a="Upon locating Iverron, he reveals that his misadventure near the spider cave has left him in dire straits, beginning a search for treatment in the follow-up quest, A Friend in Need.",al={"quest after a good friend","next step for iverron","a friend in need quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why was Dirania so quick to worry about Iverron?",a="Iverron visits Dirania at the exact same hour every single day. Because he was several hours late and frequently roamed near the dangerous spider hollows, she feared the worst had happened to him.",al={"why is dirania worried","iverron routine","why did dirania notice"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Dirania Silvershine need my help specifically?",a="Dirania is not issuing a formal military request or mobilizing the Sentinels—she is simply asking a passing adventurer for a personal favor. Because Iverron is known to frequent the hazardous hills near the northern cave, she hopes that someone capable of handling the local wildlife will keep an eye out while traveling that direction.",al={"why ask me dirania","why cant dirania look for iverron","why not send guards"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young kaldorei starting their journey under Aldrassil, answering Dirania's request is an early lesson in communal responsibility and the spreading threats that disturb the once-peaceful glade.",["class:Druid"]="Druids mindful of the natural balance will recognize the aggressive webwood spiders near Shadowthread Cave as a symptom of the wider corruption afflicting the great bough."},kw={"a good friend","aldrassil","dirania silvershine","iverron","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","spiders","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:iverron","npc:dirania-silvershine","quest:3519","quest:3521","subzone:shadowthread-cave","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Dirania Silvershine",["end"]="Iverron",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=4495},src={"A Good Friend"}}
E["quest:456"] = {t="quest",n="The Balance of Nature",z="teldrassil",s="\"The Balance of Nature\" is the introductory quest offered to newly awakened night elves in Shadowglen. Bestowed by Conservator Ilthalaine, it charges young adventurers with culling overgrown populations of young nightsabers and thistle boars. The task introduces new heroes to the ancient kaldorei duty of stewarding and preserving the natural harmony of Teldrassil.",h="\"The Balance of Nature\" is the introductory quest offered to newly awakened night elves in Shadowglen.",sec={{t="A Delicate Harmony",b="Teldrassil may appear wild and ancient, but its ecosystems are young and fragile. In Shadowglen, sheltered beneath the Great Tree's sprawling boughs, heavy spring rains have disrupted the forest's delicate cycle. Certain wildlife populations flourished beyond the land's capacity to sustain them, threatening to strip the glen of resources and plunge the entire ecosystem into famine. Preserving the forest requires proactive stewardship.",sp=0},{t="The Conservator's Call",b="Conservator Ilthalaine watches over the woods of Shadowglen, ensuring that no single element overtakes another. To prevent mass starvation among the animals, he sends young night elves out into the grove to thin the thistle boars and predatory nightsabers. It is an unglamorous but vital responsibility, establishing the core philosophy of kaldorei culture: harmony with nature demands active balance and difficult decisions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do the nightsabers and boars need to be killed?",a="Heavy spring rains caused the young nightsaber and thistle boar populations to boom. Shadowglen can only sustain so much wildlife, and the overgrown herds risk stripping the grove of food and starving themselves and other creatures.",al={"why kill boars","why kill nightsabers","balance of nature reason"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Conservator Ilthalaine?",a="Conservator Ilthalaine is a kaldorei guardian stationed in Shadowglen. His sworn duty is to monitor the grove's wildlife and vegetation to ensure nature's harmony remains intact.",al={"who is ilthalaine","quest giver","conservator ilthalaine lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The quest takes place in Shadowglen, a secluded forest enclave situated within the branches of Teldrassil, the World Tree off the coast of northern Kalimdor.",al={"quest location","where is shadowglen","starting area night elf"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What comes next after completing this task?",a="Ilthalaine tasks you with a second part of the culling, while also presenting you with a class-specific sigil that directs you to your first trainer in Aldrassil.",al={"follow up quest","next quest in chain"},it="next_step"},{q="What are the beasts you are sent to hunt?",a="You are sent against the young nightsabers and young thistle boars roaming the surrounding woods of Shadowglen. They are native wildlife of the great world tree, Teldrassil. Following unusually heavy spring rains, both populations have exploded in numbers, threatening to strip the glen of food and throw the local woodland into chaos.",al={"what are nightsabers and boars","who are you hunting in shadowglen","young nightsaber young thistle boar"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="This task marks the first step of your journey as an adult protector of the kaldorei, learning that nature's balance requires active intervention and respect.",["class:Druid"]="For budding druids, this culling is a direct lesson in the harsh realities of Cenarion stewardship: protecting the wilds sometimes requires shedding blood to save the whole.",["class:Hunter"]="Learning to track and cull aggressive wildlife forms the foundation of every hunter's communion with the beasts of Kalimdor."},kw={"aldrassil","balance of nature","ilthalaine","kaldorei","nightsaber","shadowglen","teldrassil","thistle boar"},rel={"npc:ilthalaine","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","quest:3120","quest:3117","quest:3119","quest:3118"},m={start="Conservator Ilthalaine",level="2",faction="Alliance",id=456},src={"The Balance of Nature (Classic)"}}
E["quest:457"] = {t="quest",n="The Balance of Nature",z="teldrassil",s="This task continues Conservator Ilthalaine's effort to preserve Shadowglen's fragile ecology by culling mature thistle boars and mangy nightsabers. As Teldrassil's wildlife multiplies unchecked, night elf guardians must step in to prevent the overpopulation of predators and foragers from stripping the boughs bare.",h="This task continues Conservator Ilthalaine's effort to preserve Shadowglen's fragile ecology by culling...",sec={{t="A Burden of Stewardship",b="While culling young animals stabilizes future growth, the adult populations of Shadowglen also pose an immediate threat to the World Tree's ecosystem. Conservator Ilthalaine directs young defenders deeper into the forest to hunt mature thistle boars and older, mangy nightsabers before their ravenous appetites exhaust the land's finite flora and game.",sp=0},{t="Predator and Prey",b="North of Aldrassil, the forest shifts as younger cubs give way to mottled nightsabers and aggressive boars rooting up the soil. Though killing creatures of the wild is a grim duty, kaldorei doctrine views controlled hunting as a necessary responsibility to protect the whole forest from ecological collapse.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Conservator Ilthalaine having these beasts culled?",a="Without intervention, the burgeoning populations of thistle boars and nightsabers would strip Shadowglen of its vital resources, leaving the land barren and unable to sustain any life on Teldrassil's boughs.",al={"why kill boars and sabers","why balance of nature","reason for hunting"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the mangy nightsabers and thistle boars located?",a="They wander the northern half of Shadowglen, past the boughs of Aldrassil. Look for spotted coats on the nightsabers rather than the striped coats of the younger cubs found closer to the sanctuary.",al={"where are mangy nightsabers","thistle boar location","where to find them"},gp=true},{q="Who is Conservator Ilthalaine?",a="Conservator Ilthalaine is a caretaker of Shadowglen tasked with overseeing the health of Teldrassil's starting glade and guiding newly awakened night elves in maintaining the balance of the forest.",al={"who is ilthalaine","conservator ilthalaine lore"},it="identity"},{q="How does this fit into night elf beliefs about nature?",a="Night elves venerate nature, but stewardship requires managing overgrowth. Allowing one species to overpopulate and starve out others harms the forest as a whole, making culling a sorrowful but vital duty.",al={"night elf nature beliefs","why druids kill animals","kaldorei balance"},it="origin"},{q="Is this the end of the Balance of Nature chain?",a="This is the second and final step in the initial Balance of Nature chain, though other tasks soon arise to address the deeper, more unnatural corruption troubling Teldrassil's wildlife.",al={"does balance of nature continue","what comes after balance of nature"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why are the nightsabers described as mangy?",a="They are older, rougher predators roaming the fringes of the glade whose heavy numbers push the limits of Shadowglen's food supply, leaving many scruffy and aggressive.",al={"why mangy","what is wrong with the sabers"}},{q="Why are you sent against mangy nightsabers and thistle boars?",a="These nightsabers and thistle boars populate the northern reaches of Shadowglen. Left unchecked, their unchecked numbers threaten to strip the woodland of its limited nourishment. Conservator Ilthalaine directs you to cull them so the local flora and other woodland creatures can endure.",al={"why kill nightsabers and boars","mangy nightsabers thistle boars purpose","target nightsabers and boars"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does Conservator Ilthalaine ask you instead of the Sentinels?",a="Shadowglen is a sanctum for training young night elves in their heritage, duty, and martial ways. Ilthalaine tasks you with managing the local wildlife not only to ease the burden on forest wardens and Sentinels, but to test your dedication to safeguarding the land and its harmony.",al={"why does ilthalaine need me","why not sentinels","why ask adventurer balance of nature"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves, this task represents their earliest lesson in the harsh realities of wilderness stewardship upon Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="Druidic teachings emphasize harmony over sentimentality; thinning overgrown packs preserves the great web of life.",["class:Hunter"]="Taking down swift sabers and stubborn boars teaches the tracking and culling skills essential to keeping nature in check."},kw={"aldrassil","balance of nature","culling","ilthalaine","mangy nightsaber","shadowglen","teldrassil","thistle boar"},rel={"quest:456","npc:ilthalaine","subzone:shadowglen","subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Conservator Ilthalaine",level="3",faction="Alliance",id=457},src={"The Balance of Nature (2)"}}
E["quest:458"] = {t="quest",n="The Woodland Protector",z="teldrassil",s="The Woodland Protector is an introductory task in Shadowglen given by the druid Melithar Staghelm. Alerted by the whisperings of forest spirits, Melithar asks you to seek out Tarindrella, an elusive dryad who has unexpectedly returned to the grove. Her presence hints that something troubling stirs beneath the canopy of Teldrassil.",h="The Woodland Protector is an introductory task in Shadowglen given by the druid Melithar Staghelm.",sec={{t="Whispers in the Glen",b="While training novices beneath the boughs of Aldrassil, Melithar Staghelm receives troubling omens from the woodland spirits. The dryad Tarindrella, regarded as a protector of the wild, has reappeared in Shadowglen after an absence from Kalimdor's woodlands spanning many years. Because dryads rarely emerge without cause, Melithar fears an imbalance in the natural order.",sp=0},{t="Seeking the Dryad",b="Directed by a Sentinel scouting report, newly awakened defenders venture southwest of Aldrassil into the surrounding woods. Finding Tarindrella reveals that Melithar's instincts were accurate: the daughter of Cenarius has indeed returned to address an encroaching taint affecting the barrow and surrounding glades.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Melithar Staghelm, a night elf druid stationed on the lower platforms of Aldrassil in Shadowglen, provides this quest to newly awakened adventurers.",al={"quest giver","who gives quest","melithar quest"},gp=true},{q="Where can I find Tarindrella?",a="Tarindrella is located in the forest southwest of Aldrassil, standing near the wooded paths of Shadowglen.",al={"tarindrella location","where is tarindrella","find dryad"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Tarindrella?",a="Tarindrella is a dryad, one of the immortal daughters of Cenarius. Revered as woodland protectors, dryads are deeply bound to the health of the forest and rarely intervene directly unless nature faces a significant threat.",al={"who is tarindrella","tarindrella lore","dryad shadowglen"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Melithar concerned about her return?",a="Tarindrella's presence had not been felt across the forests of Kalimdor in years. Her sudden reappearance in the newly grown boughs of Teldrassil suggests that something has gone amiss in the grove.",al={"why is melithar worried","melithar staghelm concern"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after finding Tarindrella?",a="Speaking with Tarindrella completes the errand and immediately leads into her request for aid, enlisting you to investigate the corrupted flora and fauna creeping through Shadowglen.",al={"next quest","what next","tarindrella followup"},it="next_step"},{q="Is Melithar Staghelm related to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm?",a="Melithar shares the Staghelm surname with Archdruid Fandral Staghelm, the leader of the night elf druids residing in Darnassus, though no family tie between them is known; Melithar focuses his duties on mentoring fledglings in Shadowglen.",al={"melithar fandral relation","is melithar staghelm related"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Melithar Staghelm send an adventurer instead of handling it himself?",a="Melithar Staghelm is tending to Aldrassil and the delicate spirits of Shadowglen, where strange tidings and growing unrest keep the druids and Sentinels watchful. When news arrived that the reclusive dryad Tarindrella had suddenly appeared, Melithar needed a capable, discreet courier to seek her out southwest of the boughs without abandoning his post in the glade.",al={"why send me","why melithar doesn't go","why does melithar need me"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves stepping out from Aldrassil, meeting one of Cenarius's daughters serves as their first direct duty in preserving the harmony of their fledgling World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold dryads in high esteem as kin in nature; responding to Tarindrella's presence is an early calling to heed the balance of the Emerald Dream and the woods."},kw={"aldrassil","dryad","melithar staghelm","shadowglen","tarindrella","teldrassil","woodland protector"},rel={"npc:tarindrella","npc:melithar-staghelm","subzone:shadowglen","subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","topic:sentinels"},m={start="Melithar Staghelm",["end"]="Tarindrella",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=458},src={"The Woodland Protector (Classic)"}}
E["quest:459"] = {t="quest",n="The Woodland Protector",z="teldrassil",s="Tarindrella, a dryad tending to Shadowglen, seeks to uncover the source behind the sudden aggression of local creatures and the disappearance of the nearby furbolgs. By investigating the wild grells and gathering samples of corrupt Fel Moss, adventurers confirm that dark magic has begun to fester in the roots of the World Tree.",h="Tarindrella, a dryad tending to Shadowglen, seeks to uncover the source behind the sudden aggression of local...",sec={{t="A Blight in the Glade",b="Even within the secluded heights of Shadowglen, the tranquil nature of Teldrassil has begun to fracture. Dryads like Tarindrella have noticed a dark shift sweeping through the woods. The once-placid furbolgs abandoned their ancestral dens, reorganizing into the aggressive Gnarlpine tribe, while feral grells and grellkin began overrunning the woodland paths.",sp=0},{t="Tainted Growth",b="Tarindrella suspects that unnatural corruption fuels the forest's hostility. By slaying the swarming grells and collecting samples of Fel Moss, you provide undeniable proof of dark enchantments clinging to the boughs of Teldrassil. With this grim truth confirmed, Tarindrella directs young defenders toward the village of Dolanaar to confer with Druid Athridas Bearmantle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tarindrella?",a="Tarindrella is a dryad watcher stationed in the wilds of Shadowglen. As a daughter of Cenarius, she dedicates herself to preserving the flora and fauna of the glade and alerting night elf protectors when corruption threatens the balance.",al={"tarindrella","who is the questgiver","shadowglen dryad"},it="identity"},{q="What is Fel Moss?",a="Fel Moss is a tainted growth infused with dark magic that has begun clinging to the wildlife in Shadowglen. Its presence enrages and warps creatures like the grells, driving them into unnatural aggression.",al={"fel moss","what is fel moss","moss corruption"},it="item"},{q="What happened to the furbolgs in Shadowglen?",a="The furbolgs who once lived peacefully in the glade have abandoned their traditional dwellings. Corrupted by the insidious rot spreading through Teldrassil, they have banded together under the banner of the hostile Gnarlpine tribe.",al={"furbolg mystery","gnarlpine tribe","where did the furbolgs go"},it="history"},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="Having confirmed that Fel Moss has taken root in Shadowglen, Tarindrella directs travelers deeper into Teldrassil to the settlement of Dolanaar. There, the druid Athridas Bearmantle investigates the broader spread of this corruption across the World Tree.",al={"next quest","where do i go after","athridas bearmantle"},it="next_step"},{q="What are grells and grellkin?",a="Grells and their kin are mischievous, diminutive woodland spirits native to the boughs of Teldrassil. Normally unruly pests, they become violently aggressive when exposed to corrupting influences like Fel Moss.",al={"grells","grellkin","what are grells"},it="threat"},{q="Why is corruption present on Teldrassil?",a="Though Teldrassil was grown to restore the night elves' lost immortality and give them a new sanctuary, dark energies have begun seeping into its boughs and wildlife, troubling the druids and forest spirits tasked with its warding.",al={"why is teldrassil corrupted","shadowglen corruption"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Tarindrella want you to gather Fel Moss?",a="Tarindrella senses a dark, corrupting influence creeping through Shadowglen. The peaceful furbolgs abandoned their ancestral homes to muster as the hostile Gnarlpine tribe, and grells have surged into the abandoned groves. She needs physical proof that Fel Moss is responsible for driving the local wildlife and spirits mad, allowing her to confirm the source of the taint threatening the World Tree.",al={"why does tarindrella need fel moss","tarindrella motive fel moss","why collect fel moss"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who are you being sent to fight?",a="You are sent to hunt the grells and grellkin infesting the hills where the furbolgs once lived. These small, mischievous woodland spirits have fallen under a dark enchantment, turning violently aggressive toward the inhabitants of Shadowglen while carrying the tainted Fel Moss that fuels their unnatural malice.",al={"what are we fighting","who has the fel moss","target grells and grellkin"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young Kaldorei setting out from Aldrassil, this task is an early, alarming realization that their sacred new home is vulnerable to corruption from within.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold a sacred bond with the spirits and dryads of the forest; investigating the tainted Fel Moss is vital to diagnosing the spiritual sickness afflicting the World Tree."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","fel moss","gnarlpine","grell","grellkin","shadowglen","tarindrella","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:458","npc:tarindrella","subzone:shadowglen","npc:athridas-bearmantle","subzone:dolanaar","topic:furbolg","topic:druid","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Tarindrella",level="3",faction="Alliance",id=459,ri={"Fel Moss"}},src={"The Woodland Protector (2)"}}
E["quest:475"] = {t="quest",n="A Troubling Breeze",z="teldrassil",s="A Troubling Breeze is an early task given by Athridas Bearmantle in Teldrassil to investigate missing reports from Starbreeze Village. Great Warden Gaerolas Talvethren guards the hibernating Druids of the Talon nearby, and his sudden silence suggests an unnatural danger creeping across the World Tree.",h="A Troubling Breeze is an early task given by Athridas Bearmantle in Teldrassil to investigate missing reports...",sec={{t="A Silent Watcher",b="In the bough settlements of Teldrassil, communication is normally swift and measured. Athridas Bearmantle relies on word from Gaerolas Talvethren, the Great Warden entrusted with watching over the Druids of the Talon resting within the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. These slumbering druids maintain the sacred pact with Ysera in the Emerald Dream, making their sanctuary vital to the spiritual balance of the young World Tree. When reports from the east ceased, an unsettling foreboding settled through the forest canopy.",sp=0},{t="Unease in Starbreeze",b="Athridas asks travelers to venture east across the forest to Starbreeze Village to seek out Gaerolas in person. The lack of messengers is no mere oversight; foul corruption and agitated wildlife have begun stirring in the wilderness. Reaching Gaerolas reveals that Athridas's intuition was accurate: trouble has descended upon the village, jeopardizing the security of the nearby barrow dens.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Athridas Bearmantle?",a="Athridas Bearmantle is a prominent night elf overseer in Teldrassil who tracks the well-being of the forest and ensures the sanctuaries of his slumbering druidic brethren remain undisturbed.",al={"athridas bearmantle","athridas lore","quest giver athridas"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Gaerolas Talvethren?",a="Gaerolas Talvethren is the Great Warden chosen to protect the sleeping Druids of the Talon within the nearby Ban'ethil Barrow Den, ensuring their safety while their spirits wander the Emerald Dream.",al={"gaerolas talvethren","great warden gaerolas","who is gaerolas"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="Ban'ethil Barrow Den is a sacred underground hollow on Teldrassil where night elf druids sleep for extended periods to commune with Ysera and honor their pacts in the Emerald Dream.",al={"ban'ethil barrow den","banethil","what is ban'ethil"},it="place"},{q="Why was Gaerolas out of contact?",a="Gaerolas was unable to deliver his regular reports because sudden danger and corruption began threatening Starbreeze Village and the surrounding forest, trapping him in a struggle to maintain control.",al={"why was gaerolas silent","what happened to gaerolas","trouble in starbreeze"},it="threat"},{q="Where does this quest lead next?",a="Upon finding Gaerolas Talvethren in Starbreeze Village, he sends you back to Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar with grave news of the nearby Gnarlpine furbolgs, who have succumbed to a spreading, unnatural corruption.",al={"next quest","a troubling breeze followup","what comes after a troubling breeze"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the pact with Ysera mentioned in the quest?",a="Night elf druids enter prolonged, meditative slumbers to walk the Emerald Dream alongside the Green Dragonflight and Ysera, serving as custodians of nature's pristine blueprint.",al={"pact with ysera","ysera druid pact","druids of the talon sleep"},it="history"},{q="Why does Athridas Bearmantle send you to Gaerolas?",a="Athridas is deeply uneasy because regular word from Gaerolas Talvethren is overdue. Gaerolas stands watch over the hibernating Druids of the Talon resting within the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, ensuring their safety so they can uphold their sacred pact with Ysera in the Emerald Dream. With sinister portents stirring across the boughs of Teldrassil, Athridas needs someone to travel east to Starbreeze Village and confirm that the sleeping druids remain undisturbed.",al={"why send to starbreeze","athridas bearmantle motive","why a troubling breeze quest"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, guarding the sacred rest of the Druids of the Talon is essential to safeguarding the delicate balance of their newfound home upon Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold an intimate reverence for the Ban'ethil Barrow Den and the sleepers bound to Ysera, making any disturbance to their wardens an urgent personal matter."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","ban'ethil","druids of the talon","emerald dream","gaerolas talvethren","starbreeze village","teldrassil","troubling breeze","ysera"},rel={"npc:athridas-bearmantle","npc:gaerolas-talvethren","quest:476","subzone:starbreeze-village","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Athridas Bearmantle",["end"]="Gaerolas Talvethren",faction="Alliance",id=475},src={"A Troubling Breeze"}}
E["quest:476"] = {t="quest",n="Gnarlpine Corruption",z="teldrassil",s="Gnarlpine Corruption is an urgent courier task in Teldrassil delivered on behalf of the wounded Great Warden Gaerolas Talvethren. It warns the night elf leadership in Dolanaar that the Gnarlpine furbolgs have succumbed to demonic corruption and overran Starbreeze Village. This report sets the stage for military and druidic interventions to prevent the taint from reaching the sleeping druids of Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",h="Gnarlpine Corruption is an urgent courier task in Teldrassil delivered on behalf of the wounded Great Warden...",sec={{t="A Desperate Warning",b="Gaerolas Talvethren lies grievously wounded near the ruins of Starbreeze Village after being ambushed by his former allies. The Gnarlpine furbolgs, long considered peaceful neighbors and stewards of the wild, have abruptly turned feral. Too injured to carry the news back to civilization himself, Gaerolas entrusts an adventurer to carry word swiftly to Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar before the madness spreads any further across the boughs of Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge of Fel Moss",b="The report delivered to Athridas reveals a disturbing truth: the furbolgs have not simply grown restless, but are actively being subjected to fel magic. Their chieftain, Ursal the Mauler, has harnessed the corrupted Fel Moss festering within the World Tree, driving his people into a violent frenzy. This revelation threatens more than just settlements like Starbreeze—it directly imperils the nearby Ban'ethil Barrow Den, where slumbering druids remain completely defenseless against the deranged tribe.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to Starbreeze Village?",a="Starbreeze Village was overrun and pillaged by the Gnarlpine furbolgs after they were corrupted by fel magic. The sudden ambush drove out or slaughtered the inhabitants, leaving Gaerolas Talvethren trapped and wounded.",al={"why is starbreeze abandoned","starbreeze village attacked","who destroyed starbreeze"},it="ruin"},{q="Why have the Gnarlpine furbolgs turned violent?",a="Their chieftain, Ursal the Mauler, has begun wielding the evil powers of Fel Moss found on Teldrassil. The dark magical essence has driven the tribe into an uncontrollable, violent frenzy against their former night elf allies.",al={"why are gnarlpine mad","gnarlpine madness","why attack furbolgs"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Gaerolas Talvethren?",a="Gaerolas Talvethren is the night elf Great Warden of the sleeping Druids of the Talon, who was ambushed by the Gnarlpine tribe while traveling toward Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Too injured to make the trek to Dolanaar, he relies on travelers to deliver word of the catastrophe.",al={"gaerolas","injured night elf starbreeze"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Athridas Bearmantle?",a="Athridas Bearmantle is a prominent night elf authority stationed in Dolanaar. He oversees regional security and helps coordinate the response to emerging threats against the World Tree and its inhabitants.",al={"athridas","athridas bearmantle dolanaar"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the night elves worried about Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="Ban'ethil Barrow Den houses numerous druids who are deep in the Emerald Dream. If the frenzied Gnarlpine furbolgs reach the barrows, the slumbering night elves would be utterly defenseless against their assault.",al={"ban'ethil threat","why ban'ethil barrow den matters","sleeping druids danger"},it="danger"},{q="What is Fel Moss?",a="Fel Moss is a corrupted organic growth appearing in Teldrassil, tainted by dark demonic energies. Its corruptive influence drives local wildlife and furbolgs mad when touched or wielded.",al={"what is fel moss","fel moss teldrassil"},it="item"},{q="Why does Gaerolas Talvethren want this done?",a="Gaerolas discovered firsthand that Ursal the Mauler is corrupting the Gnarlpine tribe with Fel Moss and driving them to rampage. With Starbreeze Village pillaged and the sacred Ban'ethil Barrow Den directly threatened, he knows Dolanaar must be warned immediately before the furbolgs cause even greater catastrophe.",al={"gaerolas motive","why send news to athridas","gaerolas quest reason"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why can't Gaerolas deliver the message himself?",a="Gaerolas was ambushed and severely wounded by the corrupted furbolgs as he departed for the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Barely surviving the attack, his injuries leave him entirely unable to make the long trek back to Dolanaar, forcing him to rely on you to carry the urgent warning to Athridas Bearmantle.",al={"why does gaerolas need me","why cant gaerolas walk to dolanaar","why me gaerolas"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The fall of Starbreeze Village is a tragic shock, proving that even the newly grown World Tree is already vulnerable to the demonic taint the night elves fought so hard to eradicate.",["class:Druid"]="The threat toward Ban'ethil Barrow Den is an existential emergency for the Cenarion Circle, as sleeping brothers lie vulnerable to the corrupted Gnarlpine tribe."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","ban'ethil barrow den","dolanaar","fel moss","furbolg","gaerolas talvethren","gnarlpine corruption","starbreeze village","ursal the mauler"},rel={"npc:gaerolas-talvethren","npc:athridas-bearmantle","subzone:starbreeze-village","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","quest:475","quest:483","quest:486","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Gaerolas Talvethren",["end"]="Athridas Bearmantle",level="6",faction="Alliance",id=476},src={"Gnarlpine Corruption (Classic)"}}
E["quest:483"] = {t="quest",n="The Relics of Wakening",z="teldrassil",s="The Relics of Wakening is an urgent rescue mission to save the Druids of the Talon slumbering within the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs have overrun the sacred mounds, endangering the dormant druids whose spirits wander the Emerald Dream. Without these four specific ritual artifacts, the sleepers cannot safely be roused back into the waking world.",h="The Relics of Wakening is an urgent rescue mission to save the Druids of the Talon slumbering within the...",sec={{t="A Sanctum Defiled",b="Barrow dens serve as the secluded sanctuaries where night elf druids lie in deep hibernation while walking the Emerald Dream. West of Dolanaar, the winding corridors of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den have fallen beneath a swarm of corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs. Driven to madness by the foul taint spreading across Teldrassil, these former allies desecrated the sanctum, threatening the defenseless sleepers who remain completely unaware of the danger threatening their physical bodies.",sp=0},{t="The Tools of Return",b="A druid entering the Dream cannot simply be shaken awake; jarring their slumber without proper spiritual anchor can shatter their mind or leave their spirit stranded forever. To perform the delicate awakening ceremony, Athridas Bearmantle requires four sacred relics sealed in chests across the den: the Raven Claw Talisman, the Black Feather Quill, the Sapphire of Sky, and the Rune of Nesting. Recovering them is the only hope of stirring the Druids of the Talon before the Gnarlpine butcher or abduct them completely.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why can't the druids just be shaken awake?",a="Druidic hibernation is a deeply delicate trance that bridges the mortal shell with the Emerald Dream. Rouse them improperly or without the protective rites of the Relics of Wakening, and their consciousness risks being stranded in the Dream forever, severed from their physical form.",al={"why need relics to wake druids","why wake ritual","why are relics necessary"}},{q="Who are the Druids of the Talon?",a="They are night elf druids attuned to the powers of Aviana, capable of taking the form of storm crows and commanding the winds. Many entered deep contemplation within the barrow dens of Teldrassil to commune with nature spirits and heal the newborn tree.",al={"druids of the talon","talon druids","who sleeps in ban'ethil"},it="people"},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine furbolgs attacking the barrow den?",a="The Gnarlpine tribe has fallen victim to a dark corruption that is steadily poisoning Teldrassil's wildlife and forests. Once peaceful neighbors to the night elves, their corrupted minds have turned violent, driving them to swarm ancient sanctuaries like Ban'ethil.",al={"why are furbolgs in the barrow den","gnarlpine attacks","why furbolgs aggressive"},it="hostile"},{q="What are the four relics being recovered?",a="Athridas Bearmantle tasks adventurers with gathering the Raven Claw Talisman, the Black Feather Quill, the Sapphire of Sky, and the Rune of Nesting, each stored in a sacred chest inside Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",al={"which relics","relics needed","names of relics"},it="item"},{q="Who is Athridas Bearmantle?",a="Athridas is a night elf stationed at Dolanaar who monitors the spiritual health of the surrounding wilds and organizes efforts to counter the sudden corruption afflicting the Gnarlpine furbolgs and the barrow dens.",al={"athridas bearmantle","quest giver dolanaar"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Ban'ethil Barrow Den located?",a="Ban'ethil Barrow Den is tunneled into the hills directly west of the settlement of Dolanaar on the boughs of Teldrassil.",al={"ban'ethil location","where is banethil","where is the den"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Athridas Bearmantle need the Relics of Wakening?",a="Athridas Bearmantle urgently needs the four relics to conduct the delicate awakening ritual for the Druids of the Talon. Gnarlpine furbolgs overran the Ban'ethil Barrow Den and abducted the slumberers. Because their spirits wander deep within the Emerald Dream, their hibernation cannot simply be broken by shaking them awake. Without these specific sacred artifacts, the sleeping druids will remain trapped in the Dream for eternity, utterly defenseless against their captors.",al={"why does athridas want relics","athridas bearmantle motive","relics of wakening purpose"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For young druids, the assault on Ban'ethil is a direct strike against their Cenarion brethren. Securing the relics demonstrates your duty to preserve the sacred bridge between mortal soil and the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of a barrow den on the boughs of Teldrassil itself underscores the unsettling speed with which corruption is warping the Gnarlpine tribe and unsettling the balance of your new home."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","ban'ethil barrow den","black feather quill","dolanaar","druids of the talon","emerald dream","gnarlpine","raven claw talisman","relics of wakening","rune of nesting","sapphire of sky"},rel={"npc:athridas-bearmantle","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","subzone:dolanaar","quest:476","quest:486","quest:2541","topic:emerald-dream","topic:druid"},m={start="Athridas Bearmantle",faction="Alliance",id=483,ri={"Black Feather Quill","Raven Claw Talisman","Rune of Nesting","Sapphire of Sky"}},src={"The Relics of Wakening"}}
E["quest:486"] = {t="quest",n="Ursal the Mauler",z="teldrassil",s="Ursal the Mauler is the culmination of Athridas Bearmantle's efforts to awaken the slumbering Druids of the Talon in Teldrassil. To break the unnatural sleep binding his brethren within the Barrow Den, the corrupted furbolg chief responsible for disrupting their calling must be slain.",h="Ursal the Mauler is the culmination of Athridas Bearmantle's efforts to awaken the slumbering Druids of the...",sec={{t="A Slumber Turned Nightmare",b="The Druids of the Talon secluded themselves in the Barrow Den of Ban'ethil to slumber and commune with the Emerald Dream. However, their peaceful trance was warped into an inescapable prison. Athridas Bearmantle identified the gnarlpine furbolg, specifically their vicious leader Ursal the Mauler, as the catalyst who meddled with the druids' sacred ritual, leaving them trapped between waking and the Dream.",sp=0},{t="The Den in the Cleft",b="Gathering the Relics of Wakening was only half the struggle. For Athridas's awakening ritual to pierce the spiritual fog binding the druids, the source of the interference had to be extinguished. Ursal the Mauler made his lair deep within the Cleft, a sunken, corrupted crag nestled north of the main road through Teldrassil. Striking down the furbolg warlord breaks his grasp on the sleeper's minds.",sp=0},{t="A Symptom of Deeper Rot",b="While Ursal's demise allows Athridas to conduct the ritual and rescue the Druids of the Talon, his death does not cure what ails Teldrassil. As Athridas notes upon your return, the savage furbolg was merely acting under a darker corruption spreading through the world tree's boughs. Ursal's defeat frees the sleepers, but the root cause of the madness poisoning the Gnarlpine tribe remains lurking in the shadows.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Ursal the Mauler?",a="Ursal the Mauler is a ferocious, corrupted Gnarlpine furbolg chieftain residing within the Cleft in Teldrassil. He actively meddled with the reverie of the Druids of the Talon, trapping them within their Barrow Den slumber.",al={"who is ursal","ursal lore","who is the boss in the cleft"},it="target"},{q="Why must Ursal be killed to awaken the druids?",a="Even with the sacred Relics of Wakening in hand, Athridas Bearmantle's ritual cannot take effect while Ursal lives. The furbolg's foul interference acts as an ongoing spiritual anchor, preventing the druids' spirits from returning to their bodies.",al={"why kill ursal","why does ursal need to die","relilcs of wakening purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Ursal the Mauler be found?",a="Ursal lairs inside the Cleft, an overgrown ravine located northwest along the main path from Dolanaar, branching north off the road toward Darnassus.",al={"ursal location","where is the cleft","how to find ursal"},gp=true},{q="Does killing Ursal completely save the Gnarlpine furbolgs?",a="No. Ursal's death liberates the sleeping druids, but Athridas warns that the dark corruption plaguing the Gnarlpine furbolgs and the forests of Teldrassil persists deeper within the world tree.",al={"are furbolgs cured","did we save the furbolgs","is teldrassil saved"},sp=1},{q="Who are the Druids of the Talon?",a="The Druids of the Talon are a sect of night elf druids devoted to the stormcrow totem and the guidance of Aviana. They entered deep slumber within the Barrow Den to watch over the wilds from within the Emerald Dream.",al={"druids of the talon","who is sleeping","what druids were saved"},it="people"},{q="Who is Athridas Bearmantle?",a="Athridas Bearmantle is a night elf druid stationed in Dolanaar. He directs adventurers to recover stolen relics and eliminate Ursal so that his brethren can be safely awakened.",al={"athridas bearmantle","quest giver athridas","who gives ursal quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Athridas Bearmantle need you to slay Ursal instead of doing it himself?",a="Athridas Bearmantle must remain behind to prepare the Relics of Wakening and conduct the delicate awakening ritual. If he were to leave his post to hunt down the beast himself, the ritual could not take place in time, leaving his fellow Druids of the Talon trapped forever in their deep, corrupted slumber.",al={"why me","why Athridas doesnt kill Ursal","why cant Athridas go"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Gnarlpine furbolgs were once ancient allies of the kaldorei. Putting down their maddened leader Ursal is a tragic necessity to protect your kin and the sleeping druids.",["class:Druid"]="Preserving the sacred rites of the Emerald Dream is paramount. Ursal's meddling with the Druids of the Talon represents a severe desecration of Cenarion communion.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing Teldrassil's interior roadways and restoring the circle of druids strengthens the night elves' stronghold as they integrate into the wider Alliance."},kw={"athridas","ban'ethil","bearmantle","cleft","druid","furbolg","gnarlpine","mauler","talon","teldrassil","ursal"},rel={"quest:483","npc:athridas-bearmantle","subzone:cleft","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","quest:487","npc:moon-priestess-amara","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Athridas Bearmantle",faction="Alliance",id=486},src={"Ursal the Mauler (quest)"}}
E["quest:487"] = {t="quest",n="The Road to Darnassus",z="teldrassil",s="The main road connecting the settlement of Dolanaar to the night elf capital of Darnassus is under constant threat from corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs. Moon Priestess Amara coordinates scouts and travelers to keep this crucial trade and messenger route clear of ambushes.",h="The main road connecting the settlement of Dolanaar to the night elf capital of Darnassus is under constant...",sec={{t="A Lifeline Under Siege",b="The road spanning west from Dolanaar toward Darnassus is the primary overland artery in Teldrassil. Vital trade goods, political missives, and travelers must move along it daily to maintain connection between the capital city and the boughs of the great tree. Because Teldrassil is relatively young and wild, maintaining secure roads is critical for the fledgling kaldorei communities.",sp=0},{t="The Gnarlpine Menace",b="Rather than peaceful forest dwellers, the Gnarlpine furbolg tribe in Teldrassil has fallen victim to a foul corruption. Driven mad by whatever sickness plagues the boughs of the World Tree, they strike outward from hidden dens beneath the ridges. Stalking the tree line alongside the road, Gnarlpine ambushers prey on unwary couriers and travelers, turning what should be a peaceful forest trek into a deadly gauntlet.",sp=0},{t="The Sentinels' Vigil",b="To counter the ambushers, Moon Priestess Amara keeps watch outside Dolanaar. Blending the spiritual authority of Elune's priesthood with the militant vigilance of the Sentinels, she directs capable adventurers to strike down the ambushers near their dens below the road, ensuring safe transit to the gates of Darnassus.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the road between Dolanaar and Darnassus so dangerous?",a="Corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs have established dens along the low ridges below the roadway. Driven mad by the corruption spreading through Teldrassil, they emerge from the underbrush to ambuscade travelers, couriers, and merchants.",al={"why are furbolgs attacking","gnarlpine road attacks","why is the road unsafe"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Moon Priestess Amara?",a="Moon Priestess Amara—sometimes addressed by her full name, Sentinel Amara Nightwalker—is a night elf commander stationed on the western outskirts of Dolanaar. She oversees the security of the highway and coordinates martial efforts against the nearby Gnarlpine threat.",al={"who gives the road to darnassus quest","amara nightwalker","who is amara"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine furbolgs aggressive?",a="Furbolgs were historically allies and peaceful neighbors of the kaldorei. However, the Gnarlpine tribe on Teldrassil has been twisted by the strange malady infecting the World Tree, turning their minds violent and driving them to attack anyone entering the forest.",al={"why gnarlpine mad","furbolg corruption teldrassil","are gnarlpine evil"},it="origin"},{q="Where are the ambushers hiding?",a="The ambushers dwell below the bluffs and vantage points just off the main road west of Dolanaar, where their dens allow them to leap onto travelers moving toward Darnassus.",al={"where are gnarlpine ambushers","find ambushers","ambusher den location"},gp=true},{q="Why doesn't Darnassus send a full Sentinel garrison to clear the road?",a="The Sentinels are stretched thin across Teldrassil dealing with grell infestations, corrupted timberlings, and threats along the coast. Officers like Amara must rely on competent travelers and volunteers to keep the interior transit routes clear.",al={"where are the guards","why sentinels need help","darnassus patrol"},it="why_me"},{q="Why is Amara called both a Moon Priestess and a Sentinel?",a="In kaldorei society, the sisterhood of Elune and the Sentinel military are closely intertwined. It is common for leaders within the priesthood to command Sentinel troops or to have served as front-line warriors throughout their lives.",al={"amara rank","priestess or sentinel amara","amara nightwalker title"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Moon Priestess Amara want the Gnarlpine ambushers dealt with?",a="This road is the primary lifeline between Dolanaar and the night elf capital of Darnassus. Crucial news, travelers, and vital commerce journey along this path every day. With corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs relentlessly attacking travelers, Amara cannot tolerate a rogue band disrupting communication and trade or threatening innocent forest dwellers.",al={"why does amara want this done","amara road to darnassus reason","why clear the road to darnassus"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who are the Gnarlpine ambushers?",a="They are members of the local Gnarlpine furbolg tribe who have succumbed to corruption spreading through Teldrassil. Lurking in the shadowed dens below the road's vantage, these rogue furbolgs lie in wait to launch ruthless, coordinated attacks on anyone journeying between Dolanaar and Darnassus.",al={"who are the ambushers","what are gnarlpine ambushers","why are gnarlpine attacking travelers"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Gnarlpine were once honorable kindred of the wild; putting down corrupted ambushers along the highway to Darnassus is a grim necessity born of Teldrassil's sickness.",["class:Priest"]="Assisting Moon Priestess Amara serves the Sisterhood of Elune, which provides both spiritual leadership and martial defence for the young tree.",["faction:Alliance"]="Darnassus is the heart of the Alliance presence in northern Kalimdor; keeping trade and communications flowing securely along its main highway is essential."},kw={"amara","ambusher","darnassus","dolanaar","furbolg","gnarlpine","nightwalker","road to darnassus","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:moon-priestess-amara","subzone:dolanaar","zone:darnassus","topic:furbolg","topic:sentinels","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},m={start="Moon Priestess Amara",level="8",faction="Alliance",id=487},src={"The Road to Darnassus (Classic)"}}
E["quest:488"] = {t="quest",n="Zenn's Bidding",z="teldrassil",s="Zenn's Bidding is an Alliance quest offered by Zenn Foulhoof, a solitary satyr lurking just north of the road between Shadowglen and Dolanaar. He coaxes eager adventurers into hunting local wildlife to gather animal parts for his undisclosed schemes, preying upon the trust and naivety of newcomers to Teldrassil.",h="Zenn's Bidding is an Alliance quest offered by Zenn Foulhoof, a solitary satyr lurking just north of the road...",sec={{t="A Dubious Bargain",b="Travelers emerging from Shadowglen along the path toward Dolanaar may encounter Zenn Foulhoof standing casually beneath the boughs of the Great Tree. Instead of showing outright hostility, the satyr offers promises of material reward and secrets in exchange for mundane errand running. He asks adventurers to harvest nightsaber fangs, strigid owl feathers, and webwood spider silk from the surrounding woodlands, whispering conspiratorially to keep the arrangement between themselves.",sp=0},{t="The Satyr's Joke",b="Satyrs are ancient enemies of the kaldorei, corrupted by demonic magic during the War of the Ancients, making Zenn's mere presence on Teldrassil an outrage. Unsuspecting adventurers who complete his errand quickly discover they have been mocked. Rather than providing treasures or deep insights, Zenn laughs openly at how gullible the traveler was to serve a satyr, celebrating that he fooled a naive stranger into carrying out his dirty work.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Zenn Foulhoof?",a="Zenn Foulhoof is a sly satyr found lurking by the path west of Shadowglen on the way to Dolanaar. Unlike most satyrs who openly attack on sight, Zenn uses smooth talk and false promises to manipulate naive travelers into doing chores for him.",al={"who is zenn","zenn foulhoof lore","satyr questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="Why is a satyr giving quests in Teldrassil?",a="Zenn presents himself as non-hostile to dupe fledgling adventurers who do not yet realize the treacherous, corrupt nature of satyrs. He exploits their eagerness for work and silver to gather reagents he cannot openly hunt for himself without drawing the ire of Sentinels.",al={"why is a satyr friendly","why can i talk to zenn","satyr in teldrassil"},it="why_here"},{q="What does Zenn do with the fangs, feathers, and silk?",a="Zenn claims the parts are reagents needed for his mysterious 'business in the forest.' In reality, he relishes exerting influence over mortals and using their labor for his own corrupt ends while privately mocking their gullibility.",al={"why does zenn want silk","zenn's reagents","what are the animal parts for"},it="motive"},{q="Why shouldn't night elves trust Zenn Foulhoof?",a="Satyrs were once night elves who were transformed by the demonic power of the Burning Legion ten thousand years ago during the War of the Ancients. They are ancient, sworn enemies of the kaldorei and carriers of corruption, making any bargain with one dangerous and disgraceful.",al={"why hate satyrs","night elf satyr history","are satyrs evil"},it="danger"},{q="What happens after completing Zenn's Bidding?",a="Upon handing over the items, Zenn openly mocks you for being foolish enough to obey a satyr. Realizing the deceit and the shame of aiding such a creature, adventurers are subsequently directed to seek redemption for their mistake.",al={"after zenn's bidding","seek redemption quest","what next after zenn"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where is Zenn Foulhoof located?",a="He is located in Teldrassil, standing just north of the main road that leads west out of Shadowglen toward Dolanaar.",al={"zenn foulhoof location","where is zenn","zenn map location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Zenn Foulhoof need you to gather these reagents?",a="As a satyr skulking on the edges of night elf territory, Zenn cannot simply wander the boughs of Teldrassil or hunt openly without drawing the wrath of the Sentinels. He preys upon young, eager travelers who are willing to run errands without asking questions, exploiting your naivety to gather dangerous woodland reagents while keeping his own hands clean.",al={"why me zenn","why does zenn need my help","why recruit adventurers"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For a young night elf, taking orders from a satyr is deeply shameful. Satyrs are ancestral traitors corrupted by the Burning Legion, and aiding one on the boughs of Teldrassil is an offense against nature and kaldorei heritage.",["class:Druid"]="Druids are pledged to preserve nature's balance. Poaching nightsabers, owls, and spiders on behalf of a twisted creature of corruption is an affront to Cenarion teachings."},kw={"dolanaar","foulhoof","nightsaber","satyr","shadowglen","strigid","teldrassil","webwood","zenn"},rel={"npc:zenn-foulhoof","quest:489","topic:satyr","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},m={start="Zenn Foulhoof",faction="Alliance",id=488,ri={"Nightsaber Fang","Strigid Owl Feather","Webwood Spider Silk"}},src={"Zenn's Bidding"}}
E["quest:489"] = {t="quest",n="Seek Redemption!",z="teldrassil",s="Seek Redemption! is a quest given in Dolanaar to adventurers who were duped into doing the dirty work of the satyr Zenn Foulhoof. The Council of the Forest demands penance for harming woodland beasts, sending you to trick the deceitful satyr into eating corrupted fel cones.",h="Seek Redemption!",sec={{t="A Fool's Errand Undone",b="Zenn Foulhoof, a solitary satyr lurking just outside Dolanaar, relies on deceit to trick passersby into doing his bidding. Adventurers who unwittingly slaughtered nightsabers, strigid owls, and webwood spiders for his twisted appetites soon draw the sharp disapproval of the Council of the Forest. The council does not suffer the defilement of nature lightly, especially from their own allies.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Atonement",b="Whether warned by Syral Bladeleaf, Sentinel Kyra Starsong, or Sentinel Shayla Nightbreeze, the message is plain: to remain welcome in Teldrassil, you must make amends. Rather than confronting Foulhoof with naked steel, the guardians of Dolanaar instruct you to exploit his wicked gluttony. By gathering billowing, corrupted fel cones from the forest floor, you offer the unsuspecting creature a taste of his own foul medicine.",sp=0},{t="A Croaking Retribution",b="Under the guise of another loyal errand-runner presenting a sweet snack, you hand Foulhoof the noxious cones. Unaware of the druidic snare sprung around him, Zenn eagerly devours the offerings—only to be promptly polymorphed into a helpless frog, stripped of his vile schemes and humbled before the wilderness he sought to taint.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is the Council of the Forest angry with me?",a="You accepted an earlier task from Zenn Foulhoof, slaughtering local wildlife—nightsabers, strigid owls, and spiders—to satisfy a satyr's whims. The Council views the needless killing of nature's creatures as a defilement of Teldrassil, demanding you atone to remain in good standing.",al={"why council mad","seek redemption why","why do i need redemption"},it="motive"},{q="Who can give me this quest?",a="Several watchers in and around Dolanaar offer this quest once you finish aiding Foulhoof. You can speak to Syral Bladeleaf outside the northern dwelling, Sentinel Kyra Starsong inside the inn, or Sentinel Shayla Nightbreeze along the western road.",al={"quest givers","who starts seek redemption","where to get seek redemption"},gp=true},{q="What are fel cones?",a="Fel cones are corrupted pine seeds that drop from the twisted branches around Teldrassil. Readily identified by the eerie green vapors billowing from their husks, they carry a foul magic that druids turn against unsuspecting miscreants.",al={"fel cone","what is fel cone","where fel cones come from"},it="item"},{q="What happens to Zenn Foulhoof when you feed him the cones?",a="Foulhoof mistakes the fel cones for a tasty tribute from a gullible servant. As soon as he consumes them, the volatile nature of the seed warps him instantly into a harmless, croaking frog.",al={"foulhoof frog","what happens to zenn","foulhoof fate"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is there a satyr living so close to Dolanaar?",a="Zenn Foulhoof keeps a low profile in a hollowed clearing just outside the settlement, disguising his malicious nature behind false pleasantries. Satyrs across Kalimdor are ancient servants of the Burning Legion, and Zenn's presence shows how deep corruption reaches into the young World Tree.",al={"why is zenn near dolanaar","satyr in dolanaar","zenn foulhoof lore"},it="target"},{q="Can you skip or abandon this quest without ruining your standing?",a="Yes. While the Council of the Forest scolds you sternly for helping Foulhoof, choosing not to undertake or complete the quest will not damage your standing or reputation with the night elves of Darnassus.",al={"reputation loss","can i abandon seek redemption","fail seek redemption"},gp=true},{q="Why do the Sentinels make me deal with Zenn Foulhoof instead of doing it themselves?",a="You brought this upon yourself by previously doing Zenn Foulhoof's bidding and defiling the forest. The Council of the Forest learned of your transgressions, and the local Sentinels expect you to right your own wrong. Because Zenn already trusts you to fetch items for him, you are uniquely positioned to approach the satyr with corrupted cones disguised as an innocent snack without raising his suspicions.",al={"why don't guards deal with zenn","why do i have to trick zenn","why do sentinels send me"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, aiding a satyr is deeply humiliating. Satyrs are ancient enemies warped by the Burning Legion during the War of the Ancients, making penance through the Council of the Forest a matter of cultural honor.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold the balance of Teldrassil sacred; hunting predators and scavengers at the behest of a demon-tainted outcast directly violates the Cenarion circle's tenets of guardianship."},kw={"dolanaar","fel cone","kyra starsong","satyr","seek redemption","shayla nightbreeze","syral bladeleaf","teldrassil","zenn foulhoof"},rel={"quest:488","npc:zenn-foulhoof","npc:syral-bladeleaf","subzone:dolanaar","topic:satyr","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},m={start="Sentinel Kyra StarsongSyral BladeleafSentinel Shayla Nightbreeze",["end"]="Zenn Foulhoof",faction="Alliance",id=489,ri={"Fel Cone"}},src={"Seek Redemption!"}}
E["quest:5621"] = {t="quest",n="Garments of the Moon",z="teldrassil",s="Garments of the Moon is an introductory rite of service for young night elf priests in Dolanaar. Assigned by priest trainer Laurna Morninglight, it tasks an initiate with tending to Sentinel Shaya, a wounded defender patrolling the woods south of the settlement. Fulfilling this duty marks an initiate's formal recognition within the Sisterhood of Elune.",h="Garments of the Moon is an introductory rite of service for young night elf priests in Dolanaar.",sec={{t="A Sacred Calling",b="Within the boughs of Teldrassil, the Sisterhood of Elune tends both to the spiritual life of the kaldorei and the practical defense of their borders. When Sentinel Shaya is wounded while patrolling the dangerous wilderness south of Dolanaar, priest trainer Laurna Morninglight cannot abandon her post to render aid. Instead, she charges a newly trained initiate with proving their devotion by mending Shaya's wounds and bolstering her constitution with protective magic.",sp=0},{t="Vestments of the Sisterhood",b="Priests who restore Sentinel Shaya's vigor return to Dolanaar to receive their formal robes of office. These garments signify that the young acolyte has moved beyond mere classroom instruction to practical, lifesaving service under the moon's grace. In kaldorei society, supporting the Sentinels is not merely a military task; it is an act of communion with Elune and an essential duty to the safety of Teldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Garments of the Moon?",a="The quest is offered by Laurna Morninglight, the priest trainer residing in the northern building of Dolanaar on Teldrassil.",al={"who gives garments of the moon","where to start garments of the moon","garments of the moon questgiver"},gp=true},{q="Who needs help during this task?",a="Sentinel Shaya, a night elf guardian who was wounded while patrolling the wilderness, is stationed just south of Dolanaar awaiting aid.",al={"who do i heal","injured sentinel location","where is sentinel shaya"},it="target"},{q="What magic is required to help Sentinel Shaya?",a="You must use healing magic to close Sentinel Shaya's wounds and cast protective wards to fortify her endurance before returning to Dolanaar.",al={"what spells to cast on shaya","how to complete garments of the moon","shaya objective"},gp=true},{q="Can any class take this quest?",a="No. Garments of the Moon is exclusively offered to Alliance priests as an early milestone in their spiritual training.",al={"is garments of the moon priest only","garments of the moon class requirement","can druids do garments of the moon"},gp=true},{q="What does the robe reward symbolize?",a="The robe awarded by Laurna Morninglight serves as a token of initiation, signifying that you have dutifully served Elune and earned a recognized place among the local priesthood.",al={"garments of the moon robe meaning","robe reward lore","significance of garments of the moon"}},{q="What is the relationship between this quest and In Favor of Elune?",a="In Favor of Elune serves as an introductory summons to visit the trainer in Dolanaar. While not strictly required to receive Garments of the Moon, it cannot be completed once Garments of the Moon is finished.",al={"in favor of elune prerequisite","in favor of elune missed","order of dolanaar priest quests"},gp=true},{q="Why does Laurna Morninglight want Sentinel Shaya healed?",a="Sentinel Shaya was wounded while patrolling the borders south of Dolanaar to safeguard the settlement. As a priest trainer dedicated to Elune, Laurna Morninglight considers it their sacred duty to tend to the protectors of Teldrassil. Tending Shaya's wounds and fortifying her spirit ensures that the Sentinels can endure the growing perils threatening the boughs of the World Tree.",al={"laurna morninglight motive","why heal sentinel shaya","garments of the moon motive"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Laurna send you instead of helping Shaya herself?",a="Laurna Morninglight cannot abandon her post in Dolanaar, where she is tasked with instructing and guiding the novice acolytes of the priesthood. With her duties binding her to the village sanctuary, she entrusts you to venture into the field, put your training into practice, and fulfill your duty to Elune by aiding the wounded Sentinel.",al={"why send me","why doesn't laurna heal shaya","why can't laurna go"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Priest"]="This rite demonstrates the twin pillars of the priesthood: restoring wounded allies through restorative prayer and protecting them against future danger with divine wards.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, the Sisterhood of Elune and the Sentinels have worked hand in hand for millennia to protect the forests and people from encroaching darkness."},kw={"dolanaar","garments of the moon","in favor of elune","laurna morninglight","sentinel shaya","sisterhood of elune","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:laurna-morninglight","quest:5622","subzone:dolanaar","topic:elune","topic:sentinels","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},m={start="Laurna Morninglight",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=5621},src={"Garments of the Moon"}}
E["quest:5622"] = {t="quest",n="In Favor of Elune",z="teldrassil",s="\"In Favor of Elune\" is a rite of passage for young night elf priests ready to step out of the sheltered boughs of Shadowglen. Directed by Priestess Shanda, novitiates travel down the path to Dolanaar to seek further guidance and training under Laurna Morninglight.",h="\"In Favor of Elune\" is a rite of passage for young night elf priests ready to step out of the sheltered...",sec={{t="Leaving the Glade",b="For an initiate serving Elune within Aldrassil's secluded shelter, learning begins with simple prayers and defensive invocations under the watchful eye of Priestess Shanda. Yet the cloistered life of Shadowglen cannot prepare a priestess or priest for the turmoil gripping the wider world. Once an initiate demonstrates steady faith and discipline, Shanda sends them down the shadowed forest path toward Dolanaar to continue their education.",sp=0},{t="A Step Into the Priesthood",b="Reaching Dolanaar marks an essential milestone in a night elf's divine vocation. There awaits Laurna Morninglight, a respected priestess tasked with preparing disciples for the trials facing Teldrassil. Beyond advanced instruction in moonlit spellcraft, arriving in Dolanaar prepares the acolyte to claim their first formal vestments, marking their official standing within the Sisterhood of Elune.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this journey?",a="Priestess Shanda, the night elf priest trainer stationed within the boughs of Aldrassil in Shadowglen, gives you this guidance once your initial training is complete.",al={"quest giver","who starts in favor of elune","where do i get this quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I need to go to find Laurna Morninglight?",a="Laurna Morninglight resides in Dolanaar, the first major settlement south of the Shadowglen gates in Teldrassil. She is located near the eastern buildings of the village.",al={"laurna morninglight location","where is dolanaar","where is morninglight"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can any class take this quest?",a="No. This quest is specifically designated for young night elf priests taking their initial steps into the Sisterhood and the service of Elune.",al={"is this priest only","who can do in favor of elune","druid quest?"},gp=true},{q="What happens after I speak to Laurna Morninglight?",a="Laurna Morninglight will greet you and offer the trial 'Garments of the Moon', which tests your ability to protect and heal wounded defenders before bestowing your first official clerical robes.",al={"what comes next","followup quest","garments of the moon quest"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is this quest mandatory to continue priest training?",a="It is an optional breadcrumb quest. If you travel directly to Dolanaar on your own, Laurna Morninglight will still offer her training and subsequent tasks without needing this introduction.",al={"do i have to do in favor of elune","can i skip in favor of elune","optional breadcrumb"},gp=true},{q="Why is earning garments so important to the Sisterhood?",a="Vestments in night elf culture are not merely cloth; they are sacred symbols denoting one's official station, devotion, and readiness to channel the Moon Goddess's blessings in service of their people.",al={"why robes matter","significance of garments","station of elune priestess"},it="item"},{q="Why does Shanda send you to Dolanaar?",a="Shanda has taught you the basic rites suited to a novice in Shadowglen, but your training in service to Elune must expand beyond this secluded glade. She directs you to Laurna Morninglight in Dolanaar so you can deepen your spiritual understanding and earn the ceremonial vestments appropriate to your growing station among the priesthood.",al={"why send to dolanaar","shanda motive","why see laurna morninglight"},it="motive",rc="Night Elf",add=true}},ang={["class:Priest"]="This task represents your departure from simple novitiate studies into full service, setting you on the path toward earning your first consecrated clerical vestments.",["race:NightElf"]="The Sisterhood of Elune forms the spiritual heart and historic leadership of kaldorei society, making the journey to Dolanaar a deeply traditional milestone for devotees."},kw={"dolanaar","garments of the moon","in favor of elune","laurna morninglight","priest","shadowglen","shanda","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:laurna-morninglight","npc:shanda","quest:5621","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Shanda",["end"]="Laurna Morninglight",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=5622},src={"In Favor of Elune"}}
E["quest:5636"] = {t="quest",n="Desperate Prayer",z="teldrassil",s="Desperate Prayer is an Alliance priest quest directing traveling servants of the Holy Light back to Stormwind City. Initiated by the night elf priestess Laurna Morninglight in Dolanaar, it calls human and dwarven priests visiting Teldrassil home to complete vital spiritual training under High Priestess Laurena.",h="Desperate Prayer is an Alliance priest quest directing traveling servants of the Holy Light back to Stormwind...",sec={{t="A Message from Home",b="While visiting the ancestral boughs of Teldrassil, priests faithful to the Holy Light may find themselves noticed by the local Sisterhood of Elune. In Dolanaar, Priestess Laurna Morninglight serves as an unexpected liaison, delivering word that a fellow priest traveled across continents seeking you out. Recognizing the urgency of the summons, Laurna encourages you to return to your homeland without delay, offering Elune's blessing alongside well-wishes for your own faith.",sp=0},{t="The Summons to Stormwind",b="The journey requires crossing the Great Sea to the grand Cathedral of Light situated in the heart of Stormwind City. There, High Priestess Laurena oversees the spiritual growth of the Alliance's faithful. Acolytes who have demonstrated early promise are summoned before her to master deeper mysteries of devotion, specifically the emergency invocation known as Desperate Prayer—a life-saving gift granted only to dedicated disciples in their darkest hour.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts the quest Desperate Prayer in Teldrassil?",a="Laurna Morninglight, a night elf priest trainer stationed in Dolanaar on Teldrassil, offers the quest. She passes along an urgent message left by a visiting priest from your home lands.",al={"who gives desperate prayer","desperate prayer quest giver teldrassil","laurna morninglight quest"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="Where does this quest lead?",a="The quest directs you to the Cathedral of Light within Stormwind City, where you must speak directly with High Priestess Laurena.",al={"where do i go","turn in desperate prayer","where is laurena"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why is a night elf directing a priest to Stormwind?",a="Night elf priests revere Elune, but foreign priests—such as humans or dwarves—who venture to Teldrassil still belong to the traditions of the Holy Light. Laurna Morninglight graciously respects their beliefs and relays messages sent from their homeland's religious hierarchy.",al={"why does a night elf send me to stormwind","night elf holy light"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the reward for completing this quest?",a="Reporting to High Priestess Laurena opens advanced spiritual mentorship and grants access to learn Desperate Prayer, an instantaneous healing prayer exclusive to human and dwarven priests.",al={"desperate prayer reward","what spell do i get"},gp=true},{q="Can night elf priests take this specific quest?",a="No. Night elf priests worship Elune and learn Starshards rather than Desperate Prayer. This particular summons exists specifically for human or dwarven priests who find themselves exploring Kalimdor at early levels.",al={"can night elves do desperate prayer","night elf priest desperate prayer"},gp=true},{q="How do you travel back to Stormwind from Teldrassil?",a="You must head through Darnassus to Rut'theran Village, catch a boat to Auberdine in Darkshore, take another ship across the sea to Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands, and then travel south through Loch Modan, Dun Morogh, and the Deeprun Tram into Stormwind.",al={"how to get to stormwind from dolanaar","teldrassil to stormwind route"},gp=true},{q="Why does Laurna Morninglight send you to Stormwind?",a="Laurna Morninglight has no personal stake or secret agenda; she is passing along an urgent summons. An emissary of the Holy Light visited Dolanaar seeking you specifically, instructing her that High Priestess Laurena requires your presence at the Cathedral of Light. Recognizing that your talents have drawn the notice of your leaders and that your people need you, Laurna urges you not to linger on Teldrassil when greater duties call you home.",al={"why send to stormwind","laurna morninglight motive","why desperate prayer quest"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Laurena need you instead of local priests in Stormwind?",a="You have advanced far enough in your communion with the Holy Light to warrant individual guidance from the church's highest elders. High Priestess Laurena seeks promising acolytes who demonstrate true devotion in the field, calling you back to Stormwind to undergo advanced instruction in sacred rites such as the Desperate Prayer. Your personal growth as a vessel of the Light is what commands her attention.",al={"why does laurena want me","why me desperate prayer","why summon me to stormwind"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Priest"]="This quest marks an important rite of passage at level 10, bringing priests back into the fold of the Cathedral of Light to learn distinctive racial blessings of faith.",["faction:Alliance"]="The summons demonstrates the growing cooperation across the Alliance, as night elf priestesses readily coordinate with the church leadership in Stormwind.",["race:NightElf"]="Although night elves revere the Moon Goddess Elune, Priestess Laurna Morninglight shows polite respect for foreign devotees of the Holy Light walking under the boughs of Teldrassil."},kw={"cathedral of light","desperate prayer","dolanaar","high priestess laurena","laurna morninglight","priest quest","stormwind","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:laurna-morninglight","npc:high-priestess-laurena","subzone:cathedral-of-light","zone:teldrassil","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:light","topic:elune"},m={start="Laurna Morninglight",["end"]="High Priestess Laurena",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=5636},src={"Desperate Prayer (Dolanaar)"}}
E["quest:5842"] = {t="quest",n="Welcome!",z="teldrassil",s="This quest greets newly arrived adventurers in Teldrassil carrying a special Dolanaar Gift Voucher. By bringing the token to Orenthil Whisperwind in the village of Dolanaar, travelers receive a rare companion to accompany them on their journeys across Azeroth.",h="This quest greets newly arrived adventurers in Teldrassil carrying a special Dolanaar Gift Voucher.",sec={{t="A Welcoming Gift in Dolanaar",b="Young night elves venturing south from Shadowglen soon come across the tree-shaded settlement of Dolanaar. Among its residents stands Orenthil Whisperwind, an attendant ready to greet select newcomers. Those carrying a Dolanaar Gift Voucher are directed straight to Orenthil, who eagerly exchanges the parchment for a curious, loyal companion pet.",sp=0},{t="An Honored Arrival",b="While most initiates must earn every scrap of equipment and companionship through trials against corruption in the boughs of Teldrassil, this voucher marks the bearer as a celebrated arrival. Orenthil welcomes the adventurer to Azeroth, bestowing a unique creature to follow them through wilderness, barrow dens, and beyond.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The quest directs holders of a special voucher to Orenthil Whisperwind in Dolanaar. Handing over the voucher grants the adventurer a unique vanity pet to accompany them throughout their adventures.",al={"what does this quest do","welcome quest goal","why do i have this voucher"}},{q="Who is Orenthil Whisperwind?",a="Orenthil Whisperwind is a night elf stationed in Dolanaar within Teldrassil. He assists travelers by receiving their gift vouchers and presenting them with a companion creature.",al={"who is orenthil","where is orenthil whisperwind","orenthil lore"}},{q="Where is Dolanaar?",a="Dolanaar is the primary village in central Teldrassil, located just south down the road from the novice grounds of Shadowglen and east of Darnassus.",al={"how to get to dolanaar","dolanaar location"}},{q="Can any adventurer take this quest?",a="This quest is only available to adventurers who possess the Dolanaar Gift Voucher, an exclusive parchment provided to select travelers upon entering the world.",al={"who can get welcome quest","is this quest available to everyone"}},{q="What kind of companions can you receive?",a="Orenthil Whisperwind offers a choice among rare and exotic creatures, giving the traveler a small animal companion to follow them across Azeroth.",al={"what pet do you get","what are the gifts"}},{q="Does this quest affect your standing in Teldrassil?",a="No. The quest is a ceremonial welcome and does not alter the political conflicts, demonic corruption, or spider infestations threatening the boughs of Teldrassil.",al={"does this give reputation","is it part of a main storyline"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves departing Shadowglen, receiving a companion in Dolanaar provides comfort and fellowship before facing the troubled woods of Teldrassil.",["faction:Alliance"]="The gesture marks the recipient as a celebrated arrival in Alliance territory, welcomed personally by local caretakers like Orenthil Whisperwind."},kw={"companion","dolanaar","gift voucher","orenthil whisperwind","pet","teldrassil","welcome"},rel={"npc:orenthil-whisperwind","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Dolanaar Gift Voucher",["end"]="Orenthil Whisperwind",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=5842},src={"Welcome! (Dolanaar)"}}
E["quest:6063"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="teldrassil",s="This quest is the first trial in a night elf hunter's journey to mastering beast companionship. Instructed by Dazalar in Dolanaar, an aspiring hunter must use an enchanted taming rod to bond with a wild Webwood Lurker. It tests the hunter's ability to respect and commune with nature rather than attempting to violently dominate it.",h="This quest is the first trial in a night elf hunter's journey to mastering beast companionship.",sec={{t="A Sacred Bond",b="For the kaldorei, hunting is not merely about tracking quarry or surviving in the wilds; it is a sacred relationship with nature. Hunter trainers like Dazalar teach that nature is far greater than any individual mortal. Animals are not beasts of burden or tools to be forcibly bent to one's will, but autonomous creatures that require mutual respect. To prove readiness for a lifelong beast companion, novice hunters must demonstrate mastery over the primal instincts of local wildlife through ancient techniques rather than brute force.",sp=0},{t="The First Trial",b="The trials begin with the giant arachnids infesting the boughs of Teldrassil. Dazalar entrusts the hunter with a specialized taming rod, directing them to seek out a Webwood Lurker. Venturing into the shadowed thickets, the hunter must face the venomous spider and establish an empathetic channel while withstanding its attacks. Successfully establishing this temporary mental bridge proves the hunter can commune even with the eerie, skittering predators of the World Tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="This quest initiates the training sequence required for night elf hunters to permanently tame animal companions. By using a taming rod on designated local beasts, hunters prove they possess the temper and skill to commune with wild predators.",al={"why do this quest","pet quest purpose","what does taming the beast give"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Dazalar, the hunter trainer residing in the settlement of Dolanaar on Teldrassil, offers this quest to young night elf hunters who have reached sufficient experience in their field.",al={"quest giver","where to get taming quest","who starts taming the beast"},it="identity"},{q="What creature must be tamed in this trial?",a="You are tasked with taming a Webwood Lurker, one of the venomous giant spiders that dwell in the wild thickets and woods outside Dolanaar.",al={"which pet to tame","webwood lurker target","what beast do i tame"},it="target"},{q="Do I keep the Webwood Lurker permanently?",a="No. The Webwood Lurker tamed during this quest is a temporary companion meant solely for practicing the basics of pet handling. Once returned to Dazalar, the bond is released as you prepare for the next trial.",al={"do i keep the spider","is the webwood lurker permanent","keep pet"},gp=true},{q="Why do night elves test hunters with spiders first?",a="Webwood Lurkers are predatory and aggressive, making them a stern test of a novice's composure. Mastering an unnatural-seeming arachnid proves that a hunter can bridge their consciousness with diverse, hostile manifestations of nature.",al={"why webwood lurker","why tame a spider","spider taming lore"}},{q="What comes after returning to Dazalar?",a="Dazalar sends the hunter to test their bond against other native fauna of Teldrassil—specifically a Nightsaber Stalker and a Strigid Screecher—before granting permanent taming abilities.",al={"what next","after taming the beast","next trial"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Dazalar want this done?",a="Dazalar believes that nature is not a force to be bent to a mortal's whim, but a power that demands deep reverence and respect. Before he entrusts you with the enduring art of taming wild beasts, he must ensure you grasp this sacred duty. The trial tests whether you possess the patience and humility required of a true kaldorei hunter rather than treating wild creatures as mere tools.",al={"why does dazalar test you","dazalar motive","purpose of dazalar trial"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Dazalar send you instead of doing this himself?",a="This is an essential rite of passage for your own growth as a hunter. Dazalar has already mastered the wild; his role is to guide and evaluate your progress. The trial requires you to forge a bond under your own will and prove that you have learned the discipline necessary to walk alongside Teldrassil's creatures as a trusted guardian.",al={"why do i have to tame the spider","why me dazalar","why doesnt dazalar do it"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This rite of passage marks a hunter's transition from solitary archer to a true partner of the wilderness, bound to the beasts of the forest.",["race:NightElf"]="Reflecting kaldorei philosophy, pet taming emphasizes communion and reverence for nature rather than subjugation and domination."},kw={"dazalar","dolanaar","hunter pet","kaldorei","taming","taming rod","teldrassil","webwood lurker"},rel={"npc:dazalar","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Dazalar",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6063},src={"Taming the Beast (night elf)"}}
E["quest:6101"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="teldrassil",s="This trial marks the second phase of a night elf hunter's pet taming training under Dazalar in Dolanaar. Hunters are tasked with subduing a nightsaber stalker using an enchanted taming rod to better appreciate the shifting diversity of wild beasts. It deepens the bond of understanding between the wilderness of Teldrassil and the sentinel trackers who walk beneath its boughs.",h="This trial marks the second phase of a night elf hunter's pet taming training under Dazalar in Dolanaar.",sec={{t="The Changing Nature of Beasts",b="While early lessons focus on understanding fundamental instincts, Dazalar emphasizes that nature's only constant is its continuous change. Every species of the forest carries a distinct temperament, and a hunter must learn to adapt their will accordingly. In the shadow of Teldrassil's canopy, this means engaging creatures that are cunning, stealthy, and far more predatory than simple webspinners.",sp=0},{t="Subduing the Nightsaber",b="Nightsabers are revered by the kaldorei as sacred predators, fierce guardians, and stealthy companions of the Sentinels. For a novice hunter, channeling the power of the taming rod against a nightsaber stalker requires steady nerve and calm authority. By bending the predatory aggression of the stalker into a receptive bond, the hunter proves they can command more than merely docile or lesser creatures of the woods.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="It is the intermediate trial in the night elf hunter chain that unlocks permanent beast taming. Dazalar sends you to tame a nightsaber stalker so you can observe the temperamental differences between varied predatory creatures.",al={"why do this quest","pet taming quest 2","nightsaber taming goal"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can nightsaber stalkers be found?",a="Nightsaber stalkers roam the wooded paths and undergrowth to the south of Dolanaar in central Teldrassil.",al={"where are nightsaber stalkers","stalker location","where to find the cat"},gp=true},{q="Do I get to keep the nightsaber stalker as my permanent pet?",a="No. The beast tamed with the rod is temporary and serves solely as a practice subject. Once the full three-part trial is finished and you return the rod, you will learn the true taming ability and can choose a permanent companion.",al={"do i keep the pet","can i keep the nightsaber","is this my pet forever"},gp=true},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Dazalar, the hunter trainer situated in Dolanaar within Teldrassil, issues this instruction after you have completed your first taming test.",al={"quest giver","who starts this","dazalar location"},it="people"},{q="Why do night elves revere nightsabers so deeply?",a="Nightsabers have lived alongside the kaldorei for millennia as companions, scouts, and war mounts for the Sentinels and Priestesses of Elune. Taming one is considered a proud hallmark of kaldorei woodland mastery.",al={"night elf cats lore","why nightsabers matter","lore on nightsabers"},it="origin"},{q="What comes after completing this task?",a="Dazalar will grant a final taming task involving another Teldrassil creature before teaching the innate ability to tame, feed, and manage permanent companion beasts across Azeroth.",al={"next quest","what is after nightsaber stalker","hunter trial next"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Dazalar want you to tame a nightsaber stalker?",a="Dazalar aims to teach you that nature's variance is ever-shifting yet dependable. By guiding you through diverse creatures, he wants you to perceive the unique temperament and spirit of each beast, ensuring you learn how to harmonize with different companions across Teldrassil.",al={"why tame nightsaber stalker","dazalar motive","why nightsaber stalker"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is a nightsaber stalker and why are you seeking it?",a="Nightsaber stalkers are predatory great cats native to the shadowed boughs and woods of Teldrassil. Dazalar sends you after one so you can master bonding with a cunning, agile hunter, learning to respect its instinct and balance within the wild.",al={"what is a nightsaber stalker","nightsaber stalkers teldrassil","why hunt nightsaber stalker"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This rite represents the core education of a hunter, teaching you how to respect diverse animal temperaments before you are trusted with a lifelong companion.",["race:NightElf"]="Nightsabers are deeply entwined with kaldorei history and culture, making the taming of a stalker a traditional milestone for local woodland scouts."},kw={"beast taming","dazalar","dolanaar","hunter","nightsaber stalker","taming rod","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:dazalar","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:6061","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Dazalar",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6101},src={"Taming the Beast (night elf 2)"}}
E["quest:6102"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="teldrassil",s="This quest marks the final trial in a young night elf hunter's basic training. Under the direction of Dazalar in Dolanaar, hunters must tame a predatory owl of the skies before unlocking the power to choose a true, lifelong companion.",h="This quest marks the final trial in a young night elf hunter's basic training.",sec={{t="Mastery of the Canopy",b="Before completing their initial beastcraft, night elf hunters must establish harmony with creatures from every corner of Teldrassil's ecosystem. Having previously proven their will against beasts of the underbrush, Dazalar charges the hunter with bringing down the spirit of the skies: the Strigid Screecher. These watchful birds of prey roost high across the boughs west of Dolanaar, requiring patience and a steady nerve to pacify with the enchanted Taming Rod.",sp=0},{t="A Hunter's Bond",b="Succeeding with the Strigid Screecher fulfills the ancient lessons of communion between kaldorei hunters and nature. Upon returning the spent rod to Dazalar, the apprentice leaves behind training exercises and earns the full art of calling, dismissing, and permanently taming beasts of their own choosing across Azeroth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are Strigid Screechers found?",a="Strigid Screechers roost in the woods west of Dolanaar. Hunters must seek out these predatory birds among the canopy and roots outside the village to test their rod.",al={"screecher location","where is strigid screecher","owl location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Dazalar?",a="Dazalar is a night elf hunter trainer stationed in Dolanaar. He oversees young kaldorei who have reached basic competence in archery and tracking, testing them on land and sky beasts before bestowing the ability to bind a real animal companion.",al={"dazalar role","who teaches pet taming dolanaar","hunter trainer dolanaar"},it="identity"},{q="Do I get to keep the Strigid Screecher as my pet?",a="No. The screechers tamed during this trial are temporary subjects bound only by the Taming Rod's magic. Once the trial is turned in, the rod is surrendered, and the hunter is taught how to tame a permanent companion of their own choosing in the wild.",al={"keep owl","is screecher permanent","do i keep this pet"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What happens after completing this trial?",a="Dazalar permanently unlocks your ability to tame, call, and dismiss beasts. He also points you toward further training in Darnassus to learn the vital arts of feeding and teaching your companion in combat.",al={"what comes next","after taming the beast","hunter pet quest finish"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why do night elves tame owls specifically?",a="Birds of prey such as owls hold deep cultural significance among the kaldorei as vigilant hunters of the night and trusted scouts. Mastering a creature of the skies proves the hunter understands aerial predators alongside ground-dwelling beasts.",al={"owl lore night elf","why owls","strigid screecher importance"},it="history"},{q="Can hunters choose any animal after this quest?",a="Yes. Once Dazalar teaches the permanent taming ability, a hunter is free to seek out any tameable beast of the land, water, or sky across Teldrassil and beyond.",al={"what pets can i get","choosing first pet","any beast tameable"},gp=true},{q="Why does Dazalar have you tame a Strigid Screecher?",a="This is your final trial as a novice hunter. Having proven your ability to handle two distinct creatures of the land, Dazalar requires you to master one that rules the skies. By taming a fierce Strigid Screecher, you demonstrate that your empathy and authority over beasts extend beyond the earth, proving you are ready to bond with a permanent companion of your own.",al={"why tame strigid screecher","dazalar motive","why owl trial"},it="motive",rc="Night Elf",add=true},{q="What are Strigid Screechers?",a="Strigid Screechers are large, predatory owls native to the boughs of Teldrassil. Revered by night elf hunters for their keen sight and silent flight, they hunt throughout the woods west of Dolanaar. Their fierce nature and aerial grace make them an ideal test of a hunter's patience, focus, and command before undertaking a permanent beast bond.",al={"strigid screechers","strigid screecher lore","screecher owls teldrassil"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This rite of passage is the threshold where a hunter transitions from fighting alone to forging a lifetime partnership with a wild companion.",["race:NightElf"]="Taming Teldrassil's native wildlife reflects the kaldorei path of walking in harmony with nature rather than bending it through force."},kw={"beast","dazalar","dolanaar","hunter pet","screecher","strigid screecher","taming","taming rod","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:dazalar","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","quest:6061"},m={start="Dazalar",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6102},src={"Taming the Beast (night elf 3)"}}
E["quest:6103"] = {t="quest",n="Training the Beast",z="teldrassil",s="Training the Beast is the culminating rite of passage for fledgling night elf hunters in Teldrassil. After proving their mastery by taming wild beasts across the boughs, hunters are sent to Darnassus to learn the deeper arts of pet care and discipline from Jocaste.",h="Training the Beast is the culminating rite of passage for fledgling night elf hunters in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Hunter's Rite of Passage",b="Before a night elf hunter can roam Kalimdor with a loyal companion by their side, they must master more than just the taming rod. While subduing a wild creature proves basic strength and will, an untutored beast remains an unpredictable liability. Once an initiate demonstrates their capability in the wilderness surrounding Dolanaar, Dazalar directs them inward to Darnassus to complete their training.",sp=0},{t="Guidance in the Cenarion Enclave",b="Within the serene groves of the Cenarion Enclave, the revered hunter Jocaste imparts the essential arts of companionship. She instructs the young hunter in how to properly nourish their pet, resurrect it should tragedy strike, and nurture its fighting instincts through training. To night elves, this relationship is rooted in deep reverence for nature rather than simple domination.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="This quest completes the initial hunter pet questline for night elves. It directs you to Darnassus to unlock the core skills required to maintain and train your permanent animal companion.",al={"why do this quest","pet training quest night elf","what does training the beast do"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do I find Jocaste?",a="Jocaste resides in Darnassus within the Cenarion Enclave, nestled among the towering trees and hunter lodges in the northwest portion of the capital.",al={"where is jocaste","jocaste location","find jocaste"},gp=true},{q="Who starts the quest?",a="Dazalar, the hunter trainer in Dolanaar, offers this quest after you have completed all three steps of taming trials across Teldrassil.",al={"quest giver","who gives training the beast","dazalar location"},gp=true},{q="What skills do you learn from Jocaste?",a="Speaking with Jocaste unlocks the essential arts of beast mastery: feeding your companion, reviving it if it falls in combat, and training it with new abilities.",al={"what abilities do i get","jocaste rewards","hunter pet spells"},gp=true},{q="Why does night elf culture emphasize pet training?",a="Kaldorei hunters view their pets as partners rather than subservient tools. Proper training and care reflect the race's core philosophy of living in balance and awe of nature.",al={"night elf hunter lore","why train beasts night elf"},it="origin"},{q="Is this quest available to other races?",a="This specific journey to Darnassus is unique to night elf hunters. Other hunter races undergo equivalent training rites under their own racial mentors.",al={"can dwarves do this","can horde do training the beast"},gp=true},{q="Why does Dazalar send you to Jocaste?",a="Dazalar has taught you how to tame beasts of the wild, but capturing a creature's loyalty is only the first step. Without proper guidance in feeding, caring for, and instructing your companion, the bond between hunter and beast cannot flourish. He directs you to Darnassus because Jocaste is among the night elves' most revered hunters, possessing the ancient wisdom required to elevate a fledgling tracker into a true master of beasts.",al={"why does dazalar want this done","dazalar motive","why go to darnassus hunter"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This rite marks your graduation from novice tracker to a true master of beasts, unlocking the ability to train, feed, and revive your companion.",["race:NightElf"]="The kaldorei tradition of beast companionship centers on respect and coexistence, reflecting the teachings passed down through Darnassus and the Cenarion Enclave."},kw={"cenarion enclave","darnassus","dazalar","hunter pet","jocaste","teldrassil","training the beast"},rel={"npc:jocaste","npc:dazalar","subzone:cenarion-enclave","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","quest:6081"},m={start="Dazalar",["end"]="Jocaste",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6103},src={"Training the Beast (night elf)"}}
E["quest:8357"] = {t="quest",n="Dancing for Marzipan",z="teldrassil",s="During the festive season of Hallow's End, adventurers traveling through Darnassus are tasked with collecting festive sweets for a sick orphan in Stormwind. Innkeeper Saelienne upholds the trick-or-treat tradition in full, requiring an impromptu dance performance before parting with her prized Darnassus Marzipan.",h="During the festive season of Hallow's End, adventurers traveling through Darnassus are tasked with collecting...",sec={{t="A Tradition Upheld",b="Even in the sacred forest city of Darnassus, the revelry of Hallow's End brings a lighter spirit to the long-lived night elves. When travelers arrive looking to gather holiday confections on behalf of Jesper, a sick child recovering in Stormwind, Innkeeper Saelienne insists that the rules of the season remain unbroken. Charity or not, a treat requires a proper trick first.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Marzipan",b="To earn the delicate Darnassus Marzipan, adventurers must set aside their dignified demeanor and put on a show right on the inn floor. Saelienne demands nothing less than a dance, gladly rewarding those willing to shed their pride and embrace the festive cheer with the confection needed to complete the cross-continental holiday care package.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Dancing for Marzipan?",a="The quest is part of the seasonal Alliance Hallow's End festivities. You perform a dance for Innkeeper Saelienne in Darnassus to obtain Darnassus Marzipan, one of several holiday treats required to cheer up a sick orphan named Jesper in Stormwind.",al={"why dance for marzipan","what is this quest","marzipan quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Innkeeper Saelienne?",a="Innkeeper Saelienne manages the inn within Darnassus, offering shelter and rest to travelers beneath the boughs of Teldrassil. During Hallow's End, she oversees the distribution of local holiday confections to those willing to play along with tradition.",al={"who is saelienne","saelienne lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Saelienne insist on a dance?",a="Saelienne strictly adheres to the spirit of Hallow's End. Even though the treat is destined for an ailing child, she holds fast to the custom of 'trick or treat,' playfully requiring a demonstration of dancing prowess as the trick before handing over the sweet.",al={"why dance","why does saelienne want me to dance"},it="motive"},{q="Where does the marzipan go after this?",a="Once received, the Darnassus Marzipan is bundled alongside seasonal sweets collected from the inns of Ironforge and Stormwind and from Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge to fulfill the quest to bring holiday joy to young Jesper in Stormwind.",al={"who gets the marzipan","what to do with marzipan"},it="next_step"},{q="What is Darnassus Marzipan?",a="Darnassus Marzipan is a sugary confection crafted in the night elven capital, traditionally made from ground almonds and sugar. It serves as Darnassus's signature festive treat for visiting trick-or-treaters during Hallow's End.",al={"darnassus marzipan lore","what kind of candy is it"},it="item"},{q="Can Horde players complete this quest?",a="No. Dancing for Marzipan is an Alliance-only seasonal quest. Darnassus is an Alliance stronghold, and the marzipan is gathered specifically for an Alliance orphan convalescing in Stormwind City.",al={"is this quest alliance only","horde marzipan quest"},gp=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This festive task showcases the unity and lighthearted camaraderie shared across Alliance capitals, bringing treats from distant Teldrassil all the way to a young orphan in Stormwind.",["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves, participating in Hallow's End is an endearing adoption of Alliance seasonal customs, blending their serene woodland lifestyle with playful revelry."},kw={"dance","darnassus","hallow's end","innkeeper","jesper","marzipan","saelienne","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:saelienne","quest:8311","npc:jesper","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Innkeeper Saelienne",faction="Alliance",id=8357},src={"Dancing for Marzipan (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:8715"] = {t="quest",n="Bladeleaf the Elder",z="teldrassil",s="Bladeleaf the Elder is a Lunar Festival encounter in the night elf settlement of Dolanaar. Standing beneath a shaft of celestial moonlight, Elder Bladeleaf greets travelers celebrating their ancestors and guides seekers onward across the boughs of Teldrassil. Paying respects to this honored spirit offers wisdom on reading the starry skies and honors the heritage of the night elves.",h="Bladeleaf the Elder is a Lunar Festival encounter in the night elf settlement of Dolanaar.",sec={{t="A Celestial Presence in Dolanaar",b="During the Lunar Festival, the spirit of Elder Bladeleaf manifests amid the village of Dolanaar, resting beneath the sweeping canopy of Teldrassil. Illuminated from above by an unbroken beam of radiance, the elder stands quietly among the busy sentinels and druids of the settlement, greeting wanderers who take the time to pause and pay their respects to the ancestors.",sp=0},{t="Wisdom of the Heavens",b="Elder Bladeleaf speaks of the countless stars in the night sky, reminding those who listen that celestial bodies hold answers to earthly mysteries. In night elf tradition, the stars and heavens are deeply intertwined with spirituality, fate, and the watchful gaze of Elune. Bladeleaf imparts this perspective to travelers before directing them toward other honored spirits across the world, such as Elder Bladeswift.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Bladeleaf?",a="Elder Bladeleaf is an ancestral spirit honored during the seasonal Lunar Festival. He appears in Dolanaar on Teldrassil, illuminated by a column of light from the heavens, and shares quiet reflections on wisdom and the stars.",al={"elder bladeleaf","bladeleaf","who is bladeleaf"}},{q="Where can I find Elder Bladeleaf?",a="Elder Bladeleaf can be found standing in Dolanaar, the primary town in the lower boughs of Teldrassil, marked by a bright shaft of light descending through the trees.",al={"bladeleaf location","where is bladeleaf","find elder bladeleaf"}},{q="Why is Elder Bladeleaf illuminated by light?",a="All the ancestral elders who manifest during the Lunar Festival are marked by a beam of celestial light from the sky, symbolizing their sacred connection to the heavens and the realm of the ancestors.",al={"why beam of light","bladeleaf light beam","shaft of light"}},{q="What does Elder Bladeleaf tell travelers?",a="Elder Bladeleaf muses on how the starry heavens hold answers to worldly mysteries, asking whether the wise and lucky might gaze up to discover truth. He also offers guidance on the whereabouts of other elders, such as Elder Bladeswift.",al={"bladeleaf dialogue","what does bladeleaf say"}},{q="Who does Elder Bladeleaf guide you toward next?",a="Elder Bladeleaf points seekers toward Elder Bladeswift, encouraging travelers to continue their pilgrimage of honoring the ancestors.",al={"next elder after bladeleaf","who does bladeleaf send you to"}},{q="Can Horde players visit Elder Bladeleaf?",a="The Lunar Festival allows all adventurers to honor ancestral spirits, but reaching Elder Bladeleaf requires venturing into Dolanaar, an Alliance settlement deep within Teldrassil, making it dangerous for Horde wanderers.",al={"can horde talk to bladeleaf","bladeleaf horde"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Finding an ancestor within the newly grown World Tree of Teldrassil is a poignant reminder of the enduring legacy of the kaldorei and their deep reverence for the night sky.",["class:Druid"]="The elder's presence serves as an opportunity for druids to meditate upon the bond between the earthly realm beneath the canopy and the celestial truths above.",["faction:Alliance"]="Dolanaar offers safe haven and celebration for Alliance travelers making their pilgrimage through the boughs of Teldrassil during the festival."},kw={"bladeleaf","bladeswift","dolanaar","elder bladeleaf","elders","lunar festival","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:elder-bladeleaf","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:940","topic:light"},m={start="Elder Bladeleaf",id=8715},src={"Bladeleaf the Elder"}}
E["quest:916"] = {t="quest",n="Webwood Venom",z="teldrassil",s="Webwood Venom is an Alliance quest in Shadowglen, Teldrassil. The scholar Gilshalan Windwalker tasks young night elves with gathering venom sacs from giant webwood spiders to study how the growth of the new World Tree has affected native wildlife.",h="Webwood Venom is an Alliance quest in Shadowglen, Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Naturalist's Curiosity",b="Gilshalan Windwalker has journeyed to Shadowglen to examine the unnatural size and aggression of the local webwood spiders infesting Shadowthread Cave. He notes that these beasts are cousins to much smaller varieties elsewhere. Suspecting that the immense magical energies of Teldrassil are causing rapid and disturbing mutations in local fauna, he requests venom sacs to compare their biological properties against ordinary arachnid species.",sp=0},{t="The Looming Threat in Shadowglen",b="The webwood spiders dwelling around and inside Shadowthread Cave have become increasingly hazardous to young night elf novices in the glen. Gathering their venom serves a dual purpose: it thins out a dangerous localized infestation while supplying Darnassian researchers with direct biological evidence regarding Teldrassil's volatile influence on the wild.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gilshalan Windwalker?",a="Gilshalan Windwalker is a night elf researcher stationed at Aldrassil in Shadowglen. He studies the native wildlife of Teldrassil to uncover how the rapid growth of the World Tree is affecting local ecology.",al={"gilshalan","who gives webwood venom","quest giver webwood venom"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the webwood spiders so large?",a="They are naturally cousins to much smaller spider varieties. Gilshalan Windwalker believes the rapid growth and latent magical forces of Teldrassil have unnaturally enlarged them and warped their behavior.",al={"giant spiders teldrassil","why are spiders big shadowglen","webwood mutations"},it="origin"},{q="Where is Shadowthread Cave?",a="Shadowthread Cave lies in the northern reaches of Shadowglen, nestled into the rocky ridges past the training grounds of Aldrassil.",al={"shadowthread cave location","where find webwoods","webwood spider cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What will Gilshalan do with the venom sacs?",a="He plans to transport the venom back to Darnassus to compare its chemical and magical properties with those of standard forest spiders, searching for anomalies caused by the World Tree.",al={"why venom sacs","gilshalan venom study","venom research darnassus"},it="item"},{q="Are there other quests in Shadowthread Cave?",a="Yes. While collecting venom, adventurers often assist Dirania Silvershine nearby in aiding Iverron, an elf poisoned by the very same spiders in Shadowthread Cave.",al={"other spider quests shadowglen","shadowthread cave quests","iverron quest"},gp=true},{q="What quest follows Webwood Venom?",a="After examining the venom, Gilshalan asks adventurers to retrieve a Webwood Egg directly from the depths of Shadowthread Cave to study their life cycle.",al={"next quest webwood venom","what comes after webwood venom","gilshalan followup"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Gilshalan Windwalker want Webwood venom sacs?",a="Gilshalan came to Shadowglen as a scholar intending to study the unnaturally large webwood spiders inhabiting Shadowthread Cave. He suspects that the rapid growth and latent magic of the new World Tree, Teldrassil, have altered the local wildlife. By examining venom samples from these beasts, he hopes to compare them to their smaller mainland cousins and prove Teldrassil's profound influence on nature.",al={"why does gilshalan want venom","gilshalan windwalker motive","why collect webwood venom"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What are webwood spiders and why are they in Shadowglen?",a="Webwood spiders are arachnids that have nested in and around Shadowthread Cave on the northern edge of Shadowglen. While related to common woodland spiders, these creatures have grown monstrously large and aggressive under the strange energies radiating from the new World Tree. Their sudden proliferation threatens the sheltered groves of Aldrassil.",al={"what are webwood spiders","why are webwood spiders here","webwood spiders lore"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves coming of age in Shadowglen, this task offers an early lesson in how fragile and unpredictable nature has become under the boughs of Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold a vested interest in Gilshalan's findings, as understanding whether Teldrassil heals or warps surrounding wildlife is central to the Cenarion Circle's vigilance."},kw={"aldrassil","gilshalan","shadowglen","shadowthread","spiders","teldrassil","venom","webwood","windwalker"},rel={"npc:gilshalan-windwalker","subzone:shadowthread-cave","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","quest:3521","quest:4495","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Gilshalan Windwalker",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=916,ri={"Webwood Venom Sac"}},src={"Webwood Venom"}}
E["quest:917"] = {t="quest",n="Webwood Egg",z="teldrassil",s="Gilshalan Windwalker tasks young defenders in Shadowglen with recovering an unhatched spider egg from deep inside Shadowthread Cave. Having gathered samples of their venom, he needs living specimens to study the unnatural aggression afflicting Teldrassil's wildlife. Securing an unhatched clutch allows researchers to study the creatures safely without subduing full-grown arachnids.",h="Gilshalan Windwalker tasks young defenders in Shadowglen with recovering an unhatched spider egg from deep...",sec={{t="A Safe Specimen",b="Having secured raw venom from the aggressive Webwood spiders prowling the perimeter of Shadowglen, Gilshalan Windwalker requires live subjects to better understand their unnatural corruption. Knowing that hauling a thrashing, giant arachnid out of the subterranean depths would prove deadly for any novice, Gilshalan opts for a more practical solution: an unhatched egg taken directly from the brooding clutches within Shadowthread Cave.",sp=0},{t="The Road to the Capital",b="Shadowthread Cave serves as the subterranean nursery for the forest's increasingly hostile arachnids. Penetrating the cave and recovering an intact egg provides scholars with a controlled subject that can hatch under containment. Gilshalan intends to bundle the egg alongside his venom samples and send them directly to Darnassus for further examination, marking the conclusion of his local field study and directing recruits toward higher duties atop the boughs of Aldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Gilshalan want an egg instead of an adult spider?",a="Gilshalan acknowledges that capturing a live, giant spider is far too dangerous for an unproven recruit to handle, and far too difficult for him to contain alone. An intact, unhatched egg allows researchers to transport living specimens safely and arrange containment before the brood emerges.",al={"why an egg","why not catch a live spider","why webwood egg"},it="item"},{q="Where is the Webwood egg found?",a="The egg lies within a webbed nest deep inside Shadowthread Cave, which cuts into the boughs and roots at the northern end of Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",al={"egg location","where to find webwood egg","shadowthread cave nest"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Gilshalan Windwalker?",a="Gilshalan Windwalker is a night elf researcher stationed at Aldrassil in Shadowglen. He investigates the sudden, corrupting afflictions driving Teldrassil's native creatures to violent behavior.",al={"who is gilshalan","gilshalan lore"},it="identity"},{q="What happens to the egg after it is turned in?",a="Gilshalan prepares the egg and his collected venom vials to be shipped to the capital city of Darnassus, where scholars and druids can examine them under controlled conditions once his work in Shadowglen concludes.",al={"what does gilshalan do with the egg","where does the egg go"},it="next_step"},{q="What comes after completing this task?",a="After securing the egg, Gilshalan directs you up Aldrassil to answer Tenaron's Summons, introducing you to the elder druids guiding the heart of Shadowglen.",al={"next quest after webwood egg","what to do after egg"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why are the Webwood spiders so aggressive?",a="The spiders in Teldrassil, like much of its wildlife, have been succumbing to unnatural corruption taking root across the young World Tree, turning once-docile or neutral beasts into aggressive predators.",al={"why are spiders mad","spider corruption"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Gilshalan Windwalker want this done?",a="Gilshalan seeks to thoroughly investigate the strange corruption unsettling Teldrassil's wildlife. Having already collected samples of Webwood venom, he needs living specimens to examine how the taint affects the spiders from birth. Studying an unhatched egg allows scholars in Darnassus to raise and observe captive hatchlings safely, hoping to uncover the source of the bough's creeping sickness.",al={"gilshalan egg motive","why does gilshalan want an egg","gilshalan windwalker quest reason"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Gilshalan send you into Shadowthread Cave instead of going himself?",a="Gilshalan is a researcher and scholar rather than a seasoned warrior. He openly admits that wrangling giant arachnids or venturing into their infested subterranean den exceeds his own physical capabilities. Entrusting a promising young adventurer to navigate the hazardous caverns allows him to remain safely at Aldrassil, preparing the necessary containment measures for the delicate specimen.",al={"why can't gilshalan get the egg","why send me webwood egg","gilshalan why me"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves, recovering this egg illustrates the insidious corruption taking hold on Teldrassil, forcing scholars to study their own homeland's wildlife like hostile threats.",["class:Druid"]="Studying eggs and venom gives Cenarion researchers an opportunity to diagnose whether the corruption altering these beasts can be cleansed or if the blight runs deeper."},kw={"aldrassil","gilshalan windwalker","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","spider egg","teldrassil","webwood","webwood egg"},rel={"npc:gilshalan-windwalker","subzone:shadowthread-cave","quest:916","quest:920","subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","quest:98397"},m={start="Gilshalan Windwalker",level="5",faction="Alliance",id=917,ri={"Webwood Egg"}},src={"Webwood Egg (quest)"}}
E["quest:918"] = {t="quest",n="Timberling Seeds",z="teldrassil",s="Timberling Seeds is an early task given by the botanist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth in Teldrassil. Concerned by the growing hostility of the local nature elementals, Denalan seeks to harvest their seeds to test whether enriched soil can cultivate calmer, more harmonious growth. The task offers a glimpse into the quiet efforts of night elf herbalists working to understand the subtle afflictions plaguing the World Tree.",h="Timberling Seeds is an early task given by the botanist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Restless Nature",b="Timberlings are nature elementals native to the boughs of Teldrassil, intricately linked to the health and vitality of the flora around them. Ordinarily peaceful reflections of the forest's balance, their recent and inexplicable hostility has alarmed the local night elves. Rather than merely culling them, the botanist Denalan hopes to understand the source of their agitation.",sp=0},{t="Seeds of a New Growth",b="Suspecting the blemish lies deep within the ground itself, Denalan aims to sprout fresh timberlings in enriched, carefully treated loam. By collecting seeds from the wandering timberlings near Lake Al'Ameth, he hopes to nurture a gentler generation of elementals and discover whether the land's corruption can be countered from the roots up.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are timberlings?",a="Timberlings are small plant-like nature elementals found on Teldrassil. They mirror the natural order and life cycle of the great tree's flora and fauna.",al={"timberling lore","what are timberlings","nature elementals teldrassil"},it="people"},{q="Why have the timberlings become aggressive?",a="Denalan suspects an underlying flaw or contamination in Teldrassil's soil. As elemental manifestations of the tree's ecology, the timberlings reflect the growing corruption spreading through the island.",al={"why are timberlings angry","timberling hostility","angry timberlings"},it="hostile"},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf naturalist and botanist who tends a small garden retreat on the eastern shore of Lake Al'Ameth, studying Teldrassil's unusual flora and soils.",al={"denalan lore","who is denalan","lake al'ameth botanist"},it="identity"},{q="Where can timberling seeds be gathered?",a="Timberlings roam the shaded thickets, shores, and forest glades surrounding Lake Al'Ameth in central Teldrassil.",al={"where to find timberling seeds","timberling locations","lake al'ameth seeds"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Denalan plan to do with the seeds?",a="Denalan intends to cultivate the seeds within special, purified soil mixtures he has developed, hoping to grow docile timberlings that are free from the forest's agitation.",al={"what happens to seeds","denalan plan","planting timberling seeds"},it="item"},{q="How does this connect to Teldrassil's wider troubles?",a="The aggression of these basic nature spirits is one of the earliest signs that Teldrassil is suffering from an unnatural taint, leading researchers toward deeper investigations in Darnassus.",al={"teldrassil corruption","why is teldrassil sick","tree corruption"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Denalan want timberling seeds gathered?",a="Denalan has observed Teldrassil's nature elementals growing uncharacteristically violent, a worrying sign that something is amiss with the world tree itself. Believing the corruption stems from tainted soil, he hopes to nurture new seeds using specialized earth to cultivate calm, docile timberlings and prove the land can be healed.",al={"why denalan timberling seeds","denalan motive seeds","why does denalan need seeds"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why must you hunt down the timberlings around Lake Al'Ameth?",a="Timberlings are plant-like nature elementals that wander the shores of Lake Al'Ameth. Because they are intimately tied to the environment, they carry the seeds Denalan needs for his research. Unfortunately, their sudden fury makes gathering seeds peacefully impossible, forcing you to fight them to collect the samples.",al={"why kill timberlings","timberlings target","timberlings around lake al'ameth"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, timberlings are direct barometers of Teldrassil's well-being. Watching these gentle spirits turn feral is a chilling sign that their new home is unwell.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold a deep affinity for nature spirits. Aiding Denalan's study helps preserve elemental balance without relying solely on violent culling.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Gatherers attuned to the flora of Teldrassil can appreciate Denalan's botanical experiments, which explore the delicate relationship between plant seeds and enriched soil."},kw={"botany","denalan","elementals","lake al'ameth","seeds","teldrassil","timberling"},rel={"npc:denalan","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},m={start="Denalan",level="9",faction="Alliance",id=918,ri={"Timberling Seed"}},src={"Timberling Seeds (Classic)"}}
E["quest:919"] = {t="quest",n="Timberling Sprouts",z="teldrassil",s="Timberling Sprouts is a quest given by the nature-watcher Denalan near Lake Al'Ameth in central Teldrassil. Concerned by the sudden and unnatural proliferation of woodland sprouts around the lake shores, Denalan asks travelers to uproot them before they mature into hostile timberlings. The task highlights early signs that a creeping corruption is disturbing the balance of the newly grown World Tree.",h="Timberling Sprouts is a quest given by the nature-watcher Denalan near Lake Al'Ameth in central Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Weeding Lake Al'Ameth",b="Around the serene banks of Lake Al'Ameth, strange plant-like creatures known as timberlings have begun multiplying at an alarming rate. Rather than thriving in harmony with the woodland, the emerging timberling sprouts display signs of corruption from the moment they take root. Denalan, a dedicated student of nature residing beside the lake, recognizes that these sprouts are beyond healing. Left unchecked, they rapidly mature into aggressive bark-covered creatures that menace local wildlife and unwary travelers. Gathering and destroying the sprouts serves as an immediate line of defense to keep the grove clean.",sp=0},{t="Signs of a Deeper Taint",b="While uprooting sprouts helps manage the local hazard, Denalan notes with dread just how swiftly the sprouts appear. Their unchecked proliferation is an unnatural phenomenon on Teldrassil. Rather than being an isolated infestation, the tainted sprouts are a symptom of a deeper malaise that threatens the roots and soil of the World Tree itself—a riddle Denalan and the druids of Darnassus are racing to unravel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are timberling sprouts?",a="Timberling sprouts are the nascent, juvenile forms of timberlings—small elemental plant beings native to Teldrassil's boughs. Unfortunately, those germinating along Lake Al'Ameth are tainted and rapidly grow into hostile, aggressive creatures.",al={"what are timberlings","timberling sprout lore","what is a sprout"},it="item"},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is an herbalist and nature-tender living in a quiet camp near the shores of Lake Al'Ameth. He watches over the flora of the bough and studies the ecological shifts and strange corruptions taking hold on Teldrassil.",al={"who gives timberling sprouts","denalan lore","lake al'ameth questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="Why can't these sprouts simply be healed or purified?",a="Denalan observes that the sprouts are already tainted beyond redemption by the time they surface. Attempting to restore them is futile, making culling the only practical way to prevent them from maturing into dangerous hazards.",al={"can sprouts be saved","why destroy timberlings","are sprouts beyond help"},it="threat"},{q="Where are the sprouts found?",a="The sprouts take root along the muddy shores, shallows, and lush banks surrounding Lake Al'Ameth in central Teldrassil.",al={"timberling sprout location","where to find sprouts","lake al'ameth sprouts"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What causes the timberlings to sprout so aggressively?",a="The unnatural surge of hostile timberlings is driven by a corrupting influence spreading into Teldrassil's soil and waters. Even young growths are corrupted before they fully bloom, pointing toward an underlying blight afflicting the young World Tree.",al={"why are timberlings mad","what taints the sprouts","timberling corruption"},it="origin"},{q="What happens after clearing these sprouts?",a="Denalan continues his investigation into the nature of the lake's sickness, examining samples of soil, seeds, and water to trace the root source of the blight.",al={"next quest after sprouts","what follows timberling sprouts"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Denalan want the timberling sprouts cleared?",a="Denalan watches over Lake Al'Ameth and fears the sprouts are already too corrupt to save. If left alone, they will mature into violent, full-grown timberlings that endanger anyone walking the shores. By uprooting them while they are small, he hopes to keep the surrounding land clean and buy time to uncover the root cause of the taint spreading through Teldrassil's waters.",al={"denalan motive sprouts","why clear sprouts","why does denalan want sprouts"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, Teldrassil is meant to be a fresh sanctuary, making corrupted growth around sacred waters like Lake Al'Ameth a deeply troubling omen.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold responsibility for safeguarding the delicate balance of nature; pruning blighted sprouts is a sad but necessary duty to protect the broader ecosystem.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists have a keen eye for how healthy vegetation ought to grow, recognizing instantly that these sprouts are diseased and unnaturally twisted."},kw={"corruption","denalan","lake al'ameth","taint","teldrassil","timberling sprouts","timberlings","weeding"},rel={"npc:denalan","subzone:lake-al-ameth","quest:997","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Denalan",faction="Alliance",id=919,ri={"Timberling Sprout"}},src={"Timberling Sprouts"}}
E["quest:920"] = {t="quest",n="Tenaron's Summons",z="teldrassil",s="Tenaron's Summons marks a crucial transition for young night elves in Shadowglen. After assisting Gilshalan Windwalker with local woodland perils, you are called to ascend the massive boughs of Aldrassil to confer with Tenaron Stormgrip. This summons marks the moment a novice leaves minor local chores behind to confront the deeper spiritual afflictions touching Teldrassil.",h="Tenaron's Summons marks a crucial transition for young night elves in Shadowglen.",sec={{t="A Call to the Boughs",b="Having proven your capability handling the venomous spiders and corrupted wildlife stirring in the glen, your efforts do not go unnoticed. Gilshalan Windwalker passes word that Tenaron Stormgrip himself has requested your presence. Even among the exceptionally long-lived night elves, keeping an elder druid waiting atop the great tree Aldrassil is considered poor form.",sp=0},{t="Ascending Aldrassil",b="Tenaron waits in the highest chamber of Aldrassil, looking out over the verdant boughs of Shadowglen. Answering this summons leads directly into larger matters of stewardship: the cleansing of Teldrassil's moonwells and the investigation of the unnatural corruption creeping into the World Tree's fledgling ecosystem.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tenaron Stormgrip?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip is an influential night elf druid residing in the uppermost chamber of Aldrassil in Shadowglen. He oversees the spiritual care of the glen and coordinates efforts to monitor and cleanse Teldrassil's sacred waters.",al={"who is tenaron","tenaron stormgrip lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I find Tenaron Stormgrip?",a="He is located in the topmost room of Aldrassil, the great hollow trunk-city in Shadowglen. You must climb the winding ramps inside the tree to reach his vantage point near the crown.",al={"find tenaron","tenaron location","where is tenaron"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Tenaron summon me?",a="Once you have proved your worth dealing with the blighted wildlife below, Tenaron entrusts you with greater responsibilities—specifically investigating the sacred moonwells and testing their waters for signs of corruption.",al={"why summons","what does tenaron want"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="Answering the summons leads immediately into the Crown of the Earth questline, where Tenaron tasks you with collecting water samples from the moonwells across Teldrassil to check on the tree's health.",al={"next quest","what comes after tenaron's summons"},it="next_step"},{q="Who sends you to Tenaron?",a="Gilshalan Windwalker gives you the summons once you finish assisting him with the venom-crazed Webwood spiders threatening the lower hollows of Shadowglen.",al={"who gives the quest","gilshalan windwalker"},it="origin"},{q="What is Aldrassil?",a="Aldrassil is the immense bough-tree nestled inside the secluded valley of Shadowglen, serving as the central settlement and training sanctuary for young night elf adventurers on Teldrassil.",al={"aldrassil lore","what is aldrassil"},it="place"},{q="Why does Gilshalan Windwalker send you to Tenaron?",a="Gilshalan is simply relaying a message from higher up. Having watched your progress and deeds resolving troubles in Shadowglen, he knows Tenaron Stormgrip has taken note of your capabilities and urgently requires your aid atop Aldrassil.",al={"gilshalan motive","why send me to tenaron","gilshalan windwalker summons"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="This summons marks your coming of age among the kaldorei, moving from simple woodland defense to direct service to the elders tending the World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="Reporting to Tenaron Stormgrip is an essential step toward learning how the druidic balance of Teldrassil is monitored and maintained."},kw={"aldrassil","gilshalan","shadowglen","stormgrip","summons","teldrassil","tenaron","windwalker"},rel={"npc:tenaron-stormgrip","subzone:aldrassil","quest:921","npc:gilshalan-windwalker","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Gilshalan Windwalker",["end"]="Tenaron Stormgrip",level="5",faction="Alliance",id=920},src={"Tenaron's Summons"}}
E["quest:921"] = {t="quest",n="Crown of the Earth",z="teldrassil",s="Crown of the Earth is an introductory rite given by Tenaron Stormgrip high within Aldrassil. As young night elves prepare to venture beyond the Shadowglen, they are sent to draw sacred water from a nearby moonwell and confront the painful history of Mount Hyjal and their people's lost immortality.",h="Crown of the Earth is an introductory rite given by Tenaron Stormgrip high within Aldrassil.",sec={{t="A Lesson in Recent History",b="Before any fledgling adventurer departs the sheltered boughs of Shadowglen, the elders ensure they understand the steep price the kaldorei recently paid. At the Battle of Mount Hyjal, the World Tree Nordrassil was sacrificed to defeat Archimonde and banish the Burning Legion. With that cataclysmic blast, the night elves lost their ageless immortality and their sacred shield. Tenaron Stormgrip acts as both mentor and historian, assigning novices this ritual to instill humility and purpose before they face a changing world.",sp=0},{t="Waters of the Well",b="The task requires drawing water from a moonwell north of Aldrassil using a crystal phial. These moonwells are no ordinary springs; their waters are infused with remnants of the ancient Well of Eternity. While the druids channel their restorative powers into the wild and the Sentinels revere them as tranquil shrines to the goddess Elune, the kaldorei remain acutely cautious. Arcane sorcery remains strictly outlawed across night elf society, as the wellspring that sustains their land is also a reminder of the reckless magic that once nearly broke the world.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tenaron Stormgrip?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip is a night elf druid positioned high in the upper boughs of Aldrassil in Shadowglen. He mentors young night elves nearing the end of their basic training, assigning rites that teach the solemn history of their race before sending them onward into Teldrassil.",al={"tenaron stormgrip","who gives crown of the earth","aldrassil druid npc"},it="identity"},{q="What is the purpose of collecting moonwell water?",a="Gathering water in the crystal phial is the first step in a ceremonial and practical journey across the island. The waters of the moonwell hold ancient magic that druids utilize to nourish the land, while the ritual itself serves to educate young kaldorei on their society's sacred obligations.",al={"why get moonwell water","filled crystal phial use","moonwell purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why did the night elves lose their immortality?",a="During the Third War, the night elves detonated the ancestral power woven into the World Tree Nordrassil to destroy the demon lord Archimonde atop Mount Hyjal. That sacrifice obliterated the Legion's vanguard, but it stripped the night elves of their eternal youth and disease immunity.",al={"why are night elves mortal","what happened to immortality","nordrassil destruction"},it="history"},{q="Are moonwells considered dangerous?",a="Moonwells contain diluted essences traceably linked to the Well of Eternity. While druids and priestesses safely channel their energies for healing, blessing, and nature communion, the kaldorei strictly forbid using them for arcane sorcery due to the catastrophes reckless magic caused in ancient history.",al={"are moonwells arcane","is moonwell water safe","well of eternity danger"},it="danger"},{q="Where does this quest chain lead next?",a="Returning the filled phial completes the opening lesson of the Crown of the Earth series. Tenaron will guide you onward to Dolanaar and across Teldrassil, tasking you with purifying and tending to various sacred sites across the massive boughs of the new World Tree.",al={"what comes after crown of the earth","crown of the earth questline","next quest after tenaron"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Where is the moonwell for this quest located?",a="The moonwell is situated just a short walk north of the great boughs of Aldrassil, nestled peacefully among the woods of Shadowglen.",al={"where is the moonwell","shadowglen moonwell location","find crystal phial well"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Tenaron Stormgrip send you on this task?",a="Tenaron believes you cannot properly step into the wider world without understanding the recent, painful history of the kaldorei. The sacrifice at the Battle of Mount Hyjal shattered Nordrassil and cost the night elves their immortality, reshaping their entire existence. By sending you to the sacred moonwells to gather their waters, Tenaron uses each step of the journey to teach you how your people arrived at their current state on Teldrassil.",al={"tenaron stormgrip motive","why does tenaron want moonwell water","tenaron motive crown of the earth"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Filled Crystal Phial used for?",a="The Filled Crystal Phial holds water drawn directly from the moonwell north of Aldrassil. These waters contain traces of the ancient Well of Eternity, sacred to the Sentinels and utilized carefully by druids. Tenaron requires you to bring the filled phial back to him atop Aldrassil as a symbolic first step in a larger ritual duty that will guide your path across Teldrassil.",al={"filled crystal phial use","what is filled crystal phial for","purpose of filled crystal phial"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="This rite marks your passage out of Shadowglen, connecting your personal destiny to the sacrifice made atop Mount Hyjal and the responsibilities of safeguarding Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="Moonwells are essential tools of the Cenarion circle, providing purified conduits of nature energy vital for tending to the balance of the forest.",["class:Priest"]="Dedicated to Elune, moonwells serve as reflective shrines where the waters are consecrated under the Mother Moon's gaze."},kw={"aldrassil","crown of the earth","crystal phial","hyjal","moonwell","nordrassil","shadowglen","teldrassil","tenaron stormgrip"},rel={"npc:tenaron-stormgrip","subzone:aldrassil","quest:920","zone:teldrassil","topic:nordrassil","topic:druid","topic:elune","topic:burning-legion"},m={start="Tenaron Stormgrip",level="5",faction="Alliance",id=921,ri={"Filled Crystal Phial"}},src={"Crown of the Earth"}}
E["quest:927"] = {t="quest",n="The Moss-twined Heart",z="teldrassil",s="The Moss-twined Heart is a strange, corrupted core harvested from the monstrous timberling Blackmoss the Fetid. Smothered in oily, dark moss, the heart unnervingly continues to beat on its own, prompting an investigation by the botanist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth.",h="The Moss-twined Heart is a strange, corrupted core harvested from the monstrous timberling Blackmoss the...",sec={{t="A Beating Core",b="Carved from the remains of Blackmoss the Fetid, this Timberling heart is almost unrecognizable beneath a layer of dark, oily moss. The only betrayal of its true nature is a slow, rhythmic pulse that persists even after being severed from the creature. Such unnatural resilience hints that the corruption spreading through Teldrassil's wild plant life is far more pervasive than ordinary rot.",sp=0},{t="Denalan's Examination",b="Denalan, a keen researcher of the local flora stationed near Lake Al'Ameth, recognizes the grim reality of the artifact immediately. Timberlings should be gentle beings intertwined with the boughs of the World Tree, yet this heart demonstrates a virulent blighting influence. Intrigued and troubled, Denalan resolves to plant and study the corrupted organ to understand the foul moss taking root in the island's soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Moss-twined Heart come from?",a="The heart is taken from Blackmoss the Fetid, a large and heavily corrupted timberling wandering the wilderness of Teldrassil.",al={"where do i get the heart","moss-twined heart drop","blackmoss the fetid heart"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the heart still beating?",a="The dark, oily moss infesting the timberling appears to sustain it through unnatural vitality. Even when cut from the creature, the heart maintains a slow, persistent rhythm.",al={"why does heart pulse","still beating heart","timberling heart beat"},it="power"},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf naturalist tending a nursery near the shores of Lake Al'Ameth. He dedicates himself to studying Teldrassil's flora, sproutings, and the creeping corruption affecting the island's timberlings.",al={"who is denalan","where is denalan","denalan location"},it="identity"},{q="What will Denalan do with the heart?",a="Denalan decides to plant the heart in an enchanted planter to sprout and isolate the foul moss, hoping to uncover the root cause of the blighted growth.",al={"what happens to the heart","planting the heart quest","denalan heart research"},it="purpose"},{q="What are timberlings supposed to be?",a="Timberlings are naturally peaceful plant-elementals born of the forest. However, throughout Teldrassil, dark forces and unnatural taint have driven many of them mad and aggressive.",al={"what are timberlings","timberling lore","are timberlings evil"},it="people"},{q="Is the corruption on the heart magical or natural?",a="The moss appears foul and oily rather than healthy, suggesting an unnatural blight infecting the native ecology of Teldrassil rather than normal wilderness decay.",al={"is the moss magic","source of foul moss","teldrassil moss blight"},it="danger"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, watching the young World Tree Teldrassil foster tainted, aggressive timberlings like Blackmoss is a sobering sign that their new home is troubled by a creeping sickness.",["class:Druid"]="Druids of the Cenarion Circle take keen interest in anomalies like this beating, blighted heart, seeking to diagnose whether the corruption can be purged or if it signals deeper rot.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Any student of plants can see the oily growth on this core is completely unnatural, defying standard botanical traits by keeping a severed heart alive."},kw={"blackmoss the fetid","blight","corruption","denalan","lake al'ameth","moss-twined heart","teldrassil","timberling"},rel={"npc:denalan","quest:941","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Moss-Twined Heart",["end"]="Denalan",faction="Alliance",id=927},src={"The Moss-twined Heart"}}
E["quest:928"] = {t="quest",n="Crown of the Earth",z="teldrassil",s="Crown of the Earth is a transitional journey that takes young night elves out of Shadowglen and into the broader realm of Teldrassil. Carrying sacred moonwell water consecrated atop Aldrassil, travelers are directed south along the forest road to meet Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar. It marks the graduation from secluded training to the urgent ecological defense of the great World Tree.",h="Crown of the Earth is a transitional journey that takes young night elves out of Shadowglen and into the...",sec={{t="Leaving the Glade",b="After proving their dedication by sampling the enchanted waters of Shadowglen's moonwell, initiates are summoned before Tenaron Stormgrip at the crown of Aldrassil. Recognizing their readiness, Tenaron seals the gathered water into a larger vessel and commands them to venture beyond the sheltered grove. The road leading south toward Dolanaar is the primary artery out of Shadowglen, winding through woods that have grown increasingly unpredictable and hostile.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Dolanaar",b="Dolanaar serves as the first major village travelers encounter upon exiting the starting glen. Situated along the cobblestone paths curving through central Teldrassil, the settlement bustles around its own pristine moonwell. Here awaits Corithras Moonrage, an elder tasked with overseeing broader preservation efforts across the boughs. The vessel delivered into his keeping ties the fledgling adventurer directly to the wider, troubled fate of the World Tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What am I carrying to Dolanaar?",a="You carry the Partially Filled Vessel, containing sanctified waters drawn from the moonwell in Shadowglen. Tenaron Stormgrip combined your initial offering into this container so Corithras Moonrage could continue ritual work across Teldrassil.",al={"what is the vessel","partially filled vessel lore","what water is this"},it="item"},{q="Who is Corithras Moonrage?",a="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf elder stationed beside the moonwell in Dolanaar. He directs arriving adventurers in continuing the vital rites and investigations needed to sustain the newly grown World Tree.",al={"who is corithras","corithras moonrage role","where is corithras"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Tenaron send me away from Shadowglen?",a="Shadowglen provides basic training, but the challenges confronting Teldrassil require aid across the entire bough. Having proven your ability to handle local threats and venerate the moonwells, Tenaron sends you to Dolanaar where broader tasks await.",al={"why leave shadowglen","why go to dolanaar","tenaron sending me away"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the road to Dolanaar?",a="Follow the cobblestone path south out of Aldrassil and past the gates of Shadowglen. Continue following the cobblestones as the trail bends south and west until you arrive in the village of Dolanaar.",al={"how to get to dolanaar","path to dolanaar","road out of shadowglen"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Tenaron warn about dangerous beasts?",a="Even within the sacred boughs of Teldrassil, wildlife has grown unnaturally aggressive and agitated. Straying off the paved trail risks attacks from territorial spiders, corrupted nightsabers, and aggressive timberstriders.",al={"why are beasts dangerous","corrupted beasts teldrassil","stay on the road warning"},it="danger"},{q="What happens after reaching Dolanaar?",a="Corithras Moonrage accepts the vessel and tasks you with further duties to inspect and bless other moonwells throughout Teldrassil, uncovering deeper issues affecting the forest.",al={"what next after crown of the earth","dolanaar next quest","what does corithras do"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Tenaron Stormgrip send an adventurer instead of delivering the vessel himself?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip oversees the boughs of Aldrassil and tends to the sacred matters of Shadowglen, where young night elves first hone their arts. He cannot abandon his duties atop the great tree simply to carry couriered waters across Teldrassil. Dispatching promising initiates allows him to test your discipline and readiness for the wider world, while ensuring the sacred vessel reaches Corithras Moonrage without leaving Shadowglen unattended.",al={"why send me","why does tenaron need me","why not take vessel himself"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Taking the step beyond Shadowglen's perimeter is an essential rite of passage for every young Kaldorei setting out to serve their people.",["class:Druid"]="Transporting the sanctified waters connects young druids to the ongoing, fragile efforts to nurture and balance Teldrassil's burgeoning ecosystem.",["class:Priest"]="Carrying moonwell water consecrated by Elune's grace represents the sacred duty of her priesthood to tend to the spiritual health of the community."},kw={"aldrassil","corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","moonwell","partially filled vessel","shadowglen","teldrassil","tenaron stormgrip"},rel={"quest:921","npc:corithras-moonrage","npc:tenaron-stormgrip","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:shadowglen","subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Tenaron Stormgrip",["end"]="Corithras Moonrage",level="5",faction="Alliance",id=928},src={"Crown of the Earth (2)"}}
E["quest:929"] = {t="quest",n="Crown of the Earth",z="teldrassil",s="Crown of the Earth is a sacred task assigned by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar to draw sanctified waters from the moonwell near Starbreeze Village. In exchange for replenishing the waters of Darnassus, young night elves learn the tragic history that led their people to cultivate the massive boughs of Teldrassil.",h="Crown of the Earth is a sacred task assigned by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar to draw sanctified waters from...",sec={{t="Sustaining the Moonwells",b="The great central moonwell of Darnassus demands constant communion with the lesser fonts scattered across the crown of the World Tree. Druids craft refined jade phials specifically to draw and carry these luminescent waters without disturbing their purity. By sending initiates on foot to Starbreeze Village, the elders ensure both that the civic fountains remain brimming with Elune's grace and that the youth understand the labor required to nourish Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of the Third War",b="Completing this chore rewards the initiate with oral history. Corithras Moonrage recounts the despair that gripped the kaldorei immediately after the Battle of Mount Hyjal. The sacrifice of the ancestral World Tree Nordrassil stripped the night elves of their precious immortality, and amidst the ruin, Illidan Stormrage was unleashed while Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage vanished into the Emerald Dream. This climate of grief and isolation laid the groundwork for Teldrassil's controversial planting.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of drawing moonwell water?",a="The druids residing in Darnassus regularly replenish their primary city moonwell using the waters collected from surrounding forest shrines, sustaining the sacred network across Teldrassil.",al={"why get moonwell water","moonwell water use","purpose of jade phial"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the moonwell for this task located?",a="The moonwell sits just outside Starbreeze Village, situated to the east of Dolanaar along the forest path.",al={"where is the moonwell","starbreeze moonwell location","starbreeze village well"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Corithras Moonrage?",a="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf druid stationed in Dolanaar who guides young adventurers through the ritual duties and histories surrounding the health of Teldrassil.",al={"who gives the quest","corithras moonrage lore"},it="identity"},{q="What history does Corithras teach upon return?",a="He explains the catastrophic aftermath of the Battle of Mount Hyjal, recalling how Nordrassil was burned, kaldorei immortality vanished, Illidan was freed, and Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage disappeared.",al={"what does corithras say","crown of the earth lore text"},it="history"},{q="Why do night elves feel lost after Mount Hyjal?",a="Nordrassil had bestowed perpetual life and protection to the night elves. Sacrificing the tree's power to annihilate Archimonde shattered their timeless existence, leaving them mortal, directionless, and deeply vulnerable.",al={"why did elves lose immortality","what happened after hyjal"}},{q="What is a Shan'do?",a="Shan'do is an honorific in the Darnassian tongue meaning 'honored teacher', applied here to Malfurion Stormrage, the supreme leader of the druids.",al={"what does shando mean","shando meaning"}},{q="Why does Corithras Moonrage want this done?",a="Corithras is carrying out vital duties for the Cenarion Circle while educating young night elves on their people's fragile state. Teldrassil's sacred waters require constant care and balance, and the druids in Darnassus depend on fresh water gathered from outlying moonwells across the boughs. In exchanging this service for history and guidance, Corithras ensures both that Darnassus's moonwell remains replenished and that you understand the heavy burdens your people bear following the Third War.",al={"corithras moonrage motive","why does corithras need water","corithras moonwell task"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Filled Jade Phial for?",a="The Filled Jade Phial contains sacred water gathered from the moonwell near Starbreeze Village. Specially crafted to hold and preserve moonwell waters without diminishing their latent magical potency, it delivers replenishment to the druids of Darnassus, who draw upon the combined strength of Teldrassil's springs for their rituals and healing.",al={"filled jade phial purpose","what is the jade phial used for","filled jade phial"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Every night elf must confront the loss of immortality and the disappearance of Malfurion Stormrage, making this sacred collection ritual an essential lesson in your people's recent grief.",["class:Druid"]="The moonwells are vital conduits of nature and astral magic, serving as living reservoirs that bind your order's duties in Darnassus to the roots of Teldrassil."},kw={"corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","jade phial","moonwell","nordrassil","starbreeze village","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:starbreeze-village","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:nordrassil","topic:druid","topic:shan-do"},m={start="Corithras Moonrage",level="5",faction="Alliance",id=929,ri={"Filled Jade Phial"}},src={"Crown of the Earth (3)"}}
E["quest:930"] = {t="quest",n="The Glowing Fruit",z="teldrassil",s="The Glowing Fruit is a quest in Teldrassil initiated by discovering a strange fruited plant growing wild in the forest. Suspecting something unnatural, young adventurers deliver the luminescent specimen to the herbalist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth for study.",h="The Glowing Fruit is a quest in Teldrassil initiated by discovering a strange fruited plant growing wild in...",sec={{t="An Unnatural Harvest",b="While traversing the misty boughs of Teldrassil, explorers occasionally stumble across curious, luminous flora bearing large, round fruit. Given the delicate balance of the World Tree and the recent strange behaviors among the island's wildlife, unusual botanical specimens demand careful investigation. Convinced that the strange growth should not be ignored, adventurers pluck the radiant harvest to bring to someone versed in the flora of the wild.",sp=0},{t="Denalan's Investigation",b="At Lake Al'Ameth, the knowledgeable gardener and herbalist Denalan receives the glowing fruit with both fascination and concern. He notes that the specimen appears exotic, speculating that its seeds might have arrived from distant lands across the sea, perhaps even the Eastern Kingdoms. More troubling to Denalan is how the foreign seed reacted with the soil of Teldrassil itself—a reaction that immediately yields an aggressive outburst from hostile boglings as soon as the fruit is handled.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Strange Fruited Plant found?",a="The Strange Fruited Plant grows wild out in the wilds of Teldrassil, tucked among the undergrowth away from the major settlements. Interacting with the plant yields the Glowing Fruit and begins the quest.",al={"where do i find the plant","strange fruited plant location","how to start the glowing fruit"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf herbalist and botanist stationed along the shores of Lake Al'Ameth. He spends his days tending the soil, studying regional flora, and monitoring the strange environmental disturbances affecting Teldrassil.",al={"where is denalan","denalan npc","who turns in glowing fruit"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the fruit glow?",a="Denalan observes that the fruit belongs to an exotic species foreign to Kalimdor. Its bizarre luminescence and vitality stem from a strange, volatile reaction between the foreign seed and the unique, potent soil of Teldrassil.",al={"why is the fruit glowing","what is wrong with the fruit"},it="origin"},{q="What happens when you hand the fruit to Denalan?",a="Upon concluding his brief inspection, the strange energies surrounding the fruit cause three hostile boglings to manifest suddenly around Denalan's camp, immediately attacking nearby adventurers.",al={"what spawns after quest","bogling ambush"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where does Denalan think this plant came from?",a="Denalan suspects the plant's seeds may have originated far away across the Great Sea, carried to Kalimdor from the distant eastern continent of Azeroth.",al={"where did seeds come from","fruit origin"},it="origin"},{q="Does this quest connect to other ecological problems on Teldrassil?",a="Yes. It ties into Denalan's broader research into why the boughs of Teldrassil and its local woodland creatures, like the timberlings and bog beasts, are becoming increasingly agitated and unnatural.",al={"teldrassil corruption","lake al'ameth problems"},it="threat"},{q="Why take the glowing fruit to Denalan?",a="The Strange Fruited Plant is mindless flora, but its eerie luminescence and bizarre appearance immediately stand out against Teldrassil's natural flora. Recognizing that such an unnatural anomaly warrants investigation, you take the initiative to deliver a specimen to Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth, knowing the botanist is actively studying the island's strange ecological disturbances.",al={"why denalan fruit","strange fruited plant motive","why pick glowing fruit"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids dedicated to preserving nature's balance, discovering foreign, volatile flora thriving unnaturally in Teldrassil's sacred boughs is an immediate red flag.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists will appreciate Denalan's botanical insight into how foreign seeds can cross continents and mutate when exposed to enchanted soils.",["race:NightElf"]="Kaldorei youth learn through Denalan that even the young soil of their new home, Teldrassil, is susceptible to unpredictable foreign blights."},kw={"boglings","denalan","glowing fruit","herbalism","lake al'ameth","strange fruited plant","teldrassil","timberlings"},rel={"npc:denalan","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},m={start="Strange Fruited Plant",["end"]="Denalan",faction="Alliance",id=930},src={"The Glowing Fruit"}}
E["quest:931"] = {t="quest",n="The Shimmering Frond",z="teldrassil",s="Discovered among the roots and canopies of Teldrassil, a curious flora radiates with an otherworldly shimmer. Recognizing its rarity, travelers bring a specimen to the botanist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth to uncover its origin.",h="Discovered among the roots and canopies of Teldrassil, a curious flora radiates with an otherworldly shimmer.",sec={{t="A Strange Glow",b="While wandering through the verdant boughs of Teldrassil, observant travelers may stumble across a strange fronded plant. Unlike the usual forest foliage, its fronds catch the light and shimmer with a pulsing, twisting radiance. Such an unnatural presence catches the eye of anyone mindful of the island's delicate, nascent ecosystem.",sp=0},{t="Denalan's Discovery",b="Bringing the cutting to the botanist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth reveals an unexpected truth. Denalan identifies the plant as an exotic specimen not native to northern Kalimdor, having last encountered its kind decades ago during a journey to the distant Swamp of Sorrows in the Eastern Kingdoms. Fascinated by how such a seed could travel across the ocean and thrive to such impressive size upon the World Tree, Denalan immediately sets to work cultivating and testing the sample.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the strange plant originally come from?",a="According to the botanist Denalan, the plant is native to the Swamp of Sorrows, a murky wetland far to the southeast in the Eastern Kingdoms. He had not seen a living specimen since visiting the marshlands decades earlier.",al={"frond origin","where is frond from","swamp plant"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is an inquisitive night elf botanist and herbalist stationed near the banks of Lake Al'Ameth on Teldrassil. He dedicates his time to studying and nurturing Teldrassil's burgeoning plant life, often experimenting with foreign seeds and planters.",al={"denalan lore","who is denalan"},it="identity"},{q="Why is this plant growing on Teldrassil?",a="It remains an ecological mystery. Denalan marvels at how a seed could travel all the way from the Eastern Kingdoms across the Great Sea, yet somehow take root and flourish into such a large specimen in Teldrassil's rich soil.",al={"how did it get to teldrassil","why is frond here"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens after giving the frond to Denalan?",a="Denalan immediately places the specimen into his planter at Lake Al'Ameth to conduct tests. His cultivation quickly causes several sprouted fronds to blossom, leading to further study of the exotic flora.",al={"next quest","denalan test","sprouted fronds"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Does this plant cause corruption in Teldrassil?",a="No. While much of Teldrassil's wildlife faces subtle corruption from foul influences, this plant simply appears to be an unusual, misplaced exotic breed rather than an agent of corruption.",al={"is frond corrupted","corrupted plant"},it="threat"},{q="Why take a frond from the Strange Fronded Plant to Denalan?",a="The plant itself has no conscious motive; it is merely an unusual, pulsating specimen growing wild in Teldrassil's boughs. You recognize its strange, shimmering aura as something exotic and potentially unnatural to the great tree, prompting you to harvest a cutting for Denalan, the resident botanist studying rare flora at Lake Al'Ameth.",al={"strange fronded plant motive","why bring frond to denalan","why take frond"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists and plant enthusiasts will appreciate the botanical intrigue of finding a marshland plant thriving thousands of miles from its native ecosystem.",["class:Druid"]="Druids mindful of the Great Tree's balance take note of non-native plant life introduced to Teldrassil's delicate young canopy.",["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves tending to their new home, Denalan's experiments provide vital insight into how resilient Teldrassil's soil truly is."},kw={"botany","denalan","lake al'ameth","shimmering frond","sprouted fronds","strange fronded plant","swamp of sorrows","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:denalan","quest:2399","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil","zone:swampofsorrows"},m={start="Strange Fronded Plant",["end"]="Denalan",faction="Alliance",id=931},src={"The Shimmering Frond"}}
E["quest:932"] = {t="quest",n="Twisted Hatred",z="teldrassil",s="Twisted Hatred is a covert task issued by Tallonkai Swiftroot in Teldrassil. He asks trusted champions to delve into the cavern of Fel Rock to execute Lord Melenas, a satyr marshalling the local grell into an organized, corrupting force dangerously close to night elf settlements.",h="Twisted Hatred is a covert task issued by Tallonkai Swiftroot in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Bitter Disgrace",b="For the night elves, satyrs represent the living memory of ancient betrayal. Born of Highborne who gave themselves to the Burning Legion during the War of the Ancients, these caprine demons serve as a painful, enduring stain upon kaldorei history. That a satyr would establish a foul foothold right here within Teldrassil, the young World Tree supposed to be a sanctuary, is viewed by local defenders like Tallonkai Swiftroot as an acute embarrassment.",sp=0},{t="The Threat at Fel Rock",b="North of the nearby paths lies Fel Rock, a corrupted cavern system infested with feral grell. Lord Melenas has rallied these naturally chaotic creatures into a hostile, organized force under his dark will. Fearing what the satyr intends to unleash upon the boughs of the World Tree, Tallonkai demands that Melenas be eliminated quickly, quietly, and decisively by bringing back his severed head.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Melenas?",a="Lord Melenas is a satyr who has claimed the cave of Fel Rock in northern Teldrassil. He commands a brood of aggressive grell warriors and schemes to spread corruption throughout the World Tree.",al={"lord melenas","who is melenas","fel rock boss"},it="target"},{q="Where can I find Lord Melenas?",a="He lurks deep within Fel Rock, a jagged cave system located north of Dolanaar in Teldrassil, surrounded by grell and other corrupted creatures.",al={"melenas location","where is melenas","how to find fel rock"},gp=true},{q="Why does Tallonkai Swiftroot want this kept secret?",a="Satyrs represent a horrific, ancient chapter of night elven history, having betrayed their people during the War of the Ancients. Having one lurking so boldly within the heart of the newly planted World Tree is considered an utter disgrace that Tallonkai prefers to resolve without widespread panic.",al={"why secret","why must this stay between us","tallonkai secret"},it="motive"},{q="What is the relationship between satyrs and grell?",a="Grell are small, mischievous, and naturally corrupted wild creatures found across Teldrassil. Satyrs, being cunning and inherently demonic, readily bully or bend such lesser creatures into serving their foul ambitions.",al={"grell and satyrs","why are grell following melenas","satyr grell connection"},it="ties"},{q="Why are there satyrs on Teldrassil in the first place?",a="Teldrassil was grown only a few years ago without the blessings of the Dragon Aspects. Despite the druids' hopes for a clean sanctuary, corruption and dark beings quickly crept onto the island, with satyrs sneaking in to establish footholds in shadowy places like Fel Rock.",al={"satyrs on teldrassil","how did satyrs get here","teldrassil corruption"},it="history"},{q="Who is Tallonkai Swiftroot?",a="Tallonkai Swiftroot is a night elf guardian stationed near Dolanaar who watches for emerging threats against Teldrassil and tasks adventurers with neutralizing nearby pockets of corruption.",al={"tallonkai","who gives twisted hatred"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Tallonkai Swiftroot need Melenas' Head?",a="Tallonkai Swiftroot asks for the severed head of Lord Melenas as irrefutable proof that the satyr has truly been slain. With Lord Melenas dead and his head in hand, Tallonkai can rest assured that the foul threat lurking right beside Shadowglen has been eliminated in secret, allowing him to put the humiliating matter behind him without raising alarm among the elders.",al={"melenas head purpose","why bring back melenas head","what is melenas head for"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Every satyr is an ancient reminder of your ancestors' fall to demonic ambition; putting Lord Melenas to the sword is both a duty to the World Tree and an act of ancestral penance.",["class:Druid"]="The vile presence of Melenas and his corrupted grell at Fel Rock poisons the fragile balance of Teldrassil's newly grown wilderness."},kw={"fel rock","grell","lord melenas","satyr","tallonkai swiftroot","teldrassil","twisted hatred"},rel={"npc:tallonkai-swiftroot","subzone:fel-rock","topic:satyr","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Tallonkai Swiftroot",faction="Alliance",id=932,ri={"Melenas' Head"}},src={"Twisted Hatred"}}
E["quest:933"] = {t="quest",n="Crown of the Earth",z="teldrassil",s="Crown of the Earth is an Alliance quest given by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar. He directs you to draw water from the moonwell near the Pools of Arlithrien, an area increasingly threatened by crazed Gnarlpine furbolgs. Completing this task uncovers how Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm rallied the night elves to raise Teldrassil in the wake of Malfurion Stormrage's disappearance.",h="Crown of the Earth is an Alliance quest given by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.",sec={{t="A Perilous Moonwell",b="Corithras Moonrage tasks you with taking a tourmaline phial to a moonwell resting southeast of Darnassus's entrance, along the shores of the Pools of Arlithrien. The journey is far from quiet. The once peaceful Gnarlpine furbolgs have succumbed to sudden, violent fury, ambushing travelers and harrying Sentinel patrols throughout the region. What early reports wrote off as isolated skirmishes has escalated into a pervasive threat haunting the new home of the night elves.",sp=0},{t="Fandral Staghelm's Ambition",b="Upon receiving the filled phial, Corithras shares critical history regarding Teldrassil's creation. Following the Third War, Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage vanished, leaving the Cenarion druids leaderless and fractured. In his absence, Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm seized the mantle of leadership. Staghelm persuaded the Circle of Ancients in Darkshore that the night elves could not afford idle mourning; they needed to reclaim their lost immortality and heal their civilization by planting a massive new World Tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the moonwell for this quest?",a="The moonwell is located southeast of the main entrance to Darnassus, situated along the southern shores of the Pools of Arlithrien.",al={"arlithrien moonwell","moonwell location","where to fill phial"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine furbolgs attacking?",a="The Gnarlpine were traditionally a peaceful kin of bear-men, but a dark, mindless rage has recently consumed them across Teldrassil. The Sentinels initially dismissed the early attacks as isolated incidents, but the corruption has spread rapidly, turning them into a constant menace to nearby settlements and patrols.",al={"furbolgs mad","gnarlpine aggressive","why furbolgs attack"},it="conflict"},{q="What happened to Malfurion Stormrage?",a="Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage vanished without explanation following the Third War. Even to this day, neither the Cenarion druids nor the night elf leadership know what became of him or where he currently sleeps.",al={"where is malfurion","what happened to stormrage","malfurion missing"},it="history"},{q="Who decided to plant Teldrassil?",a="With Malfurion missing, Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm stepped up to guide the druids. He convinced the Circle of Ancients in Darkshore to support raising a new World Tree, arguing it was essential for the kaldorei to rebuild and regain the immortality lost during the destruction of Nordrassil.",al={"who made teldrassil","staghelm world tree","why was teldrassil grown"},it="leader"},{q="Why does Corithras Moonrage want this done?",a="Corithras Moonrage is investigating the sacred moonwells across Teldrassil to assess and tend to the health of the World Tree. While he guides you through these rituals, he is also sharing the fraught history of Teldrassil's planting—hoping you understand both the sacred duties of your people and the troubling signs spreading across their new home.",al={"why does corithras want moonwell water","corithras motive","why crown of the earth"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Filled Tourmaline Phial for?",a="The phial holds pure water drawn from the moonwell near the Pools of Arlithrien. Corithras requires samples from Teldrassil's various moonwells to monitor the waters nourishing the World Tree and to conduct the rites needed to keep the land's spiritual balance intact amidst rising corruption.",al={"filled tourmaline phial purpose","why fill tourmaline phial","tourmaline phial moonwell"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="This leg of your journey explains the controversial political momentum that brought Teldrassil into existence following Malfurion's sudden disappearance.",["class:Druid"]="The Cenarion Circle's fracture under Fandral Staghelm's leadership becomes clearer as Corithras recounts the desperate push to regain ancient immortality."},kw={"corithras moonrage","dolanaar","fandral staghelm","gnarlpine","malfurion stormrage","pools of arlithrien","tourmaline phial"},rel={"npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:pools-of-arlithrien","subzone:dolanaar","npc:fandral-staghelm","topic:furbolg","topic:druid","topic:sentinels","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Corithras Moonrage",level="9",faction="Alliance",id=933,ri={"Filled Tourmaline Phial"}},src={"Crown of the Earth (4)"}}
E["quest:934"] = {t="quest",n="Crown of the Earth",z="teldrassil",s="Crown of the Earth is a pivotal step in the Dolanaar quest chain investigating the ailments plaguing Teldrassil. Corithras Moonrage tasks adventurers with gathering water from the sacred moonwell in the Oracle Glade, using the journey to reveal the troubling truth behind the World Tree's creation.",h="Crown of the Earth is a pivotal step in the Dolanaar quest chain investigating the ailments plaguing...",sec={{t="The Oracle Glade",b="Corithras Moonrage directs travelers far to the northwest of Teldrassil, nestled beneath the majestic canopy of the Oracle Glade. Resting directly under the massive boughs of the Oracle Tree lies the first and most potent moonwell raised upon the island. Drawing an Amethyst Phial from its shimmering waters brings seekers face to face with the prime sanctuary from which the druids and the tree itself monitor the health of their new homeland.",sp=0},{t="The Denied Blessing",b="Upon returning the phial to Dolanaar, Corithras reveals the dark flaw in Archdruid Fandral Staghelm's grand design. After the sacrifice of Nordrassil at Mount Hyjal, Staghelm sought to restore night elven immortality by planting Teldrassil and asking the Dragon Aspects for their blessings. However, Nozdormu the Timeless One refused, rebuking Staghelm for his sheer arrogance. Queen Alexstrasza followed suit, withholding the Aspect of Life's vital blessing and leaving Teldrassil's growth volatile, imperfect, and vulnerable to deep corruption.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Oracle Glade moonwell located?",a="The moonwell is located in northwestern Teldrassil, situated directly north of the primary road leading into Darnassus. It lies beneath the great boughs of the Oracle Tree.",al={"where is oracle glade","oracle glade moonwell location","oracle well"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why did Nozdormu refuse to bless Teldrassil?",a="Nozdormu, the Dragon Aspect of Time, chided Archdruid Fandral Staghelm for his hubris. The dragons viewed the rushed creation of Teldrassil as a selfish attempt by the night elves to reclaim their lost immortality rather than a selfless defense of nature.",al={"why nozdormu refused","dragon blessing teldrassil","why dragons say no"},it="conflict"},{q="Why didn't Alexstrasza bless the new World Tree?",a="Alexstrasza the Life-Binder concurred with Nozdormu's judgment against Staghelm's pride. Without her life-giving blessing, Teldrassil's growth became wild, unstable, and susceptible to the afflictions creeping through its boughs.",al={"alexstrasza blessing","why did alexstrasza refuse","dragon queen teldrassil"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Corithras Moonrage?",a="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf keeper stationed at Dolanaar. He guides young defenders across the boughs of Teldrassil to sample its moonwells and imparts the history of the tree's flawed beginnings.",al={"corithras","who is corithras moonrage"},it="identity"},{q="Did Teldrassil restore night elf immortality?",a="No. Because Nozdormu refused to bestow his temporal blessing upon Teldrassil, the night elves remain mortal following the loss of Nordrassil at the end of the Third War.",al={"are night elves immortal","teldrassil immortality","do elves live forever again"},it="power"},{q="What is the purpose of collecting water from the Oracle Glade?",a="The moonwell beneath the Oracle Tree is the island's first and most powerful well. Drawing its water allows Corithras to assess the underlying spiritual and natural health of Teldrassil.",al={"why get oracle water","amethyst phial purpose"},it="item"},{q="Why does Corithras Moonrage want this done?",a="Corithras Moonrage is guiding you through the sacred moonwells of Teldrassil to impart the true history of the new World Tree. By sending you under the boughs of the Oracle Tree to draw water from Teldrassil's first and most powerful well, he ensures you commune with its deep wisdom firsthand before he reveals why the boughs remain troubled and barren of immortality.",al={"why does corithras want the water","corithras motive","why send to oracle glade"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="This task strikes at the heart of modern kaldorei society, explaining why the grand hopes of recovering your immortality after the Third War collapsed under the scrutiny of the Great Aspects.",["class:Druid"]="For the Cenarion Circle, visiting the Oracle Tree highlights the ideological split between Fandral Staghelm's forceful ambitions and the natural balance traditionally preserved by Malfurion Stormrage.",["faction:Alliance"]="Understanding the fragile state of Teldrassil explains the persistent blight and creature madness troubling the Alliance's newest capital territory."},kw={"alexstrasza","amethyst phial","corithras moonrage","fandral staghelm","immortality","moonwell","nozdormu","oracle glade","oracle tree","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:oracle-glade","zone:teldrassil","subzone:dolanaar","topic:nordrassil","topic:druid","topic:night-elf","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Corithras Moonrage",level="11",faction="Alliance",id=934,ri={"Filled Amethyst Phial"}},src={"Crown of the Earth (5)"}}
E["quest:935"] = {t="quest",n="Crown of the Earth",z="teldrassil",s="\"Crown of the Earth\" marks the culmination of the cleansing rites across Teldrassil's sacred moonwells. Handing over the gathered waters to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus underscores the growing anxiety over the World Tree's flawed, unblessed existence.",h="\"Crown of the Earth\" marks the culmination of the cleansing rites across Teldrassil's sacred moonwells.",sec={{t="A Flawed Genesis",b="Teldrassil was raised in the wake of the Third War to grant the night elves a new home and restore their lost immortality. However, the Great Aspects Alexstrasza and Nozdormu withheld their blessings, refusing to sanction the tree's creation. Without their divine protection, Teldrassil has fallen victim to creeping sickness, causing bizarre creatures to erupt from the boughs and once-peaceful furbolg tribes to descend into madness.",sp=0},{t="Delivery to the Arch Druid",b="Corithras Moonrage tasks young adventurers with gathering waters from moonwells across the island to monitor and soothe the bough's ailments. Consolidating these samples into a single vessel, Corithras sends the runner deep into Darnassus to the Cenarion Enclave. There sits Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm, the architect of Teldrassil, who views the creeping corruption not as an omen of hubris, but as an annoying burden he alone must solve.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Fandral Staghelm want this moonwell water?",a="Fandral Staghelm commissioned the gathering of moonwell samples across Teldrassil to study and address the corruption seeping through the World Tree. As the leader who championed the tree's planting, he carries the responsibility of finding a solution to the strange beasts and crazed furbolgs unsettling the canopy.",al={"fandral water purpose","why does fandral need the vessel","what is the water for"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is Teldrassil plagued by corruption and crazed beasts?",a="Unlike the ancient World Tree Nordrassil, Teldrassil was planted without the blessings of Alexstrasza the Life-Binder or Nozdormu the Timeless. Denied these primal dragon aspects' protection, the new tree's growth is fundamentally flawed, allowing strange malignancies to take root in the soil and warp nearby wildlife and furbolgs.",al={"why is teldrassil sick","teldrassil corruption","why are furbolgs mad"},it="threat"},{q="Where is Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm located?",a="Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm resides in Darnassus within the Cenarion Enclave. You can find him atop the central druid pavilion overlooking the enclave's sacred groves.",al={"where is fandral","fandral staghelm location","how to find fandral"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Corithras Moonrage?",a="Corithras Moonrage is a druid stationed at Dolanaar who coordinates the moonwell cleansing efforts across Teldrassil. He gathers the purified phials collected by wanderers, combines them into a single vessel, and directs couriers to deliver them to Arch Druid Staghelm in Darnassus.",al={"who gives crown of the earth","corithras role","corithras moonrage"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after completing this quest?",a="Delivering the filled vessel to Fandral Staghelm concludes the primary Crown of the Earth quest chain in Teldrassil. Staghelm accepts the water rather curtly and directs his attention back to managing the broader threats facing the night elf homeland.",al={"crown of the earth follow up","what comes after crown of the earth 6","next quest after crown of the earth"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is Fandral Staghelm so dismissive upon receiving the vessel?",a="Fandral Staghelm is notoriously proud, impatient, and burdened by the daunting task of ruling the Cenarion Circle while Malfurion Stormrage remains absent. He views administrative setbacks and slow messengers with disdain, feeling the heavy yoke of Teldrassil's survival rests entirely on his own shoulders.",al={"why is fandral rude","fandral personality","is fandral always grumpy"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Corithras Moonrage want the vessel brought to Fandral?",a="Corithras is deeply worried about the growing sickness infecting Teldrassil. Because the World Tree grew without the vital blessings of the Aspects Alexstrasza and Nozdormu, strange beasts have risen from the soil and once-peaceful furbolgs have turned violently mad. Corithras believes Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm is actively researching a remedy to purge this spreading corruption, so he urgently combines the water samples you collected across the boughs and sends you to deliver them directly to Darnassus.",al={"corithras motive","why send moonwell water","why does corithras want this done"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Corithras Moonrage send you instead of going himself?",a="Corithras remains stationed at Dolanaar to oversee local matters and monitor the troubling anomalies disturbing Teldrassil's lower boughs. You have personally journeyed to the various moonwells to gather the water phials, proving your stamina and dedication. Entrusting you with the combined vessel allows Corithras to keep watch over Dolanaar while ensuring Fandral Staghelm receives the samples in Darnassus without further delay.",al={"why send player to fandral","why me corithras","why doesn't corithras deliver the vessel"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="This rite exposes the quiet anxiety beneath your new home: Teldrassil was planted in pride without the Dragon Aspects' blessings, and its growing sickness is a reminder of the fragility of your people's fresh start.",["class:Druid"]="Carrying moonwell waters to the Arch Druid of the Cenarion Circle brings you directly before Fandral Staghelm, showcasing the fierce political and spiritual divide that has gripped druidic leadership in Malfurion's absence.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the wider Alliance, Darnassus is an imposing capital of ancient mystery, but the corrupted wilderness around it proves that even the night elves face internal perils on their own sacred ground."},kw={"alexstrasza","cenarion enclave","corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","darnassus","fandral staghelm","moonwell","nozdormu","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:929","npc:fandral-staghelm","npc:corithras-moonrage","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","subzone:cenarion-enclave","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Corithras Moonrage",["end"]="Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm",level="11",faction="Alliance",id=935},src={"Crown of the Earth (6)"}}
E["quest:937"] = {t="quest",n="The Enchanted Glade",z="teldrassil",s="In the Oracle Glade on northwestern Teldrassil, Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak struggles to protect the ancient Oracle Tree from aggressive Bloodfeather harpies. After a dispatched runner bound for Darnassus is slain, defenders are called upon to strike back at the harpies' nests and recover their belts as proof.",h="In the Oracle Glade on northwestern Teldrassil, Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak struggles to protect the ancient...",sec={{t="A Glade Under Siege",b="The Oracle Glade is one of Teldrassil's sacred retreats, centered upon a colossal, ancient specimen known as the Oracle Tree. Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak was dispatched with an escort of warriors to keep watch over this venerable bough. Unfortunately, savage Bloodfeather harpies have encroached on the hollows, nesting aggressively throughout the surrounding canopy and threatening anyone who draws near.",sp=0},{t="Severed Lines to Darnassus",b="Tensions peaked when the Oracle Tree attempted to send a courier to the capital city of Darnassus carrying an urgent report. The messenger never cleared the boughs; harpies ambushed and slaughtered the runner before the report could leave the glade. In response, Arynia has tasked local adventurers with culling the flock and retrieving Bloodfeather belts to push back the encroaching flock.",sp=0},{t="A Summons from the Tree",b="Once the immediate threat of the nearby nests is diminished, the ancient tree itself responds. The Oracle Tree sheds a fragment of its enchanted bark, seeking an emissary to deliver its message into the hands of the high leadership of the kaldorei.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are harpies attacking the Oracle Glade?",a="The Bloodfeather clan nests densely across northern Teldrassil. In the Oracle Glade, they have encircled the Oracle Tree, fiercely guarding their roosts and attacking anyone attempting to travel to or from the sacred spot.",al={"harpies in oracle glade","why bloodfeather attack","oracle tree harpies"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak?",a="Arynia Cloudsbreak is a Sentinel officer stationed alongside a modest vanguard in the Oracle Glade. Her primary mission is defending the Oracle Tree from surrounding harpies and reestablishing contact with Darnassus.",al={"arynia cloudsbreak","who gives the enchanted glade","cloudsbreak lore"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to the runner sent to Darnassus?",a="The runner dispatched with a report from the Oracle Tree to Darnassus was ambushed and killed along the glade paths by Bloodfeather harpies before reaching safety.",al={"oracle tree messenger","dead runner darnassus"},it="history"},{q="What is the Oracle Tree?",a="The Oracle Tree is a massive, sentient ancient rooted in the Oracle Glade. It observes the boughs of the World Tree and communicates its wisdom and warnings to the night elf leadership.",al={"oracle tree teldrassil","who is the oracle tree"},it="place"},{q="What proof does Sentinel Cloudsbreak require?",a="Sentinel Cloudsbreak requires six Bloodfeather belts taken from the slain harpies as concrete proof that their roosts around the glade have been thinned.",al={"bloodfeather belt quest","how many belts","quest proof"},it="item"},{q="What happens after culling the harpies?",a="With the immediate perimeter secured, the Oracle Tree sheds a piece of its own bark, opening a direct line of communication for an adventurer to take its long-delayed message toward Darnassus.",al={"next quest after enchanted glade","what does oracle tree do next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak want this done?",a="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak was dispatched with a small detachment of Sentinels to defend the sacred Oracle Tree. Harpies have nested throughout the glade, hemming in the defenders and even slaughtering a courier sent to Darnassus with vital reports. Arynia cannot leave her defensive post unguarded, so she needs an adventurer to strike directly at the nests and push back the flock before the glade is overwhelmed.",al={"why kill the harpies","arynia cloudsbreak motive","why protect the oracle tree"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who are the Bloodfeather harpies threatening the glade?",a="The Bloodfeather harpies are vicious, avian predators that have roosted across the northwestern reaches of Teldrassil. Aggressive and territorial, they have built nests encircling the Oracle Glade, cutting off communication with Darnassus and seeking to drive away or slaughter the night elf protectors guarding the ancient tree.",al={"who are the harpies","bloodfeather harpies teldrassil","why are harpies here"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why can't Sentinel Cloudsbreak deal with the harpies herself?",a="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak leads only a small contingent of Sentinels stationed at the Oracle Tree. With their messenger already dead and harpies encircling the position, her remaining troops must stay grounded to guard the sacred tree from ambush. Taking the offensive into the harpy rookeries requires capable, unattached travelers willing to venture into hostile nests.",al={"why does arynia need my help","why can't the sentinels kill the harpies","why me enchanted glade"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Defending the ancient spirits of the World Tree and safeguarding Sentinels from harpy defilement is a solemn duty for any kaldorei.",["faction:Alliance"]="Assisting the Sentinels in securing the sacred groves of Teldrassil strengthens ties with the night elf leadership in nearby Darnassus.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold the sentient ancients in great reverence; clearing harpy infestations that threaten the Oracle Tree helps protect the glade's natural balance."},kw={"arynia cloudsbreak","bloodfeather","darnassus","harpies","oracle glade","oracle tree","sentinel","teldrassil","the enchanted glade"},rel={"subzone:oracle-glade","npc:sentinel-arynia-cloudsbreak","quest:940","quest:952","zone:teldrassil","topic:sentinels","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak",level="11",faction="Alliance",id=937,ri={"Bloodfeather Belt"}},src={"The Enchanted Glade (Classic)"}}
E["quest:938"] = {t="quest",n="Mist",z="teldrassil",s="Mist is an escort quest in the shaded boughs of Teldrassil. After discovering a wounded gray sabercat abandoned deep in the woods, travelers must shepherd her safely back to Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak at a nearby moon well.",h="Mist is an escort quest in the shaded boughs of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Wounded Companion",b="Tucked away amid the wild undergrowth of Teldrassil lies Mist, a distinctive gray sabercat marked by severe, slashing lacerations across her back and belly. Rather than acting as a feral beast of the wilds, Mist exhibits remarkable calm and bright intelligence in her blue eyes, immediately looking to friendly travelers for guidance and protection.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Ambush",b="Mist is the beloved companion of Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak. While patrolling the great boughs near the Oracle Tree, Arynia was caught off guard by foul witches who ambushed the pair and separated them. Believing her loyal pet had met a bloody end, Arynia withdrew in grief to the tranquility of a local moon well, where she desperately hoped against hope for Mist's survival.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mist?",a="Mist is a loyal gray sabercat companion belonging to Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak. She is found injured in the forests of Teldrassil after being separated from her master during a violent ambush.",al={"mist cat","what is mist","who is the sabercat"},it="identity"},{q="Who injured Mist?",a="Mist and her master were ambushed by local witches lurking within the woods of Teldrassil. The attackers managed to separate the pair and inflicted deep lacerations across the cat's back and stomach.",al={"who hurt mist","why is mist bleeding","witches ambush mist"},it="threat"},{q="Where should Mist be escorted?",a="Mist needs to be brought safely to Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak, who is stationed beside the moon well near the Oracle Tree.",al={"where do i take mist","mist turn in","mist destination"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who is Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak?",a="Arynia Cloudsbreak is a night elf Sentinel stationed in Teldrassil. She serves the safety of the boughs and deeply mourned Mist, blaming herself for letting the forest's witches catch them unaware.",al={"arynia cloudsbreak","cloudsbreak","mist owner"},it="people"},{q="Why are night elf Sentinels bonded with sabercats?",a="Night elf Sentinels have fought alongside the great cats of Kalimdor for millennia, relying on them as fierce partners in skirmishes, scouts in the shadowy boughs, and trusted lifelong companions.",al={"night elf cat companions","sentinel sabercats","why sabercats"},it="ties"},{q="Where is the Oracle Tree in relation to this rescue?",a="The Oracle Tree sits in northwestern Teldrassil, with a nearby moon well providing holy waters where Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak tends to her duties and mourns her lost scout companion.",al={"oracle tree location","moon well mist"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Mist need your help?",a="Mist is badly wounded with deep lacerations across her back and stomach, separated from her companion Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak after being ambushed and captured by harpies. Weakened and stranded alone in the forest, she cannot safely navigate the perils of Teldrassil on her own to reach the safety of the moon well without your protection.",al={"why help mist","mist motive","why does mist need an escort"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Mist rely on you instead of saving herself?",a="Mist is too gravely injured to fight through the hostile woods or make the long journey back unassisted. Being a beast separated from her Sentinel, she has no nearby allies or guards to turn to; when you happen upon her, she recognizes you as a friendly presence and places her trust in your ability to guide and shield her.",al={"why me mist","why cant mist escape alone","why does mist follow you"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The bond between Sentinel and sabercat is a cornerstone of night elf warfare and forest lore; rescuing Mist upholds that ancient, sacred companionship.",["class:Hunter"]="Any beastmaster will recognize the fierce devotion and intelligent gaze in Mist's eyes, making her safe return to her partner a matter of professional pride.",["faction:Alliance"]="Aiding the Sentinels in Teldrassil cements vital goodwill between the fledgling Alliance and the kaldorei defenders of the world tree."},kw={"arynia cloudsbreak","mist","moon well","oracle tree","sabercat","sentinel","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:sentinel-arynia-cloudsbreak","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Mist",["end"]="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak",faction="Alliance",id=938},src={"Mist (quest)"}}
E["quest:940"] = {t="quest",n="Teldrassil",z="teldrassil",s="Following the cleansing of the rogue harpies near the Oracle Tree, Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak entrusts you with carrying a status report to Darnassus. The inscribed bark is addressed to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm, bearing news of the state of the boughs and the ongoing corruption plaguing the World Tree.",h="Following the cleansing of the rogue harpies near the Oracle Tree, Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak entrusts you...",sec={{t="A Messenger to the Stone City",b="Deep in the boughs of Teldrassil, the Oracle Tree watches over the forest. After clearing the harpies from their nests in the Enchanted Glade, Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak decides it is finally safe to dispatch word to the kaldorei leadership. Entrusting you with a piece of inscribed bark, she sends you across the wilderness and into Darnassus—the great 'forest of stone'—to deliver the Oracle Tree's report directly to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm.",sp=0},{t="Staghelm's Ambition and Frustration",b="When presented with the report, Fandral Staghelm receives it with mixed feelings. Though grateful for the news that the harpies were pushed back, the report underlines a deeper truth: as soon as one threat is diminished on Teldrassil, another festers in its place. For Staghelm, who championed the planting of the new World Tree to reclaim the night elves' lost immortality, the ongoing afflictions of the boughs are a bitter reminder that his grand work remains far from finished.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the quest 'Teldrassil'?",a="This quest acts as a narrative bridge connecting your wilderness adventures around the Oracle Tree to the capital city. Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak tasks you with carrying an Inscribed Bark containing the Oracle Tree's report to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.",al={"teldrassil quest objective","what does this quest do","teldrassil delivery"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak?",a="Arynia Cloudsbreak is a night elf Sentinel stationed near the Oracle Tree in the Teldrassil wilds. She monitors regional threats like the local Bloodfeather harpies and coordinates forest defenses with Darnassus.",al={"arynia cloudsbreak lore","who starts teldrassil quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Arynia call Darnassus a 'forest of stone'?",a="While the night elves live within the canopy of the World Tree, the city of Darnassus is built with monumental marble and stone temples, bridges, and pavilions. Compared to the untamed wilderness around the Oracle Tree, the capital is a constructed forest of stone.",al={"forest of stone meaning","why forest of stone"},it="place"},{q="Why is Fandral Staghelm so concerned about the Oracle Tree's report?",a="Staghelm spearheaded the creation of Teldrassil in hopes of regaining kaldorei immortality after Nordrassil was damaged in the Third War. News from the Oracle Tree confirms that Teldrassil continues to suffer from spreading corruption and wildlife turmoil, putting his ambitions in jeopardy.",al={"fandral staghelm reaction","why is staghelm worried"}},{q="What quest leads into this, and what follows it?",a="This quest immediately follows 'The Enchanted Glade', where you deal with the harpies menacing the Oracle Tree. After delivering the report to Arch Druid Staghelm, he sends you onward to Darkshore with the follow-up quest 'Grove of the Ancients'.",al={"teldrassil quest chain","what quest next"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Where can Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm be found?",a="Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm resides in Darnassus, standing at the summit of the Cenarion Enclave where he oversees the druids of the Cenarion Circle and guides the governance of the kaldorei.",al={"where is fandral","fandral staghelm location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak want this report delivered?",a="Arynia needs Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm to receive the Oracle Tree's report so Darnassus remains informed on the bough's condition. The woods have suffered under harpy infestations and unnatural corruption, and past messengers failed to make the trek safely. With calm restored to the Oracle Tree's glade, the news must reach the Arch Druid so the leadership can assess the state of the world tree.",al={"why send report to fandral","arynia cloudsbreak motive","why does arynia want report delivered"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Arynia Cloudsbreak send you instead of another messenger?",a="Previous messengers sent along the forest trails failed to reach Darnassus or were lost along the way, making Arynia hesitant to risk another ordinary runner. Having proven your courage and battle prowess by cleansing the harpies from the Oracle Glade, you have earned the forest's favor and demonstrated that you can defend yourself and the message along the perilous roads to the city.",al={"why send me to darnassus","why not send another messenger","why arynia needs you"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Delivering this report brings you face-to-face with Arch Druid Staghelm, revealing his personal obsession with restoring kaldorei immortality through the troubled boughs of Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="Carrying word from the ancient Oracle Tree directly to the leader of the Cenarion Circle highlights the ongoing struggle to cleanse Teldrassil's natural balance.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions completing their early duties on the island, this mission provides a formal introduction to the night elf capital and its stern leadership."},kw={"arynia cloudsbreak","cenarion enclave","darnassus","fandral staghelm","immortality","inscribed bark","kaldorei","oracle tree","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:fandral-staghelm","npc:sentinel-arynia-cloudsbreak","quest:937","quest:952","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid"},m={start="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak",["end"]="Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm",level="11",faction="Alliance",id=940},src={"Teldrassil (quest)"}}
E["quest:941"] = {t="quest",n="Planting the Heart",z="teldrassil",s="Planting the Heart is a task undertaken for the herbalist Denalan by the shores of Lake Al'Ameth in Teldrassil. After stripping away the suffocating moss from a strange wooden heart taken from a corrupted timberling, Denalan tests whether his specially enriched soil can cleanse and heal the lingering taint within it.",h="Planting the Heart is a task undertaken for the herbalist Denalan by the shores of Lake Al'Ameth in...",sec={{t="A Second Chance at Life",b="While examining the strange wooden organ recovered from the corrupted timberling known as Blackmoss the Fetid, Denalan manages to scrape away the foul moss strangling its surface. Yet despite his efforts, a deeper, unnatural taint still pulses within the wood. Rather than burn or discard it, Denalan relies on his lifelong craft of botany and soil tending. He instructs travelers to bury the heart directly into his personal planter box, trusting the rich nutrients he blended to coax whatever natural vitality remains back toward health.",sp=0},{t="The Miracle of Enriched Earth",b="Placing the blackened wooden heart into Denalan's planter yields an unexpected reaction. The moment it touches the fertile soil, the heart burrows into the dirt as if guided by primal instinct. Moments later, it re-emerges to the surface, cleansed of its foul corruption and pulsing with a gentle, companionable warmth. By purifying the seed of a fallen, tainted creature, Denalan demonstrates that even when the wild denizens of Teldrassil fall prey to unnatural blights, careful nurturing and sacred earth can still restore harmony.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this tainted heart come from?",a="The heart originally came from Blackmoss the Fetid, a corrupted timberling lurking along the shores of Lake Al'Ameth. It was recovered choked with tangled, foul moss before Denalan scraped it clean.",al={"heart origin","where did the heart come from","blackmoss heart"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf botanist and herbalist who tends an isolated camp on the eastern edge of Lake Al'Ameth. He spends his days studying Teldrassil's plant life, investigating the strange corruption creeping through the boughs, and mixing enriched soils.",al={"who is denalan","denalan lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why put the heart in a planter instead of destroying it?",a="Denalan believes in understanding and healing nature rather than merely destroying corrupted beings. He hopes the nutritive soil he prepared can purge the taint and restore the heart's original, pure vitality.",al={"why plant the heart","why heal the heart"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when you bury the heart?",a="The heart immediately burrows into the soil upon contact. Seconds later, it wriggles back to the surface completely cleansed of its foul taint, pulsing gently as an animated companion.",al={"what happens in the planter","heart burrows"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Does this cure the corruption of the timberlings?",a="It cures only this single salvaged heart. While it proves that individual botanical spirits can be cleansed with care and rich soil, the overarching corruption spreading across Teldrassil remains an active danger.",al={"are timberlings cured","curing timberlings"},it="power"},{q="Why is the soil in Denalan's planter special?",a="Denalan has spent considerable time experimenting with compost and nutritive soil blends around Lake Al'Ameth, designing dirt potent enough to revitalize sickly flora and purge creeping decay.",al={"denalan soil","planter soil"},it="item"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For a druid, witnessing a corrupted timberling's core cleansed through rich earth offers a reassuring sign that the unnatural taint afflicting the World Tree's boughs can still be turned back through natural care.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Denalan's mastery over nutrient-rich soil and botanical rejuvenation showcases the vital link between studying the earth and mending damaged plant life.",["race:NightElf"]="Restoring living wood and coaxing life from fallen forest spirits reflects the kaldorei commitment to stewarding nature even in the face of Teldrassil's troubling ailments."},kw={"blackmoss the fetid","cleansed heart","denalan","lake al'ameth","planter","tainted heart","teldrassil","timberling"},rel={"npc:denalan","quest:927","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Denalan",["end"]="Denalan's Planter",faction="Alliance",id=941},src={"Planting the Heart"}}
E["quest:96630"] = {t="quest",n="The Adventurer",z="teldrassil",s="The Adventurer is a brief quest set in Teldrassil involving the discovery of a discarded journal in the wilds. The plain notebook recounts the humble travels and camping outings of an unknown traveler, intended for delivery to Lyreena Duskblade near Dolanaar.",h="The Adventurer is a brief quest set in Teldrassil involving the discovery of a discarded journal in the wilds.",sec={{t="A Wanderer's Journal",b="Amid the dense boughs and tangled roots of Teldrassil, travelers occasionally stumble across abandoned personal items. This simple journal recounts the unremarkable yet earnest wanderings of a nameless adventurer. Instead of grand heroics or perilous monster hunts, the bulk of its pages enthusiastically document the simple joys of making camp beneath the twilight canopy.",sp=0},{t="Delivery to Dolanaar",b="Rather than leaving the personal keepsake to weather in the damp wilderness, the finder is drawn to carry it toward Dolanaar. Lyreena Duskblade, stationed near the night elf settlement, serves as the recipient for the displaced pages, perhaps offering closure or insight into whose travels were left behind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the journal mentioned in the quest?",a="It is a plain personal notebook recovered in the wilds of Teldrassil. Its entries detail the quiet life and travels of an unfamiliar figure, highlighting ordinary adventures and an enduring fondness for camping outdoors.",al={"lost journal","what is the book","the adventurer journal"},it="item"},{q="Who is Lyreena Duskblade?",a="Lyreena Duskblade is a night elf found near Dolanaar. She is the intended recipient of the lost journal found out in the forest.",al={"lyreena","where is lyreena duskblade","turn in npc"},it="people"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The quest takes place in Teldrassil, the great bough of the night elves, focused in the wilderness surrounding the village of Dolanaar.",al={"where is the adventurer quest","quest zone"},it="place"},{q="Does the journal describe dangerous monsters or battles?",a="No. The writing is described as quite plain and focuses on the unassuming life and wanderings of an unknown individual, with particular emphasis on how enjoyable camping can be.",al={"journal lore","what is in the journal","what does it say"}},{q="Who can complete this task?",a="This task is strictly for members of the Alliance wandering the starter territory of Teldrassil, particularly novice night elves venturing near Dolanaar.",al={"can horde do this","alliance quest"},gp=true},{q="Why turn the journal in to Dolanaar?",a="Dolanaar is the central gathering post and crossroad for that region of Teldrassil, making it the most sensible place to deliver misplaced personal belongings to local sentinels and wardens like Lyreena Duskblade.",al={"why dolanaar","why lyreena"},it="purpose"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Young night elves patrolling Teldrassil often find signs of travelers passing through, turning over lost personal relics to sentinels like Lyreena Duskblade.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance novices finding their footing beneath the World Tree, returning misplaced belongings to local scouts helps maintain order in the groves."},kw={"camping","dolanaar","journal","lost journal","lyreena duskblade","teldrassil","the adventurer"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Object #654846",["end"]="Lyreena Duskblade",level="6",faction="Alliance",id=96630},src={"The Adventurer (Teldrassil)"},fv=true}
E["quest:997"] = {t="quest",n="Denalan's Earth",z="teldrassil",s="Denalan's Earth is an errand running south from the settlement of Dolanaar to the tranquil waters of Lake Al'Ameth. Syral Bladeleaf asks travelers to hand-deliver a delayed shipment of rare, enriched soil to her botanical colleague, Denalan, who studies the boughs and flora of the new World Tree.",h="Denalan's Earth is an errand running south from the settlement of Dolanaar to the tranquil waters of Lake...",sec={{t="A Courier for Dolanaar",b="As travelers pass through Dolanaar on their way south toward Lake Al'Ameth, Syral Bladeleaf flags them down with an overdue errand. Her fellow researcher, Denalan, ordered a special package of rare earth all the way from Darnassus to support his ongoing botanical studies. The parcel was delayed in transit and only recently arrived in Dolanaar. Rather than letting the rich soil spoil or sit idle, Syral seeks an accommodating courier willing to walk it down the forest trail to Denalan's lakeside campsite.",sp=0},{t="Cultivating Teldrassil",b="Denalan maintains a solitary workstation along the eastern shores of Lake Al'Ameth, where he observes how Teldrassil's sapling ecosystem takes root. Teldrassil is young, having grown rapidly in the wake of Mount Hyjal's cataclysm, and its flora behaves in unexpected ways. Denalan uses unique soil mixtures and specimens to test the vitality and behavior of the island's timberlings and native plants, making the fresh shipment of rare earth crucial to his experiments.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf researcher and herbalist who has set up camp on the eastern shores of Lake Al'Ameth. He dedicates his time to studying, cultivating, and experimenting on Teldrassil's unique plant life.",al={"denalan lore","who is denalan","denalan npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Syral Bladeleaf located?",a="Syral Bladeleaf resides in Dolanaar, the main night elf outpost in central Teldrassil, where she coordinates research supplies and assists travelers journeying across the boughs.",al={"syral bladeleaf location","where is syral"},gp=true},{q="What is the rare earth used for?",a="The shipment contains specially enriched soil sent from the capital of Darnassus. Denalan relies on it to nurture experimental plantings and test how Teldrassil's native saplings, like timberlings, react to diverse growing conditions.",al={"what does denalan need the earth for","rare earth purpose"},it="item"},{q="Where is Lake Al'Ameth?",a="Lake Al'Ameth lies south of Dolanaar, forming a peaceful body of water nestled among the southern roots of Teldrassil.",al={"lake al'ameth location","how to get to lake al'ameth"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why was the shipment late?",a="The package had to travel out from Darnassus and encountered unspecified transit delays along Teldrassil's winding roads before finally reaching the distribution hub in Dolanaar.",al={"why was the earth late","delayed parcel"}},{q="What does delivering this earth lead to?",a="Upon receiving the rare soil, Denalan recruits the courier to help gather timberling sprouts and seeds along the lake's shores, beginning a deeper series of botanical field studies.",al={"denalan earth follow up","what comes next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Syral Bladeleaf want the rare earth delivered?",a="Denalan has been eagerly awaiting this shipment from Darnassus to continue his experiments on Teldrassil's local flora. Because the rare earth was delayed in transit and only recently arrived in Dolanaar, Syral wants it brought to his lakeside camp without further delay before the material loses its potency.",al={"why deliver rare earth","syral bladeleaf motive","why send earth to denalan"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Syral ask you to make the delivery?",a="Syral Bladeleaf stays in Dolanaar tending to her duties, and she simply spots you as an able traveler heading south toward Lake Al'Ameth. Since the shipment has already suffered lengthy delays, entrusting it to someone already journeying toward Denalan's retreat is the quickest way to get it into his hands.",al={"why does syral need me","why not send a courier","why me denalan's earth"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists will appreciate Denalan's lakeside retreat, as his experiments center on understanding the fragile, burgeoning plant life unique to the newly grown World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="Druids share a natural affinity with Denalan's efforts, as tracking the growth and balance of Teldrassil's flora is essential to safeguarding nature on the new bough.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves emerging from Shadowglen, assisting Syral and Denalan serves as an early introduction to the wider stewardship required to sustain Teldrassil."},kw={"darnassus","denalan","dolanaar","lake al'ameth","rare earth","syral bladeleaf","teldrassil","timberling"},rel={"npc:denalan","npc:syral-bladeleaf","subzone:lake-al-ameth","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},m={start="Syral Bladeleaf",["end"]="Denalan",faction="Alliance",id=997},src={"Denalan's Earth"}}
E["subzone:aldrassil"] = {t="subzone",n="Aldrassil",z="teldrassil",s="Aldrassil is the colossal bough-tree and settlement nestled at the heart of Shadowglen in northeastern Teldrassil. Serving as the primary refuge and training ground for young kaldorei, its carved hollows shelter trainers, merchants, and local leadership.",h="Aldrassil is the colossal bough-tree and settlement nestled at the heart of Shadowglen in northeastern...",sec={{t="Heart of Shadowglen",b="Rising high above the secluded vale of Shadowglen, Aldrassil functions as both shelter and civic hub for young night elves taking their first steps in the world. Built into and around the colossal trunk of this ancient growth, winding ramps lead past class trainers and artisans to the high roost where Tenaron Stormgrip oversees the glade's protection. While the world bough Teldrassil stretches across the horizon, Aldrassil provides a safe, grounded canopy where novices learn their arts before venturing down into the troubled wilds of Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Aldrassil?",a="Aldrassil is the massive, hollowed-out tree and settlement situated in the center of Shadowglen, northeastern Teldrassil. It serves as the starting haven where young night elves gather training, goods, and guidance.",al={"aldrassil tree","what is aldrassil","shadowglen big tree"},it="place"},{q="Who leads the settlement at Aldrassil?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip oversees Shadowglen from his roost at the very top of Aldrassil, coordinating the defense of the vale and guiding newly awakened kaldorei.",al={"who leads aldrassil","aldrassil leader","tenaron stormgrip location"},it="in_charge"},{q="What services can be found here?",a="The tree houses class trainers for young night elf warriors, rogues, druids, hunters, and priests, alongside local supply merchants, armorers, and questgivers attending to the immediate needs of the glade.",al={"trainers in aldrassil","vendors aldrassil","what is in aldrassil"},gp=true},{q="Who lives in Aldrassil?",a="Aldrassil is home to the night elf guardians, trainers, and caretakers who watch over Shadowglen. Priests of Elune, druids, rogues, and warriors maintain quarters throughout its carved trunk and surrounding platforms, while Tenaron Stormgrip, the leader of the glen, dwells at its very boughs.",al={"who lives here","aldrassil residents","aldrassil population"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is Aldrassil dangerous?",a="The tree itself is a safe haven and the bustling heart of Shadowglen, protected by watchful night elf sentinels. However, the surrounding boughs and woodland are under growing threat from encroaching Grell, diseased nightsabers, and corrupted woodland beasts lurking just beyond its shade.",al={"is aldrassil safe","aldrassil danger","danger at aldrassil"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For many young kaldorei, the carved hollows and ramps of Aldrassil are their first memory of civic life and the foundation of their early training.",["class:Druid"]="Aldrassil demonstrates the kaldorei affinity for living architecture, shaped from living wood without breaking the balance of the forest."},kw={"aldrassil","great tree","kaldorei","night elf starting","shadowglen","teldrassil","tenaron stormgrip"},rel={"subzone:shadowglen","npc:tenaron-stormgrip","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},src={"Aldrassil"}}
E["subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den"] = {t="subzone",n="Ban'ethil Barrow Den",z="teldrassil",s="Ban'ethil Barrow Den is a sacred subterranean sanctuary hollowed out within the roots of Teldrassil. Originally created as a resting place for the sleeping Druids of the Talon, the cavern complex has recently fallen into chaos. The corrupted furbolgs of the Gnarlpine tribe have overrun its chambers, turning a place of peaceful slumber into a perilous den of madness.",h="Ban'ethil Barrow Den is a sacred subterranean sanctuary hollowed out within the roots of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Defiled Sanctuary",b="Barrow dens serve as sacred resting chambers where night elf druids slumber while projecting their spirits into the Emerald Dream. Ban'ethil Barrow Den was dedicated specifically to sheltering the Druids of the Talon as they communed with nature. Divided into upper and lower subterranean chambers, the den once resonated with tranquil reverie and deep meditative magic. However, the affliction sweeping Teldrassil's wildlife did not spare the Gnarlpine furbolgs, who invaded the complex, turning its hollowed halls into a fortified warren.",sp=0},{t="The Gnarlpine Incursion",b="Driven mad by mysterious corruption taking root across the World Tree, the Gnarlpine tribe drove out or endangered the slumbering druids within Ban'ethil. The furbolgs now fiercely guard the winding tunnels, aggressive toward any night elf who approaches. For the defenders of Teldrassil, reclaiming the barrow den is an urgent priority, not merely to drive back the hostile furbolgs, but to protect the vulnerable druids and sacred relics trapped within its lower depths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="Ban'ethil Barrow Den is a subterranean hollow in Teldrassil crafted by the night elves. It was designed to shelter sleeping Druids of the Talon while their spirits roamed the Emerald Dream.",al={"what is ban'ethil","ban'ethil barrow den purpose","what is this cave"},it="place"},{q="Why are there furbolgs inside Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="The Gnarlpine furbolgs have fallen victim to a spreading corruption affecting Teldrassil's creatures. Driven hostile and territorial, they invaded the barrow den, displacing the keepers and threatening the slumbering druids.",al={"why are gnarlpine in ban'ethil","furbolgs in barrow den","who took over ban'ethil"},it="residents"},{q="What are the sections of the barrow den?",a="The cavern complex is split into two primary interconnected tiers: the Upper Den near the entrance passages and the Lower Den deeper in the subterranean roots.",al={"ban'ethil layout","upper den lower den","ban'ethil levels"}},{q="Why are barrow dens so important to druids?",a="Barrow dens provide safe, secure physical shelter for druids who enter prolonged, deep slumbers to project their consciousness into the Emerald Dream, leaving their waking bodies helpless for years or decades.",al={"why do druids sleep in barrows","druid barrow dens lore","emerald dream barrow den"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened at Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="Constructed by the night elves as a sacred refuge to house sleeping Druids of the Talon, Ban'ethil Barrow Den was meant to be a quiet sanctuary. Recently, however, corruption took hold of the native Gnarlpine furbolgs. Driven to madness, the tribe stormed the barrows and claimed them as their own den, driving out the night elves and desecrating the sacred hollows.",al={"ban'ethil barrow den history","what happened at banethil","banethil barrow den story"},it="history",add=true},{q="Why was Ban'ethil Barrow Den abandoned?",a="The barrow den was not willingly abandoned by the night elves; it was violently overrun. When the Gnarlpine tribe succumbed to corruption, they invaded the sanctuary in force. The sleeping druids and their caretakers could not maintain control, leaving the upper and lower dens entirely in the hands of the hostile furbolgs.",al={"why is ban'ethil abandoned","why did druids leave ban'ethil","banethil barrow den overrun"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is Ban'ethil Barrow Den dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous to enter alone. The winding tunnels of both the Upper and Lower Dens are packed with aggressive, corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs. Between the cramped subterranean layout and the fierce territorial instincts of the crazed beasts, an unwary traveler can easily become surrounded and overwhelmed.",al={"is ban'ethil barrow den dangerous","how dangerous is ban'ethil","banethil danger"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Ban'ethil represents sacred ground for the Cenarion Circle, specifically built to protect Druids of the Talon while communing with the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="The occupation of Ban'ethil by corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs is an alarming sign of the growing sickness plaguing their new home of Teldrassil."},kw={"ban'ethil","barrow den","druids of the talon","emerald dream","furbolg","gnarlpine","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","topic:furbolg","topic:night-elf","quest:940"},src={"Ban'ethil Barrow Den"}}
E["subzone:ban-ethil-hollow"] = {t="subzone",n="Ban'ethil Hollow",z="teldrassil",s="Ban'ethil Hollow is a rugged ravine cutting into the woodland just south of the main road connecting Dolanaar and Darnassus. It has become a dangerous haven for corrupted, aggressive furbolgs who pose a constant threat to travelers. Tucked away in the back of the ravine lies the entrance to the Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",h="Ban'ethil Hollow is a rugged ravine cutting into the woodland just south of the main road connecting Dolanaar...",sec={{t="A Perilous Ravine",b="Situated off the highway between Dolanaar and Darnassus, Ban'ethil Hollow is a sharp reminder that the boughs of Teldrassil are not entirely safe. Furbolgs driven mad by the strange affliction plaguing the World Tree have taken refuge throughout the rocky descent. They frequently stalk the nearby path, waiting to ambush unwary couriers and wandering sentinels. Deep within the ravine sits the threshold of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, where slumbering druids and ancient tunnels face encroachment from the maddened beasts outside.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Ban'ethil Hollow located?",a="Ban'ethil Hollow is a ravine in central Teldrassil, located just south of the primary road running between the village of Dolanaar and the capital city of Darnassus.",al={"banethil hollow location","where is ban'ethil hollow","find banethil hollow"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the furbolgs here hostile?",a="The furbolgs across Teldrassil have succumbed to a spreading corruption and madness that grips the World Tree's wildlife. Instead of living peacefully alongside the night elves as they historically have, these tribes have become fiercely territorial and violent.",al={"why are furbolgs mad","hostile furbolgs banethil","banethil furbolg attack"},it="hostile"},{q="What is inside the Ban'ethil Barrow Den at the back of the hollow?",a="The Ban'ethil Barrow Den is an underground complex historically used by night elven druids to enter deep hibernation and commune with the Emerald Dream. However, with corruption rising in the hollow, the den has become dangerous ground.",al={"what is in the barrow den","banethil barrow den","den in banethil hollow"}},{q="Is the road above the hollow safe to travel?",a="The main road is generally patrolled by night elf sentinels, but furbolgs from Ban'ethil Hollow often venture up from the ravine to ambush travelers. Travelers making the journey between Dolanaar and Darnassus should remain on their guard.",al={"is the road safe","furbolg ambushes","road to darnassus safe"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="What is Ban'ethil Hollow?",a="Ban'ethil Hollow is a secluded, sunken ravine carved into central Teldrassil, resting just south of the primary roadway connecting Dolanaar to Darnassus. Dominated by dense foliage and rugged slopes, the hollow serves as an encampment for corrupted furbolgs, and at its deepest recess lies the entrance to the vast Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",al={"banethil hollow","what is this place","ban'ethil hollow overview"},it="place",add=true},{q="Who lives in Ban'ethil Hollow?",a="The ravine is overrun by aggressive, corrupted furbolgs. Once peaceful neighbors to the night elves, these creatures have fallen into madness and hostility, claiming the hollow as their territory and threatening anyone traveling nearby.",al={"who lives here","ban'ethil hollow residents","who inhabits ban'ethil hollow"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is Ban'ethil Hollow dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous. The hollow is packed with hostile furbolgs who guard the ravine fiercely. Travelers on the main road just above frequently fall victim to ambushes launched from the ravine's edges, making the area perilous even for passersby who do not venture down.",al={"how dangerous is ban'ethil hollow","is banethil hollow safe","danger in ban'ethil hollow"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Seeing the furbolgs fall to madness so close to the road between Dolanaar and Darnassus is a grim sign of Teldrassil's mounting sickness, requiring young sentinels and druids to step in.",["class:Druid"]="The hollow conceals the entrance to Ban'ethil Barrow Den, sacred ground where druids traditionally rest to commune with the Emerald Dream, now endangered by rabid wildlife."},kw={"ambush","ban'ethil barrow den","ban'ethil hollow","darnassus","dolanaar","furbolg","ravine","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:furbolg"},src={"Ban'ethil Hollow"}}
E["subzone:cleft"] = {t="subzone",n="Cleft",z="teldrassil",s="The Cleft is a darkened hollow located northwest of Dolanaar in Teldrassil. Once a tranquil corner of the boughs, it has been claimed by the corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs, who use it as a stronghold to ambush travelers moving along the main highway toward Darnassus.",h="The Cleft is a darkened hollow located northwest of Dolanaar in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Den of Corruption",b="Situated off the highway between Dolanaar and Darnassus, the Cleft has turned into one of the most perilous dens on the world tree. Driven mad by the foul taint spreading through Teldrassil, the resident Gnarlpine furbolgs have fortified this subterranean rift under the command of their vicious chieftain, Ursal the Mauler. From this redoubt, the maddened beasts terrorize the local roads, capturing unvigilant night elves and threatening to cut Dolanaar off from the capital.",sp=0},{t="The Roadway Ambushers",b="The threat posed by the Cleft grew dire enough that Moon Priestess Amara and her sentinels were forced to establish a defensive watch along the road outside its entrance. The furbolgs within carried out brazen kidnappings, dragging slumbering night elf druids into the depths of the cave to perform dark rituals. Cleansing the Cleft and slaying Ursal is crucial for the Sentinels to secure the primary artery connecting Teldrassil's villages to Darnassus.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Cleft?",a="The Cleft is a furbolg den located in the boughs of Teldrassil, situated northwest of Dolanaar along the main road that leads toward Darnassus.",al={"what is the cleft","the cleft teldrassil","cleft location"},it="place"},{q="Who controls the Cleft?",a="It is occupied by hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs who have fallen victim to Teldrassil's creeping corruption. Their local leader within the cavern is a powerful brute named Ursal the Mauler.",al={"who lives in the cleft","cleft enemies","who rules the cleft"},it="residents"},{q="Why are the night elves fighting here?",a="The Gnarlpine inside the Cleft have been ambushing travelers along the road to Darnassus. Worse, they kidnapped slumbering druids and held them captive inside the den, forcing Moon Priestess Amara and the Sentinels to intervene.",al={"why attack the cleft","cleft night elf quests","road to darnassus"},it="conflict"},{q="Is the Cleft related to the Cleft of Shadow?",a="No. Despite having a similar name, this Cleft is a furbolg cave in Teldrassil, whereas the Cleft of Shadow is the dark subterranean cavern located inside the Horde capital of Orgrimmar.",al={"cleft of shadow connection","cleft vs cleft of shadow"}},{q="What happened at the Cleft?",a="The Gnarlpine furbolgs took refuge within the cave, but foul corruption quickly overcame their minds. Falling into madness, they began raiding the nearby roadway leading toward Darnassus, attacking unwary travelers and capturing slumbering night elf druids to hold deep inside their den.",al={"history of the cleft","what happened at the cleft","cleft history"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is the Cleft dangerous?",a="The Cleft is very dangerous. Hostile, corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs pack the dark den under the command of Ursal the Mauler. They fiercely defend their hollow, having already ambushed supply lines and seized sleeping druids. Moon Priestess Amara and her sentinels must guard the road just outside to hold them back.",al={"cleft danger","is the cleft safe","threats in the cleft"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Cleft represents a painful tragedy for night elves, watching their longtime furbolg allies succumb to madness and capture sacred druids from their slumber.",["class:Druid"]="The Gnarlpine inside the Cleft dared to abduct dreaming druids from their trances, turning a sacred restorative process into a dangerous trap."},kw={"cleft","darnassus","dolanaar","furbolg","gnarlpine","moon priestess amara","ursal the mauler"},rel={"quest:486","quest:487","npc:moon-priestess-amara","topic:furbolg","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","subzone:cleft-of-shadow"},src={"Cleft"}}
E["subzone:darnassus"] = {t="subzone",n="Darnassus",z="teldrassil",s="High amidst the sweeping boughs of Teldrassil stands Darnassus, the capital refuge of the kaldorei. Built along tranquil waters and verdant groves, it serves as the spiritual heart of the night elves and the primary Alliance bastion on northern Kalimdor. From here, High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind and Archdruid Fandral Staghelm guide their people through the trials of newfound mortality.",h="High amidst the sweeping boughs of Teldrassil stands Darnassus, the capital refuge of the kaldorei.",sec={{t="Sanctuary in the Boughs",b="Constructed in the aftermath of the Third War, Darnassus was founded to honor the survival of the night elf people after the loss of the immortality granted by their sacred World Tree, Nordrassil. Unlike the dense stone metropolises of Ironforge or Stormwind, Darnassus is an open, tranquil settlement of wood-crafted lodges, glowing shrines, and arched bridges spanning crystalline lakes. Vigilant Sentinels, towering ancients of war, and tree-shaping druids keep watch over the paths, ensuring that the peaceful quiet of nature is preserved within the city's borders.",sp=0},{t="A Divided Leadership",b="While Darnassus represents the unity of the kaldorei, its governance reflects subtle fractures. High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind presides over civil and military matters from the radiant Temple of the Moon, surrounded by the Sisters of Elune. Meanwhile, the Cenarion Circle's affairs fall under Archdruid Fandral Staghelm, who championed the planting of Teldrassil to restore the elves' lost immortality. With Malfurion Stormrage lost in a mysterious slumber deep within the Emerald Dream, Staghelm's aggressive vision for their future frequently creates friction with the more patient priesthood.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who rules Darnassus?",a="High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind serves as the primary leader of night elf society from the Temple of the Moon, commanding the Sentinels. Druidic affairs are directed by Archdruid Fandral Staghelm, who leads the Cenarion Circle in the absence of Malfurion Stormrage.",al={"darnassus leader","who is in charge of darnassus","night elf leader"},it="in_charge"},{q="How do travelers reach Darnassus from outside Teldrassil?",a="Because Darnassus sits atop the massive boughs of a World Tree island, ships and flight paths connect only to Rut'theran Village at the tree's base. From Rut'theran, a magical portal transports visitors up into the city proper.",al={"how to get to darnassus","darnassus entrance","getting into darnassus"},it="arrival"},{q="Why was Darnassus founded so recently?",a="Following the destruction at Mount Hyjal during the Third War, the night elves lost their immortality and their ancient way of life. Fandral Staghelm and his allies planted Teldrassil off the coast of Kalimdor, and Darnassus took root upon its branches as a fresh sanctuary for their people.",al={"why is darnassus new","when was darnassus built","darnassus age"},it="history"},{q="Where is Malfurion Stormrage?",a="Archdruid Malfurion Stormrage is missing, his spirit trapped in a deep, unexplained slumber within the Emerald Dream. His absence leaves leadership of the Cenarion Circle in Darnassus entirely to Fandral Staghelm.",al={"where is malfurion","is malfurion in darnassus","malfurion status"}},{q="What is Darnassus?",a="Darnassus is the capital city of the night elves, nestled high within the colossal boughs of the newly grown World Tree, Teldrassil. Built around a serene lake and open to the twilight skies, it serves as the spiritual and cultural heart of their civilization following the Third War. Graceful bridges, living wood lodges, and sacred groves define its layout, anchored by the shining Temple of the Moon. It stands as an Alliance sanctuary and a living testament to the kaldorei's reverence for nature.",al={"what is this place","tell me about darnassus","darnassus city overview"},it="place",add=true},{q="Who lives in Darnassus?",a="The city is predominantly home to the night elves, welcoming druids, hunters, priests, and warriors alike. High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind presides from the grand Temple of the Moon alongside her Sisters of Elune, while Archdruid Fandral Staghelm directs the Cenarion Circle from the Cenarion Enclave. The vigilant Sentinels patrol the avenues, and ancient protectors wander the pathways. Visitors will also encounter emissaries from fellow Alliance races, along with representatives of neutral orders such as the Argent Dawn.",al={"who lives here","darnassus residents","inhabitants of darnassus"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is Darnassus dangerous?",a="For members of the Alliance, Darnassus is an exceptionally peaceful refuge, shielded from Kalimdor's harsher perils by the ocean and Teldrassil's towering height. It is closely protected by armed Sentinels and formidable Ancient Protectors. However, agents of the Horde will find it fiercely hostile, facing immediate attack by the city's stalwart defenders upon entry.",al={"is darnassus safe","threats in darnassus","any danger in darnassus"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Darnassus is the cultural and political capital of the kaldorei, serving as your people's fresh start and sovereign refuge after the harrowing sacrifices of the Third War.",["faction:Alliance"]="For travelers from the Eastern Kingdoms, Darnassus is a secluded, serene haven that stands as the Alliance's essential anchor on the continent of Kalimdor."},kw={"capital","darnassus","kaldorei","staghelm","teldrassil","temple of the moon","tyrande"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","subzone:rut-theran-village","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","npc:fandral-staghelm","npc:malfurion-stormrage","topic:alliance","topic:sentinels"},src={"Darnassus"}}
E["subzone:dolanaar"] = {t="subzone",n="Dolanaar",z="teldrassil",s="Dolanaar is a tranquil night elf settlement nestled in the central-eastern boughs of Teldrassil. Situated just southwest of Shadowglen, it serves as the first true town young kal'dorei encounter after departing their sheltered training grounds. Here, rangers, druids, and craftsmen gather to guide newcomers and address the strange, encroaching afflictions disturbing the World Tree.",h="Dolanaar is a tranquil night elf settlement nestled in the central-eastern boughs of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Crossroads of Boughs",b="Resting beneath the lush canopy southwest of Shadowglen, Dolanaar serves as a vital crossway for travelers traversing Teldrassil. Built in the traditional night elven manner, its homes and platforms sit seamlessly woven into the woodland. The village provides newcomers with their first comprehensive training in trades, martial arts, and nature crafts, and sits on the road to the capital city of Darnassus. Because of its central location, reports of corrupted wildlife, aggressive furbolgs, and foul mosses from the surrounding boughs inevitably find their way into Dolanaar's council.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Dolanaar?",a="Dolanaar is the primary questing hub and outpost for young night elves leaving the novice grounds of Shadowglen. It acts as an administrative outpost in eastern Teldrassil, housing tradesfolk, trainers for martial and magical arts, and links to the capital.",al={"what is dolanaar","dolanaar purpose","why dolanaar matters"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Dolanaar located?",a="Dolanaar lies in the central-eastern region of Teldrassil, just a short walk down the trail southwest of Shadowglen and east of the capital city of Darnassus.",al={"dolanaar location","where is dolanaar","dolanaar directions"},gp=true},{q="How can travelers reach Darnassus from here?",a="Dolanaar has no flight path of its own. Travelers follow the forest road west through Teldrassil to reach the gates of Darnassus on foot.",al={"travel to darnassus","flight master dolanaar","dolanaar to darnassus"},gp=true},{q="What threats affect Dolanaar?",a="The woodland surrounding Dolanaar suffers from a strange corruption creeping into Teldrassil, leading to diseased beasts, crazed timberlings, and hostile furbolg tribes nearby.",al={"trouble in dolanaar","dolanaar problems","dolanaar quests"},it="threat"},{q="What is Dolanaar?",a="Dolanaar is a bustling night elven village nestled in the central-eastern boughs of Teldrassil, just southwest of the training grounds of Shadowglen. Serving as the heart of regional trade and affairs on the great world tree, it is typically the very first major settlement young night elves encounter when stepping out into the wider realm.",al={"what is dolanaar","dolanaar town","dolanaar village"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is Dolanaar dangerous?",a="Within the village itself you are safe among sentinel guards, druids, and merchants. However, the surrounding woodlands harbor growing unrest. Corrupted wildlife, restless gnarlpine furbolgs, and sinister harpy clutches threaten travelers venturing just beyond the perimeter of the settlement.",al={"is dolanaar dangerous","dolanaar safety","dolanaar safe"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves, Dolanaar marks their first steps into the wider world, testing their vows to preserve nature as they witness the growing corruption upon the World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="Dolanaar is an essential stop for initiates seeking guidance on Teldrassil's ailments and learning to attune their spirits to the natural balance."},kw={"darnassus","dolanaar","kaldorei","night elf town","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:night-elf"},src={"Dolanaar"}}
E["subzone:fel-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Fel Rock",z="teldrassil",s="Fel Rock is a blighted cavern hidden within the woods just north of Dolanaar on the boughs of Teldrassil. Once a tranquil hollow, it has fallen into corruption under the influence of the satyr Lord Melenas and his horde of vicious grells.",h="Fel Rock is a blighted cavern hidden within the woods just north of Dolanaar on the boughs of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Den of Corruption",b="Tucked away in the forested hills north of Dolanaar, Fel Rock was once an ordinary, peaceful cavern carved into the wood and stone of Teldrassil. Today, it stands as an unsettling reminder of the creeping taint encroaching on the world tree. Twisted roots and unnatural shadows dominate the cavern interior, overrun by swarms of wild grells and grellkin.",sp=0},{t="The Satyr's Hold",b="The corruption within Fel Rock stems from the presence of Lord Melenas, a wicked satyr who has claimed the hollow as a stronghold. From deep within the cave, he orchestrates the spread of malevolent corruption right under the watchful gaze of the night elf sentinels. Druids from Dolanaar, particularly Tallonkai Swiftroot, actively enlist capable defenders to cleanse the cave and slay Melenas before his foul blight can spread further into the surrounding woodlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Fel Rock located?",a="Fel Rock is located in central Teldrassil, tucked into the hills directly north of the settlement of Dolanaar.",al={"fel rock location","where is fel rock","find fel rock"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who rules Fel Rock?",a="The cavern is commanded by Lord Melenas, a vile satyr who has made Fel Rock his lair and gathered a host of grells to do his bidding.",al={"who is in fel rock","boss of fel rock","lord melenas location"},it="leader"},{q="Why are druids concerned about Fel Rock?",a="The presence of a satyr and fel-tainted grells within the world tree's boughs poses an immediate threat to the natural balance of Teldrassil. Druids like Tallonkai Swiftroot dispatch adventurers to cut down Lord Melenas and stem the corruption.",al={"why clean fel rock","fel rock quest","tallonkai swiftroot quest"},it="danger"},{q="What creatures dwell inside the cavern?",a="Inside Fel Rock, you will encounter aggressive grells, grellkin, and their dark master, the satyr Lord Melenas.",al={"fel rock mobs","what is inside fel rock","fel rock enemies"},it="residents"},{q="What is Fel Rock?",a="Fel Rock is a dark, corrupted cavern carved into the boughs of Teldrassil, located just north of Dolanaar. While it was once a natural and pristine cave, vile demonic corruption has settled deep within its hollows, turning it into a foul nesting ground for wicked grells and satyrs.",al={"what is fel rock","fel rock overview","fel rock lore"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is it called Fel Rock?",a="The cavern takes its name from the foul, demonic corruption that has tainted its stone and hollows. Once a pristine, natural grotto on Teldrassil, the arrival of satyrs and the spreading influence of dark fel magic earned it the grim title of Fel Rock.",al={"why fel rock","fel rock name origin","why is it called fel rock"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, the presence of a satyr like Lord Melenas so close to Dolanaar is an alarming affront to Teldrassil that demands swift retribution.",["class:Druid"]="Druids of the Cenarion Circle view Fel Rock as a festering wound on the young world tree, requiring immediate purging before demonic corruption spreads."},kw={"dolanaar","fel rock","grell","lord melenas","satyr","tallonkai swiftroot","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:932","subzone:dolanaar","npc:tallonkai-swiftroot","topic:satyr","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","topic:night-elf","quest:940"},src={"Fel Rock"}}
E["subzone:lake-al-ameth"] = {t="subzone",n="Lake Al'Ameth",z="teldrassil",s="Lake Al'Ameth is one of the largest freshwater bodies nestled high in the boughs of Teldrassil, located just south of Dolanaar. Though once a tranquil haven featuring little more than a simple wooden jetty, its shores have grown perilous due to the violent agitation of the local plant life.",h="Lake Al'Ameth is one of the largest freshwater bodies nestled high in the boughs of Teldrassil, located just...",sec={{t="A Troubled Shoreline",b="Resting immediately south of the village of Dolanaar, Lake Al'Ameth serves as a vital natural basin in the heart of Teldrassil. Despite its serene waters and minimal settlement, peace here has evaporated. Swarms of agitated timberlings and timberling sprouts prowl the water's edge, driven mad by an unnatural sickness spreading through the world tree. Druids and researchers from Dolanaar frequently dispatch travelers to these shores to gather seeds and cull the aggressive creatures before the corruption spreads deeper into the surrounding forest.",sp=0},{t="The Roots of Wrath",b="The hostility around Lake Al'Ameth is directly tied to the woodland spirits losing their balance. Massive, corrupted treants like Oakenscowl lurk in the nearby groves, while natural timberlings lash out at any who approach. For the Cenarion Circle, diagnosing and treating the rot around Lake Al'Ameth is an urgent test of whether Teldrassil's unblessed creation can truly be sustained.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Lake Al'Ameth located?",a="Lake Al'Ameth lies directly south of the night elf settlement of Dolanaar in eastern Teldrassil.",al={"lake alameth location","where is lake al'ameth","find lake al'ameth"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the creatures around Lake Al'Ameth hostile?",a="The timberlings and plant life along the shores have fallen victim to a corrupting sickness afflicting Teldrassil, driving previously harmless woodland spriggans and treants into a territorial rage.",al={"why timberlings angry","lake alameth enemies","aggressive timberlings"},it="threat"},{q="What structures or landmarks are on the lake?",a="The lake is largely wild and undeveloped, featuring only a simple wooden fishing jetty on its northern bank near the path from Dolanaar.",al={"lake alameth pier","dock at lake alameth"},it="place"},{q="Who is Oakenscowl?",a="Oakenscowl is a powerful, corrupted ancient lurking near the groves of Lake Al'Ameth. He serves as an embodiment of the violent rot warping the forest creatures in the area.",al={"what is oakenscowl","oakenscowl lake al'ameth"},it="identity"},{q="What is Lake Al'Ameth?",a="Lake Al'Ameth is one of the largest bodies of fresh water cradled within the boughs of Teldrassil. Situated just south of Dolanaar, its tranquil waters and forested banks were once a serene natural haven, marked only by a modest wooden jetty along its shore. Recently, however, its quiet beauty has been overshadowed by mounting turmoil.",al={"what is lake al'ameth","about lake al'ameth","lake al'ameth lore"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is Lake Al'Ameth dangerous?",a="It is no longer safe to wander its banks unprepared. The shorelines have become overrun by agitated timberlings and virulent sprouts driven to violent frenzy. Between these aggressive woodland spirits and the presence of corrupted behemoths like Oakenscowl lurking nearby, any traveler visiting the water's edge must remain vigilant.",al={"is lake al'ameth safe","lake al'ameth danger","dangers at lake al'ameth"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei of Dolanaar, Lake Al'Ameth is an alarming sign of the ailments troubling their newly raised home, forcing young defenders to protect the surrounding road.",["class:Druid"]="The wild timberlings around the lake offer druids a hands-on study of the unnatural corruption undermining Teldrassil's flora and fauna."},kw={"dolanaar","kaldorei","lake al'ameth","oakenscowl","teldrassil","timberling","timberling seeds"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:918","quest:919","quest:2499","quest:922","quest:941","quest:940"},src={"Lake Al'Ameth"}}
E["subzone:oracle-glade"] = {t="subzone",n="Oracle Glade",z="teldrassil",s="Nestled in northwestern Teldrassil, the Oracle Glade is a sacred woodland sanctuary home to the wondrous Oracle Tree and the World Tree's premier moonwell. Despite its serene purpose as a center of communion and vigilance, the glade faces constant harassment from encroaching Bloodfeather harpies.",h="Nestled in northwestern Teldrassil, the Oracle Glade is a sacred woodland sanctuary home to the wondrous...",sec={{t="Heart of the Woodland",b="The Oracle Glade rests quietly between Darnassus and Wellspring Lake, serving as a vital nexus of night elven communion with nature. At its center stands the Oracle Tree, an ancient specimen whose massive boughs evoke the silhouette of an eagle perched atop a bear. Nearby shimmers the first and most potent of Teldrassil's sacred moonwells, an oasis of lunar magic bathed in Elune's grace. Alongside the Circle of the Ancients, the Oracle Tree watches over the island boughs, shedding inscribed bark that acts as vital communiques to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm regarding the World Tree's health.",sp=0},{t="A Bough Besieged",b="The glade's tranquility is fragile. Aggressive Bloodfeather harpies have descended upon the grove, establishing roosts among the high branches and threatening the sacred tree. Sentinels dispatched from Darnassus struggle to root out the avian scavengers, who actively harass traveling druids and taint the natural serenity of the moonwell. Travelers passing through the northern boughs must tread lightly, as the harpies strike swiftly at any who venture near their roosts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Oracle Tree?",a="The Oracle Tree is an ancient, magically nurtured tree shaped like a great eagle resting upon a bear. It monitors the growth and health of Teldrassil, shedding inscribed bark containing detailed reports that the druids deliver directly to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.",al={"who is the oracle tree","oracle tree lore","talking tree teldrassil"},it="identity"},{q="Why are harpies attacking the Oracle Glade?",a="The Bloodfeather clan of harpies has nested in the high canopies of the glade, drawn by its untamed wilderness and magical vitality. They violently defend their roosts and harass the Oracle Tree, requiring local Sentinels to keep them contained.",al={"bloodfeather harpies","why harpies here","oracle glade enemies"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the importance of the moonwell in this glade?",a="The pool in the Oracle Glade is the very first and most powerful moonwell established on Teldrassil. It channels the sacred energies of Elune to nourish the surrounding forest and sustain kaldorei druids and priestesses who come to draw upon its waters.",al={"oracle glade moonwell","first moonwell","teldrassil first moonwell"},it="power"},{q="Where is the Oracle Glade located?",a="It is located in northwestern Teldrassil, just west of Wellspring Lake. A southern road connects the glade directly back to the main path circling outside the gates of Darnassus.",al={"oracle glade location","where is oracle glade","how to get to oracle glade"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Oracle Glade?",a="Oracle Glade is a sacred sanctuary nestled in northwestern Teldrassil, north of Darnassus. It serves as the home to the ancient Oracle Tree and houses the first and most powerful of Teldrassil's moonwells. The glade is deeply revered by the night elves, who treat it as a peaceful place of reverence and natural communion where druids and priestesses monitor the great World Tree's health.",al={"what is oracle glade","oracle glade lore","oracle glade teldrassil"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is it called Oracle Glade?",a="The glade takes its name from the mystical Oracle Tree standing at its heart. Grown by potent nature magic, this unique entity possesses deep wisdom and constantly monitors Teldrassil's vitality. By shedding inscribed bark containing supernatural reports, the tree communicates its insights to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm, acting as a living oracle for the Kaldorei.",al={"why oracle glade","oracle glade name origin","oracle glade name meaning"},it="name",add=true},{q="Is Oracle Glade dangerous?",a="While consecrated as a serene shrine, the glade has become perilous due to an infestation of Bloodfeather harpies. These aggressive creatures have established nests throughout the trees and boughs, threatening the sacred moonwell and the Oracle Tree itself. A contingent of night elf Sentinels has been dispatched here to hold the harpies at bay and defend travelers.",al={"is oracle glade safe","oracle glade threats","oracle glade enemies"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Oracle Glade represents the tender care required to nurse Teldrassil to fruition, housing the crown's most potent moonwell and a silent watcher that speaks directly to the Cenarion leadership.",["class:Druid"]="For druids of the wild, the Oracle Tree is a living partner in stewardship, offering written records of the land's health shed directly from its very bark."},kw={"bloodfeather","fandral staghelm","harpies","moonwell","oracle glade","oracle tree","teldrassil","wellspring lake"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","quest:940","quest:937","subzone:wellspring-lake","npc:fandral-staghelm","topic:sentinels","zone:darnassus"},src={"Oracle Glade"}}
E["subzone:pools-of-arlithrien"] = {t="subzone",n="Pools of Arlithrien",z="teldrassil",s="The Pools of Arlithrien are a cluster of secluded springs resting in western Teldrassil, just south of the gates to Darnassus. Once a tranquil retreat centered around a sacred moonwell, the area has fallen into neglect and danger as local wildlife and nearby hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs encroached upon it.",h="The Pools of Arlithrien are a cluster of secluded springs resting in western Teldrassil, just south of the...",sec={{t="A Troubled Sanctuary",b="Tucked along the shaded boughs south of Darnassus, the Pools of Arlithrien were originally meant to be a quiet place of natural harmony. At their heart lies a stone moonwell, a vessel for the waters imbued with the grace of Elune. Yet despite its proximity to the night elven capital, the sanctuary has become perilous. Agitated beasts roam the shallows, and the persistent hostility of the displaced Gnarlpine furbolgs forced the night elves to abandon routine upkeep of the site, leaving a peaceful wonder shadowed by the island's growing malaise.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Pools of Arlithrien located?",a="The pools are nestled in the western reaches of Teldrassil, located just south of the main bridge and entryway into the capital city of Darnassus.",al={"pools of arlithrien location","where is arlithrien","arlithrien map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why was the moonwell here abandoned?",a="The night elves withdrew from actively tending the moonwell due to mounting danger. Hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs established a threatening presence nearby, and aggressive forest wildlife overran the surrounding waters.",al={"why abandoned","arlithrien moonwell abandoned","empty moonwell"},it="ruin"},{q="What threats can travelers find at the pools?",a="Travelers wandering near the pools must contend with aggressive woodland creatures that have taken over the waters, alongside the looming risk posed by nearby territorial Gnarlpine furbolgs.",al={"arlithrien monsters","pools of arlithrien mobs","enemies at pools"},it="danger"},{q="Can players still use the moonwell at the Pools of Arlithrien?",a="Yes. Though untended and abandoned by the priesthood and druids due to local dangers, the moonwell itself still holds its sacred waters and remains a functional source of lunar essence.",al={"use arlithrien moonwell","is moonwell active","water at pools"},gp=true},{q="What are the Pools of Arlithrien?",a="The Pools of Arlithrien are a collection of tranquil ponds nestled in western Teldrassil, just south of the gates to Darnassus. Though built as a serene sanctuary centered around a sacred moonwell, the area has fallen into neglect and disorder.",al={"pools of arlithrien lore","what is pools of arlithrien","about pools of arlithrien"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened to the Pools of Arlithrien?",a="Once a peaceful haven for reflection and worship, the sanctuary could not be maintained against the rising aggression of the local wildlife and the creeping threat of the Gnarlpine furbolgs. Night elf caretakers were eventually forced to withdraw, leaving the waters untended.",al={"pools of arlithrien history","what happened at pools of arlithrien"},it="history",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The abandonment of a holy moonwell so close to Darnassus is a troubling reminder to night elves of the corruption and disruption creeping across Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="Druids studying the imbalances of Teldrassil see the unruly wildlife and the neglected moonwell here as another sign that the Great Tree lacks nature's true blessing."},kw={"arlithrien","darnassus","furbolg","gnarlpine","moonwell","pools of arlithrien","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:furbolg"},src={"Pools of Arlithrien"}}
E["subzone:rut-theran-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Rut'theran Village",z="teldrassil",s="Rut'theran Village is a coastal haven nestled at the southern base of Teldrassil. Serving as the primary maritime harbor for Darnassus, it connects the secluded World Tree to the mainland of Kalimdor via ferry and hippogryph routes.",h="Rut'theran Village is a coastal haven nestled at the southern base of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Gateway to the World Tree",b="Perched at the water's edge below the towering heights of Teldrassil, Rut'theran Village acts as the threshold between the night elven capital and the wider world. While Darnassus rests within the boughs high above, Rut'theran provides the logistical foundation required to sustain it. A mystical portal arches beneath the trees, whisking travelers between the shore and Darnassus in an instant. For journeys across the sea, ferry service runs from the village docks directly to Auberdine on the mainland of Darkshore, accompanied by flight masters tending dedicated roosts of trained hippogryphs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do I get to Darnassus from here?",a="Walk up the gentle slope from the docks toward the giant pavilion tent. Stepping directly into the glowing purple portal on the platform will instantly transport you to the Temple Gardens inside Darnassus.",al={"get to darnassus","portal to darnassus","how to reach darnassus"},gp=true},{q="Where does the boat from the dock go?",a="The ship docked at Rut'theran Village, the Moonspray, provides passage across the Veiled Sea to the town of Auberdine on the coast of Darkshore.",al={"where does boat go","rut'theran ferry","ruttheran ship route"},gp=true},{q="Why is this village down at sea level instead of up in the tree?",a="Teldrassil's canopy is far too elevated for conventional sailing ships or sea trade. Rut'theran Village was established at its roots to provide a sea-level port and roosting ground, linked to the heights via a permanent teleportation gateway.",al={"why is ruttheran at sea level","why bottom of teldrassil"},it="purpose"},{q="Can I fly anywhere from here?",a="Yes. A hippogryph handler operates from the village roost, offering flight routes across the water to Auberdine in Darkshore, as well as specialized transport for Cenarion Circle druids to Moonglade.",al={"rut'theran flight path","where can hippogryph fly"},gp=true},{q="What is Rut'theran Village?",a="Rut'theran Village is the coastal port settlement nestled at the base of Teldrassil. Because the capital city of Darnassus sits far above upon the boughs of the World Tree, this seaside haven serves as the vital maritime threshold connecting the night elves to the mainland of Kalimdor and the wider world beyond.",al={"what is this place","ruttheran village","ruttheran overview"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Rut'theran Village?",a="Rut'theran was founded alongside the growth of Teldrassil in the wake of the Third War. Established to provide the secluded kaldorei an accessible harbor at sea level, it has grown peacefully into a bustling entry point, tended by boatmen, hippogryph handlers, and guards defending the foot of the great tree.",al={"ruttheran history","past of ruttheran","what happened here"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who lives in Rut'theran Village?",a="The settlement is populated by night elf caretakers, fishers, and sentinels tasked with securing the base of Teldrassil. It is also home to dedicated handlers who nurture hippogryphs and ferry travelers across the sea, keeping the boughs of Darnassus closely tied to the mainland shores of Darkshore.",al={"who lives here","ruttheran residents","ruttheran population"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is Rut'theran Village dangerous?",a="No, the village is an entirely peaceful and heavily guarded sanctuary of the Alliance. Sheltered beneath the canopy of Teldrassil and watched over by kaldorei sentinels, visitors can rest and travel freely without fear of hostile wildlife or lurking enemies within the village grounds.",al={"is ruttheran dangerous","threats in ruttheran","is it safe here"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Druids passing through Rut'theran Village can catch hippogryph flights directly across northern Kalimdor to the sacred sanctuary of Moonglade.",["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves leaving Teldrassil to aid the Alliance, Rut'theran Village is the final farewell to the crown of the World Tree before sailing into mainland Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","darnassus","docks","hippogryph","moonspray","port","rut'theran","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","subzone:auberdine","subzone:moonspray","zone:darkshore","topic:night-elf","topic:druid","quest:5921"},src={"Rut'theran Village"}}
E["subzone:shadowglen"] = {t="subzone",n="Shadowglen",z="teldrassil",s="Shadowglen is a secluded, twilit vale nestled within the northeastern boughs of Teldrassil. Dominated by the great barrow-tree Aldrassil, it serves as the safe haven where young night elves take their first steps into service before journeying out into the wider world.",h="Shadowglen is a secluded, twilit vale nestled within the northeastern boughs of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Sheltered Cradle",b="Tucked away in the northeastern canopy of Teldrassil, Shadowglen is ringed by high ridges that shelter it from the rest of the world. Bathed in eternal dusk, the vale centers on Aldrassil, a massive barrow-tree whose hollowed trunk houses elders, priestesses, and mentors for young night elves beginning their training. The only route out of the valley leads south through a narrow mountain pass toward Starbreeze Village and Dolanaar, making Shadowglen one of the most naturally fortified and peaceful sanctuaries on the World Tree.",sp=0},{t="Creeping Shadows",b="Despite its tranquil seclusion, Shadowglen is not entirely free from danger. In the extreme northwest lies Shadowthread Cave, a dark cavern infested with venomous spiders that constantly threaten the tranquil glade. Even on the pristine branches of Teldrassil, vigilance is required, and fledgling defenders are tasked with driving back the encroaching vermin and untamed wildlife before venturing into the broader expanse of the boughs beyond.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Shadowglen?",a="Shadowglen is the sheltered starting grove for the night elves, located in the northeastern reaches of Teldrassil. It is a peaceful, secluded haven centered around the grand tree Aldrassil, where novices train under mentors before journeying across the World Tree.",al={"what is this place","shadowglen lore","about shadowglen"},it="place"},{q="What is the massive tree at the center of the glen?",a="The tree is Aldrassil, a barrow-tree that forms the heart of Shadowglen. Its hollowed interior serves as an administrative lodge and training hub where novice night elves meet class trainers, mentors, and caretakers.",al={"big tree in shadowglen","aldrassil","shadowglen tree"},it="place",nx={8,9}},{q="What threats exist in Shadowglen?",a="The primary threat comes from the northwest in Shadowthread Cave, a cavern infested with venomous spiders that regularly creep out into the glade. Young defenders are tasked with culling the spiders and calming the restless local wildlife.",al={"why are there spiders here","shadowglen dangers","shadowthread cave"},it="threat"},{q="How do you leave Shadowglen?",a="Shadowglen is entirely surrounded by ridges except for a single path to the south. Passing through this narrow mountain gap leads southward toward Starbreeze Village and the settlement of Dolanaar.",al={"exit shadowglen","where does the path lead","way out of shadowglen"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is Teldrassil?",a="Teldrassil is an immense World Tree grown off the northwestern coast of Kalimdor. Its name means \"Crown of the Earth\" in Darnassian. Raised by the Circle of Ancients and powerful druids following the Third War, Teldrassil serves as the new homeland of the kaldorei. Its gargantuan limbs rise straight from the sea, bearing an entire forested landmass and the capital city of Darnassus in its boughs.",al={"what is this giant tree","teldrassil world tree","about teldrassil"},it="place",add=true,nx={6,7}},{q="Who grew Teldrassil?",a="After Malfurion Stormrage vanished, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm convinced the Circle of Ancients to plant a new World Tree. Powerful druids channeled their magic to raise it from the sea, hoping to restore the kaldorei's lost immortality. However, the Dragon Aspects—notably Nozdormu, who granted their ancient eternal life—refused to bless the boughs, leaving its growth flawed.",al={"who made teldrassil","who planted teldrassil","who created the world tree"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why do the night elves live in a tree now?",a="The devastation of the Third War stripped the night elves of their ancestral immortality when Nordrassil was sacrificed at Mount Hyjal. Seeking to regain their eternal life and a safe haven away from mainland threats, the kaldorei raised Teldrassil to serve as their sanctuary and established their gleaming capital of Darnassus high within its towering branches.",al={"why live in a tree","why night elves on teldrassil","why live in teldrassil"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who lives at the top of Aldrassil?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip, the leader of Shadowglen, makes his home inside the very crown of Aldrassil. From high within the boughs of the great tree, he oversees the training and initiation of fledgling night elf protectors.",al={"top of aldrassil","who is in aldrassil","tenaron stormgrip aldrassil"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is Aldrassil the same as Teldrassil?",a="No. Teldrassil is the colossal World Tree that rises out of the ocean, supporting an entire island-sized land of forests, mountains, and cities upon its upper boughs. Aldrassil is simply a singular, massive ancient tree rooted in the soil of Shadowglen, sitting atop Teldrassil itself.",al={"aldrassil vs teldrassil","is aldrassil teldrassil","difference aldrassil teldrassil"},it="place",add=true},{q="Who's in charge around here?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip oversees Shadowglen from his chamber atop Aldrassil. He guides the valley's defense, coordinating local druids, Sentinels, and mentors as they instruct new arrivals and address the growing corruption among the local wildlife.",al={"who leads shadowglen","leader of shadowglen","in charge shadowglen"},it="in_charge",add=true,nx={11}},{q="Who leads the night elves overall?",a="High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind leads the kaldorei through the Sisterhood of Elune, while Archdruid Fandral Staghelm currently directs the Cenarion Circle in the absence of Malfurion Stormrage. Together, the priesthood and the druids guide the night elf nation from their capital in Darnassus.",al={"leader of night elves","who rules the night elves","kaldorei leader"},it="leader",add=true},{q="What are the Webwood spiders and why are they here?",a="The Webwood spiders are giant arachnids that have nested in Shadowthread Cave for ages. While they once kept largely to themselves, a dark taint over Teldrassil has driven them into a vicious frenzy, pushing them out of their hollows to attack anyone wandering the northern reaches.",al={"webwood spiders teldrassil","why spiders in shadowglen","spiders shadowglen"},it="threat",add=true,nx={13}},{q="Were the Webwood spiders always in that cave?",a="Yes. Shadowthread Cave in the northwest has long been the natural home of Teldrassil's giant spiders. However, their hostility has surged dramatically in recent days under the broodmother Githyiss the Vile, turning the cavern into a deadly hazard for novice wanderers.",al={"spiders always in shadowthread","shadowthread cave history","were spiders always here"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who is Elune?",a="Elune is the revered moon goddess of the night elves, associated with peace, starlight, and healing. The kaldorei have worshipped her since ancient times, and her high priestesses—led by Tyrande Whisperwind—channel her celestial power to protect their people and smite their foes.",al={"moon goddess elune","elune night elves","goddess elune"},it="other",add=true},{q="What's Dolanaar and why does everyone keep pointing me there?",a="Dolanaar is the nearest major settlement, situated just southwest of Shadowglen through the southern mountain pass. Once your mentors in the glen have tested your abilities, you are sent to Dolanaar to further your training, learn trades, and assist with regional crises across Teldrassil.",al={"what is dolanaar","why go to dolanaar","dolanaar village"},it="next_step",add=true},{q="Why did the night elves lose their immortality?",a="During the Third War, the Burning Legion marched on Mount Hyjal to consume the original World Tree, Nordrassil. Malfurion Stormrage channeled the spirits of the forest and the ancient tree's power to obliterate the demon lord Archimonde. Sacrificing Nordrassil destroyed the enchantment granted by the Dragon Aspects, stripping the kaldorei of their agelessness.",al={"lost immortality night elves","why are night elves mortal","night elf immortality loss"},it="history",add=true},{q="How did I end up in Shadowglen?",a="You are in a secluded glade high in the northeastern boughs of Teldrassil, the young World Tree grown off the coast of northern Kalimdor. Sheltered from the wider world beneath the great tree Aldrassil, this tranquil forest serves as a safe haven and training ground for newly aspiring kaldorei. You came here to answer the call of your elders, honing your abilities in peaceful seclusion before stepping out onto the larger branches of your people's new homeland.",al={"how did i get here","how did i arrive here","why am i here"},it="arrival",add=true},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Shadowglen?",a="Your task is to aid the guardians and elders of Aldrassil with the growing problems disturbing the glade. A foul corruption has recently begun upsetting the local wildlife, causing the native Webwood spiders and woodland beasts to turn hostile. Speak with the trainers and leaders around the great tree, root out the sickness festering in Shadowthread Cave, and restore balance to the forest before continuing south down the path to Dolanaar.",al={"what should i do here","what is my purpose here","what am i doing in shadowglen"},it="purpose",add=true},{q="Why does a new Night Elf start here, in Shadowglen?",a="Following the Third War and the sacrifice of Nordrassil, the night elves relocated across the sea to Teldrassil to begin anew. Shadowglen is the most protected and secluded pocket of the crown, insulated behind ringed mountain ridges and guarded by veteran Sentinels. Because you are taking your first steps in the arts of druidism, warfare, or Elune's grace, your people cultivate your training here in the safety of Aldrassil before sending you into the wider, more perilous world.",al={"why do night elves start here","why does my night elf begin in shadowglen","why start in shadowglen"},it="arrival",rc="Night Elf",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Every young night elf begins their active journey here among the sheltered roots of Aldrassil, receiving their first blessings and instructions before facing the perils of Kalimdor.",["faction:Alliance"]="Situated high on the boughs of Teldrassil and deep behind guarded ports, Shadowglen stands as one of the Alliance's most insulated and well-defended sanctuary vales."},kw={"aldrassil","kaldorei","night elf starting area","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowthread-cave","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:starbreeze-village","topic:night-elf","zone:darnassus","subzone:rut-theran-village"},src={"Shadowglen"}}
E["subzone:shadowthread-cave"] = {t="subzone",n="Shadowthread Cave",z="teldrassil",s="Shadowthread Cave is a damp cavern carved into the northwest cliffs of Shadowglen on Teldrassil. Traditionally inhabited by indigenous Webwood spiders, the cave has recently turned dangerously aggressive under the dominion of their broodmother, Githyiss the Vile.",h="Shadowthread Cave is a damp cavern carved into the northwest cliffs of Shadowglen on Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Brood Growing Restless",b="Tucked away in the shaded perimeter of Shadowglen, Shadowthread Cave has long served as a natural lair for Teldrassil's giant spiders. In earlier years, these arachnids coexisted quietly alongside the nascent boughs of the World Tree. Recently, however, their temperament has turned fiercely territorial. Thick layers of webwood silk now choke the stone corridors, and the aggressive nature of the brood poses an immediate hazard to young kaldorei taking their first steps beyond Aldrassil.",sp=0},{t="Githyiss the Vile",b="The primary menace lurking deep within the cave's darkest recesses is Githyiss the Vile, a monstrous broodmother whose ferocity far outstrips the common webwood crawlers. Novice night elf sentinels and druids are dispatched to the cave to curb the spider infestation and slay Githyiss, ensuring that the corruption touching Teldrassil's wildlife does not overrun the sanctuary of Shadowglen entirely.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Shadowthread Cave located?",a="Shadowthread Cave lies in the northwest corner of Shadowglen, nestled against the rocky hillside bordering the night elf starting valley in Teldrassil.",al={"shadowthread cave location","where is shadowthread cave","find shadowthread cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the spiders in the cave so aggressive?",a="While spiders have always dwelled within the cave, a foul sickness and growing imbalance across Teldrassil has driven the local wildlife mad, turning the webwood spiders exceptionally violent.",al={"why are spiders hostile","spider corruption shadowthread","why spiders attacking"},it="danger"},{q="Who is Githyiss the Vile?",a="Githyiss the Vile is a massive, venomous webwood spider matriarch nestled at the deepest point of Shadowthread Cave. She is the mother of the aggressive brood threatening young kaldorei in Shadowglen.",al={"githyiss","who is githyiss","shadowthread spider boss"},it="threat"},{q="What makes the cave valuable despite the danger?",a="The cave is packed with layers of dense, naturally spun webwood silk, a valuable and resilient crafting material woven by the endless swarms of arachnids inhabiting its dark chambers.",al={"shadowthread silk","spider silk shadowglen"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Shadowthread Cave?",a="Shadowthread Cave is a subterranean cavern tucked into the northwest bluffs of Shadowglen on Teldrassil. Traditionally the natural nesting ground of the island's webwood spiders, it serves as a secluded den where the arachnids spin their intricate webs and raise their broods away from the boughs of the World Tree.",al={"what is shadowthread cave","shadowthread cave lore","shadowthread cave"},it="place",add=true},{q="Who lives in Shadowthread Cave?",a="The cavern is inhabited almost entirely by Teldrassil's native webwood spiders. At the heart of the nest rules their massive broodmother, Githyiss the Vile, who commands the swarms of arachnids that blanket the stone walls in dense webbing.",al={"who lives in shadowthread cave","shadowthread cave inhabitants","spiders in shadowthread cave"},it="residents",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves, clearing Shadowthread Cave and slaying Githyiss the Vile serves as one of their very first trials in defending their sacred home from creeping corruption.",["class:Druid"]="The unchecked aggression of the Webwood brood in Shadowthread Cave is a troubling indicator to druids that the natural harmony of Teldrassil is deeply disturbed."},kw={"githyiss the vile","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","spider silk","teldrassil","webwood spider"},rel={"subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},src={"Shadowthread Cave"}}
E["subzone:starbreeze-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Starbreeze Village",z="teldrassil",s="Starbreeze Village is an abandoned night elf settlement situated east of Dolanaar in Teldrassil. Once a tranquil woodland hamlet, it has recently fallen to the maddened furbolgs of the Gnarlpine tribe. The ruined settlement now stands as a glaring symbol of the growing corruption seeping into the roots of the World Tree.",h="Starbreeze Village is an abandoned night elf settlement situated east of Dolanaar in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Fallen Hamlet",b="Located southeast of Shadowglen and just down the road from Dolanaar, Starbreeze Village was once home to peaceful night elf families living beneath the boughs of Teldrassil. Today, the village lies in shambles, its wooden structures overrun by aggressive Gnarlpine furbolgs. Driven wild by a sinister corruption afflicting the boughs of the World Tree, the beast-men drove the elven residents out and now defend the ruined grounds ferociously.",sp=0},{t="The Threat of Ferocitas",b="The Gnarlpine presence in the village is not merely an ordinary territorial raid. Lurking on the outskirts of the settlement is Ferocitas the Dream Eater, an enigmatic, corrupted entity whose presence suggests dark, foul magic is actively driving the furbolgs mad. Together with hulking beasts like Uruson who prowl the paths, these invaders make Starbreeze an active danger to travelers journeying through eastern Teldrassil.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Starbreeze Village abandoned?",a="The village was overrun when the Gnarlpine furbolgs fell prey to a spreading corruption within Teldrassil. Driven mad and violent, the furbolgs attacked the night elf inhabitants, forcing them to flee and abandon their homes.",al={"what happened to starbreeze","why is starbreeze ruined","starbreeze empty"},it="ruin"},{q="Who lives in Starbreeze Village now?",a="Hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs now occupy the village. Prominent figures among them include the wandering patrol Uruson and the corrupt figure known as Ferocitas the Dream Eater.",al={"who is in starbreeze","starbreeze mobs","who took over starbreeze"},it="residents"},{q="Where is Starbreeze Village located?",a="Starbreeze Village is located in eastern Teldrassil, lying southeast of Shadowglen and east of Dolanaar.",al={"where is starbreeze","starbreeze map location","how to find starbreeze"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Ferocitas the Dream Eater?",a="Ferocitas is a dangerous, corrupted creature found on the outskirts of Starbreeze Village, associated with the dark forces driving the local Gnarlpine tribe into frenzy.",al={"ferocitas lore","who is ferocitas","ferocitas starbreeze"}},{q="What is Starbreeze Village?",a="Starbreeze Village is a former night elf settlement nestled in the boughs of Teldrassil, located east of Dolanaar and southeast of Shadowglen. Once a peaceful enclave consisting of small elven dwellings, it has fallen into ruin and stands as a grim reminder of the corruption currently spreading across the World Tree.",al={"what is starbreeze village","starbreeze village overview","starbreeze lore"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened to Starbreeze Village?",a="Not long ago, Starbreeze was a quiet night elven community. However, a creeping corruption took hold of the local Gnarlpine furbolg tribe, driving them into a feral, violent frenzy. Overwhelmed by the sudden assault, the kaldorei inhabitants were driven out or slaughtered, and the furbolgs took complete control of the settlement.",al={"starbreeze village history","what happened at starbreeze","how did starbreeze fall"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is Starbreeze Village dangerous?",a="Yes, it is very dangerous to enter unprepared. The ruins are swarming with hostile, corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs who attack any outsiders on sight. In addition to the aggressive tribe members, ferocious beasts such as the bear Uruson patrol the village paths, while the dread satyr Ferocitas the Dream Eater lurks on the settlement's outskirts.",al={"is starbreeze village safe","starbreeze danger","dangers of starbreeze village"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Seeing an elven settlement so close to Dolanaar fall into ruin is a painful reminder of Teldrassil's precarious state and the corruption gnawing at the World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="The madness consuming the Gnarlpine furbolgs and the defilement of Starbreeze Village directly challenge the Cenarion Circle's charge to restore balance to Teldrassil's wildlife."},kw={"dolanaar","ferocitas","furbolg","gnarlpine","starbreeze","teldrassil","uruson","village"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","topic:furbolg","subzone:dolanaar","quest:2459","subzone:shadowglen","quest:940","zone:darnassus"},src={"Starbreeze Village"}}
E["subzone:wellspring-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Wellspring Lake",z="teldrassil",s="Wellspring Lake is a serene body of fresh water resting high within the boughs of Teldrassil, situated northeast of Darnassus. Fed by natural springs originating from deep within the World Tree, its waters feed the winding Wellspring River. Once a peaceful retreat for night elf fishermen, the lake's shores have fallen prey to the growing corruption unsettling Teldrassil's wildlife.",h="Wellspring Lake is a serene body of fresh water resting high within the boughs of Teldrassil, situated...",sec={{t="A Tainted Refuge",b="Nestled beneath the canopy between Darnassus and the Oracle Glade, Wellspring Lake was long cherished by the Kaldorei as a quiet haven for fishing and contemplation. Its clear waters originate from subterranean springs running through the colossal boughs of the World Tree, which then drain northward through the Wellspring River. In recent times, however, an insidious blight has begun to seize the surrounding wilds. Aggressive spiders, prowling nightsabers, and agitated timberlings now roam the banks, making what was once an idyllic pond a treacherous place for unwary travelers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Wellspring Lake located?",a="Wellspring Lake lies in northern Teldrassil, northeast of the capital city of Darnassus and just southeast of the Oracle Glade.",al={"where is wellspring lake","wellspring lake location","how to get to wellspring lake"},gp=true},{q="Where does the lake's water come from and go?",a="The lake is fed by natural springs rising deep from within the roots and wood of Teldrassil itself. The excess water drains into the Wellspring River, which flows north to the edge of the tree.",al={"where does wellspring lake drain","wellspring river source","wellspring lake water source"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the area around Wellspring Lake dangerous?",a="While it was previously a tranquil spot favored by Kaldorei anglers, the spreading corruption across the World Tree has driven local beasts mad. Prowling nightsabers, giant webwood spiders, and corrupted timberling bark-spirits now stalk the shoreline.",al={"what lives at wellspring lake","wellspring lake mobs","why is wellspring lake hostile"},it="threat"},{q="Who used to gather at Wellspring Lake?",a="Local night elven fishermen often visited the lake for quiet reflection and angling before the recent blight agitated the wildlife and made the shores hazardous.",al={"wellspring lake history","night elf fishermen lake"},it="history"},{q="What is Wellspring Lake?",a="Wellspring Lake is a small body of water nestled in the boughs of Teldrassil, northeast of Darnassus and southeast of the Oracle Glade. Fed by a natural spring buried deep within the World Tree itself, its fresh waters flow outward into the Wellspring River, nourishing the surrounding woodland.",al={"what is wellspring lake","wellspring lake teldrassil","about wellspring lake"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why was Wellspring Lake abandoned?",a="Night elven fishermen once favored the lake's peaceful banks, but growing corruption across the World Tree drove them away. Corrupted timberlings now dwell within the waters, and aggressive nightsabers and spiders roam the surrounding wilderness, making peaceful visits impossible.",al={"why was wellspring lake abandoned","wellspring lake fishermen","why did fishermen leave wellspring lake"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is Wellspring Lake dangerous?",a="Yes. Though once a tranquil fishing retreat, the lake has been claimed by hostile, corrupted timberlings. The surrounding terrain offers no safety either, infested by predatory nightsabers and webwood spiders prowling the undergrowth.",al={"is wellspring lake dangerous","wellspring lake safe","wellspring lake dangers"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called Wellspring Lake?",a="The lake takes its name from its source: a natural spring fed from deep within the roots and soil of Teldrassil. In turn, it serves as the headwaters of the Wellspring River, giving life to the central waterways of the bough.",al={"why is it called wellspring lake","wellspring lake name origin","wellspring lake name meaning"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, the degradation of peaceful groves like Wellspring Lake into dangerous monster dens is a painful reminder that something has gone deeply wrong with their young World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="Druids study the agitated timberlings and beasts near Wellspring Lake to understand the source of the unnatural sickness spreading through Teldrassil's waters and soil."},kw={"darnassus","kaldorei","nightsaber","oracle glade","teldrassil","timberlings","wellspring lake","wellspring river"},rel={"subzone:wellspring-river","zone:teldrassil","subzone:oracle-glade","zone:darnassus"},src={"Wellspring Lake"}}
E["subzone:wellspring-river"] = {t="subzone",n="Wellspring River",z="teldrassil",s="The Wellspring River flows from a natural spring within Teldrassil, coursing north out of Wellspring Lake until it plummets off the boughs in a towering waterfall to the ocean far below. Once a peaceful source of fresh water for the World Tree's ecosystem, its banks have grown perilous due to agitated local wildlife.",h="The Wellspring River flows from a natural spring within Teldrassil, coursing north out of Wellspring Lake...",sec={{t="Waters of the World Tree",b="Nourished by the deep natural springs nestled in the boughs of Teldrassil, the Wellspring River carries water north from Wellspring Lake across the verdant forest floor before cascading dramatically over the edge of the great tree down into the sea below. Despite the serene surroundings, the riverbanks are increasingly unsafe. The timberlings that dwell along the water have grown crazed and hostile, violently attacking travelers and druids who attempt to draw near the river's edge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Wellspring River lead?",a="The Wellspring River flows northward out of Wellspring Lake. Eventually, it reaches the rim of Teldrassil's canopy and plunges over the edge in an enormous waterfall that drops all the way down into the surrounding ocean.",al={"where does river flow","wellspring river destination","where does wellspring river go"}},{q="Why are the timberlings along the river attacking people?",a="The timberlings along the Wellspring River have become erratic and crazed, turning on anyone who wanders nearby. This aggression is part of a broader disturbance spreading through Teldrassil's natural wildlife, alarming the local night elven druids.",al={"why are timberlings aggressive","crazed timberlings wellspring","why timberlings hostile"},it="danger"},{q="Where does the water in the river come from?",a="The river is fed directly by Wellspring Lake, which itself is sustained by a natural freshwater spring rising deep from within the living trunk and boughs of the World Tree.",al={"wellspring water source","where does wellspring water come from"},it="origin"},{q="What is Wellspring River?",a="Wellspring River is a vital freshwater stream flowing through Teldrassil. Originating from a natural spring deep within the boughs of the World Tree, it drains northward out of Wellspring Lake and carries its waters toward the northern cliffs, ultimately tumbling over the massive canopy's edge in a breathtaking waterfall down to the sea below.",al={"what is wellspring river","tell me about wellspring river","wellspring river lore"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is it called Wellspring River?",a="The river takes its name from its origin: a natural spring and deep wellspring nestled high within Teldrassil's crown. Flowing directly out of Wellspring Lake, the clear waters serve as one of the primary arteries of moisture sustaining the surrounding forest before spilling off the edge of the great tree.",al={"why is it called wellspring river","wellspring river name meaning","wellspring name origin"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The corrupted and maddened state of the river's native timberlings is an unsettling sign of the growing sickness creeping through Teldrassil's ecosystem.",["race:NightElf"]="The freshwater waterways flowing from the heart of Teldrassil represent the vitality of the Kaldorei's new home, making the unrest along their banks deeply concerning."},kw={"kaldorei","teldrassil","timberlings","waterfall","wellspring lake","wellspring river"},rel={"subzone:wellspring-lake","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},src={"Wellspring River"}}
E["zone:teldrassil"] = {t="zone",n="Teldrassil",z="teldrassil",s="Teldrassil, meaning 'Crown of the Earth', is a gargantuan new World Tree raised off Kalimdor's northwest coast. Grown by the druids in the wake of the Third War, its colossal boughs support an entire twilit wilderness and the night elf capital of Darnassus. Yet beneath its tranquil, moonlit canopy, a creeping corruption has begun to stir.",h="Teldrassil, meaning 'Crown of the Earth', is a gargantuan new World Tree raised off Kalimdor's northwest...",sec={{t="A Canopy Upon the Sea",b="Teldrassil is not merely a tree; it is an elevated ecosystem standing tall amidst the waters of the Veiled Sea. Its gargantuan limbs support rolling hills, flowing rivers fed by morning dew, misty lakes, and dense ancient glades. At its western edge sits Darnassus, the grand capital of the kaldorei. At the base of its monumental trunk lies Rut'theran Village, connected to the crown above by a mystical gateway and serving as the island's primary harbor.",sp=0},{t="The Refusal of the Aspects",b="Following the sacrifice of Nordrassil during the Third War and the mysterious disappearance of Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage into the Emerald Dream, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm convinced the Circle of Ancients to grow a replacement. Staghelm hoped to restore the kaldorei to their lost immortality. However, Nozdormu and the Dragon Aspects deemed the effort hubristic and withheld their blessings. Without their vital warding, Teldrassil's growth has suffered from unnatural flaws.",sp=0},{t="A Creeping Malady",b="Despite its outward majesty, the nascent World Tree harbors a dark sickness. The local wildlife has turned violent: peaceful furbolg tribes have fallen into madness, twisted grells multiply in the barrows, and vile satyrs work dark rites in shadows like Fel Rock. Down upon the shores of Darkshore, sea giants, threshers, and turtles beach themselves to flee the tainted waters around the tree. Naturalists and sentinels now labor frantically across the boughs to identify the shadow slowly strangling their new home.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why was Teldrassil grown?",a="After Nordrassil was devastated at the end of the Third War, the night elves lost their immortality. Archdruid Fandral Staghelm pushed the Circle of Ancients and Cenarion druids to plant a new World Tree in the sea, aiming to restore what their people had lost.",al={"why made","who made teldrassil","teldrassil origin"},it="origin"},{q="Why didn't Teldrassil restore night elf immortality?",a="Nordrassil originally granted immortality because Nozdormu, the Timeless One, blessed it. When Teldrassil was raised, Nozdormu judged the night elves' desire as arrogant and refused to bestow his blessing upon the new tree.",al={"immortality","why not immortal","nozdormu blessing"},it="power"},{q="How do you leave Teldrassil?",a="Travelers must head through Darnassus to the pink portal in the Temple Gardens, which transports them down to Rut'theran Village at the trunk's base. From Rut'theran, a ship sails across the sea to Auberdine on the mainland of Darkshore, alongside available hippogryph routes.",al={"how to get out","leave tree","teldrassil boat"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why are there no mining nodes in Teldrassil?",a="The entire zone is situated atop the living branches and wood of a colossal World Tree rather than natural continental rock. Because there are no stony subterranean crusts, no metal veins or ore deposits form here, though herbs flourish in great abundance.",al={"where is copper","no ore","teldrassil mining"},gp=true},{q="What is causing the furbolgs and beasts to turn mad?",a="A sinister presence has begun to seep into Teldrassil's unblessed roots. Sickness has corrupted the local water and flora, driving peaceful timberlings and the Gnarlpine furbolg tribe into frenzied aggression, while remnants of satyrs actively cultivate the taint.",al={"corrupted furbolgs","gnarlpine mad","what is the corruption"},it="threat"},{q="What is Shadowglen?",a="Shadowglen is a sheltered, secluded vale on the eastern boughs of Teldrassil surrounding the great tree Aldrassil. It serves as a peaceful sanctuary where young night elves begin their training before venturing into the wider world.",al={"shadowglen","starting area","aldrassil zone"},it="place"},{q="What is Teldrassil?",a="Teldrassil is an immense World Tree grown upon an island off the northwestern coast of Kalimdor. Its gargantuan trunk rises out of the Veiled Sea, spreading out into boughs so vast they support an entire forested realm of lakes, rivers, and the capital city of Darnassus atop its canopy.",al={"what is this place","about teldrassil","tell me about teldrassil"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Teldrassil?",a="Following the Third War and the damage done to Mount Hyjal's Nordrassil, the druid Malfurion Stormrage went missing. In his absence, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm convinced the Circle of Ancients to grow a new World Tree to replace what was lost. Though grown successfully, a creeping corruption has since begun to taint its boughs.",al={"teldrassil history","how was teldrassil created","events of teldrassil"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who lives in or runs Teldrassil?",a="Teldrassil is the ancestral refuge and current homeland of the night elves. Spiritually and civically, High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind and Archdruid Fandral Staghelm guide their people from the capital of Darnassus, supported by the Sisterhood of Elune, Cenarion druids, and Sentinel warriors guarding the woodland settlements.",al={"who leads teldrassil","teldrassil leaders","who lives here"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is Teldrassil dangerous?",a="While protected by Sentinels, Teldrassil is increasingly perilous. A dark affliction has maddened the native beasts and local furbolgs, while malicious satyrs, bloodthirsty harpies, and rampant timberlings threaten settlements beyond the patrolled highways.",al={"is it safe here","threats in teldrassil","dangers of teldrassil"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called Teldrassil?",a="In the Darnassian language of the night elves, Teldrassil translates directly to 'crown of the earth.' It was named in honor of its role as a monumental World Tree meant to cradle and shield their civilization.",al={"what does teldrassil mean","teldrassil name meaning"},it="name",add=true},{q="Who is Fandral Staghelm?",a="Fandral Staghelm is the Archdruid who stepped into leadership of the night elven druids following Malfurion Stormrage's disappearance into the Emerald Dream. Passionate, stubborn, and aggressive, Fandral championed the planting of Teldrassil and frequently clashes with High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind over policy.",al={"who is the archdruid","fandral staghelm lore","staghelm"},it="leader",add=true},{q="Who is Tyrande Whisperwind?",a="Tyrande Whisperwind is the High Priestess of the goddess Elune and supreme leader of the night elven people. Having guided her kin for ten thousand years through the Long Vigil and the Third War, she now leads from the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",al={"who is tyrande","high priestess tyrande","who leads the night elves"},it="leader",add=true},{q="How did I end up in Teldrassil?",a="If you are a night elf, this colossal World Tree is your people's new homeland. After sacrificing Nordrassil and your ancient immortality atop Mount Hyjal to defeat the Burning Legion, the kaldorei relocated off Kalimdor's northwest coast. Archdruid Fandral Staghelm and the Circle of Ancients grew Teldrassil in the Veiled Sea to give your race a renewed refuge, and you began your journey within its verdant boughs at Shadowglen. If you journeyed here from abroad, you likely sailed to the port of Rut'theran Village at the tree's base from Darkshore, then stepped through the glowing portal that carries travelers directly up into the crown.",al={"how did i get to teldrassil","how did i get here","why am i starting here"},it="arrival",add=true},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Teldrassil?",a="You are called to protect the fledgling World Tree and uncover the dark malady unsettling its boughs. Despite its lush forests, a sinister corruption is taking hold: timberlings are turning aggressive, peaceful furbolgs of the Gnarlpine tribe are slipping into madness, and vile satyrs lurk in shadowy thickets like Fel Rock. Starting from Shadowglen and aiding settlements like Dolanaar, you must help the Sentinels and druids restore balance. You will replenish the sacred moonwells, root out corrupted vermin, and learn the history of your people before venturing out into the capital of Darnassus and across the sea to mainland Kalimdor.",al={"what do i do in teldrassil","why am i here","what is my mission here"},it="purpose",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="This massive tree is your people's fresh beginning after the devastation of Mount Hyjal, but the absence of the Aspects' blessings makes defending it an urgent duty.",["class:Druid"]="With Malfurion trapped in the Emerald Dream, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm leads the Cenarion Circle here, though many druids worry that Teldrassil was raised in haste.",["faction:Alliance"]="Teldrassil serves as the northernmost bastion of the Alliance in Kalimdor, anchoring naval communication and trade between Darnassus and mainland kingdoms.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Lacking minerals and ore entirely, the tree's verdant canopy makes up for it by acting as a paradise for gatherers of Peacebloom, Silverleaf, and Earthroot."},kw={"circle of ancients","crown of the earth","darnassus","dolanaar","fandral staghelm","rut'theran","shadowglen","teldrassil","world tree"},rel={"zone:darnassus","zone:darkshore","quest:929","quest:940","npc:fandral-staghelm","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","topic:nordrassil","subzone:rut-theran-village"},m={levels="1-10"},src={"Teldrassil (Classic)","Teldrassil"}}
